\nAND PROVISIONING OF CABLE TRAYS, RUN-WAYS, STRUCTURES, FRAMES, FITTINGS, EQUIPMENT, PLANT, ELECTRICAL, AIR-CONDITIONING, ETC.,\nUNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT MEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT. THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS\nTO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT (NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS THE ITEMS IN THE ROOM TO BE REHABILITATED,\nCOMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS. THE USE OF THIS ITEM IS\nSUBJECT TO THE PROVISION AND APPROVAL OF AN ESTIMATE / QUOTATION. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ROOM, EACH (EA)'),(3027813,'R8.1','SEAL,OPNG:R8.1,FIRE,UNDR 200KM','This item consists of the Replacing of Fire Seals as directed by Telkom where the site is within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\nΓÇó	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nΓÇó	Identify and record in the SOS the number of openings to be sealed. \nΓÇó	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nΓÇó	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\nΓÇó	Replace all Fire Seals as per Telkom specification.\nΓÇó	The average sized opening to be sealed is 600mm x 600mm.\nΓÇó	This item excludes temporary fire seals using fire bags or bricks as such seals should be closed at no cost after working on such openings.\n\nThe unit for this item is per Fire Seal Replaced, each.','EA',951.60,'SEAL,OPNG:R8.1,FIRE,UNDR 200KM','SEAL, OPENING: ITEM NUMBER R8.1, TYPE FIRE, LOCATION >200 KM : THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT\nMEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT. THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT\n(NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS THE NUMBER OF OPENINGS TO BE SEALED, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS\nAND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, REPLACE ALL FIRE SEALS AS PER TELKOM SPECIFICATION, THE AVERAGE SIZED OPENING TO BE SEALED IS 600MM\nX 600MM. THIS ITEM EXCLUDES TEMPORARY FIRE SEALS USING FIRE BAGS OR BRICKS. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIRE SEAL REPLACED, EACH'),(3028538,'G10.10','PAY,FEE:G10.10 SERV,4X4 1 MAN TM 0-50KM','This item consists of the service fee for a 4X4 vehicle (up to 1.5 Ton) with 1 technical specialist person per radial km (as the crow flies) from the pre-determined dispatch point to site of works up to 50 km radius.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\nΓÇó Fuel\nΓÇó Vehicle running costs\nΓÇó Travelling losses (Labour travelling time) to site.\nΓÇó Material delivery from supply source to site.\nΓÇó Removals of debris, unused material/equipment, scrap from site on completion of project. \nΓÇó Return of recovered Telkom equipment / material to destination as indicated by Telkom.\n\nIt is assumed for calculation purposes that the size of vehicle required to execute this work would normally be one with a load capacity of 1000kg.\n\nA 20% deviation factor has been included in the rate to compensate for the difference between the radial distance and the distance travelled along the road.\n\nNote: this item will only be utilized in conditions where the use of a 4x4 vehicle is essential, such as:\nΓÇó Sandy terrain (Kalahari)\nΓÇó Off-road terrain (access to Telkom masts up a mountain)\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per radial km, per vehicle, per site or group of sites (if the sites are within a 5km radius of each other), travelled, each.','KM',14.27,'PAY,FEE:G10.10 SERV,4X4 1 MAN TM 0-50KM','PAY, FEE: TYPE G10.10 SERVICE, PURPOSE 4X4, 1 MAN TEAM 0-50KM : THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO; FUEL, VEHICLE RUNNING\nCOSTS, TRAVELLING LOSSES (LABOUR TRAVELLING TIME) TO SITE, MATERIAL DELIVERY FROM SUPPLY SOURCE TO SITE, REMOVALS OF DEBRIS, UNUSED\nMATERIAL/EQUIPMENT, SCR