on of an Electrical Certificate Of Compliance (COC) for new or existing Power installations (AC & DC).\n\nElementary installations refer to a plug from a board, or a single feed connection to a rack, or something similar - Normally an add-on at an existing site. Elementary shall be limited to the installation of a new circuit from an existing distribution board (DB). (e.g. installation of a new circuit breaker / protection device and installation of conductors to a new equipment element / rack.) \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\nΓÇó	The rectification / correction of one or more of the following minor defects / faults found at the site of inspection\nΓÇó	Provide up to 3 labels where required \nΓÇó	Correctly secure loose or incorrect terminations.[i.e Fit the correct size lug ΓÇô up to 3]\nΓÇó	Secure loose fixtures in DC boards, Should the discrimination and cascading be incorrect, it must be corrected [E.g. a 10A CB can only feed a CB with a lower rating (KA)], \nΓÇó	Install up to 3 rubber grommets on hazardous metal edges to prevent cable damage, where missing.\nΓÇó	Fit blanking covers on empty positions  \nΓÇó	Replace missing trunking covers up to 6m\nΓÇó	Secure unsupported cables with cable ties, to prevent strain on terminations,\nΓÇó	Notify the CR on site where DB keys are not available\nΓÇó	Equivalent to 1 small distribution board\n\nThe rate excludes:\nΓÇó	All travel related costs (See Service fee document) which also includes Transportation of material/equipment to and from site.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per COC per site, each (EA)','EA',945.00,'PRVD,EQUIP:PW2.4,COC ELEMT INSTLNS','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER PW2.4, TYPE COC ELEMT INSTLNS:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE RECTIFICATION/CORRECTION\nOF ONE OR MORE OF THE FOLLOWING MINOR DEFECTS/FAULTS FOUND AT THE SITE OF INSPECTION PROVIDE UP TO 3 LABELS WHERE REQUIRED\nCORRECTLY SECURE LOOSE OR INCORRECT TERMINATIONS.[I.E FIT THE CORRECT SIZE LUG # UP TO 3] SECURE LOOSE FIXTURES IN DC BOARDS,\nSHOULD THE DISCRIMINATION AND CASCADING BE INCORRECT, IT MUST BE CORRECTED [E.G. A 10A CB CAN ONLY FEED A CB WITH A LOWER RATING\n(KA), INSTALL UP TO 3 RUBBER GROMMETS ON HAZARDOUS METAL EDGES TO PREVENT CABLE DAMAGE, WHERE MISSING. FIT BLANKING COVERS ON EMPTY\nPOSITIONS REPLACE MISSING TRUNKING COVERS UP TO 6M SECURE UNSUPPORTED CABLES WITH CABLE TIES, TO PREVENT STRAIN ON TERMINATIONS,\nNOTIFY THE CR ON SITE WHERE DB KEYS ARE NOT AVAILABLE EQUIVALENT TO 1 SMALL DISTRIBUTION BOARD THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nRELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT) WHICH ALSO INCLUDES TRANSPORTATION OF MATERIAL/EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE. THE UNIT OF\nMEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER COC PER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3045334,'PW2.5','PW2.5 PRVD COC COMP INSTLNS','Provide Electrical Certificate Of Compliance for complex installations \n\nThis item consists of the general control of electrical installation, inspection, corrections to complex installations and provision of an Electrical Certificate of compliance (COC) for new or existing Power installations (AC & DC)\n\nComplex Installations refer to being the work done with rectifiers and batteries and multiple DB\'s \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\nΓÇó	The rectification / correction of one or more of the following minor defects / faults found at the site of inspection\nΓÇó	Provide labels where required\nΓÇó	Correctly secure loose or incorrect terminations.[i.e Fit the correct size lug ΓÇô up to 3]\nΓÇó	Secure loose fixtures in DC boards, Should the discrimination and cascading be incorrect, it must be corrected [E.g. a 10A CB can only feed a CB with a lower rating (KA)], \nΓÇó	Install up to 3 rubber grommets on hazardous metal edges to prevent cable damage, where missing.\nΓÇó	Fit blanking covers on empty positions \nΓÇó	Replace missing trunking covers up to 6m\nΓÇó	Secure unsupported cables with cable ties, to prevent strain on terminations,\nΓÇó	Notify the CR on site where DB keys are not available\n\nThe rate excludes:\nΓÇó	All travel related costs (See Service fee document) which also includes Transportation of material/equipment to and from site.\n \nThe unit of measure for this item is per COC per site, each (EA)','EA',1890.00,'PRVD,EQUIP:PW2.5,COC COMP INSTLNS','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER PW2.5, TYPE COC COMP INSTLNS:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE RECTIFICATION/CORRECTION\nOF ONE OR MORE OF THE FOLLOWING MINOR DEFECTS/FAULTS FOUND AT THE SITE OF INSPECTION PROVIDE LABELS WHERE REQUIRED CORRECTLY SECURE\nLOOSE OR INCORRECT TERMINATIONS.[I.E FIT THE CORRECT SIZE LUG # UP TO 3] SECURE LOOSE FIXTURES IN DC BOARDS, SHOULD THE\nDISCRIMINATION AND CASCADING BE INCORRECT, IT MUST BE CORRECTED [E.G. A 10A CB CAN ONLY FEED A CB WITH A LOWER RATING (KA)],\nINSTALL UP TO 3 RUBBER GROMMETS ON HAZARDOUS METAL EDGES TO PREVENT CABLE DAMAGE, WHERE MISSING. FIT BLANKING COVERS ON EMPTY\nPOSITIONS  REPLACE MISSING TRUNKING COVERS UP TO 6M SECURE UNSUPPORTED CABLES WITH CABLE TIES, TO PREVENT STRAIN ON TERMINATIONS,\nNOTIFY THE CR ON SITE WHERE DB KEYS ARE NOT AVAILABLE THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT) WHICH\nALSO INCLUDES TRANSPORTATION OF MATERIAL/EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER COC PER SITE, EACH\n(EA)'),(3045817,'CI2.48','CI2.48 HIRE SCFLDG','This item consists of the hiring of Scaffolding equipment for the installation of equipment where abseiling and mechanical hoisting equipment cannot be used.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Hiring of the Scaffolding equipment\nb) Labour to install and dismantle the scaffolding\nc) Adhering to all safety requirements\nd) Obtaining all necessary Work Authorizations and site access control approvals\ne) Making access arrangements including the obtaining of keys / access devices from the landlord (i.e. Exchange / gate / building keys, etc.)\nf) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required,\ng) All travel related costs within a 50km radius from the nominated dispatch point,\nh) Transportation of the scaffolding to and from site. \n\nNotes: \na) The use of this item is subject to approval from Openserve.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Travel related costs >50km radius of the nominated dispatch point (See additional items).\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per day.','DAY',9700.00,'HIRE,EQUIP:CI2.48, SCFLDG','HIRE, EQUIPMENT:TYPE CI2.48, SCFLDG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: HIRING OF THE SCAFFOLDING EQUIPMENT LABOUR TO INSTALL\nAND DISMANTLE THE SCAFFOLDING ADHERING TO ALL SAFETY REQUIREMENTS OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORK AUTHORIZATIONS AND SITE ACCESS\nCONTROL APPROVALS MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS INCLUDING THE OBTAINING OF KEYS / ACCESS DEVICES FROM THE LANDLORD (I.E. EXCHANGE /\nGATE / BUILDING KEYS, ETC.) INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS WITHIN\nA 50KM RADIUS FROM THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT, TRANSPORTATION OF THE SCAFFOLDING TO AND FROM SITE. NOTES: THE USE OF THIS ITEM IS\nSUBJECT TO APPROVAL FROM OPENSERVE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS >50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT (SEE\nADDITIONAL ITEMS). THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DAY'),(3045865,'CI1.25','CI1.25 MNHL CONSTR NON-STD 3.52M L/T RD WAY','This item consists of a manhole construction / reconstruction (nonstandard shape) 3.52M ΓÇ£LΓÇ¥ (Drawing MHGP 9A) and ΓÇ£TΓÇ¥ (Drawing MHT 9G) roadway\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Supply, delivery and casting of 20-25MPA concrete, \nb) Fitting of the frame, cover and coping, finished by with a wooden float and corner tool, \nc) All equipment, shuttering and material required, \nd) The positioning of the manhole, \ne) The loading requirements of SABS specification 558 table 2 for the particular situation of loading, i.e. heavy, medium or light pertaining, \nf) The supply of Telkom approved material, including corrugated iron - 0.6mm full hard, ΓÇÿAΓÇÖ grade, ΓÇ£IΓÇ¥ beams - 140 x 70 x 6mm, treated with approved rustproof paint to Area ManagerΓÇÖs approval ΓÇô to be used when rails are unavailable, \ng) Rustproof paint (e.g. chromites) to the Area Manager\'s approval, \nh) Costs in respect of slump tests when the Area Manager allows machine mixing,\ni) The stabilizing of the backfill around roadway manhole necks with 2 x 50kg pockets of cement per cubic metre of sand, \nj) The cutting, removal and disposal of all types of existing pipe lengths running through the manhole (empty or occupied), \nk) The supply and fitting of split pipe/s over existing electrical cables, marking of pipes with high-tension warning stickers and painting with red paint. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Frame and cover (to be supplied by Telkom), \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',32129.17,'CONSTR,MNHL:CI1.25,NON-STD 3.52M RD WAY','CONSTRUCT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.25, TYPE NON-STD 3.52M L/T RD WAY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SUPPLY, DELIVERY AND\nCASTING OF 20-25MPA CONCRETE, FITTING OF THE FRAME, COVER AND COPING, FINISHED BY WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL\nEQUIPMENT, SHUTTERING AND MATERIAL REQUIRED, THE POSITIONING OF THE MANHOLE, THE LOADING REQUIREMENTS OF SABS SPECIFICATION 558\nTABLE 2 FOR THE PARTICULAR SITUATION OF LOADING, I.E. HEAVY, MEDIUM OR LIGHT PERTAINING, THE SUPPLY OF TELKOM APPROVED MATERIAL,\nINCLUDING CORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL HARD, #A# GRADE, #I# BEAMS - 140 X 70 X 6MM, TREATED WITH APPROVED RUSTPROOF PAINT TO AREA\nMANAGER#S APPROVAL # TO BE USED WHEN RAILS ARE UNAVAILABLE,  RUSTPROOF PAINT (E.G. CHROMITES) TO THE AREA MANAGER\'S APPROVAL, COSTS\nIN RESPECT OF SLUMP TESTS WHEN THE AREA MANAGER ALLOWS MACHINE MIXING, THE STABILIZING OF THE BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS\nWITH 2 X 50KG POCKETS OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE OF SAND, THE CUTTING, REMOVAL AND DISPOSAL OF ALL TYPES OF EXISTING PIPE LENGTHS\nRUNNING THROUGH THE MANHOLE (EMPTY OR OCCUPIED), THE SUPPLY AND FITTING OF SPLIT PIPE/S OVER EXISTING ELECTRICAL CABLES, MARKING OF\nPIPES WITH HIGH-TENSION WARNING STICKERS AND PAINTING WITH RED PAINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: FRAME AND COVER (TO BE SUPPLIED BY\nTELKOM), ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3045866,'CI2.15','CI2.15 INSTLN FBR CABL PUSH-IN','This item consists of the installation of fibre cable by push-in method. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Installation of all sizes of fibre cable in ducting / micro ducts,  \nb) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water). \n \nThe rate excludes:\na) Utilizing of a Cable Jet / Blow-in machine,  \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per meter (MT) (point to point).','MT',7.24,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.15,FBR PUSH-IN','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.15, TYPE FBR PUSH-IN:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: INSTALLATION OF ALL SIZES OF FIBRE\nCABLE IN DUCTING / MICRO DUCTS, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. POLY # WATER). THE RATE EXCLUDES: UTILIZING OF A CABLE JET /\nBLOW-IN MACHINE, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: SP#AL0001\nCTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METER (MT) (POINT TO POINT)'),(3045867,'CI2.3','CI2.3 LAY/FSTN CABL>200-600PR/ RODNT FBR /7DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of laying or fastening of any of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables > 200 to 600 pair,\nΓÇó All Rodent Proof Fibre Cables,\nΓÇó 7-way and greater micro ducts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Laying and or fastening onto trays, walls, brackets, risers, under floors, ceilings, trunking, etc.,\nb) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nc) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps, etc.),\nd) Performing micro duct integrity test,\ne) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nf) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \ng) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) Quantity for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual laid and or fastened cable / duct irrespective of any slack required.\n\nThe specification for these items is:\na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable / duct per metre (MT).','MT',34.99,'LAY,CBL:CI2.3,FSTN 200-600PR','LAY, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.3, TYPE FSTN 200-600PR/RODNT FBR/7DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LAYING AND OR FASTENING\nONTO TRAYS, WALLS, BRACKETS, RISERS, UNDER FLOORS, CEILINGS, TRUNKING, ETC., PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT THAT IS NECESSARY TO\nEXECUTE THE WORK, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, SADDLES, GLUE, MICRO DUCT COUPLERS, MICRO\nDUCT END CAPS, ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS CABLES /\nDUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE WORK. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST\nOF THE CABLE / DUCTS, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: QUANTITY FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED\nFROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL LAID AND OR FASTENED CABLE / DUCT IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE\nITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE / DUCT PER METRE (MT)'),(3045868,'CI1.36','CI1.36 INSTLN PRE-FAB UTLTY BX 300/400','This item consists of the installation of a prefabricated utility box (i.e. RHI-NODE 300/400).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The necessary excavation up to existing pipe level or new trench level, backfilling, compaction and D.C.P testing, \nb) All pipe entries, \nc) The sealing of the pipe entries, utilising an approved sealing method and sealant,  \nd) The labelling of the box, according to requirements. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \nb) The cost of the prefabricated utility box.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per utility box each (EA).','EA',299.41,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI1.36,UTLTY BX 300/400','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI1.36, TYPE PRE-FAB UTLTY BX 300/400:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE NECESSARY\nEXCAVATION UP TO EXISTING PIPE LEVEL OR NEW TRENCH LEVEL, BACKFILLING, COMPACTION AND D.C.P TESTING, ALL PIPE ENTRIES, THE SEALING\nOF THE PIPE ENTRIES, UTILISING AN APPROVED SEALING METHOD AND SEALANT, THE LABELLING OF THE BOX, ACCORDING TO REQUIREMENTS. THE\nRATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE COST OF THE PREFABRICATED UTILITY BOX. THE\nSPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER UTILITY BOX EACH (EA)'),(3045869,'CI2.1','CI2.1 LAY/FSTN CABL Γëñ 10PR / Γëñ24FBR /S MICRO-DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of laying or fastening of any of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables up to 10 pair,\nΓÇó Air Pipes,\nΓÇó LAN Cables, \nΓÇó All Fibre Cables up to 24 fibres (including Inter Facility Cable),\nΓÇó Single micro ducts.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Laying and or fastening onto Trays, Risers, Under floors, Ceilings, Trunking, etc.,\nb) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nc) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps, etc.),\nd) Performing micro duct integrity test, \ne) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nf) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \ng) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) Quantity for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual laid and or fastened cable / duct irrespective of any slack required. \n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable / duct per metre (MT).','MT',19.27,'LAY,CBL:CI2.1,FSTN 10PR/4FBR/S','LAY, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.1, TYPE FSTN 10PR/4FBR/S MICRO-DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LAYING AND OR FASTENING\nONTO TRAYS, RISERS, UNDER FLOORS, CEILINGS, TRUNKING, ETC., PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT THAT IS NECESSARY TO EXECUTE THE\nWORK, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, SADDLES, GLUE, MICRO DUCT COUPLERS, MICRO DUCT END CAPS,\nETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, REMOVAL\nOF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE WORK.  THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE CABLE /\nDUCTS, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: QUANTITY FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO\nPOINT OF THE ACTUAL LAID AND OR FASTENED CABLE / DUCT IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS:\nSP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE / DUCT PER METRE (MT)'),(3045917,'ME10.5','ME10.5 ENG ME RCVY','This item consists of the detailed engineering for the recovery of the Metro Ethernet Client device/s (i.e. ATN905-V/SAS-E/SAS-D, etc.) at an existing site.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Site visit / survey\nb) Labour\nc) Detailed engineering of Metro Ethernet solution on Openserve approved system software\nd) Submission of executable file\ne) Decommissioning process\nf) All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.  Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb. Johannesburg.\nc. Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd. Ethekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne. Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata).\nf. Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per site, each (EA).','EA',1525.03,'ENGNR,STE:ME10.5,ME RCVY','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER ME10.5, TYPE ME RCVY:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR THE RECOVERY OF THE METRO\nETHERNET CLIENT DEVICE/S (I.E. ATN905-V/SAS-E/SAS-D, ETC.) AT AN EXISTING SITE. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SITE VISIT\n/ SURVEY, LABOUR, DETAILED ENGINEERING OF METRO ETHERNET SOLUTION ON OPENSERVE APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE, SUBMISSION OF EXECUTABLE\nFILE, DECOMMISSIONING PROCESS, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS WITHIN A 50-KM RADIUS TO AND FROM THE SITE CALCULATED FROM THE FOLLOWING\nTOWNS: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER,\nVREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT\nELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS\nIN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER SITE, EACH (EA).'),(3045918,'ME10.1','ME10.1 ENG ME SITE VISIT','This item consists of a site visit, full investigation, detailed engineering survey for an ME customer on all new and / or existing technologies (i.e. Fibre, copper, MW, VSAT, etc.) up to and including the Customer Premises Equipment and the creation of an RFO (Requirement for Occupation) Specification document for the customer site (ME order/s).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. manhole / Exchange keys etc.)\nb) Informing the CNFO supervisors per e-mail 48 hours prior to site investigations.\nc) Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements with CNFO sites and customer sites.\nd) making appointments with MCO Spoc within 48 hours at new building sites. \ne) Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom system/s \nf) Conducting a site visit at the customer premises and exchange site when required,\ng) Clarification of the requirements with the customer on site\nh) Obtaining written permission from the customer / Landlord or their contact details\ni) Administration costs\nj) A full technology investigation and solutions (Single site investigations and / or bulk orders)\nk) Performing a detailed engineering survey including the exposing / accessing / opening of route access points such as manholes, FDP, FTH, housings, boxes, buildings, etc.\nl) Pumping of manholes where necessary, irrespective of site conditions\nm) Providing the sketches of the requirements (i.e. fibre entry / route, power, cable trays, rack, floor plan, ducts, etc.) as well as related information including photos, spider diagram, tick sheets, etc.\nn) The compilation of the RFO Spec document/s including pipe entries, AC / DC power, ducting, wireways, etc.\no) Attaching photos or drawings of RFO requirements on RFO specifications.\np) Compiling and submitting an RFO build Estimate/Quotation \nq) Submitting and/or attaching all information including completed RFO Specification.\nr) Obtaining / confirming GPS co-ordinates.\ns) Obtaining all required information to place the site building on Netplan\nt) Supplying the DP number (pole or indoor DP). If possible SDC number and/or telephone numbers.\nu) Confirming cable size. \nv) Confirming a suitable position for the VSAT equipment\nw) Confirming that structures are secure and safe enough to mount antennas, IDUs and other fixtures\nx) Confirming that the area is free of interferences from any other RF related equipment\ny) Confirming that the IDU unit position is close to a power point, customer equipment and that there is sufficient ventilation\nz) Updating all documentation / system requirements\naa) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nbb) Labour\ncc) Administration costs\ndd) All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na. Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb. Johannesburg.\nc. Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd. Ethekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne. Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata).\nf. Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n\nNote: \na) This item may be only be claimed once per customer site irrespective of the number of services / serials required.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per customer site, each (EA)','EA',4539.68,'ENGNR,STE:ME10.1,ME VISIT','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER ME10.1, TYPE ME VISIT:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF A SITE VISIT, FULL INVESTIGATION, DETAILED ENGINEERING\nSURVEY FOR AN ME CUSTOMER ON ALL NEW AND / OR EXISTING TECHNOLOGIES (I.E. FIBRE, COPPER, MW, VSAT, ETC.) UP TO AND INCLUDING THE\nCUSTOMER PREMISES EQUIPMENT AND THE CREATION OF AN RFO (REQUIREMENT FOR OCCUPATION) SPECIFICATION DOCUMENT FOR THE CUSTOMER SITE\n(ME ORDER/S). THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS\nDEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. MANHOLE / EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), INFORMING THE CNFO SUPERVISORS PER E-MAIL 48 HOURS PRIOR TO SITE\nINVESTIGATIONS, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS WITH CNFO SITES AND CUSTOMER SITES, MAKING\nAPPOINTMENTS WITH MCO SPOC WITHIN 48 HOURS AT NEW BUILDING SITES, OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END RECORDS FROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S,\nCONDUCTING A SITE VISIT AT THE CUSTOMER PREMISES AND EXCHANGE SITE WHEN REQUIRED, CLARIFICATION OF THE REQUIREMENTS WITH THE\nCUSTOMER ON SITE, OBTAINING WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM THE CUSTOMER / LANDLORD OR THEIR CONTACT DETAILS, ADMINISTRATION COSTS, A FULL\nTECHNOLOGY INVESTIGATION AND SOLUTIONS (SINGLE SITE INVESTIGATIONS AND / OR BULK ORDERS), PERFORMING A DETAILED ENGINEERING SURVEY\nINCLUDING THE EXPOSING / ACCESSING / OPENING OF ROUTE ACCESS POINTS SUCH AS MANHOLES, FDP, FTH, HOUSINGS, BOXES, BUILDINGS, ETC.,\nPUMPING OF MANHOLES WHERE NECESSARY, IRRESPECTIVE OF SITE CONDITIONS, PROVIDING THE SKETCHES OF THE REQUIREMENTS (I.E. FIBRE ENTRY\n/ ROUTE, POWER, CABLE TRAYS, RACK, FLOOR PLAN, DUCTS, ETC.) AS WELL AS RELATED INFORMATION INCLUDING PHOTOS, SPIDER DIAGRAM, TICK\nSHEETS, ETC., THE COMPILATION OF THE RFO SPEC DOCUMENT/S INCLUDING PIPE ENTRIES, AC / DC POWER, DUCTING, WIREWAYS, ETC., ATTACHING\nPHOTOS OR DRAWINGS OF RFO REQUIREMENTS ON RFO SPECIFICATIONS, COMPILING AND SUBMITTING AN RFO BUILD ESTIMATE/QUOTATION, SUBMITTING\nAND/OR ATTACHING ALL INFORMATION INCLUDING COMPLETED RFO SPECIFICATION, OBTAINING / CONFIRMING GPS CO-ORDINATES, OBTAINING ALL'),(3045919,'ME20.4','ME20.4 RCRD & PKG EQUIP','This item consists of the recording and packaging of equipment (i.e. ATN905-V, SAS-E, SAS-D, etc.) fit for re-use into the Openserve network\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Recording/updating an inventory list of all recovered equipment, cards, modules etc.\nb) Providing labour for boxing and packaging \nc) Supplying the cardboard box and packaging i.e. packaging as per procurement specification\nd) Completion of the recovery process i.e. IE6\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per cubic metre or part thereof (M3).','M3',459.96,'PAY,FEE:ME20.4 RCRD & PKG EQP','PAY, FEE:PURPOSE ME2.4 RCRD & PKG EQUIP:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: RECORDING/UPDATING AN INVENTORY LIST OF ALL\nRECOVERED EQUIPMENT, CARDS, MODULES ETC., PROVIDING LABOUR FOR BOXING AND PACKAGING, SUPPLYING THE CARDBOARD BOX AND PACKAGING I.E.\nPACKAGING AS PER PROCUREMENT SPECIFICATION, COMPLETION OF THE RECOVERY PROCESS I.E. IE6, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS WITHIN A 50-KM\nRADIUS TO AND FROM THE SITE CALCULATED FROM THE FOLLOWING TOWNS: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING,\nRUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY,\nPIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA),\nBLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH\nPOINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUBIC METRE OR PART THEREOF (M3).'),(3045930,'CI1.4','CI1.4 EXCVT NORM SOIL RD/RLWY','This item consists trenching across all types of roads/railway deviating from the standard trench size width 0.450 metre X depth 1.2 metre (nominal depth 1.3 metre). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Cutting of tar or concrete and / or removal of paving slabs or bricks,\nb) All excavations in the roadway (including splays),\nc) Pilot holes/ crossing of services (to determine the ground condition and to identify / locate underground services or obstructions),\nd) Backfilling,\ne) All backfilling/stabilising material (i.e. 2 x 50kg pockets of cement per cubic metre of backfill or as required by wayleaves conditions. Stabilised backfill must extend 1 metre beyond kerbstone),\nf) Compacting,\ng) D.C.P testing,\nh) The supply of water if necessary to obtain optimum moisture content,\ni) Tunnelling under obstacles (i.e. kerbstones, road signs etc.), \nj) Re-instatement / replacement of kerb stones (when required),\nk) Supporting of all services (i.e. electrical, water, sewerage, etc.),\nl) Laying danger tape and screen-wire (where required),\nm) Laying of trench crete where required,\nn) Laying of all pipes/ducts and buried cable,\no) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling),\np) Ensure pipe is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc., \nq) Handling, cutting and repairing of existing pipes (supply PVC),\nr) Bedding and padding (reuse of existing material upon Telkom approval),\ns) Removal of all spoil including boulders,\nt) Clearing the surface,\nu) Removing and or erecting fencing when required,\nv) Backfilling of cavities,\nw) Removing, transporting and disposing of all surplus material,\nx) Shoring, when required,\ny) Pumping and controlling of water,\nz) Barricading of the excavation,\naa) Provision of all safety requirements (i.e. road signs, cones, flagman, etc.), \nbb) Grading of the trench where ducts need to be laid,\ncc) Maintaining of the trench until permanent re-instatement. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\nb) The cost of the supply and delivery of the Trench crete.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cubic metre (m┬│).','M3',215.61,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.4,NORM SOIL RD/RLWY','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.4, TYPE NORM SOIL RD/RLWY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CUTTING OF TAR OR CONCRETE AND\n/ OR REMOVAL OF PAVING SLABS OR BRICKS, ALL EXCAVATIONS IN THE ROADWAY (INCLUDING SPLAYS), PILOT HOLES/ CROSSING OF SERVICES (TO\nDETERMINE THE GROUND CONDITION AND TO IDENTIFY / LOCATE UNDERGROUND SERVICES OR OBSTRUCTIONS), BACKFILLING, ALL\nBACKFILLING/STABILISING MATERIAL (I.E. 2 X 50KG POCKETS OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE OF BACKFILL OR AS REQUIRED BY WAYLEAVES\nCONDITIONS. STABILISED BACKFILL MUST EXTEND 1 METRE BEYOND KERBSTONE), COMPACTING, D.C.P TESTING, THE SUPPLY OF WATER IF NECESSARY\nTO OBTAIN OPTIMUM MOISTURE CONTENT, TUNNELLING UNDER OBSTACLES (I.E. KERBSTONES, ROAD SIGNS ETC.), RE-INSTATEMENT / REPLACEMENT OF\nKERB STONES (WHEN REQUIRED), SUPPORTING OF ALL SERVICES (I.E. ELECTRICAL, WATER, SEWERAGE, ETC.), LAYING DANGER TAPE AND\nSCREEN-WIRE (WHERE REQUIRED), LAYING OF TRENCH CRETE WHERE REQUIRED, LAYING OF ALL PIPES/DUCTS AND BURIED CABLE, PIPE ENTRIES\n(EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING), ENSURE PIPE IS USEABLE BY MEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., HANDLING, CUTTING\nAND REPAIRING OF EXISTING PIPES (SUPPLY PVC), BEDDING AND PADDING (REUSE OF EXISTING MATERIAL UPON TELKOM APPROVAL), REMOVAL OF ALL\nSPOIL INCLUDING BOULDERS, CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING AND OR ERECTING FENCING WHEN REQUIRED, BACKFILLING OF CAVITIES, REMOVING,\nTRANSPORTING AND DISPOSING OF ALL SURPLUS MATERIAL, SHORING, WHEN REQUIRED, PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER, BARRICADING OF THE\nEXCAVATION, PROVISION OF ALL SAFETY REQUIREMENTS (I.E. ROAD SIGNS, CONES, FLAGMAN, ETC.), GRADING OF THE TRENCH WHERE DUCTS NEED TO\nBE LAID, MAINTAINING OF THE TRENCH UNTIL PERMANENT RE-INSTATEMENT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE COST OF THE SUPPLY AND DELIVERY OF THE TRENCH CRETE. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3045931,'CI1.53','CI1.53 PRVD ADD SFTY ASBSTS','This item consists of the additional costs required for safety precautions when working in soil conditions are contaminated with asbestos. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The provision and displaying of safety signs, \nb) The provision and disposal of asbestos specific personal protective safety gear, \nc) The provision of medical screening as per SANS requirements,  \nd) Site management (i.e. cleaning of equipment, tools, vehicles, keeping site safe from dust, etc.). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654,\nb) SANS requirements.  \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per 5-man team per day each (EA).','EA',519.83,'PRVD,EQUIP:CI1.53,ADD SFTY ASBSTS','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI1.53, TYPE ADD SFTY ASBSTS:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PROVISION AND DISPLAYING\nOF SAFETY SIGNS, THE PROVISION AND DISPOSAL OF ASBESTOS SPECIFIC PERSONAL PROTECTIVE SAFETY GEAR, THE PROVISION OF MEDICAL\nSCREENING AS PER SANS REQUIREMENTS, SITE MANAGEMENT (I.E. CLEANING OF EQUIPMENT, TOOLS, VEHICLES, KEEPING SITE SAFE FROM DUST,\nETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654, SANS REQUIREMENTS. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 5-MAN TEAM PER DAY EACH (EA)'),(3045932,'CI1.6','CI1.6 TRNCH&LY PIP (100MM W X150MM D)','This item consists of trenching (All soil types), for cut-micro trenching break-outs, on sidewalks, the laying of 20mm diameter, Stainless-Steel Bosal pipes and installing micro-ducts in all types of, verges, sidewalks with surfaces such as, gravel, grass, tar, cement, paving etc. \n(Typical trench width 100mm X depth 150mm up to 300mm).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Manual Trenching / excavating in all types of soil conditions / surfaces from the road to boundary box, pedestal, mini-manhole, etc.),\nb) Core drilling of the curb stone when required,\nc) Laying and connecting of the SS pipe (20mm dia) in the trench, \nd) Installing the micro-duct/s (any number of ducts and / or combination of micro-ducts (i.e. 8/5 mm single ways and 12/10 mm 2 ways) in the metal pipe,\ne) Supply and installing Bedding and Padding (when required),\nf) Backfilling,\ng) Compacting,\nh) Re-instatement of surfaces. (i.e. grass, gravel, tar, cement, paving, etc.),\ni) All testing to specification (i.e. Compaction, micro-duct, re-instatement, etc.),\nj) Minor Materials (i.e. bedding and padding, backfill, Micro-duct connectors, etc.),\nk) The cost of the SS metal pipe (ΓÇ£Bosal pipeΓÇ¥ 20 mm DIA) and pipe joints / connectors,\nl) Shipping and storage.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Cost of the Micro-duct/s,\nb) Cost of the pedestal, boundary box, enclosures,\nc) Building a brick and mortar Pipe Junction Box (PJB) or Accessible Pipe Junction Box,\nd) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',196.66,'EXPOS,TRNCH:CI1.6,LY PIP','EXPOSE, TRENCH:ITEM NUMBER CI1.6, TYPE LY PIP, SIZE (WD 100MM X DP 150MM) :THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MANUAL\nTRENCHING / EXCAVATING IN ALL TYPES OF SOIL CONDITIONS / SURFACES FROM THE ROAD TO BOUNDARY BOX, PEDESTAL, MINI-MANHOLE, ETC.),\nCORE DRILLING OF THE CURB STONE WHEN REQUIRED, LAYING AND CONNECTING OF THE SS PIPE (20MM DIA) IN THE TRENCH, INSTALLING THE\nMICRO-DUCT/S (ANY NUMBER OF DUCTS AND / OR COMBINATION OF MICRO-DUCTS (I.E. 8/5 MM SINGLE WAYS AND 12/10 MM 2 WAYS) IN THE METAL\nPIPE, SUPPLY AND INSTALLING BEDDING AND PADDING (WHEN REQUIRED), BACKFILLING, COMPACTING, RE-INSTATEMENT OF SURFACES. (I.E. GRASS,\nGRAVEL, TAR, CEMENT, PAVING, ETC.), ALL TESTING TO SPECIFICATION (I.E. COMPACTION, MICRO-DUCT, RE-INSTATEMENT, ETC.), MINOR\nMATERIALS (I.E. BEDDING AND PADDING, BACKFILL, MICRO-DUCT CONNECTORS, ETC.), THE COST OF THE SS METAL PIPE (#BOSAL PIPE# 20 MM DIA)\nAND PIPE JOINTS / CONNECTORS, SHIPPING AND STORAGE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: COST OF THE MICRO-DUCT/S, COST OF THE PEDESTAL, BOUNDARY\nBOX, ENCLOSURES, BUILDING A BRICK AND MORTAR PIPE JUNCTION BOX (PJB) OR ACCESSIBLE PIPE JUNCTION BOX, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM\nSITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nMETRE (MT)'),(3045933,'CI2.21','CI2.21 SEALG PIPE','This item consists of sealing of SDC, DP or pillar pipes.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The unblocking of pipes from waste, sand and re-enterable resin, \nb) All equipment and material required to complete the task. \n\nThe rate excludes:\nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is: \nd) 325. CTO-004654,\ne) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',69.24,'SEAL,PIPE:CI2.21','SEAL, PIPE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.21:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE UNBLOCKING OF PIPES FROM WASTE, SAND AND RE-ENTERABLE\nRESIN, ALL EQUIPMENT AND MATERIAL REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THE TASK. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE\nFEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH\n(EA)'),(3045934,'CI1.42','CI1.42 SUPLY & INSTLN 1.5M STL RAIL','This item consists of the supply and installation of a 1.5 metre steelrail (railway tracks / ΓÇ£i \" beams) at an SDC site. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply of the required number of steel rails / \"I\" Beams, \nb) The excavation, planting and concreting of the rails / \"I\" Beams in the holes, \nc) The treating of the rails / ΓÇ£IΓÇ¥ Beams with Zinchromate and the painting thereof.  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per 1.5 metre steelrail each (EA).','EA',701.01,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI1.42,1.5M STL RAIL,SUPLY','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI1.42, TYPE 1.5M STL RAIL, ADDITIONAL TASK SUPPLY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE\nSUPPLY OF THE REQUIRED NUMBER OF STEEL RAILS / I BEAMS, THE EXCAVATION, PLANTING AND CONCRETING OF THE RAILS / I BEAMS IN THE\nHOLES, THE TREATING OF THE RAILS / #I# BEAMS WITH ZINCHROMATE AND THE PAINTING THEREOF. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND\nFROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\n1.5 METRE STEELRAIL EACH (EA)'),(3045936,'CI2.6','CI2.6 HAUL CABL>10-200PR/2-4DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of hauling or simultaneously hauling of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables (UG and Indoor) >10PR ΓÇô 200PR,\nΓÇó 2-4 way micro ducts, \nΓÇó 32/40mm inner ducts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nb) Cleaning, preparing, threading and testing existing Telkom duct to ensure duct is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc.,\nc) Overcoming engineering difficulties such as hauling through Utility Boxes, pillar joints, entry points etc.,\nd) Pumping and controlling of water while hauling takes place,\ne) The fitting of uni-strut support / flat brackets for the supporting of the cable in Utility Boxes\nf) Cleaning Utility Boxes and surroundings on completion,\ng) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water, dry air, cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps, 32/40mm micro duct couplers etc.),\nh) Performing micro duct integrity test, \ni) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nj) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \nk) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\n\na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled. \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled.\nc) The price per metre is the same for the hauling of 1 inner-duct / micro-duct or simultaneous hauling of 2 inner-ducts (32/40mm) / micro-ducts\nd) If 3 or 4 inner-ducts / micro-ducts are simultaneously hauled then this item may be claimed twice\nl) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required \nm) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) Supply of support brackets (to be supplied by Telkom),\nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled,  \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled,\nc) The price per metre is the same for the hauling of 1 inner-duct / micro-duct or simultaneous hauling of 2 inner-ducts (32/40mm) / micro-ducts,\nd) If 3 or 4 inner-ducts / micro-ducts are simultaneously hauled, then this item may be claimed twice. \n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable/s (hauled or simultaneously hauled) per metre (MT).','MT',7.46,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.6,HAUL 10-200PR/2-4DUCT','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.6, TYPE HAUL 10-200PR/2-4DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND\nEQUIPMENT THAT IS NECESSARY TO EXECUTE THE WORK, CLEANING, PREPARING, THREADING AND TESTING EXISTING TELKOM DUCT TO ENSURE DUCT IS\nUSEABLE BY MEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., OVERCOMING ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS HAULING THROUGH\nUTILITY BOXES, PILLAR JOINTS, ENTRY POINTS ETC., PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER WHILE HAULING TAKES PLACE, THE FITTING OF\nUNI-STRUT SUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS FOR THE SUPPORTING OF THE CABLE IN UTILITY BOXES CLEANING UTILITY BOXES AND SURROUNDINGS ON\nCOMPLETION, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. POLY # WATER, DRY AIR, CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, SADDLES, GLUE, MICRO DUCT\nCOUPLERS, MICRO DUCT END CAPS, 32/40MM MICRO DUCT COUPLERS ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING,\nMEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON\nCOMPLETION OF THE WORK. FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE\nOTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED. FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED\nFROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED. THE PRICE PER METRE IS\nTHE SAME FOR THE HAULING OF 1 INNER-DUCT / MICRO-DUCT OR SIMULTANEOUS HAULING OF 2 INNER-DUCTS (32/40MM) / MICRO-DUCTS IF 3 OR 4\nINNER-DUCTS / MICRO-DUCTS ARE SIMULTANEOUSLY HAULED THEN THIS ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED TWICE FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL\nBE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT\nTHE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY\nSLACK REQUIRED THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE CABLE / DUCTS, SUPPLY OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM), ALL TRAVEL'),(3045937,'CI2.25','CI2.25 RECVR DUCT','This item consists of the recovery of all sizes of inner-ducts and micro-ducts.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The recovery of ducts from the pipe.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) The quantity recovered for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any further lengths handled / recovered, \nb) For indoor ducts the quantity recovered for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual recovered duct length irrespective of any further lengths handled / recovered.\n\nThe specification for this item is \na) 325. CTO-004654, \nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per duct per metre (MT).','MT',2.50,'RCVR,EQUIP:CI2.25,DUCT','RECOVER, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.25, TYPE DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE RECOVERY OF DUCTS FROM THE PIPE. THE\nRATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THE QUANTITY RECOVERED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE\nMEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY FURTHER LENGTHS HANDLED / RECOVERED, FOR\nINDOOR DUCTS THE QUANTITY RECOVERED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL RECOVERED DUCT LENGTH\nIRRESPECTIVE OF ANY FURTHER LENGTHS HANDLED / RECOVERED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS 325. CTO-004654, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\nTHE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DUCT PER METRE (MT)'),(3045938,'CI1.46','CI1.46 REPL MNHL LID','This item consists of the replacement existing manhole lid with a security lid. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Replacement of existing lids to combat theft, \nb) Picking up of the new lid and the return of the old lid to the stores.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Supply of the security lid (to be supplied by Telkom), \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per lid each (EA)','EA',81.16,'REPL,LID:CI1.46,MNHL','REPLACE, LID:ITEM NUMBER CI1.46, TYPE MNHL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: REPLACEMENT OF EXISTING LIDS TO COMBAT THEFT,\nPICKING UP OF THE NEW LID AND THE RETURN OF THE OLD LID TO THE STORES. THE RATE EXCLUDES: SUPPLY OF THE SECURITY LID (TO BE\nSUPPLIED BY TELKOM), ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER LID EACH (EA)'),(3045939,'CI2.35','CI2.35 INSTL 12 DRWR SHLF','This item consists of the Installation of a 12-drawer shelf.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Labour for the installation of a 12-drawer shelf,\nb) Labelling,\nc) Minor build material.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\nb) The cost of the shelf.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per 12 drawer shelf, each (EA).','EA',637.69,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.35,12 DRWR SHLF','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.35, TYPE 12 DRWR SHLF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION OF A\n12-DRAWER SHELF, LABELLING, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE COST OF\nTHE SHELF. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 12 DRAWER SHELF, EACH (EA)'),(3045940,'CI1.20','CI1.20 MNHL CONSTR STD 3.52M FT WAY','This item consists of a manhole construction / reconstruction (standard shape) 3.52M footway (Drawing SMH 9C). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Supply, delivery and casting of 20-25MPA concrete, \nb) Fitting of the frame, cover and coping, finished with a wooden float and corner tool, \nc) All equipment, shuttering and material required, \nd) Positioning of the manhole, \ne) Loading requirements of SABS specification 558 table 2 for the particular situation of loading, i.e. heavy, medium or light pertaining, \nf) The supply of Telkom approved material, including corrugated iron - 0.6mm full hard, ΓÇ£A\" grade, \"I\" beams - 140 x 70 x 6mm, treated with approved rustproof paint (e.g. chromites) to the Area Manager\'s approval - to be used when rails are unavailable, \ng) Costs in respect of slump tests when the Area Manager allows machine mixing, \nh) The stabilizing of the backfill around roadway manhole necks with 2 x 50kg of cement per cubic metre of sand,  \ni) The cutting, removal and disposal of all types of existing pipe lengths running through the manhole (empty or occupied), \nj) The supply and fitting of split pipe/s over existing electrical cables, marking of pipes with high-tension warning stickers and painting with red paint. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',19898.18,'CONSTR,MNHL:CI1.20,STD 3.52M FT WAY','CONSTRUCT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.20, TYPE STD 3.52M FT WAY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SUPPLY, DELIVERY AND CASTING\nOF 20-25MPA CONCRETE, FITTING OF THE FRAME, COVER AND COPING, FINISHED WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL EQUIPMENT,\nSHUTTERING AND MATERIAL REQUIRED, POSITIONING OF THE MANHOLE, LOADING REQUIREMENTS OF SABS SPECIFICATION 558 TABLE 2 FOR THE\nPARTICULAR SITUATION OF LOADING, I.E. HEAVY, MEDIUM OR LIGHT PERTAINING, THE SUPPLY OF TELKOM APPROVED MATERIAL, INCLUDING\nCORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL HARD, #A GRADE, I BEAMS - 140 X 70 X 6MM, TREATED WITH APPROVED RUSTPROOF PAINT (E.G. CHROMITES) TO\nTHE AREA MANAGER\'S APPROVAL - TO BE USED WHEN RAILS ARE UNAVAILABLE, COSTS IN RESPECT OF SLUMP TESTS WHEN THE AREA MANAGER ALLOWS\nMACHINE MIXING, THE STABILIZING OF THE BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS WITH 2 X 50KG OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE OF SAND, THE\nCUTTING, REMOVAL AND DISPOSAL OF ALL TYPES OF EXISTING PIPE LENGTHS RUNNING THROUGH THE MANHOLE (EMPTY OR OCCUPIED), THE SUPPLY AND\nFITTING OF SPLIT PIPE/S OVER EXISTING ELECTRICAL CABLES, MARKING OF PIPES WITH HIGH-TENSION WARNING STICKERS AND PAINTING WITH RED\nPAINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3045942,'CI1.47','CI1.47 STAB BCKFLL MTRL','This item consists of stabilizing backfill material with cement (i.e. crossing driveways, parking areas and walkways). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) 2 x 50-kg pockets cement per cubic metre soil to be used for stabilizing and to be supplied by the service provider, \nb) This item is not to be used for stabilizing of backfill at road-crossings.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cubic metre (m┬│).','M3',268.70,'SPRT,EXCAV:CI1.47,STAB BCKFLL MTRL','SUPPORT, EXCAVATION:ITEM NUMBER CI1.47, TYPE STAB BCKFLL MTRL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: 2 X 50-KG POCKETS CEMENT PER\nCUBIC METRE SOIL TO BE USED FOR STABILIZING AND TO BE SUPPLIED BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER, THIS ITEM IS NOT TO BE USED FOR STABILIZING\nOF BACKFILL AT ROAD-CROSSINGS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION\nFOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3045944,'CI1.49','CI1.49 PMPNG & CNTRL WTR','This item consists of control and pumping water where it is necessary to provide, operate and maintain pumping equipment required for possible wet conditions. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The cost of operating, maintaining and removal of the pumps throughout the period during which the facilities are required, \nb) The supply of a pump capable of pumping at a rate of at least 520 litres / minute, \nc) Pumping of water up to a max of 4 hours per day.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per hour (H).','H',110.20,'PMP,WTR:CI1.49,CNTRL','PUMP, WATER:ITEM NUMBER CI1.49, ADDITIONAL TASK CNTRL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE COST OF OPERATING, MAINTAINING\nAND REMOVAL OF THE PUMPS THROUGHOUT THE PERIOD DURING WHICH THE FACILITIES ARE REQUIRED, THE SUPPLY OF A PUMP CAPABLE OF PUMPING AT\nA RATE OF AT LEAST 520 LITRES / MINUTE, PUMPING OF WATER UP TO A MAX OF 4 HOURS PER DAY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND\nFROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nHOUR (H)'),(3045945,'CI2.36','CI2.36 PRVD 12 DRWR SHLF','This item consists of the provisioning of a 12-drawer housing with the shelves and midcouplers.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na) The cost of the housing, shelves and midcouplers,\nb) Shipping (Local and Foreign),\nc) Storage.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per 12 drawer shelf, each (EA).','EA',20793.19,'PRVD,EQUIP:CI2.36,12 DRWR SHLF','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.36, TYPE 12 DRWR SHLF:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE COST OF THE HOUSING,\nSHELVES AND MIDCOUPLERS, SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 12 DRAWER SHELF,\nEACH (EA)'),(3045946,'CI1.32','CI1.32 ADDL LYR BRICK','This item consists of additional layer bricks (baked bricks only).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The necessary excavation up to existing PJB level, backfilling, compaction and D.C.P testing, \nb) The supply of all materials required to add layers with an internal size of 600mm x 600mm x 110mm,\nc) Building in a single wall configuration with strength of 20MPA, \nd) All pipe entries.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per 100mm layer each (EA).','EA',195.60,'LAY,BRICK:CI1.32,ADDL LYR','LAY, BRICK:ITEM NUMBER CI1.32, TYPE ADDL LYR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE NECESSARY EXCAVATION UP TO EXISTING PJB\nLEVEL, BACKFILLING, COMPACTION AND D.C.P TESTING, THE SUPPLY OF ALL MATERIALS REQUIRED TO ADD LAYERS WITH AN INTERNAL SIZE OF 600MM\nX 600MM X 110MM, BUILDING IN A SINGLE WALL CONFIGURATION WITH STRENGTH OF 20MPA, ALL PIPE ENTRIES. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nCOSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR\nTHIS ITEM IS PER 100MM LAYER EACH (EA)'),(3045947,'CI2.37','CI2.37 PRVD IFC MAT','This item consists of the sourcing and providing of the IFC material items by the Service Provider, including a 10 % handling fee.\n\nΓÇó The cost of the cable irrespective of the cable size in any of the following configurations, per meter:\no   No tails spliced,\no   Tail spliced on one side,\no   Tails spliced on both sides.\n\nΓÇó The cost of the FOMS (Fibre Optic Management System) complete.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na) The sourcing, providing, storage and delivery of the above mentioned items from the supplier to the site,\nb) The cost of the abovementioned items at the contracted Telkom rate,\nc) The Service Provider utilising equipment/material from the Telkom toolbox and/or as per SABS standard or recognised local authorities,\nd) 10 % handling fee.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is each (EA).','EA',1.00,'PRVD,EQUIP:CI2.37,IFC MAT','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.37, TYPE IFC MAT:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SOURCING, PROVIDING, STORAGE\nAND DELIVERY OF THE ABOVE MENTIONED ITEMS FROM THE SUPPLIER TO THE SITE, THE COST OF THE ABOVEMENTIONED ITEMS AT THE CONTRACTED\nTELKOM RATE, THE SERVICE PROVIDER UTILISING EQUIPMENT/MATERIAL FROM THE TELKOM TOOLBOX AND/OR AS PER SABS STANDARD OR RECOGNISED\nLOCAL AUTHORITIES, 10% HANDLING FEE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3045949,'CI2.24','CI2.24 RECVR FBR CABL','This item consists of the recovery of all fibre cables. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The recovery of the all fibre cables overhead or underground (i.e. from ducts, poles, manholes, etc.),\nb) The cost to redrum, test, measure, and label recovered cables for reuse,\nc) The coiling of cables if not suitable for re-use, and returning to Telkom stores,\nd) Transporting the recovered material from site to destination. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:  \na) 325. CTO-004654,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per kilogram (KG).','KG',5.00,'RCVR,CBL:CI2.24,FBR','RECOVER, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.24, TYPE FBR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE RECOVERY OF THE ALL FIBRE CABLES OVERHEAD\nOR UNDERGROUND (I.E. FROM DUCTS, POLES, MANHOLES, ETC.), THE COST TO REDRUM, TEST, MEASURE, AND LABEL RECOVERED CABLES FOR REUSE,\nTHE COILING OF CABLES IF NOT SUITABLE FOR RE-USE, AND RETURNING TO TELKOM STORES, TRANSPORTING THE RECOVERED MATERIAL FROM SITE TO\nDESTINATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS:\n325. CTO-004654, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER KILOGRAM (KG)'),(3045950,'CI1.3','CI1.3 TRNCH & LAY RD/RLWY','This item consists of trenching across all types of roads/railway lines width 0.450 metre X depth 1.2 metre and laying of pipes, ducts, buried cables, etc. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Cutting of tar or concrete and / or removal of paving slabs or bricks,\nb) All excavations in the roadway,\nc) Pilot holes/ crossing of services (to determine the ground condition and to identify / locate underground services or obstructions),\nd) Backfilling,\ne) All backfilling/stabilising material (i.e. 2 x 50kg pockets of cement per cubic metre of backfill or as required by wayleaves conditions. Stabilised backfill must extend 1 metre beyond kerbstone.),\nf) Compacting,\ng) D.C.P testing, \nh) The supply of water if necessary to obtain optimum moisture content,\ni) Tunnelling under obstacles (i.e. kerbstones, road signs etc.),\nj) Re-instatement / replacement of kerb stones (when required),\nk) Supporting of all services (i.e. electrical, water, sewerage, etc.), \nl) Laying danger tape and screen-wire (where required),\nm) Laying of trench crete where required,\nn) Laying of all pipes/ducts and buried cable,\no) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling),\np) Ensure pipe is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc.,\nq) Handling, cutting and repairing of existing pipes (supply PVC),\nr) Bedding and padding (reuse of existing material upon Openserve approval),\ns) Removal of all spoil including boulders,\nt) Clearing the surface,\nu) Removing and or erecting fencing when required, \nv) Backfilling of cavities,\nw) Removing, transporting and disposing of all surplus material,\nx) Shoring, when required,\ny) Pumping and controlling of water,\nz) Barricading of the excavation,\naa) Provision of all safety requirements (i.e. road signs, cones, flagman, etc.), \nbb) Grading of the trench where ducts need to be laid,\ncc) Maintaining of the trench until permanent re-instatement.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\nb) The cost of the supply and delivery of the Trench crete.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',249.68,'EXPOS,TRNCH:CI1.3,RD/RLWY','EXPOSE, TRENCH:ITEM NUMBER CI1.3, TYPE RD/RLWY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CUTTING OF TAR OR CONCRETE AND / OR REMOVAL\nOF PAVING SLABS OR BRICKS, ALL EXCAVATIONS IN THE ROADWAY, PILOT HOLES/ CROSSING OF SERVICES (TO DETERMINE THE GROUND CONDITION AND\nTO IDENTIFY / LOCATE UNDERGROUND SERVICES OR OBSTRUCTIONS), BACKFILLING, ALL BACKFILLING/STABILISING MATERIAL (I.E. 2 X 50KG\nPOCKETS OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE OF BACKFILL OR AS REQUIRED BY WAYLEAVES CONDITIONS. STABILISED BACKFILL MUST EXTEND 1 METRE\nBEYOND KERBSTONE.), COMPACTING, D.C.P TESTING, THE SUPPLY OF WATER IF NECESSARY TO OBTAIN OPTIMUM MOISTURE CONTENT, TUNNELLING\nUNDER OBSTACLES (I.E. KERBSTONES, ROAD SIGNS ETC.), RE-INSTATEMENT / REPLACEMENT OF KERB STONES (WHEN REQUIRED), SUPPORTING OF ALL\nSERVICES (I.E. ELECTRICAL, WATER, SEWERAGE, ETC.), LAYING DANGER TAPE AND SCREEN-WIRE (WHERE REQUIRED), LAYING OF TRENCH CRETE\nWHERE REQUIRED, LAYING OF ALL PIPES/DUCTS AND BURIED CABLE, PIPE ENTRIES (EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING), ENSURE PIPE IS USEABLE BY MEANS\nOF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., HANDLING, CUTTING AND REPAIRING OF EXISTING PIPES (SUPPLY PVC), BEDDING AND\nPADDING (REUSE OF EXISTING MATERIAL UPON OPENSERVE APPROVAL), REMOVAL OF ALL SPOIL INCLUDING BOULDERS, CLEARING THE SURFACE,\nREMOVING AND OR ERECTING FENCING WHEN REQUIRED, BACKFILLING OF CAVITIES, REMOVING, TRANSPORTING AND DISPOSING OF ALL SURPLUS\nMATERIAL, SHORING, WHEN REQUIRED, PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER, BARRICADING OF THE EXCAVATION, PROVISION OF ALL SAFETY\nREQUIREMENTS (I.E. ROAD SIGNS, CONES, FLAGMAN, ETC.), GRADING OF THE TRENCH WHERE DUCTS NEED TO BE LAID, MAINTAINING OF THE TRENCH\nUNTIL PERMANENT RE-INSTATEMENT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE COST OF THE\nSUPPLY AND DELIVERY OF THE TRENCH CRETE. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER METRE (MT)'),(3045951,'CI2.10','CI2.10 OVHL CABL>10-200PR/48-144FBR/2-4DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of over hauling of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables (UG and Indoor) >10PR ΓÇô 200PR,\nΓÇó Z-Screen cables,\nΓÇó Fibre cables 48-144 Fibres,\nΓÇó 2-4 way micro ducts,\nΓÇó 32/40mm inner ducts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nb) Cleaning, preparing, threading and testing existing Telkom duct to ensure duct is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc., \nc) Overcoming engineering difficulties such as hauling through Utility Boxes, pillar joints, entry points etc., \nd) Pumping and controlling of water while hauling takes place,\ne) The fitting of uni-strut support / flat brackets for the supporting of the cable in Utility Boxes, \nf) Cleaning Utility Boxes and surroundings on completion,\ng) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water, dry air, cable ties, fasteners, labels, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps etc.),\nh) Performing micro duct integrity test, \ni) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nj) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \nk) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\nl) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled. \nm) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled.\nn) The price per metre is the same for the simultaneously overhauling of 1 inner-duct / micro-duct or simultaneous overhauling of 2 inner-ducts (32/40mm) / micro-ducts\no) If more than 2 inner-ducts or micro-ducts are simultaneously overhauled then this item may be claimed twice\np) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required \nq) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) Supply of support brackets (to be supplied by Telkom),\nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled, \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled,\nc) The price per metre is the same for the simultaneously overhauling of 1 inner-duct / micro-duct or simultaneous overhauling of 2 inner-ducts (32/40mm) / micro-ducts,\nd) If more than 2 inner-ducts or micro-ducts are simultaneously overhauled, then this item may be claimed twice.\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable / duct (over hauled) per metre (MT).','MT',15.00,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.10,OVHL 10-200PR','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.10, TYPE OVHL 10-200PR/48-144FBR/2-4DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PROVIDING ALL\nTOOLS AND EQUIPMENT THAT IS NECESSARY TO EXECUTE THE WORK, CLEANING, PREPARING, THREADING AND TESTING EXISTING TELKOM DUCT TO\nENSURE DUCT IS USEABLE BY MEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., OVERCOMING ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS\nHAULING THROUGH UTILITY BOXES, PILLAR JOINTS, ENTRY POINTS ETC., PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER WHILE HAULING TAKES PLACE, THE\nFITTING OF UNI-STRUT SUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS FOR THE SUPPORTING OF THE CABLE IN UTILITY BOXES, CLEANING UTILITY BOXES AND\nSURROUNDINGS ON COMPLETION, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. POLY # WATER, DRY AIR, CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, MICRO DUCT\nCOUPLERS, MICRO DUCT END CAPS ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF\nSURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE WORK. FOR UG THE\nQUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY\nSLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED. FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE\nACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED. THE PRICE PER METRE IS THE SAME FOR THE\nSIMULTANEOUSLY OVERHAULING OF 1 INNER-DUCT / MICRO-DUCT OR SIMULTANEOUS OVERHAULING OF 2 INNER-DUCTS (32/40MM) / MICRO-DUCTS IF\nMORE THAN 2 INNER-DUCTS OR MICRO-DUCTS ARE SIMULTANEOUSLY OVERHAULED THEN THIS ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED TWICE FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED\nFOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED FOR\nINDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH\nIRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE CABLE / DUCTS, SUPPLY OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (TO BE SUPPLIED BY'),(3045952,'CI1.60','CI1.60 REINST ESTBD LAWN / GRVL SURF','This item consists of surface re-instatements for established lawns, flower beds, conservation areas (sidewalks, private property) / established gravelled surfaces (sidewalks, private property and roads). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Careful removal of the existing material (i.e. grass, gravel, etc.),\nb) Maintaining of grass, flower beds, shrubs, plants, conservation areas, etc. until restored to original state or replacement if required,  \nc) The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing road / sidewalk / private property levels.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M2).','M2',38.49,'REINST,SURF:CI1.60,ESTBD LAWN/GRVL SURF','REINSTATE, SURFACE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.60, SURFACE TYPE ESTBD LAWN/GRVL SURF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CAREFUL REMOVAL\nOF THE EXISTING MATERIAL (I.E. GRASS, GRAVEL, ETC.), MAINTAINING OF GRASS, FLOWER BEDS, SHRUBS, PLANTS, CONSERVATION AREAS, ETC.\nUNTIL RESTORED TO ORIGINAL STATE OR REPLACEMENT IF REQUIRED, THE FINISHING OF LEVELS TO BE AESTHETICALLY TRUE TO THE SURROUNDING\nEXISTING ROAD / SIDEWALK / PRIVATE PROPERTY LEVELS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SQUARE METRE (M2)'),(3045953,'CI2.22','CI2.22 ARNG MNHL CABL','This item consists of re-arranging existing cables in a manhole.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Cleaning of the cable and brackets, securing the cable and cable slack to the hangers and flat cable support brackets, labelling the cable and inserting pipe entry shoes, \nb) Supply and installing of cable ties, pipe entry shoes and labels, \nc) Cleaning of the manhole and surrounding area (i.e. cables, labelling, securing, etc.).\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is \na) 325. CTO-004654, \nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable each (EA).','EA',68.43,'ARNG,CBL:CI2.22,MNHL','ARRANGE, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.22, TYPE MANHOLE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CLEANING OF THE CABLE AND BRACKETS,\nSECURING THE CABLE AND CABLE SLACK TO THE HANGERS AND FLAT CABLE SUPPORT BRACKETS, LABELLING THE CABLE AND INSERTING PIPE ENTRY\nSHOES, SUPPLY AND INSTALLING OF CABLE TIES, PIPE ENTRY SHOES AND LABELS, CLEANING OF THE MANHOLE AND SURROUNDING AREA (I.E. CABLES,\nLABELLING, SECURING, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR\nTHIS ITEM IS 325. CTO-004654, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE EACH (EA)'),(3045954,'CI1.26','CI1.26 CONSTR MNHL NECK','This item consists of construction / reconstruction of manhole necks with 20MPA concrete and / or bricks \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Supply and laying of SABS approved baked bricks, (Double Wall)\nb) Stabilizing of backfill around roadway manhole necks using 2 x 50kg pockets of cement per cubic metre, \nc) Supply, delivery and placement of 20-25MPA concrete, \nd) Design and shuttering, \ne) Stabilizing of backfill around roadway manhole necks using 2 x 50kg pockets of cement per cubic metre. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is:  \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit for this item is per 100mm layer each (EA).','EA',423.88,'CONSTR,MNHL:CI1.26,NECK','CONSTRUCT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.26, TYPE NECK:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SUPPLY AND LAYING OF SABS APPROVED BAKED\nBRICKS, (DOUBLE WALL) STABILIZING OF BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS USING 2 X 50KG POCKETS OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE,\nSUPPLY, DELIVERY AND PLACEMENT OF 20-25MPA CONCRETE, DESIGN AND SHUTTERING, STABILIZING OF BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS\nUSING 2 X 50KG POCKETS OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT).\nTHE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 100MM LAYER EACH (EA)'),(3045956,'CI1.11','CI1.11 SPCLZD XNG PIP JCKG','This item consists of the specialized crossings (not trenches) excavating pits and setting up jacking equipment. Jack one 350mm internal diameter steel pipe in all soil conditions.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The setting up of jacking equipment and excavation on both sides,\nb) Supply of a 350mm I/D steel pipe and jacking of the pipe, \nc) The installation of 5 x PVC / HDPE 110mm O / D pipes (to be supplied by Telkom) into the 350mm I / D steel pipe, \nd) Tunnelling under kerbstones, supporting of services, backfilling and removal of soil and rocks, \ne) The costs for damages incurred by the Service Provider and the repair of roads or existing services, \nf) The cost of clearing the surface, removing boulders with a size of up to 0.015 cubic metres (If the boulders are bigger than 0.015 cubic metres in size, a separate rate must be negotiated), grubbing of tree stumps, \ng) Backfilling of cavities, demolishing structures and removal thereof.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) This item will be used for payment when pipe jacking is to be done instead of trenching at roads, driveways etc.,\nb) Measurement for payment will be done from kerbstone to kerbstone, per pipe per meter, and only for successful attempts,\nc) This item will be applicable in all soil conditions except in rock. (including clay and or waterlogged ground conditions). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per quote per metre (MT)','MT',1.00,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.11,XNG PIP JCKG','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.11, TYPE XNG PIP JCKG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SETTING UP OF JACKING EQUIPMENT\nAND EXCAVATION ON BOTH SIDES, SUPPLY OF A 350MM I/D STEEL PIPE AND JACKING OF THE PIPE, THE INSTALLATION OF 5 X PVC / HDPE 110MM O\n/ D PIPES (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM) INTO THE 350MM I / D STEEL PIPE, TUNNELLING UNDER KERBSTONES, SUPPORTING OF SERVICES,\nBACKFILLING AND REMOVAL OF SOIL AND ROCKS, THE COSTS FOR DAMAGES INCURRED BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER AND THE REPAIR OF ROADS OR\nEXISTING SERVICES, THE COST OF CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING BOULDERS WITH A SIZE OF UP TO 0.015 CUBIC METRES (IF THE BOULDERS ARE\nBIGGER THAN 0.015 CUBIC METRES IN SIZE, A SEPARATE RATE MUST BE NEGOTIATED), GRUBBING OF TREE STUMPS, BACKFILLING OF CAVITIES,\nDEMOLISHING STRUCTURES AND REMOVAL THEREOF. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE:\nTHIS ITEM WILL BE USED FOR PAYMENT WHEN PIPE JACKING IS TO BE DONE INSTEAD OF TRENCHING AT ROADS, DRIVEWAYS ETC., MEASUREMENT FOR\nPAYMENT WILL BE DONE FROM KERBSTONE TO KERBSTONE, PER PIPE PER METER, AND ONLY FOR SUCCESSFUL ATTEMPTS, THIS ITEM WILL BE\nAPPLICABLE IN ALL SOIL CONDITIONS EXCEPT IN ROCK. (INCLUDING CLAY AND OR WATERLOGGED GROUND CONDITIONS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS\nITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER QUOTE PER METRE (MT)'),(3045957,'CI2.34','CI2.34 PRVD 4 DRWR SHLF','This item consists of the provisioning of a 4-drawer housing with the shelves and midcouplers.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na) The cost of the shelf,\nb) Shipping (Local and Foreign),\nc) Storage.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per 4 drawer shelf, each (EA).','EA',8046.87,'PRVD,EQUIP:CI2.34,4 DRWR SHLF','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.34, TYPE 4 DRWR SHLF:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE COST OF THE SHELF,\nSHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 4 DRAWER SHELF, EACH (EA)'),(3045958,'CI1.34','CI1.34 CONSTR JP 1MX0.8MX1.5M','This item consists of the construction / casting of a brick / concrete jointing pit measuring 1m x 0.8m x 1.5m deep (internal) with a manhole frame and cover, supplied by Telkom SA.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply and delivery of all concrete, \nb) The excavation, backfilling, compaction and coping finished with a wooden float and corner tool, \nc) All material required to build walls of 150mm concrete or double brick (baked bricks only) with a minimum strength of 20MPA, \nd) The supply of Telkom approved material, including corrugated iron - 0.6mm full hard, ΓÇÿAΓÇÖ grade, \ne) All pipe entries, \nf) Plastering and / or bagging of walls in specified areas.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Manhole frame and cover (supplied by Telkom SA), \nb) Hard rock excavation is an over and above item and will be paid separately under the hard rock excavation items, \nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654,\nb) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nc) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), \nd) B3001 (CTO-003944).\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per jointing pit each (EA).','EA',7958.05,'CONSTR,JP:CI1.34,1X0.8X1.5M','CONSTRUCT, JOINTING PIT:ITEM NUMBER CI1.34, SIZE 1X0.8X1.5 M:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY AND DELIVERY OF\nALL CONCRETE, THE EXCAVATION, BACKFILLING, COMPACTION AND COPING FINISHED WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL MATERIAL\nREQUIRED TO BUILD WALLS OF 150MM CONCRETE OR DOUBLE BRICK (BAKED BRICKS ONLY) WITH A MINIMUM STRENGTH OF 20MPA, THE SUPPLY OF\nTELKOM APPROVED MATERIAL, INCLUDING CORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL HARD, #A# GRADE, ALL PIPE ENTRIES, PLASTERING AND / OR BAGGING OF\nWALLS IN SPECIFIED AREAS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: MANHOLE FRAME AND COVER (SUPPLIED BY TELKOM SA), HARD ROCK EXCAVATION IS AN OVER AND\nABOVE ITEM AND WILL BE PAID SEPARATELY UNDER THE HARD ROCK EXCAVATION ITEMS, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654, SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944).\nTHE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER JOINTING PIT EACH (EA)'),(3045959,'CI1.43','CI1.43 RCVY SDC','This item consists the complete recovery of the SDC and to seal pipes at both ends. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The removal of all cable tails, jumpers, termination blocks and back frames, \nb) The sealing of all the pipes in the manhole and at the plinth, \nc) The cleaning of the manhole and surrounding area, \nd) The removal of all the recovered material to the destination as specified. (Document no. ITSD-43967). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per SDC complete each (EA)','EA',479.01,'RCVR,CABNT:CI1.43 SDC','RECOVER, CABINET:ITEM NUMBER CI1.43 SDC:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE REMOVAL OF ALL CABLE TAILS, JUMPERS,\nTERMINATION BLOCKS AND BACK FRAMES, THE SEALING OF ALL THE PIPES IN THE MANHOLE AND AT THE PLINTH, THE CLEANING OF THE MANHOLE AND\nSURROUNDING AREA, THE REMOVAL OF ALL THE RECOVERED MATERIAL TO THE DESTINATION AS SPECIFIED. (DOCUMENT NO. ITSD-43967). THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SDC COMPLETE EACH (EA)'),(3045960,'CI1.58','CI1.58 REINST CONCRT RD','This item consists of the surface re-instatements concrete roads.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply and delivery of the concrete to site,\nb) All the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification, \nc) The DCP test requirements, according to roads authority specification,\nd) The preparation and cleaning of the re-instatement area and the removal of spoil from site, \ne) The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing road / sidewalk levels.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) If the local authority executes the re-instatements on behalf of the Service Provider, then the Service Provider remains liable for the payment to the local authority, \nb) The Service Provider must familiarize himself with the re-instatement specifications of the various authorities, \nc) Quantities will be calculated against the applicable proposed trenching dimensions.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M2).','M2',287.43,'REINST,SURF:CI1.58,RD,CONCRT','REINSTATE, SURFACE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.58, SURFACE TYPE ROAD, SURFACE MATERIAL CONCRETE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE\nSUPPLY AND DELIVERY OF THE CONCRETE TO SITE, ALL THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING\nTO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE DCP TEST REQUIREMENTS, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE PREPARATION AND\nCLEANING OF THE RE-INSTATEMENT AREA AND THE REMOVAL OF SPOIL FROM SITE, THE FINISHING OF LEVELS TO BE AESTHETICALLY TRUE TO THE\nSURROUNDING EXISTING ROAD / SIDEWALK LEVELS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE:\nIF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY EXECUTES THE RE-INSTATEMENTS ON BEHALF OF THE SERVICE PROVIDER, THEN THE SERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS LIABLE FOR\nTHE PAYMENT TO THE LOCAL AUTHORITY, THE SERVICE PROVIDER MUST FAMILIARIZE HIMSELF WITH THE RE-INSTATEMENT SPECIFICATIONS OF THE\nVARIOUS AUTHORITIES, QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED AGAINST THE APPLICABLE PROPOSED TRENCHING DIMENSIONS. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS\nITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SQUARE METRE (M2)'),(3045961,'CI2.11','CI2.11 OVHL CABL>200-600PR/ 7DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of over hauling of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables (UG and Indoor) >200PR ΓÇô 600PR, \nΓÇó 7-way and greater micro ducts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work, \nb) Cleaning, preparing, threading and testing existing Telkom duct to ensure duct is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc., \nc) Overcoming engineering difficulties such as hauling through Utility Boxes, pillar joints, entry points etc., \nd) Pumping and controlling of water while hauling takes place,\ne) The fitting of uni-strut support / flat brackets for the supporting of the cable in Utility Boxes, \nf) Cleaning Utility Boxes and surroundings on completion,\ng) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water, dry air, cable ties, fasteners, labels, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps etc.),\nh) Performing micro duct integrity test,  \ni) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nj) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \nk) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) Supply of support brackets (to be supplied by Telkom), \nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled,  \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled, \nc) The price per metre is the same for the simultaneously overhauling of 1 micro-duct or simultaneous overhauling of 2 micro-ducts.\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable / duct (over hauled) per metre (MT).','MT',20.00,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.11,OVHL 200-600PR/7DUCT','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.11, TYPE OVHL 200-600PR/7DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND\nEQUIPMENT THAT IS NECESSARY TO EXECUTE THE WORK, CLEANING, PREPARING, THREADING AND TESTING EXISTING TELKOM DUCT TO ENSURE DUCT IS\nUSEABLE BY MEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., OVERCOMING ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS HAULING THROUGH\nUTILITY BOXES, PILLAR JOINTS, ENTRY POINTS ETC., PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER WHILE HAULING TAKES PLACE, THE FITTING OF\nUNI-STRUT SUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS FOR THE SUPPORTING OF THE CABLE IN UTILITY BOXES, CLEANING UTILITY BOXES AND SURROUNDINGS ON\nCOMPLETION, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. POLY # WATER, DRY AIR, CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, MICRO DUCT COUPLERS, MICRO\nDUCT END CAPS ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS CABLES /\nDUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE WORK. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST\nOF THE CABLE / DUCTS, SUPPLY OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM), ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). NOTE: FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB\nLID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED, FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM\nPOINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED, THE PRICE PER METRE IS THE\nSAME FOR THE SIMULTANEOUSLY OVERHAULING OF 1 MICRO-DUCT OR SIMULTANEOUS OVERHAULING OF 2 MICRO-DUCTS. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE\nITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE / DUCT (OVER HAULED) PER METRE\n(MT)'),(3045962,'CI1.44','CI1.44 SUPLY & INSTLN CONCRT SLAB','This item consists of the supply and installation of concrete slabs for separation purposes between Telkom plant and electrical cables.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The cost of acquiring, loading and transporting the material from the supply source to site and distributing the material along the length of the trench.  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',83.12,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI1.44,CONCRT SLAB,SUPLY','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI1.44, TYPE CONCRT SLAB, ADDITIONAL TASK SUPPLY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE COST\nOF ACQUIRING, LOADING AND TRANSPORTING THE MATERIAL FROM THE SUPPLY SOURCE TO SITE AND DISTRIBUTING THE MATERIAL ALONG THE LENGTH\nOF THE TRENCH. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS:\n325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT)'),(3045963,'CI1.10','CI1.10 SPCLZD XNG BORE RCK 2 PIPE','This item consists of the specialized crossings (not trenches) excavating pits and setting up boring equipment. bore to accommodate and install two 110mm outside diameter rigid PVC pipe in rock conditions.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The setting up of boring equipment, excavation on both sides, boring, supply and installation of two 110MM continuous class 10 HDPE pipe, \nb) Tunnelling under kerbstones, supporting of services, backfilling and removal of soil, \nc) The cost for damages incurred by the Service Provider and the repair of roads or existing services, \nd) The cost of clearing the surface, removing boulders with a size of up to 0.015 cubic metres (If the boulders are bigger than 0.015 cubic metres in size, a separate rate must be negotiated.), grubbing of tree stumps, \ne) Backfilling of cavities, demolishing structures and removal thereof.\nf) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',3000.00,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.10,RCK 2 PIPE','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.10, TYPE RCK 2 PIPE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SETTING UP OF BORING EQUIPMENT,\nEXCAVATION ON BOTH SIDES, BORING, SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF TWO 110MM CONTINUOUS CLASS 10 HDPE PIPE, TUNNELLING UNDER KERBSTONES,\nSUPPORTING OF SERVICES, BACKFILLING AND REMOVAL OF SOIL, THE COST FOR DAMAGES INCURRED BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER AND THE REPAIR OF\nROADS OR EXISTING SERVICES,  THE COST OF CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING BOULDERS WITH A SIZE OF UP TO 0.015 CUBIC METRES (IF THE\nBOULDERS ARE BIGGER THAN 0.015 CUBIC METRES IN SIZE, A SEPARATE RATE MUST BE NEGOTIATED.), GRUBBING OF TREE STUMPS, BACKFILLING OF\nCAVITIES, DEMOLISHING STRUCTURES AND REMOVAL THEREOF. PIPE ENTRIES (EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS\nTO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER METRE (MT)'),(3045964,'CI2.7','CI2.7 HAUL CABL>200-600PR/7DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of hauling or simultaneously hauling of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables (UG and Indoor) >200PR ΓÇô 600PR (hauling only), \nΓÇó 7-way and greater micro ducts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nb) Cleaning, preparing, threading and testing existing Telkom duct to ensure duct is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc.,\nc) Overcoming engineering difficulties such as hauling through Utility Boxes, pillar joints, entry points etc.,\nd) Pumping and controlling of water while hauling takes place,\ne) The fitting of uni-strut support / flat brackets for the supporting of the cable in Utility Boxes,\nf) Cleaning Utility Boxes and surroundings on completion,\ng) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water, dry air, cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps etc.),\nh) Performing micro duct integrity test, \ni) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nj) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \nk) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled. \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled ca