materials (i.e. Clamps, Cable ties, Labels, Dry air, Rawl Bolts, etc.).\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Supply of support brackets (to be supplied by Telkom),\nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per Utility Box rehabilitated each (EA).','EA',371.87,'RCVR,BX:CI1.63,REHABLT UTLTY','RECOVER, BOX:ITEM NUMBER CI1.63, TYPE REHABLT UTLTY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PRESSURE TESTING, SUPPORTING,\nCLAMPING, LABELLING AND BONDING OF AFFECTED CABLES / JOINTS, THE INSTALLATION OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (I.E. UNI-STRUT, FLAT SUPPORT,\nHANGERS, ETC.), CLAMPING AND RE-CLAMPING OF CABLES TO STRUTS, THE DRILLING OF HOLES WHERE REQUIRED, PUMPING AND CONTROL OF WATER,\nTHE CLEANING OF THE MANHOLE AND IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA AND REMOVAL OF SAND / RUBBLE / TERMITES NESTS UP TO HALF A CUBIC METRE,\nTHE CLEANING OF THE CABLES AND BRACKETS, SECURING THE CABLE AND CABLE SLACK TO THE HANGERS AND FLAT CABLE SUPPORT BRACKETS,\nNUMBERING / LABELLING OF CABLES, JOINTS, MANHOLES, UTILITY BOXES, ETC., SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS (I.E. CLAMPS, CABLE TIES,\nLABELS, DRY AIR, RAWL BOLTS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: SUPPLY OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM), ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO\nAND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER UTILITY BOX REHABILITATED EACH (EA)'),(3045967,'CI2.5','CI2.5 INSTL-HAUL CABL Γëñ10PR/S-DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of hauling or simultaneously hauling of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables (UG and Indoor) up to 10 pair,\nΓÇó Air pipe,\nΓÇó LAN Cabling, \nΓÇó Single micro ducts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nb) Cleaning, preparing, threading and testing existing Telkom duct to ensure duct is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc.,\nc) Overcoming engineering difficulties such as hauling through Utility Boxes, pillar joints, entry points etc.,\nd) Pumping and controlling of water while hauling takes place,\ne) The fitting of uni-strut support / flat brackets for the supporting of the cable in Utility Boxes,\nf) Cleaning Utility Boxes and surroundings on completion,\ng) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water, dry air, cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps etc.),\nh) Performing micro duct integrity test, \ni) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nj) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \nk) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) Supply of support brackets (to be supplied by Telkom)\nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled, \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled.\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable/s (hauled or simultaneously hauled) per metre (MT).','MT',4.05,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.5,HAUL 10PR/S-DUCT','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.5, TYPE HAUL 10PR/S-DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT\nTHAT IS NECESSARY TO EXECUTE THE WORK, CLEANING, PREPARING, THREADING AND TESTING EXISTING TELKOM DUCT TO ENSURE DUCT IS USEABLE BY\nMEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., OVERCOMING ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS HAULING THROUGH UTILITY\nBOXES, PILLAR JOINTS, ENTRY POINTS ETC., PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER WHILE HAULING TAKES PLACE, THE FITTING OF UNI-STRUT\nSUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS FOR THE SUPPORTING OF THE CABLE IN UTILITY BOXES, CLEANING UTILITY BOXES AND SURROUNDINGS ON COMPLETION,\nSUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. POLY # WATER, DRY AIR, CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, SADDLES, GLUE, MICRO DUCT COUPLERS,\nMICRO DUCT END CAPS ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS\nCABLES / DUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE WORK. THE RATE EXCLUDES:\nTHE COST OF THE CABLE / DUCTS, SUPPLY OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM) ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE\nFEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER\nUB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED, FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM\nPOINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE\nITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE/S (HAULED OR SIMULTANEOUSLY\nHAULED) PER METRE (MT)'),(3045968,'CI1.13','CI1.13 PROVD BCKFIL','This item consists of the provision of imported backfill material, where excavated material is unsuitable.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The acquiring, loading and transporting the material from the supply source to the job site and distributing the material along the entire length of the trench, \nb) Collecting suitable material further than 500m from point of requirement on site.  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) This item may only be used for payment when additional backfill material has to be imported to replace excavated rock, unsuitable soil or as topsoil for trench dressings,\nb) Quantities will be calculated and paid against the proposed trenching/excavation dimensions ΓÇô over-breaks excluded.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item per cubic metre (M┬│)','M3',256.88,'BKFILL,TRNCH:CI1.13','BACKFILL, TRENCH:ITEM NUMBER CI1.13:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE ACQUIRING, LOADING AND TRANSPORTING THE MATERIAL\nFROM THE SUPPLY SOURCE TO THE JOB SITE AND DISTRIBUTING THE MATERIAL ALONG THE ENTIRE LENGTH OF THE TRENCH, COLLECTING SUITABLE\nMATERIAL FURTHER THAN 500M FROM POINT OF REQUIREMENT ON SITE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED FOR PAYMENT WHEN ADDITIONAL BACKFILL MATERIAL HAS TO BE IMPORTED TO REPLACE EXCAVATED\nROCK, UNSUITABLE SOIL OR AS TOPSOIL FOR TRENCH DRESSINGS, QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED AND PAID AGAINST THE PROPOSED\nTRENCHING/EXCAVATION DIMENSIONS OVER-BREAKS EXCLUDED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR\nTHIS ITEM PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3045969,'CI1.35','CI1.35 CONSTR JP 1.2MX1.2MX1.7M','This item consists of the construction / casting of a brick / concrete jointing pit measuring 1.2m x 1.2m x 1.7m deep (internal) with a manhole frame and cover, supplied by Telkom SA.  \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply and delivery of all concrete,\nb) The excavation, backfilling, compaction and coping finished with a wooden float and corner tool,\nc) All material required to build walls of 150mm concrete or double brick (baked bricks only) with a minimum strength of 20MPA,\nd) Plastering and / or bagging of walls in specified areas,\ne) The supply of Telkom approved material, including corrugated iron - 0.6mm full hard, ΓÇÿAΓÇÖ grade,\"I\" beams - 140 x 70 x 6mm, treated with approved rustproof paint (e.g. chromites) to the Area ManagerΓÇÖs approval,\nf) All pipe entries.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Hard rock excavation is an over and above item and will be paid separately under the hard rock excavation items, \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654,\nb) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nc) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), \nd) B3001 (CTO-003944).\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per jointing pit each (EA).','EA',10689.43,'CONSTR,JP:CI1.35,SQ1.2 X 1.7M','CONSTRUCT, JOINTING PIT:ITEM NUMBER CI1.35, SIZE SQ1.2 X 1.7 M:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY AND DELIVERY OF\nALL CONCRETE, THE EXCAVATION, BACKFILLING, COMPACTION AND COPING FINISHED WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL MATERIAL\nREQUIRED TO BUILD WALLS OF 150MM CONCRETE OR DOUBLE BRICK (BAKED BRICKS ONLY) WITH A MINIMUM STRENGTH OF 20MPA, PLASTERING AND / OR\nBAGGING OF WALLS IN SPECIFIED AREAS, THE SUPPLY OF TELKOM APPROVED MATERIAL, INCLUDING CORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL HARD, #A#\nGRADE,I BEAMS - 140 X 70 X 6MM, TREATED WITH APPROVED RUSTPROOF PAINT (E.G. CHROMITES) TO THE AREA MANAGER#S APPROVAL, ALL PIPE\nENTRIES. THE RATE EXCLUDES: HARD ROCK EXCAVATION IS AN OVER AND ABOVE ITEM AND WILL BE PAID SEPARATELY UNDER THE HARD ROCK\nEXCAVATION ITEMS, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654, SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944). THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER JOINTING\nPIT EACH (EA)'),(3045970,'CI1.61','CI1.61 REINST SLAB/INTRLCK BRICK/CONCRT','This item consists of surface re-instatements of slabbed / interlocking bricks / concrete slabs / paving etc. on sidewalks or in private property. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Careful removal and stacking of the existing material (i.e. pavers, slabs, etc.),\nb) Replacement and compacting of bedding material, \nc) Replacement of any damaged pavers, slabs, concrete, etc., \nd) The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing si