from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',18559.93,'CONSTR,MNHL:CI1.17,STD 2.75M FT WAY','CONSTRUCT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.17, TYPE STD 2.75M FT WAY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SUPPLY, DELIVERY AND CASTING\nOF 20-25MPA CONCRETE, FITTING OF THE FRAME, COVER AND COPING, FINISHED WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL EQUIPMENT,\nSHUTTERING AND MATERIAL REQUIRED, POSITIONING OF THE MANHOLE, LOADING REQUIREMENTS OF SABS SPECIFICATION 558 TABLE 2 FOR THE\nPARTICULAR SITUATION OF LOADING, I.E. HEAVY, MEDIUM OR LIGHT PERTAINING, THE SUPPLY OF TELKOM APPROVED MATERIAL, INCLUDING\nCORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL HARD, #A GRADE, I BEAMS - 140 X 70 X 6MM, TREATED WITH APPROVED RUSTPROOF PAINT (E.G. CHROMITES) TO\nTHE AREA MANAGER\'S APPROVAL - TO BE USED WHEN RAILS ARE UNAVAILABLE, COSTS IN RESPECT OF SLUMP TESTS WHEN THE AREA MANAGER ALLOWS\nMACHINE MIXING, THE STABILIZING OF THE BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS WITH 2 X 50KG OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE OF SAND, THE\nCUTTING, REMOVAL AND DISPOSAL OF ALL TYPES OF EXISTING PIPE LENGTHS RUNNING THROUGH THE MANHOLE (EMPTY OR OCCUPIED). THE SUPPLY AND\nFITTING OF SPLIT PIPE/S OVER EXISTING ELECTRICAL CABLES, MARKING OF PIPES WITH HIGH-TENSION WARNING STICKERS AND PAINTING WITH RED\nPAINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3045978,'CI1.54','CI1.54 REINST HOT TAR 80ΓÇô100mm RD','This item consists of the surface re-instatements for roads (hot tar) 80 ΓÇô 100 mm thick.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply of 150 mm G2 crusher run and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specifications, \nb) The DCP test requirements, according to roads authority specifications,\nc) The preparation and cleaning of the re-instatement area and the removal of spoil from site, \nd) The supply and brushing on of liquid emulsion to the vertical sides of the existing trench, \ne) The supply of hot tar and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specifications,\nf) The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing road / sidewalk levels.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nNote:\na) If the local authority executes the re-instatements on behalf of the Service Provider, then the Service Provider remains liable for the payment to the local authority,\nb) The Service Provider must familiarize himself with the re-instatement specifications of the various authorities.\nc) Quantities will be calculated against the applicable proposed trenching dimensions.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M2).','M2',590.28,'REINST,TAR:CI1.54,HOT 80#100MM RD','REINSTATE, TAR:ITEM NUMBER CI1.54, TYPE HOT 80#100MM RD:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY OF 150 MM G2 CRUSHER\nRUN AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATIONS, THE DCP\nTEST REQUIREMENTS, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATIONS, THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE RE-INSTATEMENT AREA AND THE\nREMOVAL OF SPOIL FROM SITE,  THE SUPPLY AND BRUSHING ON OF LIQUID EMULSION TO THE VERTICAL SIDES OF THE EXISTING TRENCH, THE SUPPLY\nOF HOT TAR AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATIONS,\nTHE FINISHING OF LEVELS TO BE AESTHETICALLY TRUE TO THE SURROUNDING EXISTING ROAD / SIDEWALK LEVELS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nCOSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: IF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY EXECUTES THE RE-INSTATEMENTS ON BEHALF OF THE\nSERVICE PROVIDER, THEN THE SERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS LIABLE FOR THE PAYMENT TO THE LOCAL AUTHORITY, THE SERVICE PROVIDER MUST\nFAMILIARIZE HIMSELF WITH THE RE-INSTATEMENT SPECIFICATIONS OF THE VARIOUS AUTHORITIES. QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED AGAINST THE\nAPPLICABLE PROPOSED TRENCHING DIMENSIONS. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER SQUARE METRE (M2)'),(3045979,'CI2.14','CI2.14 CABL PULLG','This item consists of the pulling of slack between manholes (existing cables only).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The opening and closing of manholes,  \nb) Unclamp and re-clamp cables to support brackets in all affected manholes,  \nc) The pulling of slack between manholes for jointing purposes on existing cables only. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) The rate per metre will only be paid for the total length of slack pulled into the manhole where the jointing must take place and not for each manhole. \nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',162.89,'RETNSN,CBL:CI2.14,PULLG','RETENSION, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.14, TYPE PULLG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE OPENING AND CLOSING OF MANHOLES,\nUNCLAMP AND RE-CLAMP CABLES TO SUPPORT BRACKETS IN ALL AFFECTED MANHOLES, THE PULLING OF SLACK BETWEEN MANHOLES FOR JOINTING\nPURPOSES ON EXISTING CABLES ONLY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THE RATE\nPER METRE WILL ONLY BE PAID FOR THE TOTAL LENGTH OF SLACK PULLED INTO THE MANHOLE WHERE THE JOINTING MUST TAKE PLACE AND NOT FOR\nEACH MANHOLE. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER METRE (MT)'),(3045980,'CI2.32','CI2.32 PRVD 2 DRWR SHLF','This item consists of the provisioning of a 2-drawer housing with the shelves and midcouplers.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na) The cost of the shelf,\nb) Shipping (Local and Foreign),\nc) Storage.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per 2 drawer shelf, each (EA).','EA',4157.74,'PRVD,EQUIP:CI2.32,2 DRWR SHLF','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.32, TYPE 2 DRWR SHLF:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE COST OF THE SHELF,\nSHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 2 DRAWER SHELF, EACH (EA)'),(3045981,'CI1.30','CI1.30 PAINT MNHL','This item consists of the painting of Manholes with wet seal.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The painting of manhole walls with wet seal where required, upon instruction from the Contract Representative, \nb) All necessary preparations i.e. cleaning, sealing of all holes with silicone, etc., \nc) The supply of the specified sealing paint to the Area ManagerΓÇÖs approval.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per manhole, each (EA).','EA',1192.84,'PAINT,MNHL:CI1.30','PAINT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.30:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PAINTING OF MANHOLE WALLS WITH WET SEAL WHERE\nREQUIRED, UPON INSTRUCTION FROM THE CONTRACT REPRESENTATIVE, ALL NECESSARY PREPARATIONS I.E. CLEANING, SEALING OF ALL HOLES WITH\nSILICONE, ETC., THE SUPPLY OF THE SPECIFIED SEALING PAINT TO THE AREA MANAGER#S APPROVAL. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO\nAND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER MANHOLE, EACH (EA)'),(3045983,'CI1.29','CI1.29 RECONST MH ROOF','This item consists of the reconstruction of a manhole roof, all sizes and shapes.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \na) Supply, delivery and casting of 20-25MPA concrete, \nb) Fitting of the frame, cover and coping, finished by with a wooden float and corner tool, \nc) All equipment, shuttering and material required, \nd) The loading requirements of SABS specification 558 table 2 for the particular situation of loading, i.e. heavy, medium or light pertaining, \ne) The supply of Telkom SA approved material, including corrugated iron - 0.6mm full hard, ΓÇÿAΓÇÖ grade, ΓÇ£IΓÇ¥ beams - 140 x 70 x 6mm, treated with approved rustproof paint to Area ManagerΓÇÖs approval ΓÇô to be used when rails are unavailable, \nf) Rustproof paint (e.g. chromites) to the Area Manager\'s approval, \ng) Costs in respect of slump tests when the Area Manager allows machine mixing,\nh) The stabilizing of the backfill around roadway manhole necks with 2 x 50kg pockets of cement per cubic metre of sand,  \ni) Material and labour used to support any existing joints, cables and services, \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \nb) The demolishing existing masonry and manmade structure and the removal thereof (See demolishing of masonary).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per manhole, each (EA)','EA',8789.49,'RECONST,MNHL:CI1.29,ROOF','RECONSTRUCT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.29, TYPE ROOF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SUPPLY, DELIVERY AND CASTING OF\n20-25MPA CONCRETE, FITTING OF THE FRAME, COVER AND COPING, FINISHED BY WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL EQUIPMENT,\nSHUTTERING AND MATERIAL REQUIRED, THE LOADING REQUIREMENTS OF SABS SPECIFICATION 558 TABLE 2 FOR THE PARTICULAR SITUATION OF\nLOADING, I.E. HEAVY, MEDIUM OR LIGHT PERTAINING, THE SUPPLY OF TELKOM SA APPROVED MATERIAL, INCLUDING CORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL\nHARD, #A# GRADE, #I# BEAMS - 140 X 70 X 6MM, TREATED WITH APPROVED RUSTPROOF PAINT TO AREA MANAGER#S APPROVAL # TO BE USED WHEN\nRAILS ARE UNAVAILABLE, RUSTPROOF PAINT (E.G. CHROMITES) TO THE AREA MANAGER\'S APPROVAL, COSTS IN RESPECT OF SLUMP TESTS WHEN THE\nAREA MANAGER ALLOWS MACHINE MIXING, THE STABILIZING OF THE BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS WITH 2 X 50KG POCKETS OF CEMENT\nPER CUBIC METRE OF SAND, MATERIAL AND LABOUR USED TO SUPPORT ANY EXISTING JOINTS, CABLES AND SERVICES, THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL\nTRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE DEMOLISHING EXISTING MASONRY AND MANMADE STRUCTURE AND THE REMOVAL\nTHEREOF (SEE DEMOLISHING OF MASONARY). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER MANHOLE, EACH (EA)'),(3045984,'CI1.31','CI1.31 CONSTR PJB','This item consists of the construction of a pipe junction box (brick and or concrete). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The necessary excavation up to existing pipe level or new trench level, backfilling, compaction and D.C.P testing, \nb) The supply of all materials required to build the PJB, with an internal size of 600mm x 600mm x 550mm high, (five layers of bricks) (baked bricks only) and should have a steel reinforced concrete base and cover, \nc) Building in a single wall configuration with strength of 20MPA, \nd) All pipe entries.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',1355.85,'ERCT,BLDG:CI1.31 CONSTR PJB','ERECT, BUILDING:NAME CI1.31 CONSTR PJB:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE NECESSARY EXCAVATION UP TO EXISTING PIPE LEVEL\nOR NEW TRENCH LEVEL, BACKFILLING, COMPACTION AND D.C.P TESTING, THE SUPPLY OF ALL MATERIALS REQUIRED TO BUILD THE PJB, WITH AN\nINTERNAL SIZE OF 600MM X 600MM X 550MM HIGH, (FIVE LAYERS OF BRICKS) (BAKED BRICKS ONLY) AND SHOULD HAVE A STEEL REINFORCED\nCONCRETE BASE AND COVER, BUILDING IN A SINGLE WALL CONFIGURATION WITH STRENGTH OF 20MPA, ALL PIPE ENTRIES. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL\nTRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654.  THE UNIT OF MEASURE\nFOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3045985,'CI1.12','CI1.12 EXCVT RCK','This item consists of all hard rock excavation up to any depth. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The drilling, blasting, breaking and removal of the excavated rock, boulders and spoil by means of pneumatic tools, heavy machinery and or blasting equipment.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) This is an extra over item that will always be used in conjunction with trenching or an excavation item,\nb) Quantities will be calculated and paid against the proposed trenching / excavation dimensions ΓÇô over-breaks excluded.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item per cubic metre (M┬│)','M3',582.45,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.12,RCK','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.12, TYPE RCK:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE DRILLING, BLASTING, BREAKING AND REMOVAL\nOF THE EXCAVATED ROCK, BOULDERS AND SPOIL BY MEANS OF PNEUMATIC TOOLS, HEAVY MACHINERY AND OR BLASTING EQUIPMENT. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS IS AN EXTRA OVER ITEM THAT WILL ALWAYS BE USED\nIN CONJUNCTION WITH TRENCHING OR AN EXCAVATION ITEM, QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED AND PAID AGAINST THE PROPOSED TRENCHING /\nEXCAVATION DIMENSIONS OVER-BREAKS EXCLUDED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nPER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3045986,'CI1.27','CI1.27 CAST CONCRT','This item consists of the supply and casting of concrete (20-25MPA) (i.e. encasement of pipes, plinths, slabs, copings, poles, struts, stays, new or replacement of an existing frame and cover for manhole, accessible pipe junction box, jointing pit, etc.).  \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Shoring of the excavation, fitting and removal of shutters, \nb) Pumping and controlling of water, \nc) Barricading, \nd) Supply and delivery of concrete to site,  \ne) Casting of 20-25MPA concrete, \nf) The fitting of the frame, cover and coping, which should be finished by means of a wooden float and corner tool, \ng) All equipment and material required to complete the task. \n\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All excavations. (See item CI1.1 to CI1.3)\nb) Demolishing of masonry (See item CI1.28)\n\nNote:\na) Method to calculate = Length x Width x Depth of the concrete supplied, \nb) When the minimum required depth cannot be excavated for poles, struts and stays, concrete must be installed to be a minimum depth of 600mm and remainder of the depth to be built above ground level with rock and concrete (as per CR approval). \n\nThe Specification for this item is:  \na) 325. CTO-004654, \nb) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nc) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), \nd) B3001 (CTO-003944).\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cubic metre (m┬│).','M3',1588.37,'CAST,CONCRT:CI1.27','CAST, CONCRETE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.27:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SHORING OF THE EXCAVATION, FITTING AND REMOVAL OF\nSHUTTERS, PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER, BARRICADING, SUPPLY AND DELIVERY OF CONCRETE TO SITE, CASTING OF 20-25MPA CONCRETE, THE\nFITTING OF THE FRAME, COVER AND COPING, WHICH SHOULD BE FINISHED BY MEANS OF A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL EQUIPMENT AND\nMATERIAL REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THE TASK. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL EXCAVATIONS. (SEE ITEM CI1.1 TO CI1.3) DEMOLISHING OF MASONRY (SEE\nITEM CI1.28) NOTE: METHOD TO CALCULATE = LENGTH X WIDTH X DEPTH OF THE CONCRETE SUPPLIED, WHEN THE MINIMUM REQUIRED DEPTH CANNOT BE\nEXCAVATED FOR POLES, STRUTS AND STAYS, CONCRETE MUST BE INSTALLED TO BE A MINIMUM DEPTH OF 600MM AND REMAINDER OF THE DEPTH TO BE\nBUILT ABOVE GROUND LEVEL WITH ROCK AND CONCRETE (AS PER CR APPROVAL). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654,\nSP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944). THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3045987,'CI1.23','CI1.23 MNHL CONSTR NON-STD 3.52M ΓÇ£LΓÇ¥ & ΓÇ£TΓÇ¥ FT WAY','This item consists of a manhole construction / reconstruction (nonstandard shape) 3.52M ΓÇ£LΓÇ¥ (Drawing MHGP 9A) and ΓÇ£TΓÇ¥ (Drawing MHT 9G) footway.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Supply, delivery and casting of 20-25MPA concrete, \nb) Fitting of the frame, cover and coping, finished by with a wooden float and corner tool, \nc) All equipment, shuttering and material required, \nd) The positioning of the manhole, \ne) The loading requirements of SABS specification 558 table 2 for the particular situation of loading, i.e. heavy, medium or light pertaining, \nf) The supply of Telkom SA approved material, including corrugated iron - 0.6mm full hard, ΓÇÿAΓÇÖ grade, ΓÇ£IΓÇ¥ beams - 140 x 70 x 6mm, treated with approved rustproof paint to Area ManagerΓÇÖs approval ΓÇô to be used when rails are unavailable, \ng) Rustproof paint (e.g. chromites) to the Area Manager\'s approval, \nh) Costs in respect of slump tests when the Area Manager allows machine mixing, \ni) The stabilizing of the backfill around roadway manhole necks with 2 x 50kg pockets of cement per cubic metre of sand,  \nj) The cutting, removal and disposal of all types of existing pipe lengths running through the manhole (empty or occupied), \nk) The supply and fitting of split pipe/s over existing electrical cables, marking of pipes with high-tension warning stickers and painting with red paint. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Frame and cover (to be supplied by Telkom), \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',28871.23,'CONSTR,MNHL:CI1.23,NON-STD 3.52M FT WAY','CONSTRUCT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.23, TYPE NON-STD 3.52M L&T FT WAY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SUPPLY, DELIVERY AND\nCASTING OF 20-25MPA CONCRETE, FITTING OF THE FRAME, COVER AND COPING, FINISHED BY WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL\nEQUIPMENT, SHUTTERING AND MATERIAL REQUIRED, THE POSITIONING OF THE MANHOLE, THE LOADING REQUIREMENTS OF SABS SPECIFICATION 558\nTABLE 2 FOR THE PARTICULAR SITUATION OF LOADING, I.E. HEAVY, MEDIUM OR LIGHT PERTAINING, THE SUPPLY OF TELKOM SA APPROVED MATERIAL,\nINCLUDING CORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL HARD, #A# GRADE, #I# BEAMS - 140 X 70 X 6MM, TREATED WITH APPROVED RUSTPROOF PAINT TO AREA\nMANAGER#S APPROVAL # TO BE USED WHEN RAILS ARE UNAVAILABLE, RUSTPROOF PAINT (E.G. CHROMITES) TO THE AREA MANAGER\'S APPROVAL, COSTS\nIN RESPECT OF SLUMP TESTS WHEN THE AREA MANAGER ALLOWS MACHINE MIXING, THE STABILIZING OF THE BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS\nWITH 2 X 50KG POCKETS OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE OF SAND, THE CUTTING, REMOVAL AND DISPOSAL OF ALL TYPES OF EXISTING PIPE LENGTHS\nRUNNING THROUGH THE MANHOLE (EMPTY OR OCCUPIED), THE SUPPLY AND FITTING OF SPLIT PIPE/S OVER EXISTING ELECTRICAL CABLES, MARKING OF\nPIPES WITH HIGH-TENSION WARNING STICKERS AND PAINTING WITH RED PAINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: FRAME AND COVER (TO BE SUPPLIED BY\nTELKOM), ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3045988,'CI2.9','CI2.9 OVHL CABL Γëñ10PR/S MICRO-DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of over hauling of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables (UG and Indoor) up to 10 pair,\nΓÇó Air pipe,\nΓÇó LAN Cabling, \nΓÇó Single micro ducts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nb) Cleaning, preparing, threading and testing existing Telkom duct to ensure duct is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc.,\nc) Overcoming engineering difficulties such as hauling through Utility Boxes, pillar joints, entry points etc.,\nd) Pumping and controlling of water while hauling takes place,\ne) The fitting of uni-strut support / flat brackets for the supporting of the cable in Utility Boxes,\nf) Cleaning Utility Boxes and surroundings on completion,\ng) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water, dry air, cable ties, fasteners, labels, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps etc.),\nh) Performing micro duct integrity test,\ni) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nj) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \nk) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled. \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled.\nc) The price per metre is the same for the simultaneously overhauling of 1 inner-duct / micro-duct or simultaneous overhauling of 2 inner-ducts (32/40mm) / micro-ducts\nd) If 3 inner-ducts or 3-4 micro-ducts are simultaneously overhauled then this item may be claimed twice\n\nFor UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required \nFor indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) Supply of support brackets (to be supplied by Telkom)\nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled,\nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled,\nc) The price per metre is the same for the simultaneously overhauling of 1 inner-duct / micro-duct or simultaneous overhauling of 2 inner-ducts (32/40mm) / micro-ducts,\nd) If 3 inner-ducts or 3-4 micro-ducts are simultaneously overhauled, then this item may be claimed twice.\n\nThe specification for these items is:  \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable / duct (over hauled) per metre (MT).','MT',9.17,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.9,OVHL 10PR/S MICRO-DUCT','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.9, TYPE OVHL 10PR/S MICRO-DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND\nEQUIPMENT THAT IS NECESSARY TO EXECUTE THE WORK, CLEANING, PREPARING, THREADING AND TESTING EXISTING TELKOM DUCT TO ENSURE DUCT IS\nUSEABLE BY MEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., OVERCOMING ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS HAULING THROUGH\nUTILITY BOXES, PILLAR JOINTS, ENTRY POINTS ETC., PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER WHILE HAULING TAKES PLACE, THE FITTING OF\nUNI-STRUT SUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS FOR THE SUPPORTING OF THE CABLE IN UTILITY BOXES, CLEANING UTILITY BOXES AND SURROUNDINGS ON\nCOMPLETION, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. POLY # WATER, DRY AIR, CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, MICRO DUCT COUPLERS, MICRO\nDUCT END CAPS ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS CABLES /\nDUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE WORK. FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED\nFOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR\nHANDLED. FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE /\nDUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED. THE PRICE PER METRE IS THE SAME FOR THE SIMULTANEOUSLY OVERHAULING OF 1\nINNER-DUCT / MICRO-DUCT OR SIMULTANEOUS OVERHAULING OF 2 INNER-DUCTS (32/40MM) / MICRO-DUCTS IF 3 INNER-DUCTS OR 3-4 MICRO-DUCTS\nARE SIMULTANEOUSLY OVERHAULED THEN THIS ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED TWICE FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE\nCENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED\nFOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED THE\nRATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE CABLE / DUCTS, SUPPLY OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM) ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM'),(3045990,'CI2.26','CI2.26 INST OFTP','This item consists of the Installation of an Optical Fibre Termination Panel (OFTP).\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals,\nb) Obtaining all work refs.,\nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required,\nd) Labour for the installation of the equipment,\ne) Labelling,\nf) Minor build material,\ng) Submission of documentation, such as:\na. Quality acceptance certificate,\nb. Quality tick sheet,\nc. IE6 document,\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items),\nb) Cost of OFTP with faceplates and midcouplers / connectors / couplers\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per OFTP, each (EA).','EA',4644.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.26,OFTP','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.26, TYPE OFTP:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, LABOUR\nFOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE EQUIPMENT, LABELLING, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL, SUBMISSION OF DOCUMENTATION, SUCH AS: QUALITY ACCEPTANCE\nCERTIFICATE, QUALITY TICK SHEET, IE6 DOCUMENT, THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS), COST OF OFTP\nWITH FACEPLATES AND MIDCOUPLERS / CONNECTORS / COUPLERS THE UNIT OF 