ITH HIGH-TENSION WARNING STICKERS AND PAINTING WITH RED\nPAINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3045994,'CI2.29','CI2.29 INSTL FBR TERM CABNT','This item consists of the Installation of a fibre termination cabinet (i.e 600mm x 300mm x 2200mm, 600mm x 600mm x 2200mm).\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na) Labour for the installation of the cabinet,\nb) Minor build material. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items),\nb) The cost of the cabinet (Telkom to supply the cabinet).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per cabinet, each (EA).','EA',1653.01,'INSTL,CABNT:CI2.29,FBR TERM','INSTALL, CABINET:TYPE FBR TERM:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE CABINET, MINOR BUILD\nMATERIAL. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS), THE COST OF THE CABINET (TELKOM TO SUPPLY THE\nCABINET). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABINET, EACH (EA)'),(3045995,'CI1.28','CI1.28 DEM MSNRY','This item consists of the demolishing existing masonry and manmade structure and the removal thereof\n \nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \na) The removal of all masonry spoils from site, \nb) All equipment required to complete the work, \nc) Material and labour used to support any existing joints, cables and services, \nd) Pressure testing of cables and joints during and after reconstruction of manholes. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nNote:\na) This item will be used to pay for the demolishing of any masonry structures (i.e manholes, manhole roofs, jointing pits, pipe junction boxes, SDC plinths or part thereof, etc.). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cubic metre (m┬│).','M3',946.15,'DEMOL,MASON:CI1.28','DEMOLISH, MASONARY:ITEM NUMBER CI1.28:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE REMOVAL OF ALL MASONRY SPOILS FROM SITE, ALL\nEQUIPMENT REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THE WORK, MATERIAL AND LABOUR USED TO SUPPORT ANY EXISTING JOINTS, CABLES AND SERVICES, PRESSURE\nTESTING OF CABLES AND JOINTS DURING AND AFTER RECONSTRUCTION OF MANHOLES. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM WILL BE USED TO PAY FOR THE DEMOLISHING OF ANY MASONRY STRUCTURES (I.E MANHOLES, MANHOLE\nROOFS, JOINTING PITS, PIPE JUNCTION BOXES, SDC PLINTHS OR PART THEREOF, ETC.). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654.\nTHE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3045996,'CI1.48','CI1.48 BLD RETANG WALL','This item consists of building a retaining wall as specified (i.e. terraces). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The construction of a retaining wall, 230mm thick (double brick) with a minimum strength of 20MPA with an appropriate foundation, \nb) Plastering and painting with an approved paint when required, \nc) All equipment and material required to complete the task. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M┬▓).','M2',764.31,'BLD,WALL:CI1.48,RETANG','BUILD, WALL:ITEM NUMBER CI1.48, TYPE RETAINING:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE CONSTRUCTION OF A RETAINING WALL, 230MM\nTHICK (DOUBLE BRICK) WITH A MINIMUM STRENGTH OF 20MPA WITH AN APPROPRIATE FOUNDATION, PLASTERING AND PAINTING WITH AN APPROVED\nPAINT WHEN REQUIRED, ALL EQUIPMENT AND MATERIAL REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THE TASK. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE\n(SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SQUARE\nMETRE (M2)'),(3045998,'CI1.62','CI1.62 OPN/CLS WELDED MNHL','This item consists of the opening and closing of welded manholes.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The opening by means of cold cutting (drilling) of the welded plate to access the key mechanism, \nb) Opening of the manhole by the normal hydraulic method,\nc) Grinding the plate off the lid and cleaning the lid surface, \nd) The opening by means of a hydraulic nibbler in the case of failed manhole lids to gain access to the locking pin for the removal and replacement of the cover,\ne) The supplying and welding of a (75mm x 75mm x 5mm) steel plate over the keyhole,\nf) The supply of all equipment to open and close welded manholes, including minor materials, \ng) Updating of Telkom records/databases of welded manholes.\n\nNote: \nThis item may be claimed separately once for opening and once for closing. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document)\n\nNote: \na) This item may be claimed separately once for opening and once for closing.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per manhole opened or closed, each (EA)','EA',250.00,'SPRT,MNHL:CI1.62,WELDED,OPN/CLS','SUPPORT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.62, TYPE WELDED, LABOR OPN/CLS:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE OPENING BY MEANS OF\nCOLD CUTTING (DRILLING) OF THE WELDED PLATE TO ACCESS THE KEY MECHANISM, OPENING OF THE MANHOLE BY THE NORMAL HYDRAULIC METHOD,\nGRINDING THE PLATE OFF THE LID AND CLEANING THE LID SURFACE, THE OPENING BY MEANS OF A HYDRAULIC NIBBLER IN THE CASE OF FAILED\nMANHOLE LIDS TO GAIN ACCESS TO THE LOCKING PIN FOR THE REMOVAL AND REPLACEMENT OF THE COVER, THE SUPPLYING AND WELDING OF A (75MM X\n75MM X 5MM) STEEL PLATE OVER THE KEYHOLE, THE SUPPLY OF ALL EQUIPMENT TO OPEN AND CLOSE WELDED MANHOLES, INCLUDING MINOR MATERIALS,\nUPDATING OF TELKOM RECORDS/DATABASES OF WELDED MANHOLES. NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY ONCE FOR OPENING AND ONCE FOR\nCLOSING. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT) NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY\nONCE FOR OPENING AND ONCE FOR CLOSING. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER MANHOLE OPENED OR CLOSED, EACH (EA)'),(3045999,'CI2.8','CI2.8 HAUL CABL >800-2400PR','This item consists of the installation by means of hauling of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables (UG and Indoor) >800PR ΓÇô 2400PR.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nb) Cleaning, preparing, threading and testing existing Telkom duct to ensure duct is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc.,\nc) Overcoming engineering difficulties such as hauling through Utility Boxes, pillar joints, entry points etc.,\nd) Pumping and controlling of water while hauling takes place,\ne) The fitting of uni-strut support / flat brackets for the supporting of the cable in Utility Boxes,\nf) Cleaning Utility Boxes and surroundings on completion,\ng) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. poly ΓÇô water, dry air, cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps etc.),\nh) Performing micro duct integrity test, \ni) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nj) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \nk) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\n\na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled. \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled.\na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required \nb) For indoor cable /duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required\nc) \nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) Supply of support brackets (to be supplied by Telkom),\nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) For UG the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid irrespective of any slack required or handled,\nb) For indoor cable / duct the quantity hauled for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual hauled cable / duct length irrespective of any slack required or handled.\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable/s (hauled) per metre (MT).','MT',42.03,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.8,HAUL 800-2400PR','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.8, TYPE HAUL 800-2400PR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT\nTHAT IS NECESSARY TO EXECUTE THE WORK, CLEANING, PREPARING, THREADING AND TESTING EXISTING TELKOM DUCT TO ENSURE DUCT IS USEABLE BY\nMEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., OVERCOMING ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS HAULING THROUGH UTILITY\nBOXES, PILLAR JOINTS, ENTRY POINTS ETC., PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER WHILE HAULING TAKES PLACE, THE FITTING OF UNI-STRUT\nSUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS FOR THE SUPPORTING OF THE CABLE IN UTILITY BOXES, CLEANING UTILITY BOXES AND SURROUNDINGS ON COMPLETION,\nSUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. POLY # WATER, DRY AIR, CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, SADDLES, GLUE, MICRO DUCT COUPLERS,\nMICRO DUCT END CAPS ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS\nCABLES / DUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE WORK. FOR UG THE QUANTITY\nHAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK\nREQUIRED OR HANDLED. FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL\nHAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED. FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED\nFROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED FOR INDOOR CABLE /DUCT THE\nQUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL HAULED CABLE / DUCT LENGTH IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK\nREQUIRED THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE CABLE / DUCTS, SUPPLY OF SUPPORT BRACKETS (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM), ALL TRAVEL COSTS\nTO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: FOR UG THE QUANTITY HAULED FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB\nLID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED OR HANDLED, FOR INDOOR CABLE / DUCT THE QUANTITY HAULED'),(3046000,'CI1.14','CI1.14 PROVD BCKFIL TRNCH CRETE','This item consists of the provision of trench crete. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The cost of acquiring, loading and transporting / delivery of the trench crete / material from the supply source to site. \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item per cubic metre (M┬│)','M3',2251.89,'BKFILL,TRNCH:CI1.14 CRETE','BACKFILL, TRENCH:ITEM NUMBER CI1.14 CRETE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE COST OF ACQUIRING, LOADING AND TRANSPORTING\n/ DELIVERY OF THE TRENCH CRETE / MATERIAL FROM THE SUPPLY SOURCE TO SITE. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3046001,'CI2.13','CI2.13 BCKFLL OPN TRNCH','This item consists of the backfilling of a trench left open by 3rd party.\n\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Backfilling of the trench with existing excavated material,  \nb) Compaction and D.C.P. testing, \nc) The cleaning of site and removal of spoil. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Any additional imported backfill material required,\nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) This item may only be claimed where the trench / excavation was performed by a 3rd party.\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe rate excludes:\nAny additional imported backfill material required,\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',37.49,'BKFILL,TRNCH:CI2.13 OPN','BACKFILL, TRENCH:ITEM NUMBER CI2.13 OPN:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: BACKFILLING OF THE TRENCH WITH EXISTING EXCAVATED\nMATERIAL, COMPACTION AND D.C.P. TESTING, THE CLEANING OF SITE AND REMOVAL OF SPOIL. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ANY ADDITIONAL IMPORTED\nBACKFILL MATERIAL REQUIRED, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE CLAIMED WHERE\nTHE TRENCH / EXCAVATION WAS PERFORMED BY A 3RD PARTY. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040\nCTO-010225. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ANY ADDITIONAL IMPORTED BACKFILL MATERIAL REQUIRED, THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE\n(MT)'),(3046002,'CI2.2','CI2.2 LAY/FSTN CABL>10-200PR/48-144FBR/2-4DUCT','This item consists of the installation by means of laying or fastening of any of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables > 10 to 200 pair,\nΓÇó Z Screen Cable,\nΓÇó All Fibre Cables 48 to 144 fibres (including Inter Facility Cable), \nΓÇó 2-4 way micro ducts, \nΓÇó 32/40mm inner ducts.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Laying and or fastening onto trays, walls, brackets, risers, under floors, ceilings, trunking, etc.,\nb) Providing all tools and equipment that is necessary to execute the work,\nc) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, micro duct couplers, micro duct end caps, 32/40mm couplers and end caps, etc.),\nd) Performing micro duct integrity test,\ne) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables / ducts,\nf) Removal of surplus cables / ducts, \ng) Cleaning the work site during and on completion of the work.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable / ducts, \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) Quantity for payment will be measured from point to point of the actual laid and or fastened cable / duct irrespective of any slack required\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable / duct per metre (MT).','MT',25.93,'LAY,CBL:CI2.2,FSTN 10-200PR','LAY, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.2, TYPE FSTN 10-200PR/48-144FBR/2-4DUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LAYING AND OR FASTENING\nONTO TRAYS, WALLS, BRACKETS, RISERS, UNDER FLOORS, CEILINGS, TRUNKING, ETC., PROVIDING ALL TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT THAT IS NECESSARY TO\nEXECUTE THE WORK, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, SADDLES, GLUE, MICRO DUCT COUPLERS, MICRO\nDUCT END CAPS, 32/40MM COUPLERS AND END CAPS, ETC.), PERFORMING MICRO DUCT INTEGRITY TEST, THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND\nLABELLING OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, REMOVAL OF SURPLUS CABLES / DUCTS, CLEANING THE WORK SITE DURING AND ON COMPLETION OF THE\nWORK. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE CABLE / DUCTS, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE:\nQUANTITY FOR PAYMENT WILL BE MEASURED FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL LAID AND OR FASTENED CABLE / DUCT IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK\nREQUIRED THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nCABLE / DUCT PER METRE (MT)'),(3046003,'CI1.9','CI1.9 SPCLZD XNG BORE NORM SOIL 2 PIPE','This item consists of the specialized crossings (not trenches). excavating pits and setting up boring equipment. bore to accommodate and install two 110mm outside diameter rigid HDPE pipe in all soil conditions except rock.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The setting up of boring equipment, excavation on both sides, boring, supply and installation of two 110MM continuous class 10 HDPE pipe,\nb) Tunnelling under kerbstones, supporting of services, backfilling and removal of soil,\nc) The cost for damages incurred by the Service Provider and the repair of roads or existing services,\nd) The cost of clearing the surface, removing boulders with a size of up to 0.015 cubic metres (If the boulders are bigger than 0.015 cubic metres in size, a separate rate must be negotiated.), grubbing of tree stumps,\ne) Backfilling of cavities, demolishing structures and removal thereof,\nf) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling).\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) This item will be used for payment when boring is to be done instead of trenching at roads, driveways etc.,\nb) Measurement for payment will be done from kerbstone to kerbstone, per pipe per meter, and only for successful attempts,\nc) This item will be applicable in all soil conditions except in rock. (including clay and or waterlogged ground conditions).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',2167.42,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.9,NORM SOIL 2 PIPE','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.9, TYPE NORM SOIL 2 PIPE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SETTING UP OF BORING\nEQUIPMENT, EXCAVATION ON BOTH SIDES, BORING, SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF TWO 110MM CONTINUOUS CLASS 10 HDPE PIPE, TUNNELLING UNDER\nKERBSTONES, SUPPORTING OF SERVICES, BACKFILLING AND REMOVAL OF SOIL, THE COST FOR DAMAGES INCURRED BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER AND THE\nREPAIR OF ROADS OR EXISTING SERVICES, THE COST OF CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING BOULDERS WITH A SIZE OF UP TO 0.015 CUBIC METRES\n(IF THE BOULDERS ARE BIGGER THAN 0.015 CUBIC METRES IN SIZE, A SEPARATE RATE MUST BE NEGOTIATED.), GRUBBING OF TREE STUMPS,\nBACKFILLING OF CAVITIES, DEMOLISHING STRUCTURES AND REMOVAL THEREOF, PIPE ENTRIES (EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL\nTRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM WILL BE USED FOR PAYMENT WHEN BORING IS TO BE DONE\nINSTEAD OF TRENCHING AT ROADS, DRIVEWAYS ETC., MEASUREMENT FOR PAYMENT WILL BE DONE FROM KERBSTONE TO KERBSTONE, PER PIPE PER\nMETER, AND ONLY FOR SUCCESSFUL ATTEMPTS, THIS ITEM WILL BE APPLICABLE IN ALL SOIL CONDITIONS EXCEPT IN ROCK. (INCLUDING CLAY AND OR\nWATERLOGGED GROUND CONDITIONS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE\n(MT)'),(3046004,'CI1.7','CI1.7 SPCLZD XNG BORE NORM SOIL 1 PIPE','This item consists of the specialized crossings (not trenches). excavating pits and setting up boring equipment. bore to accommodate and install one 110mm outside diameter rigid HDPE pipe in all soil conditions except rock.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The setting up of boring equipment, excavation on both sides, boring, supply and installation of a 110MM continuous class 10 HDPE pipe, \nb) Tunnelling under kerbstones, supporting of services, backfilling and removal of soil, \nc) The cost for damages incurred by the Service Provider and the repair of roads or existing services, \nd) The cost of clearing the surface, removing boulders with a size of up to 0.015 cubic metres (If the boulders are bigger than 0.015 cubic metres in size, a separate rate must be negotiated.), grubbing of tree stumps, \ne) Backfilling of cavities, demolishing structures and removal thereof, \nf) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) This item will be used for payment when boring is to be done instead of trenching at roads, driveways etc.,\nb) Measurement for payment will be done from kerbstone to kerbstone, per pipe per meter, and only for successful attempts,\nc) This item will be applicable in all soil conditions except in rock. (including clay and or waterlogged ground conditions).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',1486.86,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.7,NORM SOIL 1 PIPE','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.7, TYPE NORM SOIL 1 PIPE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SETTING UP OF BORING\nEQUIPMENT, EXCAVATION ON BOTH SIDES, BORING, SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF A 110MM CONTINUOUS CLASS 10 HDPE PIPE, TUNNELLING UNDER\nKERBSTONES, SUPPORTING OF SERVICES, BACKFILLING AND REMOVAL OF SOIL, THE COST FOR DAMAGES INCURRED BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER AND THE\nREPAIR OF ROADS OR EXISTING SERVICES, THE COST OF CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING BOULDERS WITH A SIZE OF UP TO 0.015 CUBIC METRES\n(IF THE BOULDERS ARE BIGGER THAN 0.015 CUBIC METRES IN SIZE, A SEPARATE RATE MUST BE NEGOTIATED.), GRUBBING OF TREE STUMPS,\nBACKFILLING OF CAVITIES, DEMOLISHING STRUCTURES AND REMOVAL THEREOF, PIPE ENTRIES (EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL\nTRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM WILL BE USED FOR PAYMENT WHEN BORING IS TO BE DONE\nINSTEAD OF TRENCHING AT ROADS, DRIVEWAYS ETC., MEASUREMENT FOR PAYMENT WILL BE DONE FROM KERBSTONE TO KERBSTONE, PER PIPE PER\nMETER, AND ONLY FOR SUCCESSFUL ATTEMPTS, THIS ITEM WILL BE APPLICABLE IN ALL SOIL CONDITIONS EXCEPT IN ROCK. (INCLUDING CLAY AND OR\nWATERLOGGED GROUND CONDITIONS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE\n(MT)'),(3046005,'CI1.18','CI1.18 MNHL CONSTR STD 2.3M RD WAY','This item consists of a manhole construction / reconstruction 2.3m roadway (Drawing NSMH 9A).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Supply, delivery and casting of 20-25MPA concrete, \nb) Fitting of the frame, cover and coping, finished with a wooden float and corner tool, \nc) All equipment, shuttering and material required, \nd) Positioning of the manhole, \ne) Loading requirements of SABS specification 558 table 2 for the particular situation of loading, i.e. heavy, medium or light pertaining, \nf) The supply of Telkom SA approved material, including corrugated iron - 0.6mm full hard, ΓÇ£A\" grade, \"I\" beams - 140 x 70 x 6mm, treated with approved rustproof paint (e.g. chromites) to the Area Manager\'s approval - to be used when rails are unavailable, \ng) Costs in respect of slump tests when the Area Manager allows machine mixing, \nh) The stabilizing of the backfill around roadway manhole necks with 2 x 50kg of cement per cubic metre of sand, \ni) The cutting, removal and disposal of all types of existing pipe lengths running through the manhole (empty or occupied).\nj) The supply and fitting of split pipe/s over existing electrical cables, marking of pipes with high-tension warning stickers and painting with red paint. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',16944.11,'CONSTR,MNHL:CI1.18,STD 2.3M RD WAY','CONSTRUCT, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.18, SIZE STD 2.3M RD WAY :THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SUPPLY, DELIVERY AND CASTING\nOF 20-25MPA CONCRETE, FITTING OF THE FRAME, COVER AND COPING, FINISHED WITH A WOODEN FLOAT AND CORNER TOOL, ALL EQUIPMENT,\nSHUTTERING AND MATERIAL REQUIRED, POSITIONING OF THE MANHOLE, LOADING REQUIREMENTS OF SABS SPECIFICATION 558 TABLE 2 FOR THE\nPARTICULAR SITUATION OF LOADING, I.E. HEAVY, MEDIUM OR LIGHT PERTAINING, THE SUPPLY OF TELKOM SA APPROVED MATERIAL, INCLUDING\nCORRUGATED IRON - 0.6MM FULL HARD, #A GRADE, I BEAMS - 140 X 70 X 6MM, TREATED WITH APPROVED RUSTPROOF PAINT (E.G. CHROMITES) TO\nTHE AREA MANAGER\'S APPROVAL - TO BE USED WHEN RAILS ARE UNAVAILABLE, COSTS IN RESPECT OF SLUMP TESTS WHEN THE AREA MANAGER ALLOWS\nMACHINE MIXING, THE STABILIZING OF THE BACKFILL AROUND ROADWAY MANHOLE NECKS WITH 2 X 50KG OF CEMENT PER CUBIC METRE OF SAND, THE\nCUTTING, REMOVAL AND DISPOSAL OF ALL TYPES OF EXISTING PIPE LENGTHS RUNNING THROUGH THE MANHOLE (EMPTY OR OCCUPIED). THE SUPPLY AND\nFITTING OF SPLIT PIPE/S OVER EXISTING ELECTRICAL CABLES, MARKING OF PIPES WITH HIGH-TENSION WARNING STICKERS AND PAINTING WITH RED\nPAINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3046006,'CI2.17','CI2.17 INSTLN MICRO FBR CABL FLOAT','This item consists of the installation of micro fibre cable by floating method.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Installation of all sizes of micro fibre cable in ducting / micro ducts by utilizing of a Cable Jet / Blow-in machine,\nb) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. lubricant). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) The quantity for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid or from point to point of the actual duct length (where the is no UB), irrespective of any slack required.\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per meter (MT).','MT',7.39,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.17,MCR FBR FLOAT','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.17, TYPE MICRO FBR FLOAT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: INSTALLATION OF ALL SIZES OF MICRO\nFIBRE CABLE IN DUCTING / MICRO DUCTS BY UTILIZING OF A CABLE JET / BLOW-IN MACHINE, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E.\nLUBRICANT). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THE QUANTITY FOR PAYMENT WILL BE\nMEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID OR FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL DUCT LENGTH (WHERE THE\nIS NO UB), IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\nTHE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METER (MT)'),(3046007,'CI2.19','CI2.19 FIT END CAP','This item consists of the fitting of cable end caps all sizes - with or without valves.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Cleaning and roughening of the cable.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is \na) 325. CTO-004654,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',12.78,'INSTL,CAP:CI2.19,END','INSTALL, CAP:ITEM NUMBER CI2.19, TYPE END:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CLEANING AND ROUGHENING OF THE CABLE. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS 325. CTO-004654,\nPR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3046008,'CI2.28','CI2.28 INST FBR PTCH TLS','This item consists of the Installation and Testing of Duplex (1.7mm) Fibre Patch Tails, all lengths and connector types (i.e. LC to LC, LC to LX5, LX.5 to LX.5, LC to SC, FCPC to LC, FCPC to SC, FCPC to FCPC, etc.).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Labour for the installation of the cable,\nb) Labelling,\nc) Minor build material,\nd) Cleaning of the patch tail with a fibre scope\ne) Testing of the fibre patch tail, with a minimum of a Power meter and Light source,\nf) Shipping (Local and Foreign),\ng) Storage.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\nb) Supply of the Fibre Patch tail and Connectors,\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per Duplex Patch Tail, each (EA).','EA',575.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.28,FBR PTCH TLS','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.28, TYPE FBR PTCH TLS:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION OF\nTHE CABLE, LABELLING, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL, CLEANING OF THE PATCH TAIL WITH A FIBRE SCOPE TESTING OF THE FIBRE PATCH TAIL, WITH A\nMINIMUM OF A POWER METER AND LIGHT SOURCE, SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE\nSERVICE FEE ITEMS). SUPPLY OF THE FIBRE PATCH TAIL AND CONNECTORS, THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DUPLEX PATCH\nTAIL, EACH (EA)'),(3046009,'CI2.23','CI2.23 RECVR CU CABL','This item consists of the recovery of all copper cables.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The recovery of the all copper cables overhead or underground (i.e. from ducts, poles, manholes, etc.),\nb) The cost to redrum, test, measure, pressurize and label recovered cables for reuse,\nc) The cutting of cables into short (1.5m) lengths if not suitable for re-use, weighing, tagging and returning to Telkom stores,\nd) Transporting the recovered material from site to destination. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is \na) 325. CTO-004654, \nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per kilogram (KG).','KG',11.90,'RCVR,CBL:CI2.23,CU','RECOVER, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.23, TYPE CU:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE RECOVERY OF THE ALL COPPER CABLES OVERHEAD\nOR UNDERGROUND (I.E. FROM DUCTS, POLES, MANHOLES, ETC.), THE COST TO REDRUM, TEST, MEASURE, PRESSURIZE AND LABEL RECOVERED CABLES\nFOR REUSE, THE CUTTING OF CABLES INTO SHORT (1.5M) LENGTHS IF NOT SUITABLE FOR RE-USE, WEIGHING, TAGGING AND RETURNING TO TELKOM\nSTORES, TRANSPORTING THE RECOVERED MATERIAL FROM SITE TO DESTINATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS 325. CTO-004654, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER KILOGRAM (KG)'),(3046010,'CI1.5','CI1.5 CUT MCRTRNCHG(10-30MM WX150MM D)','This item consists of cut Micro Trenching (Width 10mm to 30mm X depth 150mm to 200mm) and installing micro-ducts by means of an approved mechanical cutting / trenching machine in all types of roads, verges, sidewalks with surfaces such as tar, cement, paving, etc.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Cutting and excavating by means of a mechanical cutting / trenching machine in all types of surfaces and soil conditions, \nb) Manual excavation where necessary,  \nc) Laying and connecting of the Micro-duct/s in the micro trench. Any number of ducts and / or combination of micro-ducts (i.e. 8/5 mm single ways and 12/10 mm 2 ways, \nd) Backfilling / Bedding and Padding (i.e. special slurry specified by the local authority, HOA, etc.), \ne) Compacting, \nf) Re-instatement of surfaces.  (i.e. tar, cement, paving, etc.), \ng) All testing to specification (i.e. Compaction, micro-duct, re-instatement, etc.), \nh) Minor Materials (i.e. bedding and padding, backfill, concrete, special slurry specified by the local authority, HOA, Micro-duct connectors, etc.).\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the Micro-duct/s, \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',233.50,'EXPOS,TRNCH:CI1.5,MCRTRNCHG','EXPOSE, TRENCH:ITEM NUMBER CI1.5, TYPE MCRTRNCHG, SIZE (WD 10-30MM X DP 150MM) :THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CUTTING\nAND EXCAVATING BY MEANS OF A MECHANICAL CUTTING / TRENCHING MACHINE IN ALL TYPES OF SURFACES AND SOIL CONDITIONS, MANUAL EXCAVATION\nWHERE NECESSARY, LAYING AND CONNECTING OF THE MICRO-DUCT/S IN THE MICRO TRENCH. ANY NUMBER OF DUCTS AND / OR COMBINATION OF\nMICRO-DUCTS (I.E. 8/5 MM SINGLE WAYS AND 12/10 MM 2 WAYS, BACKFILLING / BEDDING AND PADDING (I.E. SPECIAL SLURRY SPECIFIED BY THE\nLOCAL AUTHORITY, HOA, ETC.), COMPACTING, RE-INSTATEMENT OF SURFACES. (I.E. TAR, CEMENT, PAVING, ETC.), ALL TESTING TO SPECIFICATION\n(I.E. COMPACTION, MICRO-DUCT, RE-INSTATEMENT, ETC.), MINOR MATERIALS (I.E. BEDDING AND PADDING, BACKFILL, CONCRETE, SPECIAL SLURRY\nSPECIFIED BY THE LOCAL AUTHORITY, HOA, MICRO-DUCT CONNECTORS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE MICRO-DUCT/S, ALL TRAVEL\nCOSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR\nTHIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT)'),(3046011,'CI2.4','CI2.4 LAY/FSTN CABL >800-2400PR','This item consists of the installation by means of laying or fastening of any of the following: \n\nΓÇó All Copper Cables 800 to 2400 pair.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Laying and or fastening onto trays, walls, brackets, risers, under floors, ceilings, trunking, etc.,\nb) Supplying all equipment and tools required,\nc) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. cable ties, fasteners, labels, saddles, glue, etc.),\nd) The re-drumming, testing, measuring, and labelling of surplus cables,\ne) The cutting of surplus cables into short (1.5m) lengths if not suitable for re-use and weighing, tagging and returning them to Telkom stores, \nf) Cleaning of surrounding site upon completion.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the cable,  \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable per metre (MT).','MT',79.04,'LAY,CBL:CI2.4,FSTN 800-2400PR','LAY, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.4, TYPE FSTN 800-2400PR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LAYING AND OR FASTENING ONTO TRAYS,\nWALLS, BRACKETS, RISERS, UNDER FLOORS, CEILINGS, TRUNKING, ETC., SUPPLYING ALL EQUIPMENT AND TOOLS REQUIRED, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR\nMATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, SADDLES, GLUE, ETC.), THE RE-DRUMMING, TESTING, MEASURING, AND LABELLING OF SURPLUS\nCABLES, THE CUTTING OF SURPLUS CABLES INTO SHORT (1.5M) LENGTHS IF NOT SUITABLE FOR RE-USE AND WEIGHING, TAGGING AND RETURNING THEM\nTO TELKOM STORES, CLEANING OF SURROUNDING SITE UPON COMPLETION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE CABLE, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND\nFROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF\nMEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE PER METRE (MT)'),(3046012,'CI1.59','CI1.59 REINST INTRLCK BRICK RD','This item consists of the surface re-instatements inter-locking brick roads.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The preparation of bedding material,\nb) All the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification, \nc) Laying and compacting of the inter-locking bricks,  \nd) Replacement of any damaged material / bricks, \ne) The DCP test requirements, according to roads authority specification,\nf) The preparation and cleaning of the re-instatement area and the removal of spoil from site, \ng) The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing road levels. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) If the local authority executes the re-instatements on behalf of the Service Provider, then the Service Provider remains liable for the payment to the local authority, \nb) The Service Provider must familiarize himself with the re-instatement specifications of the various authorities, \nc) Quantities will be calculated against the applicable proposed trenching dimensions.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M2)','M2',470.08,'REINST,BRICK:CI1.59,INTRLCK RD','REINSTATE, BRICK:ITEM NUMBER CI1.59, TYPE INTRLCK RD:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PREPARATION OF BEDDING MATERIAL,\nALL THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, LAYING AND\nCOMPACTING OF THE INTER-LOCKING BRICKS, REPLACEMENT OF ANY DAMAGED MATERIAL / BRICKS, THE DCP TEST REQUIREMENTS, ACCORDING TO ROADS\nAUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE RE-INSTATEMENT AREA AND THE REMOVAL OF SPOIL FROM SITE, THE FINISHING\nOF LEVELS TO BE AESTHETICALLY TRUE TO THE SURROUNDING EXISTING ROAD LEVELS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE\n(SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: IF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY EXECUTES THE RE-INSTATEMENTS ON BEHALF OF THE SERVICE PROVIDER, THEN THE\nSERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS LIABLE FOR THE PAYMENT TO THE LOCAL AUTHORITY, THE SERVICE PROVIDER MUST FAMILIARIZE HIMSELF WITH THE\nRE-INSTATEMENT SPECIFICATIONS OF THE VARIOUS AUTHORITIES, QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED AGAINST THE APPLICABLE PROPOSED TRENCHING\nDIMENSIONS. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SQUARE METRE (M2)'),(3046014,'CI2.33','CI2.33 INSTL 4 DRWR SHLF','This item consists of the Installation of a 4-drawer shelf.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Labour for the installation of a 4-drawer shelf,\nb) Labelling,\nc) Minor build material.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\nb) The cost of the shelf (Telkom to supply)\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per 4 drawer shelf, each (EA).','EA',367.74,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.33,4 DRWR SHLF','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.33, TYPE 4 DRWR SHLF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION OF A\n4-DRAWER SHELF, LABELLING, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE COST OF\nTHE SHELF (TELKOM TO SUPPLY) THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 4 DRAWER SHELF, EACH (EA)'),(3046015,'CI2.31','CI2.31 INSTL 2 DRWR SHLF','This item consists of the Installation of a 2-drawer shelf into a cabinet (i.e 600mm x 300mm x 2200mm, 600mm x 600mm x 2200mm)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Labour for the installation of the 2-drawer shelf,\nb) Labelling,\nc) Minor build material.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items),\nb) The cost of the shelf.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per 2 drawer shelf, each (EA).','EA',242.03,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.31,2 DRWR SHLF','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.31, TYPE 2 DRWR SHLF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE\n2-DRAWER SHELF, LABELLING, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS), THE COST OF\nTHE SHELF. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER 2 DRAWER SHELF, EACH (EA).'),(3046016,'CI2.16','CI2.16 INSTLN CONVNTL FBR CABL FLOAT','This item consists of the installation of conventional fibre cable by floating method. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Installation of all sizes of conventional fibre cable in ducting / micro ducts by utilizing of a Cable Jet / Blow-in machine,  \nb) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. lubricant).  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) The quantity for payment will be measured from the centre of a UB lid to the centre of the other UB lid or from point to point of the actual duct length (where the is no UB), irrespective of any slack required. \n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) SPΓÇôAL0001 CTO-004655,\nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per meter (MT) (point to point).','MT',9.19,'INSTL,CBL:CI2.16,CONVNTL FBR FLOAT','INSTALL, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.16, TYPE CONVNTL FBR FLOAT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: INSTALLATION OF ALL SIZES OF\nCONVENTIONAL FIBRE CABLE IN DUCTING / MICRO DUCTS BY UTILIZING OF A CABLE JET / BLOW-IN MACHINE, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL\n(I.E. LUBRICANT). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THE QUANTITY FOR PAYMENT\nWILL BE MEASURED FROM THE CENTRE OF A UB LID TO THE CENTRE OF THE OTHER UB LID OR FROM POINT TO POINT OF THE ACTUAL DUCT LENGTH\n(WHERE THE IS NO UB), IRRESPECTIVE OF ANY SLACK REQUIRED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: SP#AL0001 CTO-004655, PR-AL0040\nCTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METER (MT) (POINT TO POINT)'),(3046017,'CI1.8','CI1.8 SPCLZD XNG BORE RCK 1 PIPE','This item consists of the specialized crossings (not trenches). excavating pits and setting up boring equipment. bore to accommodate and install one 110mm outside diameter rigid PVC pipe in rock conditions.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The setting up of boring equipment, excavation on both sides, boring, supply and installation of a 110MM continuous class 10 HDPE pipe,\nb) Tunnelling under kerbstones, supporting of services, backfilling and removal of soil,\nc) The cost for damages incurred by the Service Provider and the repair of roads or existing services,\nd) The cost of clearing the surface, removing boulders with a size of up to 0.015 cubic metres (If the boulders are bigger than 0.015 cubic metres in size, a separate rate must be negotiated.), grubbing of tree stumps,\ne) Backfilling of cavities, demolishing structures and removal thereof,\nf) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling),\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',2408.16,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.8,RCK 1 PIPE','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.8, TYPE RCK 1 PIPE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SETTING UP OF BORING EQUIPMENT,\nEXCAVATION ON BOTH SIDES, BORING, SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF A 110MM CONTINUOUS CLASS 10 HDPE PIPE, TUNNELLING UNDER KERBSTONES,\nSUPPORTING OF SERVICES, BACKFILLING AND REMOVAL OF SOIL, THE COST FOR DAMAGES INCURRED BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER AND THE REPAIR OF\nROADS OR EXISTING SERVICES, THE COST OF CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING BOULDERS WITH A SIZE OF UP TO 0.015 CUBIC METRES (IF THE\nBOULDERS ARE BIGGER THAN 0.015 CUBIC METRES IN SIZE, A SEPARATE RATE MUST BE NEGOTIATED.), GRUBBING OF TREE STUMPS, BACKFILLING OF\nCAVITIES, DEMOLISHING STRUCTURES AND REMOVAL THEREOF, PIPE ENTRIES (EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING), THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS\nTO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER METRE (MT)'),(3046018,'CI1.33','CI1.33 CONSTR ACESBL PJB','This item consists of the construction of an accessible pipe junction box. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The necessary excavations up to existing pipe level or new trench level, backfilling, compaction and D.C.P testing, \nb) The supply of all building materials required to build the PJB with an internal size of 600mm x 600mm to ground level (ten to twelve layers of bricks) (baked bricks only) in single wall configuration) and have a steel reinforced concrete base, \nc) The setting of a frame and cover in a 20MPA concrete coping, \nd) All pipe entries.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the frame and cover (to be supplied by Telkom), \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per accessible PJB each (EA).','EA',5256.75,'ERCT,BLDG:CI1.33 CONSTR ACESBL PJB','ERECT, BUILDING:NAME CI1.33 CONSTR ACESBL PJB:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE NECESSARY EXCAVATIONS UP TO EXISTING\nPIPE LEVEL OR NEW TRENCH LEVEL, BACKFILLING, COMPACTION AND D.C.P TESTING, THE SUPPLY OF ALL BUILDING MATERIALS REQUIRED TO BUILD\nTHE PJB WITH AN INTERNAL SIZE OF 600MM X 600MM TO GROUND LEVEL (TEN TO TWELVE LAYERS OF BRICKS) (BAKED BRICKS ONLY) IN SINGLE WALL\nCONFIGURATION) AND HAVE A STEEL REINFORCED CONCRETE BASE, THE SETTING OF A FRAME AND COVER IN A 20MPA CONCRETE COPING, ALL PIPE\nENTRIES. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE FRAME AND COVER (TO BE SUPPLIED BY TELKOM), ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ACCESSIBLE PJB\nEACH (EA)'),(3046019,'CI1.64','CI1.64 CLEANG MNHL/AJB >0.5M3','This item consists of the cleaning of a manhole / Accessible Junction Box AJB filled with sand / rubble / termite nests greater than half a cubic metre.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The open and close of manhole / AJB, \nb) The cleaning of pipe entries, \nc) Removal of all sand / rubble / termite nests. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit for this item is per cubic metre (m┬│).','M3',172.00,'CLEAN,EQUIP:CI1.64 MNHL/AJB >0.5M3','CLEAN, EQUIPMENT:TYPE CI1.64 MNHL/AJB >0.5M3:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE OPEN AND CLOSE OF MANHOLE / AJB, THE\nCLEANING OF PIPE ENTRIES, REMOVAL OF ALL SAND / RUBBLE / TERMITE NESTS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3046021,'CI2.12','CI2.12 LAYG DUCT/CABL IN OPN TRNCH','This item consists of the laying of all ducts and / or cables in an open trench (Excavated by a 3rd party).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The setting up of the drum and handling of the cable / pipes / Ducts. (unrolling),  \nb) Placing the cables / pipe / duct in the open trench, . \nc) Placing the bedding and padding in the open trench, .\nd) Any engineering difficulties such as service crossings, driveway and road crossings. (closed with a steel plate),  \ne) Safe guarding the pipe,  \nf) Supply and Installation of all couplings and end caps in all pull-through manholes, JP\'s, open trenches, etc., and the like. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote: \na) This item may only be claimed where the trench / excavation was performed by a 3rd party.\n\nThe specification for these items is: \na) PR-AL0027. CTO-000779.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',4.39,'LAY,CBL:CI2.12 LAYG,DCT IN OPN TRNCH','LAY, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI2.12 LAYG, TYPE DUCT IN OPN TRNCH:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SETTING UP OF THE DRUM AND\nHANDLING OF THE CABLE / PIPES / DUCTS. (UNROLLING), PLACING THE CABLES / PIPE / DUCT IN THE OPEN TRENCH, PLACING THE BEDDING AND\nPADDING IN THE OPEN TRENCH, ANY ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS SERVICE CROSSINGS, DRIVEWAY AND ROAD CROSSINGS. (CLOSED WITH A\nSTEEL PLATE), SAFE GUARDING THE PIPE, SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF ALL COUPLINGS AND END CAPS IN ALL PULL-THROUGH MANHOLES, JP\'S,\nOPEN TRENCHES, ETC., AND THE LIKE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM\nMAY ONLY BE CLAIMED WHERE THE TRENCH / EXCAVATION WAS PERFORMED BY A 3RD PARTY. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THESE ITEMS IS: PR-AL0027.\nCTO-000779. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT)'),(3046022,'CI2.20','CI2.20 SEALG SDC FLR','This item consists of sealing of SDC floors.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The preparation of the floor and the sealing with approved re-enterable resin / Bitumen,\nb) All equipment and material required to complete the task. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is \na) 325. CTO-004654, \nb) PR-AL0040 CTO-010225.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',118.33,'SEAL,FLR:CI2.20,SDC','SEAL, FLOOR:ITEM NUMBER CI2.20, TYPE STREET DISTRIBUTION CABINET:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PREPARATION OF THE\nFLOOR AND THE SEALING WITH APPROVED RE-ENTERABLE RESIN / BITUMEN, ALL EQUIPMENT AND MATERIAL REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THE TASK. THE\nRATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS 325. CTO-004654,\nPR-AL0040 CTO-010225. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3046024,'CI3.26','CI3.26 RECVR STAY','This item consists of the recovery of all sizes and types of stays. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The recoveries of stay guards stay wire, overhead stays and the excavation of the complete stay,\nb) The backfilling and ramming of holes to existing ground level, \nc) The transporting of the recovered material from the site to the destination as specified.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per stay, each (EA).','EA',108.17,'RCVR,STAY:CI3.26','RECOVER, STAY:ITEM NUMBER CI3.26:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE RECOVERIES OF STAY GUARDS STAY WIRE, OVERHEAD STAYS\nAND THE EXCAVATION OF THE COMPLETE STAY, THE BACKFILLING AND RAMMING OF HOLES TO EXISTING GROUND LEVEL, THE TRANSPORTING OF THE\nRECOVERED MATERIAL FROM THE SITE TO THE DESTINATION AS SPECIFIED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE\nFEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003.\nCTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER STAY, EACH (EA)'),(3046025,'CI4.40','CI4.40 TST OPTIC 1KM-10KM TRMNTD','This item consists of an Optic Fibre test for overhead and underground optic fibre cables, which are terminated on both ends and are from 1km to 10 km in total length.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Performing the following tests according to specification end to end irrespective of the number of splices/patch tails there are in between:\no OTDR (i.e. Attenuation, Return Loss, Splice Loss, Connector loss)\no OLTS (IL & ORL)\nb) Submitting a soft copy (DVD/CD) of the test results for each fibre tested to Telkom (C.R./SPOC) and upon request also providing a printout copy of the test results. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-007539,\nc) CTO-006426. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre, end to end each (EA)','EA',123.63,'TST,CBL:CI4.40,OPTIC FBR TRMNTD,1-10KM','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.40, TYPE OPTIC FIBER TRMNTD, DISTANCE 1-10 KM:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PERFORMING THE\nFOLLOWING TESTS ACCORDING TO SPECIFICATION END TO END IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SPLICES/PATCH TAILS THERE ARE IN BETWEEN: OTDR\n(I.E. ATTENUATION, RETURN LOSS, SPLICE LOSS, CONNECTOR LOSS) OLTS (IL & ORL) SUBMITTING A SOFT COPY (DVD/CD) OF THE TEST RESULTS\nFOR EACH FIBRE TESTED TO TELKOM (C.R./SPOC) AND UPON REQUEST ALSO PROVIDING A PRINTOUT COPY OF THE TEST RESULTS. THE RATE EXCLUDES:\nALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000043, CTO-007539, CTO-006426. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIBRE, END TO END EACH (EA'),(3046026,'CI4.33','CI4.33 CTS TST FBR SNGL','This item consists of the conformance testing to specification of a fibre for 2.5 G compliance.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The testing of the fibre from ODF/OMDF to fibre termination point i.e. customer termination, Telkom node to ascertain the optical power loss for the cable distance under test, \nb) The testing of the fibre to ascertain the optical return loss - ORL to be > than 30 dBΓÇÖs. (Point to point), \nc) The provisioning of test data in a 2.5 G Optic Summary test report. Template to be provided by Telkom SA, \nd) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services/equipment to complete the required conformance testing of the fibre to specification.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs. (See Service fee items). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-008417. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre, (EA).','EA',67.10,'TST,CBL:CI4.33,FBR SNGL','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.33, TYPE FBR SNGL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE TESTING OF THE FIBRE FROM ODF/OMDF TO\nFIBRE TERMINATION POINT I.E. CUSTOMER TERMINATION, TELKOM NODE TO ASCERTAIN THE OPTICAL POWER LOSS FOR THE CABLE DISTANCE UNDER\nTEST, THE TESTING OF THE FIBRE TO ASCERTAIN THE OPTICAL RETURN LOSS ORL TO BE > THAN 30 DB#S. (POINT TO POINT), THE PROVISIONING OF\nTEST DATA IN A 2.5 G OPTIC SUMMARY TEST REPORT. TEMPLATE TO BE PROVIDED BY TELKOM SA, THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS,\nTOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED SERVICES/EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED CONFORMANCE TESTING OF THE FIBRE TO\nSPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS:\nCTO-000043, CTO-008417. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIBRE, (EA)'),(3046027,'CI4.39','CI4.39 TST OPTIC <1KM NON TRMNTD','This item consists of an Optic Fibre test for overhead and underground optic fibre cables, which are not terminated on either end and are less than 1km in total length.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The preparation of the cable ends to specification and splice to a test block or pigtails.\nb) OLTS (Optical Loss Test Set) Test Only, end to end irrespective of the number of splices/patch tails there are in between,\nc) All materials to perform the test such as cleaning consumables and test block or pigtails.\nd) Sealing the cable ends upon completion,\ne) Submitting a soft copy (DVD/CD) of the test results for each fibre tested to Telkom (C.R./SPOC) and upon request also providing a printout copy of the test results. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\nNote:\na) This item may also be used for the testing of optic patch tails and optic Tie cables.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-007539,\nc) CTO-006426. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre, end to end each (EA)','EA',142.32,'TST,CBL:CI4.39,OPTIC FBR NON TRMNTD,1KM','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.39, TYPE OPTIC FIBER NON TRMNTD, DISTANCE 1 KM:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PREPARATION\nOF THE CABLE ENDS TO SPECIFICATION AND SPLICE TO A TEST BLOCK OR PIGTAILS. OLTS (OPTICAL LOSS TEST SET) TEST ONLY, END TO END\nIRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SPLICES/PATCH TAILS THERE ARE IN BETWEEN, ALL MATERIALS TO PERFORM THE TEST SUCH AS CLEANING\nCONSUMABLES AND TEST BLOCK OR PIGTAILS. SEALING THE CABLE ENDS UPON COMPLETION, SUBMITTING A SOFT COPY (DVD/CD) OF THE TEST RESULTS\nFOR EACH FIBRE TESTED TO TELKOM (C.R./SPOC) AND UPON REQUEST ALSO PROVIDING A PRINTOUT COPY OF THE TEST RESULTS. THE RATE EXCLUDES:\nALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ALSO BE USED FOR THE TESTING OF OPTIC PATCH TAILS AND OPTIC\nTIE CABLES. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000043, CTO-007539, CTO-006426. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIBRE,\nEND TO END EACH (EA)'),(3046032,'CI3.9','CI3.9 PLNT POLE/STRUT/STAY-HRD RCK','This item consists of the hard rock excavation for poles, stays and struts.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The drilling, blasting (as specified by the C.R.), breaking and removal of the excavated rock, boulders and spoil,\nb) All material / equipment used to excavate the rock,\nc) Supply of all minor material.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs to and from site (See Service Fees Document).\n\nNote:\na) This is an extra over item and may only be claimed in conjunction with any other pole / strut / stay planting item.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole / strut / stay (EA).','EA',669.04,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI3.9,PLE/STUT/STY-HRD RK','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI3.9, TYPE PLE/STUT/STY-HRD RK:THE DRILLING, BLASTING (AS SPECIFIED BY THE C.R.), BREAKING AND\nREMOVAL OF THE EXCAVATED ROCK, BOULDERS AND SPOIL, ALL MATERIAL / EQUIPMENT USED TO EXCAVATE THE ROCK, SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR\nMATERIAL. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEES DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS IS AN EXTRA OVER\nITEM AND MAY ONLY BE CLAIMED IN CONJUNCTION WITH ANY OTHER POLE / STRUT / STAY PLANTING ITEM. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS:\nSP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nPOLE / STRUT / STAY (EA)'),(3046033,'CI2.45','CI2.45 INSTL SPLICE RACK','This item consists of the installation of an Optic Main Distribution Frame (OMDF) Splice Rack.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.),\nb) Obtaining work refs.,\nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nd) All Labour costs, to install a Splic Rack\ne) Project management,\nf) Unpacking, Assembling and installing the Rack and associated components according to Telkom / Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications,\ng) Labelling,\nh) Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, etc.),\ni) The supply of all minor build materials. \n\nNote: this item may only be claimed where an existing OMDF is expanded.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs. \nb) The cost of the Splice Rack\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per Splice Rack, each (EA)','EA',370.00,'INSTL,RACK,ELECTR:CI2.45,SPLIC','INSTALL, RACK, ELECTRONIC:ITEM NUMBER CI2.45, TYPE SPLICE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT\nWITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED ALL LABOUR COSTS, TO INSTALL A SPLIC RACK PROJECT MANAGEMENT, UNPACKING,\nASSEMBLING AND INSTALLING THE RACK AND ASSOCIATED COMPONENTS ACCORDING TO TELKOM / OPENSERVE M&P#S WI#S, SPECIFICATIONS, LABELLING,\nCHECKING THE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E. CABLE CONNECTIONS, ETC.), THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIALS. NOTE: THIS ITEM\nMAY ONLY BE CLAIMED WHERE AN EXISTING OMDF IS EXPANDED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. THE COST OF THE SPLICE RACK\nTHE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SPLICE RACK, EACH (EA)'),(3046034,'CI4.22','CI4.22 SPLC FO','This item consists of the splicing of an optic fibre only. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The splicing (fusion / mechanical / connector) of the fibre to approved Telkom spec.,\nb) The preparation of tails to specification, splicing of the tail, coiling the slack, inserting it into the bracket and inserting the bracket into the drawer, \nc) The testing of each splice. The loss per splice may not exceed approved Telkom spec., \nd) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services / equipment to complete the required fibre optic splice to specification, \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The supply of optic enclosure, slack box / bracket, fibre optic mechanical splices / connectors and uni-strut support / flat brackets (Telkom to supply), \nb) The preparation of the various types and sizes of joints, which may be claimed for separately, \nc) The supply of the fibre patch tail, mid-alignment sleeve and FO splice protector tubing for terminations (Telkom to supply),\nd) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000778. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre, each (EA).','EA',56.76,'JOIN,CBL,FO:CI4.22,SPLICG','JOIN, CABLE, FIBER OPTIC:ITEM NUMBER CI4.22, TYPE SPLICING:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SPLICING (FUSION /\nMECHANICAL / CONNECTOR) OF THE FIBRE TO APPROVED TELKOM SPEC. THE PREPARATION OF TAILS TO SPECIFICATION, SPLICING OF THE TAIL,\nCOILING THE SLACK, INSERTING IT INTO THE BRACKET AND INSERTING THE BRACKET INTO THE DRAWER, THE TESTING OF EACH SPLICE. THE LOSS\nPER SPLICE MAY NOT EXCEED APPROVED TELKOM SPEC., THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED\nSERVICES / EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED FIBRE OPTIC SPLICE TO SPECIFICATION, THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE SUPPLY OF OPTIC\nENCLOSURE, SLACK BOX / BRACKET, FIBRE OPTIC MECHANICAL SPLICES / CONNECTORS AND UNI-STRUT SUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS (TELKOM TO\nSUPPLY), THE PREPARATION OF THE VARIOUS TYPES AND SIZES OF JOINTS, WHICH MAY BE CLAIMED FOR SEPARATELY,  THE SUPPLY OF THE FIBRE\nPATCH TAIL, MID-ALIGNMENT SLEEVE AND FO SPLICE PROTECTOR TUBING FOR TERMINATIONS (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE\nSERVICE FEES). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000778. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIBRE, EACH (EA)'),(3046037,'CI4.7','CI4.7 OPN & RESEAL EXSTG UG JNT','This item consists of opening and closing existing foam seal closure / heat shrink / plumb (lead) joints. (All sizes)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The opening and closing of the existing joint, \nb) The fitting of uni-strut supports / flat brackets to support the joint, \nc) The pressure testing, supporting, clamping, labelling and bonding of affected cable / joints, \nd) The supply of cable ties, pipe entry shoes and labels / label holders, \ne) The cleaning of the utility box and the immediate surrounding area, \nf) The control and pumping of water, \ng) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services / equipment to complete the required opening and resealing of existing UG joint to specification.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The enclosures and uni-strut support / flat brackets. (Telkom to supply), \nb) Corrective jointing or when a cable cutover has to be done,\nc) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nNote: \na) This item may not be claimed in conjunction with a preparation item.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000778. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per joint, each (EA).','EA',497.04,'SEAL,JNT:CI4.7,OPN & RESEAL EXSTG UG','SEAL, JOINT:ITEM NUMBER CI4.7, TYPE OPEN & RESEAL EXISTING UG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE OPENING AND CLOSING OF\nTHE EXISTING JOINT, THE FITTING OF UNI-STRUT SUPPORTS / FLAT BRACKETS TO SUPPORT THE JOINT, THE PRESSURE TESTING, SUPPORTING,\nCLAMPING, LABELLING AND BONDING OF AFFECTED CABLE / JOINTS,  THE SUPPLY OF CABLE TIES, PIPE ENTRY SHOES AND LABELS / LABEL HOLDERS,\nTHE CLEANING OF THE UTILITY BOX AND THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, THE CONTROL AND PUMPING OF WATER, THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL\nMINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED SERVICES / EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED OPENING AND RESEALING OF\nEXISTING UG JOINT TO SPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE ENCLOSURES AND UNI-STRUT SUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS. (TELKOM TO SUPPLY),\nCORRECTIVE JOINTING OR WHEN A CABLE CUTOVER HAS TO BE DONE, TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY NOT BE\nCLAIMED IN CONJUNCTION WITH A PREPARATION ITEM. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000778. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER JOINT, EACH (EA)'),(3046038,'CI4.34','CI4.34 CTS TST FBR DUAL SIMPLX','This item consists of the simplex end to end conformance testing to specification of a fibre pair (transmit & receive) for 2.5 G compliance. (Single Node)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The testing of the fibre pair from OFTP to fibre termination point i.e. customer termination, OFTP at Telkom node to ascertain the optical power loss for the cable route under test. A loss margin between the two fibres of < 2 dBΓÇÖs is required, \nb) The testing of the fibre pair to ascertain the optical return loss ΓÇô ORL to be > than 30 dBΓÇÖs. (End to end), \nc) The installing of simplex/duplex patch cords at the end nodes, \nd) The labelling of simplex/duplex patch cords on the ODF/OMDF (End). The labelling of system information at OFTP (End), \ne) The provisioning of test data in a 2.5 G Optic Summary test report. Template to be provided by Telkom SA, \nf) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services/equipment to complete the required conformance testing of the fibre to specification.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs. (See Service fee items),\nb) The simplex/duplex patch cords. (supplied by Telkom).\n\nNote: \na) Service Provider to supply test tails/cords.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-008417. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre pair, (EA).','PR',1765.61,'TST,CBL:CI4.34,FBR DUAL SIMPLX','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.34, TYPE FBR DUAL SIMPLX:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE TESTING OF THE FIBRE PAIR FROM\nOFTP TO FIBRE TERMINATION POINT I.E. CUSTOMER TERMINATION, OFTP AT TELKOM NODE TO ASCERTAIN THE OPTICAL POWER LOSS FOR THE CABLE\nROUTE UNDER TEST. A LOSS MARGIN BETWEEN THE TWO FIBRES OF < 2 DB#S IS REQUIRED, THE TESTING OF THE FIBRE PAIR TO ASCERTAIN THE\nOPTICAL RETURN LOSS ORL TO BE > THAN 30 DB#S. (END TO END), THE INSTALLING OF SIMPLEX/DUPLEX PATCH CORDS AT THE END NODES, THE\nLABELLING OF SIMPLEX/DUPLEX PATCH CORDS ON THE ODF/OMDF (END). THE LABELLING OF SYSTEM INFORMATION AT OFTP (END), THE PROVISIONING\nOF TEST DATA IN A 2.5 G OPTIC SUMMARY TEST REPORT. TEMPLATE TO BE PROVIDED BY TELKOM SA, THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS,\nTOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED SERVICES/EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED CONFORMANCE TESTING OF THE FIBRE TO\nSPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS), THE SIMPLEX/DUPLEX PATCH CORDS. (SUPPLIED BY\nTELKOM). NOTE: SERVICE PROVIDER TO SUPPLY TEST TAILS/CORDS. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000043, CTO-008417. THE UNIT OF\nMEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIBRE PAIR, (EA).'),(3046039,'CI2.43','CI2.43 INSTL OMDF (COMPL)','This item consists of the installation of an Optic Main Distribution Frame (OMDF) Complete.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.),\nb) Obtaining work refs.,\nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nd) All Labour costs, to install;\na. OMDF Equipment rack\nb. OMDF Racks (2x)\nc. Splice Racks (2x A-Route & 2x B-Route)\ne) Project management,\nf) Unpacking, Assembling and installing the Cabinet / Racks and associated components according to Telkom / Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications,\ng) Labelling,\nh) Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, etc.),\ni) The supply of all minor build materials. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs. \nb) The cost of the OMDF Equipment / Racks\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per OMDF set, complete, each (EA)','EA',4500.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.43,OMDF (COMPL)','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.43, TYPE OMDF (COMPL):THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT\nWITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED ALL LABOUR COSTS, TO INSTALL; OMDF EQUIPMENT RACK OMDF RACKS (2X) SPLICE RACKS\n(2X A-ROUTE & 2X B-ROUTE) PROJECT MANAGEMENT, UNPACKING, ASSEMBLING AND INSTALLING THE CABINET / RACKS AND ASSOCIATED COMPONENTS\nACCORDING TO TELKOM / OPENSERVE M&P#S WI#S, SPECIFICATIONS, LABELLING, CHECKING THE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E. CABLE\nCONNECTIONS, ETC.), THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIALS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. THE COST OF THE OMDF\nEQUIPMENT / RACKS THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER OMDF SET, COMPLETE, EACH (EA)'),(3046040,'CI2.38','CI2.38 INSTL ODF (SML)Γëñ720FBR','This item consists of the installation of an Optical Distribution Frame (ODF), small (up to and including 720 fibres)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals.\n