n required. \n\nThe rate excludes: \na) All other fittings such as arms, brackets, straps, enclosures, etc. which will be paid for under item CI3.9.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',5.50,'ERCT,WRE:CI3.13,CU AERL/SPNSN','ERECT, WIRE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.13, TYPE CU AERL/SPNSN:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE ERECTING OF AERIAL CABLE ON\nEXISTING OR NEW TELKOM ROUTES OR ESKOM / POWER ROUTES AND MOUNTING OF ALL INCIDENTAL FITTINGS (I.E. #S# HOOKS, SUPPORT CLAMPS), THE\nREGULATING, BONDING AND TERMINATING, INCLUDING FALSE TERMINATIONS (NOT EXCEEDING 8 TO 14 DEGREES) (FITTING OF CROSBY CLAMPS /\nLINE-TAPS) OF THE SUSPENSION WIRE, THE HANDLING OF CABLE WHERE OVERHEAD CABLE IS TO BE INSTALLED INTO A CABLE DUCT AT ROAD, RAILWAY\nOR POWER CROSSINGS AND INTO THE PROTECTION PIPES ON BOTH SIDES OF THE CROSSING (LENGTH TO BE CLAIMED WILL BE FROM POLE TO POLE\nINCLUDING THE POLE LENGTH ON EITHER SIDE), SLACK MANAGEMENT AND THE CLEATING OF CABLE TO THE POLE, FASTENING AERIAL CABLE TO WALLS\nWHEN NECESSARY, THE 3M SLACK THAT MUST BE LEFT FOR TERMINATION. (PER POLE & CR APPROVAL), THE TESTING OF POLES WHEN WORKING ON ALL\nEXISTING POLES / ROUTES. THE SERVICE PROVIDER IS RESPONSIBLE TO ENSURE THAT ALL EXISTING POLES ARE SAFE TO BE WORKED ON, JOINT AND\nTERMINATE SHORT LENGTHS SUSPENSION WIRE ON EXISTING AERIAL CABLES, THE CUTTING OF OVERHANGING BRANCHES TO WITHIN 1M OF THE EXISTING\nROUTE, ERECT OVERHEAD STAY, FALSE TERMINATION OF THE SUSPENSION WIRE (CABLE NOT CUT NO JOINT) AT PLACES, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR\nMATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, ETC.), LABELLING OF THE CABLE WHEN REQUIRED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL OTHER FITTINGS\nSUCH AS ARMS, BRACKETS, STRAPS, ENCLOSURES, ETC. WHICH WILL BE PAID FOR UNDER ITEM CI3.9. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS:\nSP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nMETRE (MT)'),(3046056,'CI4.26','CI4.26 FO CABL LBLG','This item consists of the labelling of fibre optic cable in pull-through manholes/jointing pits/jointing box and any area it deemed necessary.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na) The preparation and cleaning of the cable to be labelled,\nb) The labelling of the identified cable to spec., \nc) The cleaning of the immediate surrounding area, \nd) Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site, \ne) All minor build material (i.e. consumables, Labels, etc.). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-011866.  \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable labeled, (EA).','EA',80.19,'MARK,EQUIP:CI4.26 FO CABL LBLG','MARK, EQUIPMENT:TYPE CI4.26 FO CABL LBLG:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE CABLE TO\nBE LABELLED, THE LABELLING OF THE IDENTIFIED CABLE TO SPEC. THE CLEANING OF THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL\nTOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE, ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CONSUMABLES, LABELS, ETC.). THE SPECIFICATION FOR\nTHIS ITEM IS: CTO-011866. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE LABELED, (EA)'),(3046057,'CI4.21','CI4.21 FIT INDOOR DP BOX','This item consists of the fitting of an indoor DP at a customerΓÇÖs building/premises. (All sizes & types). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The drilling of holes. The service provider must supply approved rawlbolts, \nb) The fitting of the indoor DP at the customerΓÇÖs building/premises, \nc) The numbering of the DP, according to Telkom spec., \nd) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services/equipment to complete the required fitting of the indoor DP to the customer premises to specification.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The indoor DP (Telkom to supply),\nb) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000778. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is DP, each (EA).','EA',143.21,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI4.21,INDOR DP BX','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI4.21, TYPE INDOOR DP BOX:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE DRILLING OF HOLES. THE\nSERVICE PROVIDER MUST SUPPLY APPROVED RAWLBOLTS, THE FITTING OF THE INDOOR DP AT THE CUSTOMER#S BUILDING/PREMISES, THE NUMBERING OF\nTHE DP, ACCORDING TO TELKOM SPEC, THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED\nSERVICES/EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED FITTING OF THE INDOOR DP TO THE CUSTOMER PREMISES TO SPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES:\nTHE INDOOR DP (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000778. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS DP, EACH (EA)'),(3046060,'CI3.2','CI3.2 GRAS CTNG','This item consists of grass cutting to enable surveying for new routes and to clear existing routes. (only routes where no cable or wire work is to be done). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Grass cutting 6m is measured as 3m both sides of the route at ground level,  \nb) The clearing around poles, struts and stays fitted with stay guards. (clearing to have a radius of 1m), \nc) The clearing of the surface, removing, transporting and disposing of material,  \nd) The re-instatement of fences when damaged. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per running metre (MT)','MT',5.27,'CLEAR,GRAS:CI3.2','CLEAR, GRASS:ITEM NUMBER CI3.2:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: GRASS CUTTING 6M IS MEASURED AS 3M BOTH SIDES OF THE ROUTE\nAT GROUND LEVEL, THE CLEARING AROUND POLES, STRUTS AND STAYS FITTED WITH STAY GUARDS. (CLEARING TO HAVE A RADIUS OF 1M), THE\nCLEARING OF THE SURFACE, REMOVING, TRANSPORTING AND DISPOSING OF MATERIAL, THE RE-INSTATEMENT OF FENCES WHEN DAMAGED. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753),\nWI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER RUNNING METRE (MT)'),(3046061,'CI3.11','CI3.11 INSTL POLE FTGS','This item consists of the installation / repositioning / replacement of all fittings required on a pole complete.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) All arms (i.e. 2, 4, & 8/12 wire arms, single or double, etc.), \nb) All brackets and straps (i.e. KA brackets, L bracket for guard circuit, bracing straps, transposition brackets, etc.),\nc) All attachments (i.e. ΓÇ£SΓÇ¥ hooks, combiners, \"U\" spindles, spindles, insulators, felt washers, bolts, poles steps, etc.), \nd) All boxes, enclosures, joints, housings, slack management, and the numbering and labelling thereof, etc.,  \ne) Refastening of galvanised pipe / cable to pole when required, \nf) Drilling of holes in arms and poles and creosote treatment if necessary. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs to and from site (See Service Fees Document).\n\nNote:\na) This item may also be claimed where only refastening / re-hooking of loose hanging cable is required. \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole, each (EA).','EA',52.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.11,POLE FTGS','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI3.11, TYPE POLE FTGS:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ALL ARMS (I.E. 2, 4, & 8/12 WIRE\nARMS, SINGLE OR DOUBLE, ETC.), ALL BRACKETS AND STRAPS (I.E. KA BRACKETS, L BRACKET FOR GUARD CIRCUIT, BRACING STRAPS,\nTRANSPOSITION BRACKETS, ETC.), ALL ATTACHMENTS (I.E. S HOOKS, COMBINERS, U SPINDLES, SPINDLES, INSULATORS, FELT WASHERS, BOLTS,\nPOLES STEPS, ETC.), ALL BOXES, ENCLOSURES, JOINTS, HOUSINGS, SLACK MANAGEMENT, AND THE NUMBERING AND LABELLING THEREOF, ETC.,\nREFASTENING OF GALVANISED PIPE / CABLE TO POLE WHEN REQUIRED, DRILLING OF HOLES IN ARMS AND POLES AND CREOSOTE TREATMENT IF\nNECESSARY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEES DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ALSO BE\nCLAIMED WHERE ONLY REFASTENING / RE-HOOKING OF LOOSE HANGING CABLE IS REQUIRED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001\n(CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER POLE,\nEACH (EA)'),(3046062,'CI4.8','CI4.8 OPN & RESEAL EXSTG JNT','This item consists of the opening and closing of existing dome / pillar joints. (All sizes). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The opening and closing of the existing joint, \nb) The pressure testing, supporting, clamping, labelling and bonding of affected cable / joints, \nc) The supply of cable ties, pipe entry shoes and labels / label holders, \nd) The cleaning of the utility box and the immediate surrounding area, \ne) The control and pumping of water, \nf) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services / equipment to complete the required dome / pillar joint to specification.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Corrective jointing or when a cable cutover must be done,\nb) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nNote: \na) This item may not be claimed in conjunction with a preparation item.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000778. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per joint, each (EA).','EA',56.00,'SEAL,JNT:CI4.8,OPN & RESEAL EXSTG','SEAL, JOINT:ITEM NUMBER CI4.8, TYPE OPN & RESEAL EXSTG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE OPENING AND CLOSING OF THE\nEXISTING JOINT, THE PRESSURE TESTING, SUPPORTING, CLAMPING, LABELLING AND BONDING OF AFFECTED CABLE / JOINTS, THE SUPPLY OF CABLE\nTIES, PIPE ENTRY SHOES AND LABELS / LABEL HOLDERS, THE CLEANING OF THE UTILITY BOX AND THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, THE CONTROL\nAND PUMPING OF WATER, THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED SERVICES / EQUIPMENT TO\nCOMPLETE THE REQUIRED DOME / PILLAR JOINT TO SPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: CORRECTIVE JOINTING OR WHEN A CABLE CUTOVER MUST BE\nDONE, TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). NOTE:  THIS ITEM MAY NOT BE CLAIMED IN CONJUNCTION WITH A PREPARATION ITEM. THE\nSPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000778. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER JOINT, EACH (EA)'),(3046063,'CI3.21','CI3.21 REPOSN AERL & FO CABL','This item consists of the repositioning of all sizes aerial and optic fibre cables.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The removing and re-fitting of the suspension hooks, two bolt cable clamps and fitting the cable in the clamp, \nb) Re-terminating of the existing cable with 3 bolt clamp or preformed make-offs,\nc) The re-tensioning of the cable, \nd) The drilling of holes through poles or arms where required, \ne) Treating drilled holes with creosote. (The Service Provider to supply creosote). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cable per pole, each (EA).','EA',15.85,'REPOS,CBL:CI3.21,AERL & FO','REPOSITION, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.21, TYPE AERL & FO:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE REMOVING AND RE-FITTING OF THE\nSUSPENSION HOOKS, TWO BOLT CABLE CLAMPS AND FITTING THE CABLE IN THE CLAMP, RE-TERMINATING OF THE EXISTING CABLE WITH 3 BOLT CLAMP\nOR PREFORMED MAKE-OFFS, THE RE-TENSIONING OF THE CABLE, THE DRILLING OF HOLES THROUGH POLES OR ARMS WHERE REQUIRED, TREATING\nDRILLED HOLES WITH CREOSOTE. (THE SERVICE PROVIDER TO SUPPLY CREOSOTE). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944),\nPR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABLE PER POLE, EACH (EA)'),(3046064,'CI4.5','CI4.5 MAKE BLCK JNT 10-600 PR','This item consists of making a block joint 10pr- 600pr on air core cables, using approved blocking methods only.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The opening and preparation of the cable to spec, bonding the cables, fitting a closure and injecting the resin into the joint, \nb) The fitting of uni-strut supports / flat brackets to support the joint, \nc) The pressure testing, supporting and clamping of affected cables / joints, \nd) The cleaning of the utility box and the immediate surrounding area, \ne) The control and pumping of water, \nf) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services / equipment to complete the required block joint to specification.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The blocking enclosure, blocking resin and uni-strut support / flat brackets. (Telkom to supply),\nb) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000778. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per block joint, each (EA).','EA',451.56,'MAKE,JNT:CI4.5,BLCK 10-600PR','MAKE, JOINT:ITEM NUMBER CI4.5, TYPE BLOCK 10-600PR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE OPENING AND PREPARATION OF THE\nCABLE TO SPEC, BONDING THE CABLES, FITTING A CLOSURE AND INJECTING THE RESIN INTO THE JOINT, THE FITTING OF UNI-STRUT SUPPORTS /\nFLAT BRACKETS TO SUPPORT THE JOINT, THE PRESSURE TESTING, SUPPORTING AND CLAMPING OF AFFECTED CABLES / JOINTS, THE CLEANING OF THE\nUTILITY BOX AND THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, THE CONTROL AND PUMPING OF WATER, THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS,\nMECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED SERVICES / EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED BLOCK JOINT TO SPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE\nBLOCKING ENCLOSURE, BLOCKING RESIN AND UNI-STRUT SUPPORT / FLAT BRACKETS. (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE\nFEES). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000778. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER BLOCK JOINT, EACH (EA)'),(3046067,'CI4.25','CI4.25 MNHL MRKG','This item consists of the marking of a manhole, containing underground network.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The preparation and cleaning of the manhole coping and wall for marking, \nb) The supply of road marking paint and the marking of the manhole coping and wall to specification, \nc) The cleaning of the immediate surrounding area, \nd) Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site, \ne) All minor build material (i.e. consumables, Labels, etc.). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-011866.  \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per manhole, each (EA).','EA',66.43,'LBL,MNHL:CI4.25,MRKG','LABEL, MANHOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.25, TYPE MARKING:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE\nMANHOLE COPING AND WALL FOR MARKING, THE SUPPLY OF ROAD MARKING PAINT AND THE MARKING OF THE MANHOLE COPING AND WALL TO\nSPECIFICATION, THE CLEANING OF THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM\nSITE, ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CONSUMABLES, LABELS, ETC.). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-011866. THE UNIT OF\nMEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER MANHOLE, EACH (EA)'),(3046069,'CI4.27','CI4.27 INSTL JNT FO Nano-Tube','This item consists of the Installation of a new Nano-tube fibre joint box (2/6/12 fibre).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The fitting and securing of the joint / Splice box in the manhole / jointing pit / boundary box / wall / etc., \nb) The preparation and cleaning of the Nano-tube fibre cable to spec.,  \nc) The presenting, identifying and coiling of the required fibre/s in the splice organizer / Splice box, \nd) The coiling and inserting of the slack into the split flex protection pipe and slack box / organiser / brackets (ie X,Y,E etc), \ne) The marking / labelling of the cable, joints, fibres and slack box / organiser / brackets (ie X,Y,E etc), \nf) The pumping and control of water, \ng) The cleaning of the manhole / jointing pit / boundary box and the immediate surrounding area, \nh) Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site, \ni) All minor build material (i.e. consumables, Labels, etc.). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All Travel related costs (See Service Fees), \nb) The splicing of the optic fibre, which may be claimed for separately.\n\nNote: \na) This item may also be claimed for installing just a loop through break-out box, \nb) This item may not be claimed in conjunction with the prep joint item.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000786, \nb) CTO-0011156,\nc) CTO-011866. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per joint box, (EA).','EA',467.88,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI4.27,JNT FO NANO-TUBE','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI4.27, TYPE JNT FO NANO-TUBE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE FITTING AND SECURING OF\nTHE JOINT / SPLICE BOX IN THE MANHOLE / JOINTING PIT / BOUNDARY BOX / WALL / ETC., THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE NANO-TUBE\nFIBRE CABLE TO SPEC., THE PRESENTING, IDENTIFYING AND COILING OF THE REQUIRED FIBRE/S IN THE SPLICE ORGANIZER / SPLICE BOX, THE\nCOILING AND INSERTING OF THE SLACK INTO THE SPLIT FLEX PROTECTION PIPE AND SLACK BOX / ORGANISER / BRACKETS (IE X,Y,E ETC), THE\nMARKING / LABELLING OF THE CABLE, JOINTS, FIBRES AND SLACK BOX / ORGANISER / BRACKETS (IE X,Y,E ETC), THE PUMPING AND CONTROL OF\nWATER, THE CLEANING OF THE MANHOLE / JOINTING PIT / BOUNDARY BOX AND THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS,\nMATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE, ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CONSUMABLES, LABELS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nRELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEES), THE SPLICING OF THE OPTIC FIBRE, WHICH MAY BE CLAIMED FOR SEPARATELY.  NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ALSO\nBE CLAIMED FOR INSTALLING JUST A LOOP THROUGH BREAK-OUT BOX, THIS ITEM MAY NOT BE CLAIMED IN CONJUNCTION WITH THE PREP JOINT ITEM.\nTHE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000786, CTO-0011156, CTO-011866. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER JOINT BOX, (EA).'),(3046070,'CI4.28','CI4.28 REPR FO NETW','This item consists of the complete fault localisation and repair / restoration of existing Fibre Optic cable from the OMDF to the NDP.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Making and / or confirming appointment for access to infrastructure, \nb) Dispatching resources and all Logistical activities, \nc) The complete fault localisation (testing with testing equipment) of the reported fibre infrastructure (OMDF to DP / OMDF to OMDF / etc.), \nd) The replacement or repair of fibre cabling where necessary through the IE195/TBI process, \ne) All dispatching and fault locating tools and test equipment (i.e. Laptop, Smartphone, multi-meters, test sets, OTDR, etc.), \nf) All Travel related costs, \ng) Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site, \nh) Interface / administration management functions when required, such as:\na. Tasking an activity to another section in Telkom\nb. Arranging and obtaining all access and/or references\nc. Quality and Safety activities / inspections\nd. Site management\ni) All minor build material (i.e. consumables, Labels, etc.). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of major materials / equipment such as aerial cable, underground cable, pipes, poles, joint closures, etc.\n\nNotes: \na) This item may only be claimed when the reported faulty cable has been permanently repaired / restored and cleared, \nb) If the fault is handed back to Telkom or another party for further attention / repairs the Service Provider remains responsible until tested and cleared, \nc) This also applies where permanent repairs cannot be undertaken immediately and temporary service is provided. The item may only be claimed once the permanent repairs have been completed, \nd) This item may only be claimed once, irrespective of the number of customers affected, \ne) This item may be claimed in conjunction with any other CI BOQ items (i.e. remake of joint / hauling of cable / etc.). \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per Fibre Cable repaired, each (EA)','EA',621.45,'REPR HRDWR:CI4.28 FO NETW','REPAIR, HARDWARE:TYPE CI4.28 FO NETW:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MAKING AND / OR CONFIRMING APPOINTMENT FOR ACCESS TO\nINFRASTRUCTURE, DISPATCHING RESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL ACTIVITIES, THE COMPLETE FAULT LOCALISATION (TESTING WITH TESTING\nEQUIPMENT) OF THE REPORTED FIBRE INFRASTRUCTURE (OMDF TO DP / OMDF TO OMDF / ETC.), THE REPLACEMENT OR REPAIR OF FIBRE CABLING\nWHERE NECESSARY THROUGH THE IE195/TBI PROCESS, ALL DISPATCHING AND FAULT LOCATING TOOLS AND TEST EQUIPMENT (I.E. LAPTOP,\nSMARTPHONE, MULTI-METERS, TEST SETS, OTDR, ETC.), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT\nTO AND FROM SITE, INTERFACE / ADMINISTRATION MANAGEMENT FUNCTIONS WHEN REQUIRED, SUCH AS: TASKING AN ACTIVITY TO ANOTHER SECTION IN\nTELKOM ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL ACCESS AND/OR REFERENCES QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS SITE MANAGEMENT ALL MINOR\nBUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CONSUMABLES, LABELS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF MAJOR MATERIALS / EQUIPMENT SUCH AS AERIAL CABLE,\nUNDERGROUND CABLE, PIPES, POLES, JOINT CLOSURES, ETC. NOTES: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE CLAIMED WHEN THE REPORTED FAULTY CABLE HAS BEEN\nPERMANENTLY REPAIRED / RESTORED AND CLEARED, IF THE FAULT IS HANDED BACK TO TELKOM OR ANOTHER PARTY FOR FURTHER ATTENTION / REPAIRS\nTHE SERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS RESPONSIBLE UNTIL TESTED AND CLEARED, THIS ALSO APPLIES WHERE PERMANENT REPAIRS CANNOT BE UNDERTAKEN\nIMMEDIATELY AND TEMPORARY SERVICE IS PROVIDED. THE ITEM MAY ONLY BE CLAIMED ONCE THE PERMANENT REPAIRS HAVE BEEN COMPLETED, THIS\nITEM MAY ONLY BE CLAIMED ONCE, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF CUSTOMERS AFFECTED, THIS ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED IN CONJUNCTION WITH ANY\nOTHER CI BOQ ITEMS (I.E. REMAKE OF JOINT / HAULING OF CABLE / ETC.).   THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIBRE CABLE\nREPAIRED, EACH (EA)'),(3046071,'CI3.28','CI3.28 DISMNTL & RECVR POLE FTG','This item consists of the dismantling and recovery of all fittings on a pole complete.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) All arms (i.e. 2, 4, & 8/12 wire arms, single or double, etc.), \nb) All brackets and straps (i.e. KA brackets, L bracket for guard circuit, bracing straps, transposition brackets, etc.),\nc) All attachments (i.e. s-hooks, combiners, \"U\" spindles, spindles, insulators, felt washers, bolts, poles steps, etc.), \nd) All boxes, enclosures, joints, housings, slack management, and the numbering and labelling thereof, etc.,  \ne) The bagging, tagging and returning of serviceable arms, bolts, spindles and insulators to the destination as specified,\nf) The disposing of unserviceable arms, bolts, spindles and insulators. (Document no ITSD - 43967).\n \nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs to and from site (See Service Fees Document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole each (EA).','EA',94.79,'DISASML,EQUIP:CI3.28 POLE FTG,RECVR','DISASSEMBLE, EQUIPMENT:TYPE CI3.28 POLE FTG, ADDITIONAL TASK RECVR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ALL ARMS (I.E. 2, 4, &\n8/12 WIRE ARMS, SINGLE OR DOUBLE, ETC.), ALL BRACKETS AND STRAPS (I.E. KA BRACKETS, L BRACKET FOR GUARD CIRCUIT, BRACING STRAPS,\nTRANSPOSITION BRACKETS, ETC.), ALL ATTACHMENTS (I.E. S-HOOKS, COMBINERS, U SPINDLES, SPINDLES, INSULATORS, FELT WASHERS, BOLTS,\nPOLES STEPS, ETC.), ALL BOXES, ENCLOSURES, JOINTS, HOUSINGS, SLACK MANAGEMENT, AND THE NUMBERING AND LABELLING THEREOF, ETC. THE\nBAGGING, TAGGING AND RETURNING OF SERVICEABLE ARMS, BOLTS, SPINDLES AND INSULATORS TO THE DESTINATION AS SPECIFIED, THE DISPOSING\nOF UNSERVICEABLE ARMS, BOLTS, SPINDLES AND INSULATORS. (DOCUMENT NO ITSD 43967). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND\nFROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEES DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001\n(CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER POLE EACH (EA)'),(3046073,'CI3.25','CI3.25 RECVR STL/CONCRT POLE','This item consists of the recovery of all sizes steel and / or concrete poles. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The excavation and the removal of the complete pole and strut (inclusive of concrete around base of pole),\nb) Hoisting and recovering of poles and struts by means of a mechanical aid,\nc) The stripping of the pole - completely of staples, cable, make-offs etc., \nd) The backfilling and compaction of holes to existing ground levels, \ne) The transporting of the recovered material from the site to the destination as specified.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole, each (EA).','EA',401.63,'RCVR,POLE:CI3.25','RECOVER, POLE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.25:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE EXCAVATION AND THE REMOVAL OF THE COMPLETE POLE AND\nSTRUT (INCLUSIVE OF CONCRETE AROUND BASE OF POLE), HOISTING AND RECOVERING OF POLES AND STRUTS BY MEANS OF A MECHANICAL AID, THE\nSTRIPPING OF THE POLE COMPLETELY OF STAPLES, CABLE, MAKE-OFFS ETC., THE BACKFILLING AND COMPACTION OF HOLES TO EXISTING GROUND\nLEVELS, THE TRANSPORTING OF THE RECOVERED MATERIAL FROM THE SITE TO THE DESTINATION AS SPECIFIED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nCOSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005\n(CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER POLE, EACH (EA)'),(3046074,'CI2.46','CI2.46 INSTL OMDF BLCK','This item consists of the installation of an Optic Main Distribution Frame (OMDF) block.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.),\nb) Obtaining work refs.,\nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required,\nd) All Labour costs,\ne) Project management,\nf) Installing the Block according to Telkom / Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications,\ng) Labelling,\nh) Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, etc.),\ni) The supply of all minor build materials. \na) Submission of documentation, such as:\na. Quality acceptance certificate,\nb. Quality tick sheet,\nc. IE6 document,\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\nb) Cost of the OMDF Block.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per block, each (EA)','EA',370.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.46,OMDF BLCK','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.46, TYPE OMDF BLCK:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT\nWITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, ALL LABOUR COSTS, PROJECT MANAGEMENT, INSTALLING THE BLOCK ACCORDING TO TELKOM /\nOPENSERVE M&P#S WI#S, SPECIFICATIONS, LABELLING, CHECKING THE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E. CABLE CONNECTIONS, ETC.), THE\nSUPPLY OF ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIALS. SUBMISSION OF DOCUMENTATION, SUCH AS: QUALITY ACCEPTANCE CERTIFICATE, QUALITY TICK SHEET, IE6\nDOCUMENT, THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). COST OF THE OMDF BLOCK. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS\nITEM IS PER BLOCK, EACH (EA)'),(3046075,'CI4.23','CI4.23 PREP JNT FO ALL','This item consists of the preparation only, of all fibre cables (i.e. underground, overhead, rodent proof, conventional, micro-fibre etc.) for  new, loop through, straight, forked, cut in joints, etc.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The fitting and securing of the joint, split flex protection pipe and slack box / organiser / brackets (ie X,Y,E etc) in the manhole / jointing pit, \nb) The preparation and cleaning of the cable to spec, \nc) The presenting, identifying and coiling of the required fibre/s in the splice organizer, \nd) The coiling and inserting of the slack into the split flex protection pipe and slack box / organiser / brackets (ie X,Y,E etc), \ne) The labelling of the cable, joints, fibres, pole and slack box / organiser, \nf) The inserting of the cable into the protection pipe and UV resistant sprague on pole, \ng) The marking/labelling of the cable, joints, fibres and slack box/ organiser / brackets (ie X,Y,E etc), \nh) The cleaning of the immediate surrounding area, \ni) Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site, \nj) All minor build material (i.e. consumables, Labels, etc.). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The supply of optic enclosure, slack box/organiser and fibre optic mechanical splices/connectors, (Telkom to supply), \nb) The splicing of the optic fibre, which may be claimed separately,\nc) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nNote:\na) In the case of straight or forked joints the quantity is determined by the total of all new fibres prepared, \nb) In the case of cut-in joints or terminations the quantity is determined by all the new incoming fibres that need to be prepared, collectively.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000786, \nb) CTO-0011156,\nc) CTO-011866. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre prepared, each (EA).','EA',15.00,'PAY,FEE:CI4.23 PREP JNT FO ALL','PAY, FEE:PURPOSE CI4.23 PREP JNT FO ALL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE FITTING AND SECURING OF THE JOINT, SPLIT FLEX\nPROTECTION PIPE AND SLACK BOX / ORGANISER / BRACKETS (IE X,Y,E ETC) IN THE MANHOLE / JOINTING PIT, THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF\nTHE CABLE TO SPEC, THE PRESENTING, IDENTIFYING AND COILING OF THE REQUIRED FIBRE/S IN THE SPLICE ORGANIZER, THE COILING AND\nINSERTING OF THE SLACK INTO THE SPLIT FLEX PROTECTION PIPE AND SLACK BOX / ORGANISER / BRACKETS (IE X,Y,E ETC), THE LABELLING OF\nTHE CABLE, JOINTS, FIBRES, POLE AND SLACK BOX / ORGANISER, THE INSERTING OF THE CABLE INTO THE PROTECTION PIPE AND UV RESISTANT\nSPRAGUE ON POLE, THE MARKING/LABELLING OF THE CABLE, JOINTS, FIBRES AND SLACK BOX/ ORGANISER / BRACKETS (IE X,Y,E ETC), THE\nCLEANING OF THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE, ALL MINOR BUILD\nMATERIAL (I.E. CONSUMABLES, LABELS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE SUPPLY OF OPTIC ENCLOSURE, SLACK BOX/ORGANISER AND FIBRE OPTIC\nMECHANICAL SPLICES/CONNECTORS, (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), THE SPLICING OF THE OPTIC FIBRE, WHICH MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY, TRAVEL RELATED\nCOSTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). NOTE: IN THE CASE OF STRAIGHT OR FORKED JOINTS THE QUANTITY IS DETERMINED BY THE TOTAL OF ALL NEW FIBRES\nPREPARED, IN THE CASE OF CUT-IN JOINTS OR TERMINATIONS THE QUANTITY IS DETERMINED BY ALL THE NEW INCOMING FIBRES THAT NEED TO BE\nPREPARED, COLLECTIVELY. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000786, CTO-0011156, CTO-011866. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER FIBRE PREPARED, EACH (EA)'),(3046076,'CI4.43','CI4.43 TST OPTIC >10KM NON TRMNTD','This item consists of an Optic Fibre test (Pre-or Post-Installation) for overhead and underground optic fibre cables, which are not terminated on either end and are greater than 10 km in total length.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The preparation of the cable ends to specification and splice to a test block or pigtails, \nb) Performing the following tests according to specification (Test Criteria for the Acceptance Of 10Gbit/S Fibres) end to end irrespective of the number of splices/patch tails there are in between:\no OTDR (i.e. Attenuation, Return Loss, Splice Loss, Connector loss)\no OLTS (IL & ORL)\no Chromatic Dispersion (CD)\no Polarization Mode Dispersion (PMD)\nc) All materials to perform the test such as cleaning consumables and test block or pigtails, \nd) Sealing the cable ends upon completion, \ne) Submitting a soft copy (DVD/CD) of the test results for each fibre tested to Telkom (C.R./SPOC) and upon request also providing a printout copy of the test results. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-007539,\nc) CTO-006426. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre, end to end each (EA)','EA',204.98,'TST,CBL:CI4.43,OPTIC FBR NON TRMNTD,>10','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.43, TYPE OPTIC FIBER NON TRMNTD, DISTANCE >10 KM:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE\nPREPARATION OF THE CABLE ENDS TO SPECIFICATION AND SPLICE TO A TEST BLOCK OR PIGTAILS, PERFORMING THE FOLLOWING TESTS ACCORDING TO\nSPECIFICATION (TEST CRITERIA FOR THE ACCEPTANCE OF 10GBIT/S FIBRES) END TO END IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SPLICES/PATCH TAILS\nTHERE ARE IN BETWEEN: OTDR (I.E. ATTENUATION, RETURN LOSS, SPLICE LOSS, CONNECTOR LOSS) OLTS (IL & ORL) CHROMATIC DISPERSION (CD)\nPOLARIZATION MODE DISPERSION (PMD) ALL MATERIALS TO PERFORM THE TEST SUCH AS CLEANING CONSUMABLES AND TEST BLOCK OR PIGTAILS,\nSEALING THE CABLE ENDS UPON COMPLETION,  SUBMITTING A SOFT COPY (DVD/CD) OF THE TEST RESULTS FOR EACH FIBRE TESTED TO TELKOM\n(C.R./SPOC) AND UPON REQUEST ALSO PROVIDING A PRINTOUT COPY OF THE TEST RESULTS.   THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE\nSERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000043, CTO-007539, CTO-006426. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER FIBRE, END TO END EACH (EA)'),(3046077,'CI3.14','CI3.14 ERECT FBR BLCK DISTRN','This item consists of the erecting, terminating and tensioning of optic fibre cables all sizes on block distribution routes (FTTH).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The erecting of fibre cable on existing or new Telkom routes or Eskom / power routes and mounting of all incidental fittings (i.e. ΓÇ£SΓÇ¥ hooks, support clamps, replacing of a single suspension hook with a double hook),\nb) Termination of fibre at each pole with 15m slack for splicing into slimbox or as per CR instruction, \nc) The fitting of specialised optic fibre pulleys on all poles and the feeding of the hauling rope, \nd) The sealing of the cable ends, \ne) The hanging and the regulating of the cable (using dynamometer meter) and the entire general handling of the cable, \nf) The cutting of overhanging branches to within 1m of the existing route, \ng) The testing of poles when working on all existing poles / routes. It is the Service ProviderΓÇÖs responsibility to ensure all existing poles are safe to be worked on, \nh) The cleaning of the work site upon completion of the work, \ni) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. cable ties, fasteners, labels, etc.),\nj) Labelling of the cable when required. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',6.90,'ERCT,WRE:CI3.14,FBR BLCK DISTRN','ERECT, WIRE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.14, TYPE FBR BLCK DISTRN:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE ERECTING OF FIBRE CABLE ON\nEXISTING OR NEW TELKOM ROUTES OR ESKOM / POWER ROUTES AND MOUNTING OF ALL INCIDENTAL FITTINGS (I.E. #S# HOOKS, SUPPORT CLAMPS,\nREPLACING OF A SINGLE SUSPENSION HOOK WITH A DOUBLE HOOK), TERMINATION OF FIBRE AT EACH POLE WITH 15M SLACK FOR SPLICING INTO\nSLIMBOX OR AS PER CR INSTRUCTION, THE FITTING OF SPECIALISED OPTIC FIBRE PULLEYS ON ALL POLES AND THE FEEDING OF THE HAULING ROPE,\nTHE SEALING OF THE CABLE ENDS, THE HANGING AND THE REGULATING OF THE CABLE (USING DYNAMOMETER METER) AND THE ENTIRE GENERAL\nHANDLING OF THE CABLE, THE CUTTING OF OVERHANGING BRANCHES TO WITHIN 1M OF THE EXISTING ROUTE, THE TESTING OF POLES WHEN WORKING ON\nALL EXISTING POLES / ROUTES. IT IS THE SERVICE PROVIDER#S RESPONSIBILITY TO ENSURE ALL EXISTING POLES ARE SAFE TO BE WORKED ON, THE\nCLEANING OF THE WORK SITE UPON COMPLETION OF THE WORK, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, FASTENERS, LABELS, ETC.),\nLABELLING OF THE CABLE WHEN REQUIRED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE\nSPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT)'),(3046078,'CI3.7','CI3.7 PLNT POLE (WOD)/STRUT/STAY','This item consists of the survey, digging and planting of all sizes and types of wooden poles, struts and stays.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The surveying, digging or drilling for wooden poles / struts / stays in normal soil conditions, \nb) Survey sketches to be handed to CR for recommendation prior to construction,\nc) The clearing of the surface and removing of boulders,\nd) The grubbing tree stumps in line of the route,\ne) Hoisting and planting of poles and struts by means of a crane if required,\nf) The supply of water if necessary to obtain the correct moisture content, \ng) Back filling (mixed with 5 kg of cement per pole/strut) the hole and compacted as a dry mix in layers,\nh) The back filling of cavities, demolishing and removing of structures, \ni) The transporting and distributing of material along the route,\nj) The cutting of branches or bush within 1m radius of the pole / strut / stay, \nk) The removal of spoil and importing of backfill where required,\nl) Provision of temporary stay / strut and the recovery thereof on completion of installation of the new stay. (When replacing stay plate and rod), \nm) Making off the stay (top and / or bottom) by hand or by means of a preformed make off ΓÇô complete, \nn) The fitting of stay guards, stay brackets (i.e. short spread, etc.) and strain insulators where required, \no) Supply of all minor material (i.e. survey pegs, cement, etc.).\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the pole / strut / stay (Telkom to provide),\nb) All travel related costs to and from site (See Service Fees Document). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole / strut / stay each (EA).','EA',320.61,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.7,POLE WOD/STRUT/STAY','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI3.7, LOCATION POLE WOD/STRUT/STAY, ADDITIONAL TASK SURVEY, PLANT, DIG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT\nLIMITED TO: THE SURVEYING, DIGGING OR DRILLING FOR WOODEN POLES / STRUTS / STAYS IN NORMAL SOIL CONDITIONS, SURVEY SKETCHES TO BE\nHANDED TO CR FOR RECOMMENDATION PRIOR TO CONSTRUCTION, THE CLEARING OF THE SURFACE AND REMOVING OF BOULDERS, THE GRUBBING TREE\nSTUMPS IN LINE OF THE ROUTE, HOISTING AND PLANTING OF POLES AND STRUTS BY MEANS OF A CRANE IF REQUIRED, THE SUPPLY OF WATER IF\nNECESSARY TO OBTAIN THE CORRECT MOISTURE CONTENT, BACK FILLING (MIXED WITH 5 KG OF CEMENT PER POLE/STRUT) THE HOLE AND COMPACTED AS\nA DRY MIX IN LAYERS, THE BACK FILLING OF CAVITIES, DEMOLISHING AND REMOVING OF STRUCTURES, THE TRANSPORTING AND DISTRIBUTING OF\nMATERIAL ALONG THE ROUTE, THE CUTTING OF BRANCHES OR BUSH WITHIN 1M RADIUS OF THE POLE / STRUT / STAY, THE REMOVAL OF SPOIL AND\nIMPORTING OF BACKFILL WHERE REQUIRED, PROVISION OF TEMPORARY STAY / STRUT AND THE RECOVERY THEREOF ON COMPLETION OF INSTALLATION OF\nTHE NEW STAY. (WHEN REPLACING STAY PLATE AND ROD), MAKING OFF THE STAY (TOP AND / OR BOTTOM) BY HAND OR BY MEANS OF A PREFORMED\nMAKE OFF COMPLETE, THE FITTING OF STAY GUARDS, STAY BRACKETS (I.E. SHORT SPREAD, ETC.) AND STRAIN INSULATORS WHERE REQUIRED, SUPPLY\nOF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. SURVEY PEGS, CEMENT, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE POLE / STRUT / STAY (TELKOM TO PROVIDE),\nALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEES DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753),\nWI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER POLE / STRUT / STAY\nEACH (EA)'),(3046079,'CI2.42','CI2.42 INSTL HDF SPLIC TRAY','This item consists of the installation of a High-Density Frame (HDF) FACT splice and patch tray for 48 fibres, 96 fibres or 144 fibres, connect type LC/APC.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.),\nb) Obtaining work refs, \nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required, \nd) All Labour costs, \ne) Project management, \nf) Unpacking, Assembling and installing the splice tray and associated components according to Telkom / Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications, \ng) Labelling, \nh) Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, etc.), \ni) The supply of all minor build materials. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per splice tray (48/96/144 fibres) each (EA)','EA',386.12,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.42,HDF SPLIC TRAY','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.42, TYPE HDF SPLIC TRAY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL\nSITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS, INTERFACE\nMANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, ALL LABOUR COSTS, PROJECT MANAGEMENT, UNPACKING, ASSEMBLING AND\nINSTALLING THE SPLICE TRAY AND ASSOCIATED COMPONENTS ACCORDING TO TELKOM / OPENSERVE M&P#S WI#S, SPECIFICATIONS, LABELLING,\nCHECKING THE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E. CABLE CONNECTIONS, ETC.), THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIALS. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SPLICE TRAY (48/96/144 FIBRES) EACH (EA)'),(3046080,'CI3.29','CI3.29 LWR WEAVER NEST','This item consists of the lowering of weaver nests on optic and open wire routes. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The removal of the nest material,\nb) The supplying of pole steps, \nc) The lowering of the existing basket,\nd) The building of a basket (SP to supply material), \ne) The transfer of the nest material to basket,\nf) The cleaning of the site on completion of the job. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) Nature Conservation specification CTO-000986,\nb) Nature Conservation specification CTO-003168.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is each (EA).','EA',218.98,'PAY,FEE:CI3.29 LWR WEAVER NEST','PAY, FEE:PURPOSE CI3.29 LWR WEAVER NEST:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE REMOVAL OF THE NEST MATERIAL, THE SUPPLYING OF\nPOLE STEPS, THE LOWERING OF THE EXISTING BASKET, THE BUILDING OF A BASKET (SP TO SUPPLY MATERIAL), THE TRANSFER OF THE NEST\nMATERIAL TO BASKET, THE CLEANING OF THE SITE ON COMPLETION OF THE JOB, THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: NATURE CONSERVATION SPECIFICATION CTO-000986, NATURE CONSERVATION\nSPECIFICATION CTO-003168. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS EACH (EA)'),(3046082,'CI3.15','CI3.15 ERECT FBR LG HAUL','This item consists of the erecting, terminating and tensioning of optic fibre cables all sizes on long haul routes.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The erecting of fibre cable on existing or new Telkom routes or Eskom / power routes and mounting of all incidental fittings (i.e. ΓÇ£SΓÇ¥ hooks, support clamps, replacing of a single suspension hook with a double hook), \nb) The handling of cable slack on major aerial routes where joints are to be made (30m of slack per cable end or as per CR approval), \nc) The fitting of specialised optic fibre pulleys on all poles and the feeding of the hauling rope. \nd) The sealing of the cable ends, \ne) The hanging and the regulating of the cable (using dynamometer meter) and the entire general handling of the cable, \nf) The cutting of overhanging branches to within 1m of the existing route,  \ng) The testing of poles when working on all existing poles / routes. It is the Service ProviderΓÇÖs responsibility to ensure all existing poles are safe to be worked on,  \nh) The cleaning of the work site upon completion of the work,  \ni) Supplying of all minor material (i.e. cable ties, fasteners, labels, etc.),\nj) Labelling of the cable when required. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',5.70,'ERCT,WRE:CI3.15,FBR LG HAUL','ERECT, WIRE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.15, TYPE FBR LG HAUL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE ERECTING OF FIBRE CABLE ON EXISTING\nOR NEW TELKOM ROUTES OR ESKOM / POWER ROUTES AND MOUNTING OF ALL INCIDENTAL FITTINGS (I.E. S HOOKS, SUPPORT CLAMPS, REPLACING OF A\nSINGLE SUSPENSION HOOK WITH A DOUBLE HOOK), THE HANDLING OF CABLE SLACK ON MAJOR AERIAL ROUTES WHERE JOINTS ARE TO BE MADE (30M OF\nSLACK PER CABLE END OR AS PER CR APPROVAL), THE FITTING OF SPECIALISED OPTIC FIBRE PULLEYS ON ALL POLES AND THE FEEDING OF THE\nHAULING ROPE. THE SEALING OF THE CABLE ENDS, THE HANGING AND THE REGULATING OF THE CABLE (USING DYNAMOMETER METER) AND THE ENTIRE\nGENERAL HANDLING OF THE CABLE, THE CUTTING OF OVERHANGING BRANCHES TO WITHIN 1M OF THE EXISTING ROUTE, THE TESTING OF POLES WHEN\nWORKING ON ALL EXISTING POLES / ROUTES. IT IS THE SERVICE PROVIDER#S RESPONSIBILITY TO ENSURE ALL EXISTING POLES ARE SAFE TO BE\nWORKED ON, THE CLEANING OF THE WORK SITE UPON COMPLETION OF THE WORK, SUPPLYING OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, FASTENERS,\nLABELS, ETC.), LABELLING OF THE CABLE WHEN REQUIRED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003.\nCTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT)'),(3046083,'CI3.27','CI3.27 RECVR OPN WRE','This item consists of the recovery of all types of open wires inclusive of residuals.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The binding out of wires,  \nb) The unbinding of the wire and the return of the wire to Telkom stores. Only applicable to pieces of wire left on insulators due to thefts and breaks, \nc) The measuring, coiling and tagging of the wire, \nd) The weighing and securing of the wire, \ne) The transporting of the recovered material from the site to the destination as specified.  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pair per metre (MT).','MT',0.90,'RCVR,WRE:CI3.27,OPN','RECOVER, WIRE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.27, TYPE OPEN:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE BINDING OUT OF WIRES, THE UNBINDING OF THE\nWIRE AND THE RETURN OF THE WIRE TO TELKOM STORES. ONLY APPLICABLE TO PIECES OF WIRE LEFT ON INSULATORS DUE TO THEFTS AND BREAKS,\nTHE MEASURING, COILING AND TAGGING OF THE WIRE, THE WEIGHING AND SECURING OF THE WIRE, THE TRANSPORTING OF THE RECOVERED MATERIAL\nFROM THE SITE TO THE DESTINATION AS SPECIFIED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE\nSPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PAIR PER METRE (MT)'),(3046085,'CI4.31','CI4.31 BASC CTS TST CU','This item consists of the basic conformance testing to specification of a copper pair to support digital services i.e. ADSL etc.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The testing of the copper pair for resistance, capacitance, loop resistance, distance and longitudinal balance, utilising the approved equipment/tools from the S/L to SDC or SDC to DP or S/L to DP in case of direct feed. (Point to point), \nb) The re-numbering of DPΓÇÖs and SDCΓÇÖs, according to Telkom spec, if required, \nc) The cleaning of the utility box and the immediate surrounding area, \nd) The provisioning of test data in a copper test report. Template to be provided by Telkom SA, \ne) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services/equipment to complete the required conformance testing of the copper pair to specification. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The opening and closing of the existing UG DP dome joint, which may be claimed separately, \nb) All travel related costs. (See Service fee items). \n\nNote: \na) Normally all spare pairs in the cable to be tested.\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-005503. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pair, (PR).','PR',36.05,'TST,CBL:CI4.31,BASC CTS CU','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.31, TYPE BASC CTS CU:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE TESTING OF THE COPPER PAIR FOR\nRESISTANCE, CAPACITANCE, LOOP RESISTANCE, DISTANCE AND LONGITUDINAL BALANCE, UTILISING THE APPROVED EQUIPMENT/TOOLS FROM THE S/L TO\nSDC OR SDC TO DP OR S/L TO DP IN CASE OF DIRECT FEED. (POINT TO POINT), THE RE-NUMBERING OF DP#S AND SDC#S, ACCORDING TO TELKOM\nSPEC, IF REQUIRED, THE CLEANING OF THE UTILITY BOX AND THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, THE PROVISIONING OF TEST DATA IN A COPPER\nTEST REPORT. TEMPLATE TO BE PROVIDED BY TELKOM SA, THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED\nSERVICES/EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED CONFORMANCE TESTING OF THE COPPER PAIR TO SPECIFICATION THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE OPENING\nAND CLOSING OF THE EXISTING UG DP DOME JOINT, WHICH MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS).\nNOTE: NORMALLY ALL SPARE PAIRS IN THE CABLE TO BE TESTED. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000043, CTO-005503. THE UNIT OF\nMEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PAIR, (PR)'),(3046087,'CI3.24','CI3.24 RECVR WOD POLE STRUT','This item consists of the recovery of all sizes wooden poles & struts. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The excavation and the removal of the complete pole & strut (inclusive of concrete around base of pole & strut),\nb) Hoisting and recovering of poles and struts by means of a mechanical aid, \nc) The stripping of the pole - completely of staples, cable, make-offs etc., \nd) The backfilling and compaction of holes to existing ground levels,  \ne) The transporting of the recovered material from the site to the destination as specified. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole/strut, each (EA).','EA',216.54,'RCVR,EQUIP:CI3.24,WOD POLE STRUT','RECOVER, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI3.24, TYPE WOD POLE STRUT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE EXCAVATION AND THE REMOVAL\nOF THE COMPLETE POLE & STRUT (INCLUSIVE OF CONCRETE AROUND BASE OF POLE & STRUT), HOISTING AND RECOVERING OF POLES AND STRUTS BY\nMEANS OF A MECHANICAL AID, THE STRIPPING OF THE POLE COMPLETELY OF STAPLES, CABLE, MAKE-OFFS ETC., THE BACKFILLING AND COMPACTION\nOF HOLES TO EXISTING GROUND LEVELS, THE TRANSPORTING OF THE RECOVERED MATERIAL FROM THE SITE TO THE DESTINATION AS SPECIFIED. THE\nRATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001\n(CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nPOLE/STRUT, EACH (EA)'),(3046088,'CI4.19','CI4.19 CUT OUT & RMV EXSTG JNT','This item consists of the cutting out and removal of existing joints (All sizes) to enable the recovery of a cable\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The identification of the correct cable, cutting the cable and sealing both ends by means of a cable end seal cap, \nb) The removal and recovery of the joint,\nc) The recovery of uni-strut supports/flat brackets used to support the joint, \nd) The return of the recovered material to a Telkom store as specified, \ne) The cleaning of the utility box and the immediate surrounding area, \nf) The control and pumping of water, \ng) The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, mechanical aids or specialised services / equipment to complete the required cut-out and removing of existing joint to specification.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nNote:\na) This item is not applicable in cases where a cable cut-over was done. \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000778. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per joint, each (EA).','EA',99.91,'REMV,INSTLTN:CUT OUT & RMV EXSTG JNT','REMOVE, INSTALLATION:TYPE CUT OUT & RMV EXSTG JNT, ITEM NUMBER CI4.19:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE IDENTIFICATION\nOF THE CORRECT CABLE, CUTTING THE CABLE AND SEALING BOTH ENDS BY MEANS OF A CABLE END SEAL CAP, THE REMOVAL AND RECOVERY OF THE\nJOINT, THE RECOVERY OF UNI-STRUT SUPPORTS/FLAT BRACKETS USED TO SUPPORT THE JOINT, THE RETURN OF THE RECOVERED MATERIAL TO A TELKOM\nSTORE AS SPECIFIED, THE CLEANING OF THE UTILITY BOX AND THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, THE CONTROL AND PUMPING OF WATER, THE\nSUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED SERVICES / EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE REQUIRED CUT-OUT\nAND REMOVING OF EXISTING JOINT TO SPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). NOTE: THIS ITEM IS NOT\nAPPLICABLE IN CASES WHERE A CABLE CUT-OVER WAS DONE. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000778. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS\nITEM IS PER JOINT, EACH (EA)'),(3046089,'CI3.4','CI3.4 BRNCH CTNG >300MM RADIUS','This item consists of the cutting of tree branches exceeding 300mm in circumference where new infrastructure is provided or for maintenance purposes. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Branches to be cut only when instructed to do so by a site instruction from contract representative,  \nb) Telkom to obtain permission from the owner to cut the branches,  \nc) The cost of cutting branches exceeding 300mm in circumference, \nd) The cutting up of the branch and foliage into transportable lengths, removing, transporting and the disposal thereof,  \ne) Engineering difficulties such as avoiding damage to infrastructure and / or private property,  \nf) The supply of suitable wound sealer and dressing immediately after cutting. (Must be thorough, two or three coats to be applied if necessary),  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per branch each (EA).','EA',103.17,'CLEAR,TREE:CI3.4 BRNCH 300MM RAD','CLEAR, TREE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.4 BRNCH CTNG >300MM CIRC:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: BRANCHES TO BE CUT ONLY WHEN\nINSTRUCTED TO DO SO BY A SITE INSTRUCTION FROM CONTRACT REPRESENTATIVE, TELKOM TO OBTAIN PERMISSION FROM THE OWNER TO CUT THE\nBRANCHES, THE COST OF CUTTING BRANCHES EXCEEDING 300MM IN CIRCUMFERENCE, THE CUTTING UP OF THE BRANCH AND FOLIAGE INTO\nTRANSPORTABLE LENGTHS, REMOVING, TRANSPORTING AND THE DISPOSAL THEREOF, ENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS AVOIDING DAMAGE TO\nINFRASTRUCTURE AND / OR PRIVATE PROPERTY, THE SUPPLY OF SUITABLE WOUND SEALER AND DRESSING IMMEDIATELY AFTER CUTTING. (MUST BE\nTHOROUGH, TWO OR THREE COATS TO BE APPLIED IF NECESSARY), THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003.\nCTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER BRANCH EACH (EA)'),(3046090,'CI2.41','CI2.41 INSTL HDF CAB','This item consists of the installation of a High-Density Frame (HDF) cabinet.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.),\nb) Obtaining work refs.,\nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required,\nd) All Labour costs,\ne) Project management,\nf) Unpacking, Assembling and installing the rack and associated components according to Telkom / Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications,\ng) Labelling,\nh) Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, etc.),\ni) The supply of all minor build materials.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The installation of the FACT Splice and patch tray,\nb) All travel related costs. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per Cabinet, each (EA)','EA',4500.00,'INSTL,CABNT:CI2.41,HDF','INSTALL, CABINET:TYPE HDF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS\nINCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM\nSUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, ALL LABOUR COSTS, PROJECT MANAGEMENT, UNPACKING, ASSEMBLING AND INSTALLING THE RACK AND ASSOCIATED\nCOMPONENTS ACCORDING TO TELKOM / OPENSERVE M&P#S WI#S, SPECIFICATIONS, LABELLING, CHECKING THE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E.\nCABLE CONNECTIONS, ETC.), THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIALS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE INSTALLATION OF THE FACT SPLICE AND PATCH\nTRAY, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CABINET, EACH (EA)'),(3046091,'CI4.41','CI4.41 TST OPTIC 1KM-10KM NON TRMNTD','This item consists of an Optic Fibre test for overhead and underground optic fibre cables, which are not terminated on either end and are from 1km to 10 km in total length.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The preparation of the cable ends to specification and splice to a test block or pigtails,\nb) Performing the following tests according to specification end to end irrespective of the number of splices/patch tails there are in between:\no OTDR (i.e. Attenuation, Return Loss, Splice Loss, Connector loss)\no OLTS (IL & ORL)\nc) All materials to perform the test such as cleaning consumables and test block or pigtails,\nd) Sealing the cable ends upon completion,\ne) Submitting a soft copy (DVD/CD) of the test results for each fibre tested to Telkom (C.R./SPOC) and upon request also providing a printout copy of the test results. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-007539,\nc) CTO-006426. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre, end to end each (EA)','EA',164.61,'TST,CBL:CI4.41,OPTIC FBR NON TRMNTD,1-10','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.41, TYPE OPTIC FIBER NON TRMNTD, DISTANCE 1-10 KM:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE\nPREPARATION OF THE CABLE ENDS TO SPECIFICATION AND SPLICE TO A TEST BLOCK OR PIGTAILS, PERFORMING THE FOLLOWING TESTS ACCORDING TO\nSPECIFICATION END TO END IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SPLICES/PATCH TAILS THERE ARE IN BETWEEN: OTDR (I.E. ATTENUATION, RETURN\nLOSS, SPLICE LOSS, CONNECTOR LOSS) OLTS (IL & ORL) ALL MATERIALS TO PERFORM THE TEST SUCH AS CLEANING CONSUMABLES AND TEST BLOCK OR\nPIGTAILS, SEALING THE CABLE ENDS UPON COMPLETION, SUBMITTING A SOFT COPY (DVD/CD) OF THE TEST RESULTS FOR EACH FIBRE TESTED TO\nTELKOM (C.R./SPOC) AND UPON REQUEST ALSO PROVIDING A PRINTOUT COPY OF THE TEST RESULTS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS\n(SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000043, CTO-007539, CTO-006426. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER FIBRE, END TO END EACH (EA)'),(3046092,'CI3.6','CI3.6 TREE FELLING','This item consists of trees and / or tree trunks that needs to be felled.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The felling of trees and / or tree trunks,\nb) Obtaining permission to fell tree and or tree trunk, \nc) The cutting of branches, secondary branches and foliage into transportable lengths, \nd) The cost of removing, transporting and the disposing thereof, \ne) The re-instatement of surfaces and or fences if damaged,\nf) Engineering difficulties such as avoiding damage to infrastructure and / or private property. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The removal of entire tree stumps, \nb) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) For the cutting of trees with circumferences from 300mm to 800mm the quantity is 1 time the rate (Measurement to be done at ground level). \nb) If circumference is 801mm upto 1200mm then the quantity is 2 times the rate.\nc) If circumference is greater that 1200mm then the quantity is 3 times the rate. \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per tree, each (EA).','EA',1000.00,'CLEAR,TREE:CI3.6,FELLING','CLEAR, TREE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.6, METHOD FELLING:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE FELLING OF TREES AND / OR TREE TRUNKS,\nOBTAINING PERMISSION TO FELL TREE AND OR TREE TRUNK, THE CUTTING OF BRANCHES, SECONDARY BRANCHES AND FOLIAGE INTO TRANSPORTABLE\nLENGTHS, THE COST OF REMOVING, TRANSPORTING AND THE DISPOSING THEREOF, THE RE-INSTATEMENT OF SURFACES AND OR FENCES IF DAMAGED,\nENGINEERING DIFFICULTIES SUCH AS AVOIDING DAMAGE TO INFRASTRUCTURE AND / OR PRIVATE PROPERTY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE REMOVAL OF\nENTIRE TREE STUMPS, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: FOR THE CUTTING OF TREES WITH\nCIRCUMFERENCES FROM 300MM TO 800MM THE QUANTITY IS 1 TIME THE RATE (MEASUREMENT TO BE DONE AT GROUND LEVEL). IF CIRCUMFERENCE IS\n801MM UPTO 1200MM THEN THE QUANTITY IS 2 TIMES THE RATE. IF CIRCUMFERENCE IS GREATER THAT 1200MM THEN THE QUANTITY IS 3 TIMES THE\nRATE. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003.\nCTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER TREE, EACH (EA)'),(3046094,'CI2.44','CI2.44 INSTL OMDF RACK','This item consists of the installation of an Optic Main Distribution Frame (OMDF) Rack.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.),\nb) Obtaining work refs.,\nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nd) All Labour costs, to install an OMDF Rack\ne) Project management,\nf) Unpacking, Assembling and installing the Rack and associated components according to Telkom / Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications,\ng) Labelling,\nh) Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, etc.),\ni) The supply of all minor build materials. \n\nNote: this item may only be claimed where an existing OMDF is expanded.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs. \nb) The cost of the OMDF Rack\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per OMDF Rack, each (EA)','EA',1500.00,'INSTL,RACK,ELECTR:CI2.44,OMDF','INSTALL, RACK, ELECTRONIC:ITEM NUMBER CI2.44, TYPE OMDF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT\nWITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED ALL LABOUR COSTS, TO INSTALL AN OMDF RACK PROJECT MANAGEMENT, UNPACKING,\nASSEMBLING AND INSTALLING THE RACK AND ASSOCIATED COMPONENTS ACCORDING TO TELKOM / OPENSERVE M&P#S WI#S, SPECIFICATIONS, LABELLING,\nCHECKING THE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E. CABLE CONNECTIONS, ETC.), THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIALS. NOTE: THIS ITEM\nMAY ONLY BE CLAIMED WHERE AN EXISTING OMDF IS EXPANDED. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. THE COST OF THE OMDF RACK THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER OMDF RACK, EACH (EA)'),(3046095,'CI3.20','CI3.20 RETN & REMAKE STAY','This item consists of the retention and remake of all types and sizes of stays.  \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The reset of the cross-head to its original position. (four stay rod threads to protrude), \nb) The re-make of the top and bottom make-off (hand or preformed) ΓÇô complete, \nc) The fitting of stay guards where required,\nd) The provision and recovery of any temporary stays or struts. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per stay, each (EA).','EA',62.46,'RETNSN,STAY:CI3.20','RETENSION, STAY:ITEM NUMBER CI3.20:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE RESET OF THE CROSS-HEAD TO ITS ORIGINAL POSITION.\n(FOUR STAY ROD THREADS TO PROTRUDE), THE RE-MAKE OF THE TOP AND BOTTOM MAKE-OFF (HAND OR PREFORMED) COMPLETE, THE FITTING OF STAY\nGUARDS WHERE REQUIRED, THE PROVISION AND RECOVERY OF ANY TEMPORARY STAYS OR STRUTS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM\nSITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001\n(CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER STAY, EACH (EA)'),(3046097,'CI3.10','CI3.10 STRGHTNG POLE','This item consists of the straightening of all types and sizes of poles.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The un-bind and re-bind of all the wires and the un-hook and re-hook of all the cables, \nb) Loosen and re - terminate cable suspender wire,\nc) The cost to dig the pole loose, straightening the pole, back filling (mixed with 5 kg of cement per pole/strut) the hole and compacted as a dry mix in layers,\nd) The supply of water if necessary to obtain the correct moisture content. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole, each (EA).','EA',170.87,'ALGN,POLE:CI3.10,STRGHTNG','ALIGN, POLE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.10, TYPE STRGHTNG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE UN-BIND AND RE-BIND OF ALL THE WIRES AND\nTHE UN-HOOK AND RE-HOOK OF ALL THE CABLES, LOOSEN AND RE TERMINATE CABLE SUSPENDER WIRE, THE COST TO DIG THE POLE LOOSE,\nSTRAIGHTENING THE POLE, BACK FILLING (MIXED WITH 5 KG OF CEMENT PER POLE/STRUT) THE HOLE AND COMPACTED AS A DRY MIX IN LAYERS, THE\nSUPPLY OF WATER IF NECESSARY TO OBTAIN THE CORRECT MOISTURE CONTENT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944),\nPR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER POLE, EACH (EA)'),(3046099,'CI3.3','CI3.3 BSH CTNG 1M RADIUS','This item consists of cutting of branches or bush inclusive of reeds less than 300mm in circumference within 1 metre radius of new or existing routes.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The clearing around overhead cables, poles, struts and stays fitted with stay guards (clearing to have a radius of 1m), \nb) The cutting of bush, reeds, tree stumps, trunks, branches into transportable lengths and disposing thereof,  \nc) The supply of a suitable wound sealer and dressing (must be thorough, two or three coats being applied if necessary) immediately after cutting,  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per running metre (MT).','MT',4.87,'CUT,BSH:CI3.3,1M RAD','CUT, BUSH:ITEM NUMBER CI3.3, TYPE 1M RADIUS:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE CLEARING AROUND OVERHEAD CABLES, POLES,\nSTRUTS AND STAYS FITTED WITH STAY GUARDS (CLEARING TO HAVE A RADIUS OF 1M), THE CUTTING OF BUSH, REEDS, TREE STUMPS, TRUNKS,\nBRANCHES INTO TRANSPORTABLE LENGTHS AND DISPOSING THEREOF, THE SUPPLY OF A SUITABLE WOUND SEALER AND DRESSING (MUST BE THOROUGH,\nTWO OR THREE COATS BEING APPLIED IF NECESSARY) IMMEDIATELY AFTER CUTTING, THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944),\nPR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER RUNNING METRE (MT)'),(3046100,'CI4.24','CI4.24 INSL FTTH SPLTR','This item consists of the installation of a splitter (ie: 1:2, 1:4, 1:32 etc) in a FTTH overhead or underground fibre optic joint. (All joints type and sizes). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The preparation of the joint for the splitter installation (enclosures such as FIST, Slim joints, FTTH Hub, Budi box, etc.), \nb) The presenting, identifying and coiling of the required fibre/s in the splice organizer.\nc) The fitting, routing and labelling of the splitters, \nd) The marking/labelling of the cable, joints, fibres, pole or slack box/organiser/ brackets (ie X,Y,E etc), \ne) Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site, \nf) All minor build material (i.e. consumables, Labels, etc.). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The supply of fibre optic mechanical splices/connectors and splitter/s, (Telkom to supply), \nb) The splicing of the optic fibre, which may be claimed for separately,\nc) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-011156.  \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per splitter, each (EA).','EA',683.15,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI4.24,FTTH SPLTR','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI4.24, TYPE FTTH SPLTR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE PREPARATION OF THE JOINT FOR\nTHE SPLITTER INSTALLATION (ENCLOSURES SUCH AS FIST, SLIM JOINTS, FTTH HUB, BUDI BOX, ETC.), THE PRESENTING, IDENTIFYING AND COILING\nOF THE REQUIRED FIBRE/S IN THE SPLICE ORGANIZER. THE FITTING, ROUTING AND LABELLING OF THE SPLITTERS, THE MARKING/LABELLING OF THE\nCABLE, JOINTS, FIBRES, POLE OR SLACK BOX/ORGANISER/ BRACKETS (IE X,Y,E ETC), TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT\nTO AND FROM SITE, ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CONSUMABLES, LABELS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE SUPPLY OF FIBRE OPTIC\nMECHANICAL SPLICES/CONNECTORS AND SPLITTER/S, (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), THE SPLICING OF THE OPTIC FIBRE, WHICH MAY BE CLAIMED FOR\nSEPARATELY, TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-011156. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS\nITEM IS PER SPLITTER, EACH (EA).'),(3046101,'CI3.8','CI3.8 PLNT POLE/STRUT-CONCRT/STL','This item consists of the survey, digging and planting of all sizes of concrete or steel poles and struts.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The surveying, digging or drilling for the pole / strut in normal soil conditions, \nb) Survey sketches to be handed to CR for recommendation prior to construction, \nc) The clearing of the surface and removing of boulders, \nd) The grubbing tree stumps in line of the route, \ne) Hoisting and planting of the pole or strut by means of a crane. A crane truck must be used, if the site is accessible,\nf) The supply of water if necessary to obtain the correct moisture content,\ng) Back filling (mixed with 5 kg of cement per pole/strut) the hole and compacted as a dry mix in layers, \nh) The back filling of cavities, demolishing and removing of structures, \ni) The transporting and distributing of material along the route,\nj) The cutting of branches or bush within 1m radius of the pole / strut / stay, \nk) The removal of spoil and importing of backfill where required, \nl) Provision of temporary stay / strut and the recovery thereof on completion of installation of the new stay. (When replacing stay plate and rod), \nm) Making off the stay (top and / or bottom) by hand or by means of a preformed make off ΓÇô complete,\nn) The fitting of stay guards, stay brackets (i.e. short spread, etc.) and strain insulators where required, \no) Supply of all minor material (i.e. survey pegs, cement, etc.),\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The cost of the Concrete / steel pole/strut (Telkom to provide),\nb) All travel related costs to and from site (See Service Fees Document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pole / strut / stay, (EA).','EA',641.48,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.8,POLE/STRUT-CONCRT/STL','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI3.8, TYPE POLE/STRUT-CONCRT/STL, ADDITIONAL TASK SURVEY, PLANT DIG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT\nLIMITED TO: THE SURVEYING, DIGGING OR DRILLING FOR THE POLE / STRUT IN NORMAL SOIL CONDITIONS, SURVEY SKETCHES TO BE HANDED TO CR\nFOR RECOMMENDATION PRIOR TO CONSTRUCTION, THE CLEARING OF THE SURFACE AND REMOVING OF BOULDERS, THE GRUBBING TREE STUMPS IN LINE OF\nTHE ROUTE, HOISTING AND PLANTING OF THE POLE OR STRUT BY MEANS OF A CRANE. A CRANE TRUCK MUST BE USED, IF THE SITE IS ACCESSIBLE,\nTHE SUPPLY OF WATER IF NECESSARY TO OBTAIN THE CORRECT MOISTURE CONTENT, BACK FILLING (MIXED WITH 5 KG OF CEMENT PER POLE/STRUT)\nTHE HOLE AND COMPACTED AS A DRY MIX IN LAYERS, THE BACK FILLING OF CAVITIES, DEMOLISHING AND REMOVING OF STRUCTURES, THE\nTRANSPORTING AND DISTRIBUTING OF MATERIAL ALONG THE ROUTE, THE CUTTING OF BRANCHES OR BUSH WITHIN 1M RADIUS OF THE POLE / STRUT /\nSTAY, THE REMOVAL OF SPOIL AND IMPORTING OF BACKFILL WHERE REQUIRED, PROVISION OF TEMPORARY STAY / STRUT AND THE RECOVERY THEREOF\nON COMPLETION OF INSTALLATION OF THE NEW STAY. (WHEN REPLACING STAY PLATE AND ROD), MAKING OFF THE STAY (TOP AND / OR BOTTOM) BY\nHAND OR BY MEANS OF A PREFORMED MAKE OFF COMPLETE, THE FITTING OF STAY GUARDS, STAY BRACKETS (I.E. SHORT SPREAD, ETC.) AND STRAIN\nINSULATORS WHERE REQUIRED, SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. SURVEY PEGS, CEMENT, ETC.), THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COST OF THE\nCONCRETE / STEEL POLE/STRUT (TELKOM TO PROVIDE), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEES DOCUMENT). THE\nSPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER POLE / STRUT / STAY, (EA)'),(3046102,'CI4.42','CI4.42 TST OPTIC >10KM TRMNTD','This item consists of an Optic Fibre test for overhead and underground optic fibre cables, which are terminated on both ends and are greater than 10 km in total length.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Performing the following tests according to specification (Test Criteria for the Acceptance Of 10Gbit/S Fibres) end to end irrespective of the number of splices/patch tails there are in between:\no OTDR (i.e. Attenuation, Return Loss, Splice Loss, Connector loss)\no OLTS (IL & ORL)\no Chromatic Dispersion (CD)\no Polarization Mode Dispersion (PMD)\nb) Submitting a soft copy (DVD/CD) of the test results for each fibre tested to Telkom (C.R./SPOC) and upon request also providing a printout copy of the test results.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000043, \nb) CTO-007539,\nc) CTO-006426. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per fibre, end to end each (EA)','EA',129.81,'TST,CBL:CI4.42,OPTIC FBR TRMNTD,>10KM','TEST, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER CI4.42, TYPE OPTIC FIBER TRMNTD, DISTANCE >10 KM:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PERFORMING THE\nFOLLOWING TESTS ACCORDING TO SPECIFICATION (TEST CRITERIA FOR THE ACCEPTANCE OF 10GBIT/S FIBRES) END TO END IRRESPECTIVE OF THE\nNUMBER OF SPLICES/PATCH TAILS THERE ARE IN BETWEEN: OTDR (I.E. ATTENUATION, RETURN LOSS, SPLICE LOSS, CONNECTOR LOSS) OLTS (IL &\nORL) CHROMATIC DISPERSION (CD) POLARIZATION MODE DISPERSION (PMD) SUBMITTING A SOFT COPY (DVD/CD) OF THE TEST RESULTS FOR EACH\nFIBER TESTED TO TELKOM (C.R./SPOC) AND UPON REQUEST ALSO PROVIDING A PRINTOUT COPY OF THE TEST RESULTS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL\nTRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000043, CTO-007539, CTO-006426. THE UNIT OF\nMEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER FIBER, END TO END EACH (EA)'),(3046103,'CI2.47','CI2.47 INSTL OMDF SPLIC TRAY','This item consists of the installation of a OMDF splicing bay tray.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.),\nb) Obtaining work refs.,\nc) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required,\nd) All Labour costs,\ne) Project management,\nf) Unpacking, Assembling and installing the splice tray and associated components according to Telkom / Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications,\ng) Labelling,\nh) Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, etc.),\ni) The supply of all minor build materials. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs. \n\nNote: \na) If the Installation is requested in conjunction with the Backbone project (i.e. From the Exchange to the FDP) then no additional traveling costs may be charged.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per splice tray each (EA).','EA',370.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI2.47,OMDF SPLIC TRAY','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI2.47, TYPE OMDF SPLIC TRAY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL\nSITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., INTERFACE\nMANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, ALL LABOUR COSTS, PROJECT MANAGEMENT, UNPACKING, ASSEMBLING AND\nINSTALLING THE SPLICE TRAY AND ASSOCIATED COMPONENTS ACCORDING TO TELKOM / OPENSERVE M&P#S WI#S, SPECIFICATIONS, LABELLING,\nCHECKING THE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E. CABLE CONNECTIONS, ETC.), THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR BUILD MATERIALS. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS. NOTE: IF THE INSTALLATION IS REQUESTED IN CONJUNCTION WITH THE BACKBONE PROJECT (I.E. FROM THE\nEXCHANGE TO THE FDP) THEN NO ADDITIONAL TRAVELING COSTS MAY BE CHARGED. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SPLICE TRAY EACH\n(EA)'),(3046105,'CI4.20','CI4.20 FIT OUTDOOR DP/FBR JNT WALL','This item consists of the fitting of a Demarcation Point / Distribution Point (DP) / fibre optic joint at the customer dwelling / premises (All sizes and types, copper and / or fibre) on wall.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The fitting / mounting of the Demarcation Point / DP/ fibre optic joint,  \nb) Fitting of splitter/s into the fibre optic joint, \nc) The drilling of holes, \nd) Numbering of Demarcation Point / DP / Joint according to Telkom spec., \ne) The supply of all minor materials (i.e. rawbolts, etc.), \nf) The supply and use of all tools, mechanical aids or specialised services / equipment. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The supply of the DP / fibre optic joint, (Telkom to supply), \nb) The fitting of the DP / fibre optic joint on a pole, \nc) The fitting of an ATB,\nd) Travel related costs (See Service Fees). \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) CTO-000778. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per DP / joint, each (EA).','EA',85.59,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI4.20,OTDOR DP/FBR JNT WALL','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI4.20, TYPE OUTDOOR DP/FBR JNT WALL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE FITTING / MOUNTING\nOF THE DEMARCATION POINT / DP/ FIBRE OPTIC JOINT, FITTING OF SPLITTER/S INTO THE FIBRE OPTIC JOINT, THE DRILLING OF HOLES,\nNUMBERING OF DEMARCATION POINT / DP / JOINT ACCORDING TO TELKOM SPEC, THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS (I.E. RAWBOLTS, ETC.), THE\nSUPPLY AND USE OF ALL TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED SERVICES / EQUIPMENT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE SUPPLY OF THE DP / FIBRE\nOPTIC JOINT, (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), THE FITTING OF THE DP / FIBRE OPTIC JOINT ON A POLE, THE FITTING OF AN ATB, TRAVEL RELATED COSTS\n(SEE SERVICE FEES). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: CTO-000778. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DP / JOINT, EACH (EA)'),(3046106,'CI3.1','CI3.1 BSH CTNG 6M WIDE','This item consists of bush cutting inclusive of reeds to enable surveying for new routes and to clear existing routes (only routes where no cable or wire work is to be done).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Bush cutting 6m is measured as 3m both sides of the route at ground level,  \nb) The clearing around poles, struts and stays fitted with stay guards (clearing to have a radius of 1m), \nc) The cutting of bush, reeds, tree stumps, trunks, branches into transportable lengths and disposing thereof,  \nd) The supply of a suitable wound sealer and dressing (must be thorough, two or three coats being applied if necessary) immediately after cutting,  \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe specification for this item is:\na) SP-AH0001 (CTO-004753), \nb) WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987),  \nc) B3001 (CTO-003944), \nd) PR-AH0003. CTO-000706.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per running metre (MT).','MT',10.52,'CUT,BSH:CI3.1,6M WD','CUT, BUSH:ITEM NUMBER CI3.1, TYPE 6M WIDE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: BUSH CUTTING 6M IS MEASURED AS 3M BOTH SIDES OF\nTHE ROUTE AT GROUND LEVEL, THE CLEARING AROUND POLES, STRUTS AND STAYS FITTED WITH STAY GUARDS (CLEARING TO HAVE A RADIUS OF 1M),\nTHE CUTTING OF BUSH, REEDS, TREE STUMPS, TRUNKS, BRANCHES INTO TRANSPORTABLE LENGTHS AND DISPOSING THEREOF, THE SUPPLY OF A\nSUITABLE WOUND SEALER AND DRESSING (MUST BE THOROUGH, TWO OR THREE COATS BEING APPLIED IF NECESSARY) IMMEDIATELY AFTER CUTTING, THE\nRATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: SP-AH0001\n(CTO-004753), WI-AH0005 (CTO-000987), B3001 (CTO-003944), PR-AH0003. CTO-000706. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER RUNNING\nMETRE (MT)'),(3046108,'CE1.9','CE1.9 ENGR ODF (MED) 721-1752FBR','This item consists of the detailed engineering of the new generation Optical Distribution Frame (ODF), medium (721 up to and including 1752 fibres).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Site visits / Surveys,\nb) Detailed Engineering of ODF on Telkom approved system software and submission of an executable file (i.e. Netplan, etc.),\nc) Detailed engineering of the medium ODF that can accommodate 721 up to and including 1752 fibres,\nd) Detailed engineering for all Pre-Build requirements directly related to the ODF such as power, air con, floor, cable runways, tie cables, termination blocks, etc.,\ne) Labour.\nf) Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\ng) Capturing of all as-build plant / elements after completion of the work. (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per site, each (EA).','EA',4847.43,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.9,ODF (MED) 721-1752FBR','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.9, TYPE ODF (MED) 721-1752FBR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SITE VISITS / SURVEYS,\nDETAILED ENGINEERING OF ODF ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE AND SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE (I.E. NETPLAN, ETC.), DETAILED\nENGINEERING OF THE MEDIUM ODF THAT CAN ACCOMMODATE 721 UP TO AND INCLUDING 1752 FIBRES, DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR ALL PRE-BUILD\nREQUIREMENTS DIRECTLY RELATED TO THE ODF SUCH AS POWER, AIR CON, FLOOR, CABLE RUNWAYS, TIE CABLES, TERMINATION BLOCKS, ETC. LABOUR.\nPROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE PROJECT (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12\nMONTHS) CAPTURING OF ALL AS-BUILD PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER COMPLETION OF THE WORK. (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE\nCOMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS\nITEM IS PER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046109,'CE1.8','CE1.8 ENGR ODF (SML) Γëñ720FBR','This item consists of the detailed engineering of the new generation Optical Distribution Frame (ODF), small up to and including 720 fibres)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Site visits / Surveys,\nb) Detailed Engineering of ODF on Telkom approved system software and submission of an executable file (i.e. Netplan, etc.),\nc) Detailed engineering of the small ODF that can accommodate up to and including 720 fibres,\nd) Detailed engineering for all Pre-Build requirements directly related to the ODF such as power, air con, floor, cable runways, tie cables, termination blocks, etc.,\ne) Labour.\nf) Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\ng) Capturing of all as-build plant / elements after completion of the work. (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per site, each (EA).','EA',3231.82,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.8,ENGR ODF (SML) <720FBR','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.8, TYPE ENGR ODF (SML) <720FBR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SITE VISITS / SURVEYS,\nDETAILED ENGINEERING OF ODF ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE AND SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE (I.E. NETPLAN, ETC.), DETAILED\nENGINEERING OF THE SMALL ODF THAT CAN ACCOMMODATE UP TO AND INCLUDING 720 FIBRES, DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR ALL PRE-BUILD\nREQUIREMENTS DIRECTLY RELATED TO THE ODF SUCH AS POWER, AIR CON, FLOOR, CABLE RUNWAYS, TIE CABLES, TERMINATION BLOCKS, ETC, LABOUR.\nPROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE PROJECT (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12\nMONTHS) CAPTURING OF ALL AS-BUILD PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER COMPLETION OF THE WORK. (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE\nCOMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS\nITEM IS PER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046110,'CE1.7','CE1.7 ENGR OMDF','This item consists of the detailed engineering for an Optic Main Distribution Frame (OMDF) at a new or existing site.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.)\nb) Obtaining work refs.\nc) Site visit / Survey \nd) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\ne) All Labour costs\nf) Project management\ng) Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom / Openserve\nh) Detailed engineering of all OMDF / network elements on Telkom approved system software, \ni) Detailed engineering for recoveries of all types of plant and/or equipment to enable the installation of the OMDF\nj) Submission of an Executable file as per Telkom SpecΓÇÖs, Work Instructions, Method &Procedures, Policies, etc.\nk) Submission of an Executable file with all the relevant recovery information, such as:\na. asset decommissioning form\nb. inventory list of all equipment and cables to be recovered (copper, fibre, cards, modules, racks, sub-racks, etc.)\nl) Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\nm) Capturing of all as-build plant / elements after completion of the work. (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\nn) All travel related costs\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per OMDF site, each (EA)','EA',5853.44,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.7,OMDF','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.7, TYPE OMDF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS\nCONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.) OBTAINING WORK REFS. SITE VISIT / SURVEY\nINTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED ALL LABOUR COSTS PROJECT MANAGEMENT OBTAINING EXISTING\nEND-TO-END RECORDS FROM TELKOM / OPENSERVE DETAILED ENGINEERING OF ALL OMDF / NETWORK ELEMENTS ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE,\nDETAILED ENGINEERING FOR RECOVERIES OF ALL TYPES OF PLANT AND/OR EQUIPMENT TO ENABLE THE INSTALLATION OF THE OMDF SUBMISSION OF AN\nEXECUTABLE FILE AS PER TELKOM SPEC#S, WORK INSTRUCTIONS, METHOD &PROCEDURES, POLICIES, ETC. SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE WITH\nALL THE RELEVANT RECOVERY INFORMATION, SUCH AS: ASSET DECOMMISSIONING FORM INVENTORY LIST OF ALL EQUIPMENT AND CABLES TO BE\nRECOVERED (COPPER, FIBRE, CARDS, MODULES, RACKS, SUB-RACKS, ETC.) PROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE\nPROJECT (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) CAPTURING OF ALL AS-BUILD PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER\nCOMPLETION OF THE WORK. (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nRELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER OMDF SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046111,'CE1.6','CE1.6 ENGR HDF','This item consists of the detailed engineering for a High-Density Frame (HDF) at a new or existing site.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.)\nb) Obtaining work refs.\nc) Site visit / Survey \nd) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\ne) All Labour costs\nf) Project management\ng) Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom / Openserve\nh) Detailed engineering of all HDF / network elements on Telkom approved system software, \ni) Detailed engineering for recoveries of all types of plant and/or equipment to enable the installation of the HDF\nj) Submission of an Executable file as per Telkom SpecΓÇÖs, Work Instructions, Method &Procedures, Policies, etc.\nk) Submission of an Executable file with all the relevant recovery information, such as:\na. asset decommissioning form\nb. inventory list of all equipment and cables to be recovered (copper, fibre, cards, modules, racks, sub-racks, etc.)\nl) Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\nm) Capturing of all as-build plant / elements after completion of the work. (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n \nNote: \na) If the Engineering of the HDF site is requested in conjunction with the Engineering of the Backbone project (i.e. From the Exchange to the FDP) then no additional traveling costs may be charged.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per HDF site, each (EA)','EA',6030.98,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.6,HDF','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.6, TYPE HDF:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS CONTROL\nAPPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.) OBTAINING WORK REFS. SITE VISIT / SURVEY  INTERFACE\nMANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED ALL LABOUR COSTS PROJECT MANAGEMENT OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END\nRECORDS FROM TELKOM / OPENSERVE DETAILED ENGINEERING OF ALL HDF / NETWORK ELEMENTS ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE,  DETAILED\nENGINEERING FOR RECOVERIES OF ALL TYPES OF PLANT AND/OR EQUIPMENT TO ENABLE THE INSTALLATION OF THE HDF SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE\nFILE AS PER TELKOM SPEC#S, WORK INSTRUCTIONS, METHOD &PROCEDURES, POLICIES, ETC. SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE WITH ALL THE\nRELEVANT RECOVERY INFORMATION, SUCH AS: ASSET DECOMMISSIONING FORM INVENTORY LIST OF ALL EQUIPMENT AND CABLES TO BE RECOVERED\n(COPPER, FIBRE, CARDS, MODULES, RACKS, SUB-RACKS, ETC.) PROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE PROJECT (IT IS\nEXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) CAPTURING OF ALL AS-BUILD PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER COMPLETION OF THE\nWORK. (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE\nSERVICE FEE ITEMS) NOTE:  IF THE ENGINEERING OF THE HDF SITE IS REQUESTED IN CONJUNCTION WITH THE ENGINEERING OF THE BACKBONE\nPROJECT (I.E. FROM THE EXCHANGE TO THE FDP) THEN NO ADDITIONAL TRAVELING COSTS MAY BE CHARGED. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS\nITEM IS PER HDF SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046113,'CE1.4','CE1.4 ENG NETW FBR BCKBONE','This item consists of the complete detailed engineering for FTTx on existing or new routes and / or sites consisting of ΓÇô Underground (UG) and / or Overhead (OH) Plant, for backbone fibre routes from the Exchange (Central Office) to the Fibre Distribution Point (FDP).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. manhole / streetbox / Exchange keys etc.)\nb) Obtain