ELDED MANHOLES (MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY) THE UNIT OF MEASURE'),(3046114,'CE1.3','CE1.3 ENG CORE NETW FBR','This item consists of the complete detailed engineering for core fibre on existing or new routes and / or sites consisting of ΓÇô Underground (UG) and / or Overhead (OH) Plant, for fibre routes from Exchange (Central Office) to Exchange or part thereof.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. manhole / streetbox / Exchange keys etc.)\nb) Obtaining work refs.\nc) Site visit / Survey including the exposing / accessing / opening of route access points such as manholes, streetboxes, DPΓÇÖs, housings, boxes, buildings, etc.\nd) Pumping of manholes where necessary, irrespective of site conditions\ne) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nf) Labour\ng) Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom system/s\nh) Detailed engineering of all plant / infrastructure / network elements on Telkom approved system software. (I.e. Fibre, Distribution points, Manholes, junction boxes, pipes, ducts, runways, grids, risers, etc.\ni) Creating of Stac codes for manholes, joints, etc.\nj) Detailed engineering for recoveries of all types of plant and/or equipment\nk) Compilation and submission of wayleaves to Telkom representative / Wayleave section, irrespective of the number of agencies / departments / divisions / utilities, such as municipality, power, water, road, rail, gas, etc.\nl) Update wayleave database / systems & archive the records\nm) Submission of Executable file/s (i.e. KL, LL, recoveries, etc.) as per Telkom SpecΓÇÖs, Work Instructions, Method & Procedures, Policies, etc.\nn) Submission of an Executable file with all the relevant recovery information, such as:\no) asset decommissioning form\np) inventory list of all equipment and cables to be recovered (copper, fibre, etc.)\nq) Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\nr) Capturing of all as-built plant / elements after completion of the work. (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\nb) The opening and closing of welded manholes (May be claimed separately)\n\nNote: The minimum claim for this item is 10km. \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per km of route, each (EA)','KM',1000.00,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.3,CRE NETW FBR','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.3, TYPE CORE NETW FBR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. MANHOLE / STREETBOX / EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.) OBTAINING WORK REFS.\nSITE VISIT / SURVEY INCLUDING THE EXPOSING / ACCESSING / OPENING OF ROUTE ACCESS POINTS SUCH AS MANHOLES, STREETBOXES, DP#S,\nHOUSINGS, BOXES, BUILDINGS, ETC. PUMPING OF MANHOLES WHERE NECESSARY, IRRESPECTIVE OF SITE CONDITIONS INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN\nOR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED LABOUR OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END RECORDS FROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S DETAILED ENGINEERING OF\nALL PLANT / INFRASTRUCTURE / NETWORK ELEMENTS ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE. (I.E. FIBRE, DISTRIBUTION POINTS, MANHOLES,\nJUNCTION BOXES, PIPES, DUCTS, RUNWAYS, GRIDS, RISERS, ETC. CREATING OF STAC CODES FOR MANHOLES, JOINTS, ETC. DETAILED ENGINEERING\nFOR RECOVERIES OF ALL TYPES OF PLANT AND/OR EQUIPMENT COMPILATION AND SUBMISSION OF WAYLEAVES TO TELKOM REPRESENTATIVE / WAYLEAVE\nSECTION, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF AGENCIES / DEPARTMENTS / DIVISIONS / UTILITIES, SUCH AS MUNICIPALITY, POWER, WATER, ROAD,\nRAIL, GAS, ETC. UPDATE WAYLEAVE DATABASE / SYSTEMS & ARCHIVE THE RECORDS SUBMISSION OF EXECUTABLE FILE/S (I.E. KL, LL, RECOVERIES,\nETC.) AS PER TELKOM SPEC#S, WORK INSTRUCTIONS, METHOD & PROCEDURES, POLICIES, ETC. SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE WITH ALL THE\nRELEVANT RECOVERY INFORMATION, SUCH AS: ASSET DECOMMISSIONING FORM INVENTORY LIST OF ALL EQUIPMENT AND CABLES TO BE RECOVERED\n(COPPER, FIBRE, ETC.) PROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE PROJECT (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE\nCOMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) CAPTURING OF ALL AS-BUILT PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER COMPLETION OF THE WORK. (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE\nPROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS) THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE OPENING AND\nCLOSING OF WELDED MANHOLES (MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY) NOTE: THE MINIMUM CLAIM FOR THIS ITEM IS 10KM. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR'),(3046120,'ME20.3','ME20.3 RECVR ME CLNT DVC','This item consists of the recovery of a Metro Ethernet Client Device (i.e. ATN905-V/SAS-E/SAS-D, etc.) at an existing site.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Labour to recover the Metro Ethernet Client device\nb) Recovery of patch tails to metro node \nc) Return of equipment as per decommissioning process\nd) All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.  Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb. Johannesburg.\nc. Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd. Ethekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne. Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata).\nf. Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per site, each (EA).','EA',663.23,'RCVR,EQUIP:ME20.3,ME CLNT DVC','RECOVER, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER ME20.3, TYPE ME CLNT DVC:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE RECOVERY OF A METRO ETHERNET CLIENT DEVICE (I.E.\nATN905-V/SAS-E/SAS-D, ETC.) AT AN EXISTING SITE. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR TO RECOVER THE METRO ETHERNET\nCLIENT DEVICE, RECOVERY OF PATCH TAILS TO METRO NODE, RETURN OF EQUIPMENT AS PER DECOMMISSIONING PROCESS, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS\nWITHIN A 50-KM RADIUS TO AND FROM THE SITE CALCULATED FROM THE FOLLOWING TOWNS: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE,\nVEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY,\nPIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA),\nBLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH\nPOINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SITE, EACH (EA).'),(3046121,'ME10.2','ME10.2 ENG ME CLNT DVC (DL)','This item consists of the detailed Engineering for a new Metro Ethernet Client Device. (i.e. ATN905-V, SAS-D / E /, etc.)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Detailed engineering of the Metro Ethernet device and all Customer premises / Inside Plant / network elements on Telkom approved system software, (i.e. Equipment racks / cabinets, Wireways, device, patch tails, etc.) \nb) Capturing and updating on Netplan (Includes the placement of the Building on NetPlan when required)\nc) Creation of STAC\nd) Application of WAP\ne) Tasking for:\na. Fibre allocations\nb. CTS-Pretesting\nc. RINP ref\nd. WBS creations\nf) Loading of:\na. all cost on SAP/R3 (SAP Estimator)\nb. Deliverables\ng) Submission of Executable file (i.e. DL) including fibre allocations\nh) Capturing/Updating of all as-built elements /device after completion of the installation.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The initial site visit.\nb) Fibre Engineering\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per site, each (EA)','EA',5000.00,'ENGNR,STE:ME10.2,ME CLNT DVC (DL)','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER ME10.2, TYPE ME CLNT DVC (DL):THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR A NEW METRO ETHERNET\nCLIENT DEVICE. (I.E. ATN905-V, SAS-D / E /, ET