d (copper, fibre, cards, modules, racks, sub-racks, etc.)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) The initial site visit.\n\nNote: \na) This item may be only be claimed once per customer site irrespective of the number of services required.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per customer site, each (EA)','EA',5500.00,'ENGNR,STE:ME10.3,ME FBR (KL)','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER ME10.3, TYPE ME FBR (KL):THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE COMPLETE DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR A METRO-ETHERNET\nCUSTOMER SITE (ME ORDER/S) ON EXISTING OR NEW FIBRE ROUTES FROM THE FDP TO THE CUSTOMER PREMISES EQUIPMENT. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT\nIS NOT LIMITED TO: OBTAINING WORK REFS., LABOUR, OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END RECORDS FROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S, DETAILED ENGINEERING\nOF ALL PLANT / INFRASTRUCTURE / NETWORK ELEMENTS FROM THE FDP TO THE CUSTOMER SITE, ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE. (I.E. FIBRE\n/ COPPER CABLES, DISTRIBUTION POINTS, MANHOLES, JUNCTION BOXES, PIPES, DUCTS, RUNWAYS, GRIDS, RISERS, ETC. (INCLUDES THE PLACEMENT\nOF THE BUILDING ON NETPLAN WHEN REQUIRED), CREATING AND REGISTERING OF STAC CODES FOR MANHOLES, FDP#S ETC., DETAILED ENGINEERING\nFOR RECOVERIES OF ALL TYPES OF PLANT AND/OR EQUIPMENT, COMPILATION AND SUBMISSION OF WAYLEAVES TO TELKOM REPRESENTATIVE / WAYLEAVE\nSECTION, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF AGENCIES / DEPARTMENTS / DIVISIONS / UTILITIES, SUCH AS MUNICIPALITY, POWER, WATER, ROAD,\nRAIL, GAS, ETC., UPDATE WAYLEAVE DATABASE / SYSTEMS & ARCHIVE THE RECORDS, SUBMISSION OF EXECUTABLE FILE/S (I.E. KL, RECOVERIES,\nETC.) AS PER TELKOM SPEC#S, WORK INSTRUCTIONS, METHOD & PROCEDURES, POLICIES, ETC., SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE WITH ALL THE\nRELEVANT RECOVERY INFORMATION, SUCH AS: ASSET DECOMMISSIONING FORM, INVENTORY LIST OF ALL EQUIPMENT AND CABLES TO BE RECOVERED\n(COPPER, FIBRE, CARDS, MODULES, RACKS, SUB-RACKS, ETC.), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS WITHIN A 50-KM RADIUS TO AND FROM THE SITE, WHEN\nNECESSARY FOR VO#S AND COMPLETIONS, CALCULATED FROM THE FOLLOWING TOWNS: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING,\nRUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY,\nPIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA),\nBLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY BE ONLY BE CLAIMED ONCE PER CUSTOMER SITE IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SERVICES'),(3046124,'ME20.2','ME20.2 INSTALL GE SFP','This item consists of the Installation and commissioning of GE SFP/s relating directly to a Metro Ethernet service/s on site at the customer premises and / or Exchange site.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Labour to install and commission the Metro Ethernet GE SFP/s,\nb) Minor build material\nc) Transportation of minor materials / equipment, tools to and from site.  \nd) All travel related costs\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Supply of the GE SFP/s\n\nNote: \na) This is a standalone item which may not be used in conjunction with a ME Client Device installation item.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per site, each (EA)','EA',300.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:ME20.2,GE SFP','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER ME20.2, TYPE GE SFP:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE INSTALLATION AND COMMISSIONING OF GE SFP/S RELATING\nDIRECTLY TO A METRO ETHERNET SERVICE/S ON SITE AT THE CUSTOMER PREMISES AND / OR EXCHANGE SITE. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT\nLIMITED TO: LABOUR TO INSTALL AND COMMISSION THE METRO ETHERNET GE SFP/S, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL, TRANSPORTATION OF MINOR MATERIALS /\nEQUIPMENT, TOOLS TO AND FROM SITE, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS WITHIN A 50-KM RADIUS TO AND FROM THE SITE CALCULATED FROM THE\nFOLLOWING TOWNS: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN),\nWORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT\nELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: SUPPLY OF THE GE\nSFP/S, TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). NOTE: THIS IS A\nSTANDALONE ITEM WHICH MAY NOT BE USED IN CONJUNCTION WITH A ME CLIENT DEVICE INSTALLATION ITEM. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS\nITEM IS PER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046125,'ME20.1','ME20.1 INSTL CLNT DVC','This item consists of the complete installation and commissioning of a Metro-Ethernet Client Device (i.e. ATN 905, SAS-D, SAS-E, etc.) and service/s from the network connection point to the device on all technologies (i.e. Fibre, copper, MW, VSAT, etc.)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \na) Making and / or confirming customer appointment.\nb) Arranging and obtaining all site access approvals\nc) All project management and administrative activities\nd) Tasking the appropriate sections on Telkom tasking system/s (i.e. Soak & Management, Removal of Soak, Request QA & Build task completed activities, etc.)\ne) Dispatching resources and all Logistical activities \nf) Obtaining all work refs\ng) The complete Installation of the ME client device (e.g. ATN905-V/SAS-E/SAS-D), Power cable, earth cable, patch cords, all SFP/s (both the exchange and the customer site), etc.\nh) Supply of all Minor material (e.g. cable ties, Velcro straps, Labels, etc.)\ni) Confirmation of metro levels (node and customer)\nj) Labelling\nk) Commissioning and testing of the ME client device (Ports and Uplink) as per the relevant Acceptance Test Procedure (ATP) for ATN 905V/SAS D/E, etc.\nl) Recording and updating of all the necessary information on the relevant Telkom systems / platforms\nm) Storage and local shipping / transport to regional despatch points for all equipment and material.\nn) Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from the site \no) Quality and Safety activities / inspections \np) Site management\nq) Taking and submitting photos of the complete installation for QA purposes\nr) All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.  Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb. Johannesburg.\nc. Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd. Ethekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne. Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata).\nf. Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n\nThe rate excludes the Supply of:\na) Client device (Telkom to supply)\nb) Patch cord (Telkom to supply)\n\nThe specifications for this item:\na) CTO- 011636.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per Client device, each (EA)','EA',7039.68,'INSTL,EQUIP:ME20.1,CLNT DVC','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER ME20.1, TYPE CLNT DVC:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION AND COMMISSIONING OF A\nMETRO-ETHERNET CLIENT DEVICE (I.E. ATN 905, SAS-D, SAS-E, ETC.) AND SERVICE/S FROM THE NETWORK CONNECTION POINT TO THE DEVICE ON\nALL TECHNOLOGIES (I.E. FIBRE, COPPER, MW, VSAT, ETC.). THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MAKING AND / OR CONFIRMING CUSTOMER\nAPPOINTMENT, ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS APPROVALS, ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES, TASKING THE\nAPPROPRIATE SECTIONS ON TELKOM TASKING SYSTEM/S (I.E. SOAK & MANAGEMENT, REMOVAL OF SOAK, REQUEST QA & BUILD TASK COMPLETED\nACTIVITIES, ETC.), DISPATCHING RESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL ACTIVITIES, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS, THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION OF THE\nME CLIENT DEVICE (E.G. ATN905-V/SAS-E/SAS-D), POWER CABLE, EARTH CABLE, PATCH CORDS, ALL SFP/S (BOTH THE EXCHANGE AND THE CUSTOMER\nSITE), ETC., SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (E.G. CABLE TIES, VELCRO STRAPS, LABELS, ETC.), CONFIRMATION OF METRO LEVELS (NODE AND\nCUSTOMER), LABELLING, COMMISSIONING AND TESTING OF THE ME CLIENT DEVICE (PORTS AND UPLINK) AS PER THE RELEVANT ACCEPTANCE TEST\nPROCEDURE (ATP) FOR ATN 905V/SAS D/E, ETC., RECORDING AND UPDATING OF ALL THE NECESSARY INFORMATION ON THE RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS\n/ PLATFORMS, STORAGE AND LOCAL SHIPPING / TRANSPORT TO REGIONAL DESPATCH POINTS FOR ALL EQUIPMENT AND MATERIAL, TRANSPORTATION OF\nALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM THE SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE MANAGEMENT, TAKING AND\nSUBMITTING PHOTOS OF THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION FOR QA PURPOSES, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS WITHIN A 50-KM RADIUS TO AND FROM THE SITE\nCALCULATED FROM THE FOLLOWING TOWNS: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE\n(CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA\nMETROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES THE'),(3046615,'CI2.49','CI2.49 HIRE HSTNG EQUIP','This item consists of the hiring of a mechanical hoisting equipment (i.e. Cherry picker, hoist platform, sky jack, etc.) for the installation of Network Infrastructure where the installation height exceeds the health and safety limit for ladders.\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	Obtaining all necessary Work Authorizations and site access control approvals,\nb.	Making access arrangements including the obtaining of keys / access devices from the landlord (i.e. Exchange / gate / building keys, etc.),\nc.	Hiring of the hoist equipment,\nd.	The labour costs of the hoist equipment operator, \ne.	All travel related costs within a 50km radius from the nominated dispatch point.\nNotes: \na.	This item may be claimed in conjunction with the installation items,\nb.	The use of this item is subject to approval from Openserve.\nThe rate excludes:\na.	Travel related costs >50km radius of the nominated dispatch point (See Service fee document).\nThe unit of measure for this item is per estimate per site, each (EA).','EA',1.00,'CI2.49 HIRE HSTNG EQUIP','HIRE, EQUIPMENT:TYPE CI2.49 HSTNG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: A) OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORK AUTHORIZATIONS AND SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS, B) MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS INCLUDING THE OBTAINING OF KEYS / ACCESS DEVICES FROM THE LANDLORD (I.E.\nEXCHANGE / GATE / BUILDING KEYS, ETC.), C) HIRING OF THE HOIST EQUIPMENT, D) THE LABOUR COSTS OF THE HOIST EQUIPMENT OPERATOR, E)\nALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS WITHIN A 50KM RADIUS FROM THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT. NOTES: A) THIS ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED IN CONJUNCTION\nWITH THE INSTALLATION ITEMS, B) THE USE OF THIS ITEM IS SUBJECT TO APPROVAL FROM OPENSERVE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: A) TRAVEL RELATED\nCOSTS >50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ESTIMATE\nPER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046702,'CE3.2','CE3.2 UPDT WRKBOOK NEW INFRASTRUCT','This item consists of the updating of new infrastructure after the completion of TBI / maintenance project/s.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Receive workbook back with information of new infrastructure after the completion of TBI / maintenance project/s\n2) Update all relevant Telkom systems (i.e. NedLMP, Netplan)\n3) Task for QA\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per workbook, per TBI / maintenance project, each (EA)','EA',150.00,'EDIT,MDA:CE3.2 WRKBOOK NW INFRASTRUCT','EDIT, MEDIA:TYPE CE3.2 WRKBOOK NEW INFRASTRUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: RECEIVE WORKBOOK BACK WITH INFORMATION OF\nNEW INFRASTRUCTURE AFTER THE COMPLETION OF TBI / MAINTENANCE PROJECT/S, UPDATE ALL RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS (I.E. NEDLMP, NETPLAN),\nTASK FOR QA. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER WORKBOOK, PER TBI / MAINTENANCE PROJECT, EACH (EA)'),(3046703,'CI1.67','CI1.67 LCT, CLEAN, PROVE EXSTG PIPE','This item consists of the locating, cleaning and proving of existing pipe/s (110mm and above), installed by developers / road developers.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Measuring actual length of existing pipe cleaned\n2) Testing of the pipe in both directions\n3) Cost to supply ski rope, brush, mandrill or test piece of cable \n\nNote:  This item may not be claimed:\n1) In conjunction with hauling / over-hauling\n2) When laying new pipes\n\nThe specification:\n325A, SP-0325\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per pipe, per meter, MT','MT',30.00,'PAY,FEE:CI1.67 LCT, CLN, PRV EX PIPE','PAY, FEE:TYPE CI1.67 LCT, CLN, PRV EX PIPE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MEASURING ACTUAL LENGTH OF EXISTING PIPE\nCLEANED, TESTING OF THE PIPE IN BOTH DIRECTIONS, COST TO SUPPLY SKI ROPE, BRUSH, MANDRILL OR TEST PIECE OF CABLE. NOTE: THIS ITEM\nMAY NOT BE CLAIMED: IN CONJUNCTION WITH HAULING / OVER-HAULING, WHEN LAYING NEW PIPES. THE SPECIFICATION: 325A, SP-0325. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PIPE, PER METER, M'),(3046704,'CE1.12','CE1.12 ENG ACES FBR CMPLTN (KL)','This item consists of the amendments of the detailed Engineering during Build and the Capturing of all as-built plant / elements after completion of the work for a Service-On-Demand customer Access fibre (excluding Metro-Ethernet / FTTx) on existing or new routes and / or sites consisting of ΓÇô Underground (UG) and / or Overhead (OH) Plant, and / or Inside Plant, and / or Customer Premises Equipment.  \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \n1) Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project  \n2) Capturing/Updating of all as-built plant / elements after completion of the work on Telkom approved system software (i.e. NetPlan).  \n3) Tasking to ECC  \n4) All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site: \na. Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg. \nb. Johannesburg. \nc. Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam \nd. Ethekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle. \ne. Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata). \nf. Bloemfontein, Kimberley.  \n\nThe rate excludes: \nTravel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).  \n\nNote: This item may only be claimed  \n1) Once per customer site, irrespective of the number of services required\n2) Once in conjunction with Access Fibre engineering executable \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per customer site, each (EA)','EA',2000.00,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.12,ACES FBR CMPLTN (KL)','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.12, TYPE ACES FBR CMPLTN (KL):THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: PROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION\nORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE PROJECT, CAPTURING/UPDATING OF ALL AS-BUILT PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER COMPLETION OF THE WORK ON TELKOM\nAPPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE (I.E. NETPLAN), TASKING TO ECC, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE FOLLOWING DISPATCH\nPOINTS, TO AND FROM THE SITE: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE\nTOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA\nMETROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES:\nTRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY\nONLY BE CLAIMED, ONCE PER CUSTOMER SITE, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SERVICES REQUIRED, ONCE IN CONJUNCTION WITH ACCESS FIBRE\nENGINEERING EXECUTABLE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUSTOMER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046705,'CE3.1','CE3.1 CMPL WRKBOOK EXSTG TELKOM INFRASTRUCT','This item consists of the compilation of a workbook template on Telkom system/s (i.e. NedLMP) indicating the existing Telkom infrastructure for the execution of TBI / maintenance projects.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Obtaining existing Telkom infrastructure records from the system (i.e. NedLMP) \n2) Compiling a workbook template with existing Telkom infrastructure information (i.e. topographical location, job description, etc.) to assist in the execution of TBI / maintenance project/s\n3) Update all relevant Telkom system/s (i.e. NedLMP)\n4) Populate the workbook via email to the Telkom SPOC / CR\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per workbook, per TBI / maintenance project, each (EA)','EA',60.00,'CRET,DOC:CE3.1 WRKBK EX TKM INFR','CREATE, DOCUMENT:TYPE CE3.1 WRKBOOK EXSTG TELKOM INFRASTRUCT:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: OBTAINING EXISTING TELKOM\nINFRASTRUCTURE RECORDS FROM THE SYSTEM (I.E. NEDLMP), COMPILING A WORKBOOK TEMPLATE WITH EXISTING TELKOM INFRASTRUCTURE INFORMATION\n(I.E. TOPOGRAPHICAL LOCATION, JOB DESCRIPTION, ETC.) TO ASSIST IN THE EXECUTION OF TBI / MAINTENANCE PROJECT/S, UPDATE ALL RELEVANT\nTELKOM SYSTEM/S (I.E. NEDLMP), POPULATE THE WORKBOOK VIA EMAIL TO THE TELKOM SPOC / CR. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS\nPER WORKBOOK, PER TBI / MAINTENANCE PROJECT, EACH (EA)'),(3046706,'CE1.11','CE1.11 ENG ACES FBR (KL)','This item consists of the complete detailed engineering for a Service-On-Demand customer Access fibre (excluding Metro-Ethernet / FTTx) on existing or new Fibre routes from the FDP to the customer premises equipment.  \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \n1) Obtaining work refs. \n2) Labour \n3) Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom system/s \n4) Detailed engineering of all plant / infrastructure / network elements from the FDP to the customer site, on Telkom approved system software. (I.e. Fibre / copper cables, Distribution points, Manholes, junction boxes, pipes, ducts, runways, grids, risers, etc. (Includes the placement of the Building on NetPlan when required) \n5) Creating and registering of STAC codes for manholes, FDPΓÇÖs etc. \n6) Detailed engineering for recoveries of all types of plant and/or equipment \n7) Compilation and submission of wayleaves to Telkom representative / Wayleave section, irrespective of the number of agencies / departments / divisions / utilities, such as municipality, power, water, road, rail, gas, etc. \n8) Update wayleave database / systems & archive the records \n9) Submission of Executable file/s (i.e. KL, recoveries, etc.) as per Telkom SpecΓÇÖs, Work Instructions, Method & Procedures, Policies, etc. \n10) Submission of an Executable file with all the relevant recovery information, such as: asset decommissioning form inventory list of all equipment and cables to be recovered (copper, fibre, cards, modules, racks, sub-racks, etc.)  \n\nThe rate excludes: \n1) The initial site visit\n\nNote:  This item may only be claimed once per customer site irrespective of the number of services required.  \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per customer site, each (EA)','EA',5500.00,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.11,ACES FBR (KL)','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.11, TYPE ACES FBR (KL):THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: OBTAINING WORK REFS., LABOUR,\nOBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END RECORDS FROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S, DETAILED ENGINEERING OF ALL PLANT / INFRASTRUCTURE / NETWORK ELEMENTS\nFROM THE FDP TO THE CUSTOMER SITE, ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE. (I.E. FIBRE / COPPER CABLES, DISTRIBUTION POINTS, MANHOLES,\nJUNCTION BOXES, PIPES, DUCTS, RUNWAYS, GRIDS, RISERS, ETC. (INCLUDES THE PLACEMENT OF THE BUILDING ON NETPLAN WHEN REQUIRED),\nCREATING AND REGISTERING OF STAC CODES FOR MANHOLES, FDP#S ETC., DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR RECOVERIES OF ALL TYPES OF PLANT AND/OR\nEQUIPMENT, COMPILATION AND SUBMISSION OF WAYLEAVES TO TELKOM REPRESENTATIVE / WAYLEAVE SECTION, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF\nAGENCIES / DEPARTMENTS / DIVISIONS / UTILITIES, SUCH AS MUNICIPALITY, POWER, WATER, ROAD, RAIL, GAS, ETC., UPDATE WAYLEAVE DATABASE\n/ SYSTEMS & ARCHIVE THE RECORDS, SUBMISSION OF EXECUTABLE FILE/S (I.E. KL, RECOVERIES, ETC.) AS PER TELKOM SPEC#S, WORK\nINSTRUCTIONS, METHOD & PROCEDURES, POLICIES, ETC., SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE WITH ALL THE RELEVANT RECOVERY INFORMATION,\nSUCH AS: ASSET DECOMMISSIONING FORM INVENTORY LIST OF ALL EQUIPMENT AND CABLES TO BE RECOVERED (COPPER, FIBRE, CARDS, MODULES,\nRACKS, SUB-RACKS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE INITIAL SITE VISIT. NOTE:  THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE CLAIMED ONCE PER CUSTOMER SITE\nIRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SERVICES REQUIRED. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUSTOMER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046709,'CE1.10','CE1.10 ENG SITE VISIT (EXCL ME & FTTX)','This item consists of a site visit, full investigation, detailed engineering survey for a customer on all new and / or existing technologies excluding ME and FTTx up to and including the Customer Premises Equipment and the creation of an RFO (Requirement for Occupation) Specification document for the customer site. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \n1) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. manhole / Exchange keys etc.) \n2) Informing the CNFO supervisors per e-mail 48 hours prior to site investigations. \n3) Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements with CNFO sites and customer sites. \n4) Making appointments with MCO Spoc within 48 hours at new building sites.  \n5) Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom system/s  \n6) Conducting a site visit at the customer premises and exchange site when required, \n7) Clarification of the requirements with the customer on site \n8) Obtaining written permission from the customer / Landlord or their contact details \n9) Administration costs \n10) A full technology investigation and solutions (Single site investigations and / or bulk customer orders) \n11) Performing a detailed engineering survey including the exposing / accessing / opening of route access points such as manholes, FDP, FTH, housings, boxes, buildings, etc. \n12) Pumping of manholes where necessary, irrespective of site conditions \n13) Providing the sketches of the requirements (i.e. fibre entry / route, power, cable trays, rack, floor plan, ducts, etc.) as well as related information including photos, spider diagram, tick sheets, etc. \n14) The compilation of the RFO Spec document/s including pipe entries, AC / DC power, ducting, wireways, etc. \n15) Attaching photos or drawings of RFO requirements on RFO specifications. \n16) Compiling and submitting an RFO build Estimate/Quotation  \n17) Submitting and/or attaching all information including completed RFO Specification. \n18) Obtaining / confirming GPS co-ordinates. \n19) Obtaining all required information to place the site building on Netplan \n20) Supplying the DP number (pole or indoor DP). \n21) If possible SDC number and/or telephone numbers. \n22) Updating all documentation / system requirements \n23) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required \n24) Labour \n25) Administration costs \n26) All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site: \na. Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg. \nb. Johannesburg. \nc. Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam \nd. Ethekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle. \ne. Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata). \nf. Bloemfontein, Kimberley.  \n\nThe rate excludes: \n1) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).  \n\nNote:  This item may only be claimed once per customer site irrespective of the number of services / serials required.  \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per customer site, each (EA)','EA',4500.00,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.10,EXCL ME & FTTX','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.10, TYPE EXCL ME & FTTX:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE\nACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. MANHOLE / EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), INFORMING THE CNFO SUPERVISORS\nPER E-MAIL 48 HOURS PRIOR TO SITE INVESTIGATIONS, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS WITH CNFO\nSITES AND CUSTOMER SITES, MAKING APPOINTMENTS WITH MCO SPOC WITHIN 48 HOURS AT NEW BUILDING SITES, OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END\nRECORDS FROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S, CONDUCTING A SITE VISIT AT THE CUSTOMER PREMISES AND EXCHANGE SITE WHEN REQUIRED, CLARIFICATION OF\nTHE REQUIREMENTS WITH THE CUSTOMER ON SITE, OBTAINING WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM THE CUSTOMER / LANDLORD OR THEIR CONTACT DETAILS,\nADMINISTRATION COSTS, A FULL TECHNOLOGY INVESTIGATION AND SOLUTIONS (SINGLE SITE INVESTIGATIONS AND / OR BULK CUSTOMER ORDERS),\nPERFORMING A DETAILED ENGINEERING SURVEY INCLUDING THE EXPOSING / ACCESSING / OPENING OF ROUTE ACCESS POINTS SUCH AS MANHOLES, FDP,\nFTH, HOUSINGS, BOXES, BUILDINGS, ETC., PUMPING OF MANHOLES WHERE NECESSARY, IRRESPECTIVE OF SITE CONDITIONS, PROVIDING THE SKETCHES\nOF THE REQUIREMENTS (I.E. FIBRE ENTRY / ROUTE, POWER, CABLE TRAYS, RACK, FLOOR PLAN, DUCTS, ETC.) AS WELL AS RELATED INFORMATION\nINCLUDING PHOTOS, SPIDER DIAGRAM, TICK SHEETS, ETC., THE COMPILATION OF THE RFO SPEC DOCUMENT/S INCLUDING PIPE ENTRIES, AC / DC\nPOWER, DUCTING, WIREWAYS, ETC., ATTACHING PHOTOS OR DRAWINGS OF RFO REQUIREMENTS ON RFO SPECIFICATIONS, COMPILING AND SUBMITTING AN\nRFO BUILD ESTIMATE/QUOTATION, SUBMITTING AND/OR ATTACHING ALL INFORMATION INCLUDING COMPLETED RFO SPECIFICATION, OBTAINING /\nCONFIRMING GPS CO-ORDINATES, OBTAINING ALL REQUIRED INFORMATION TO PLACE THE SITE BUILDING ON NETPLAN, SUPPLYING THE DP NUMBER\n(POLE OR INDOOR DP), IF POSSIBLE SDC NUMBER AND/OR TELEPHONE NUMBERS, UPDATING ALL DOCUMENTATION / SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS, INTERFACE\nMANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, LABOUR, ADMINISTRATION COSTS, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM'),(3046758,'CI1.65','CI1.65 LPS PROJ','This item consists of all the Services and / or Goods to complete the scope of an all-inclusive Lump Sum (LPS) Network Infrastructure project.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Site visits / Surveys, \nb) Detailed engineering, \nc) All pre-build and build activities, \nd) All integration activities, \ne) Obtaining all necessary working refs and site access control approvals, \nf) Making access arrangements including the obtaining of keys / access devices from the landlord (Exchange / gate / building keys), \ng) Environmental, Health and Safety Controls / Requirements / Medical screening, \nh) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required, \ni) Obtaining all quality acceptance documents from the relevant sections in Openserve on completion of work, \nj) Updating the Telkom approved system software, \nk) Submission of an updated executable file, \nl) Compiling the wayleave documents for all utilities / authorities and submitting them to the Telkom representative for application,  \nm) Project management, \nn) Site management, \no) Labour, \np) Tools and Test Equipment, \nq) Supply and installation of all required materials, equipment and licences, \nr) Labelling in accordance to Telkom specifications if required, \ns) All testing and commissioning (including management interfaces), \nt) All travel related costs such as:\ni. Vehicle costs, \nii. Fuel, \niii. Travelling losses (Labour), \niv. Accommodation, \nv. S&T, \nvi. Flights, \nvii. Vehicle hire, \nviii. Toll fees\nu) Transportation of material, equipment, and tools to and from site, \nv) Shipping (local and foreign), \nw) Storage, \nx) All other requirements, \ny) Site security, \nz) Updating of all documentation, \naa) Updating of Telkom systems. \n\nNote: This item may include some or all the activities listed above depending on the Scope of the project. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item per lump sum project, each (EA)','EA',1.00,'PAY,FEE:CI1.65 LUMP SUM PROJ','PAY, FEE:PURPOSE CI1.65 LUMP SUM PROJ:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SITE VISITS / SURVEYS, DETAILED ENGINEERING, ALL\nPRE-BUILD AND BUILD ACTIVITIES, ALL INTEGRATION ACTIVITIES, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND SITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS,\nMAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS INCLUDING THE OBTAINING OF KEYS / ACCESS DEVICES FROM THE LANDLORD (EXCHANGE / GATE / BUILDING KEYS),\nENVIRONMENTAL, HEALTH AND SAFETY CONTROLS / REQUIREMENTS / MEDICAL SCREENING, INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM\nSUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, OBTAINING ALL QUALITY ACCEPTANCE DOCUMENTS FROM THE RELEVANT SECTIONS IN OPENSERVE ON COMPLETION OF\nWORK, UPDATING THE TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE, SUBMISSION OF AN UPDATED EXECUTABLE FILE, COMPILING THE WAYLEAVE DOCUMENTS FOR\nALL UTILITIES / AUTHORITIES AND SUBMITTING THEM TO THE TELKOM REPRESENTATIVE FOR APPLICATION, PROJECT MANAGEMENT, SITE MANAGEMENT,\nLABOUR, TOOLS AND TEST EQUIPMENT, SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF ALL REQUIRED MATERIALS, EQUIPMENT AND LICENCES, LABELLING IN\nACCORDANCE TO TELKOM SPECIFICATIONS IF REQUIRED, ALL TESTING AND COMMISSIONING (INCLUDING MANAGEMENT INTERFACES), ALL TRAVEL\nRELATED COSTS SUCH AS: VEHICLE COSTS, FUEL, TRAVELLING LOSSES (LABOUR), ACCOMMODATION, S&T, FLIGHTS, VEHICLE HIRE, TOLL FEES,\nTRANSPORTATION OF MATERIAL, EQUIPMENT, AND TOOLS TO AND FROM SITE, SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE, ALL OTHER REQUIREMENTS,\nSITE SECURITY, UPDATING OF ALL DOCUMENTATION, UPDATING OF TELKOM SYSTEMS. NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY INCLUDE SOME OR ALL THE ACTIVITIES\nLISTED ABOVE DEPENDING ON THE SCOPE OF THE PROJECT. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM PER LUMP SUM PROJECT, EACH (EA)'),(3046801,'CI3.31','CI3.31 INSTL GALV PIPE 100MM: BRDG XNG','This item consists of the supply and installation of 100mm (internal diameter) galvanised pipe/s for bridge crossings, in accordance with the requirements of local authorities\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply and installation of the 100mm galvanised metal pipe (internal diameter) - SPECIFY WALL THICKNESS AND CLASS OF PIPE 3.9 ΓÇô 4.5 mm\nb) The cleating / fastening of the pipe (i.e. to structures, bridge, etc.), \nc) The supply of the cleating material. (Galvanized steel tape, buckles, saddles etc.), as per requirement set out by Local Authorities\nd) The installing of all sizes and types of cable / ducts in the pipe when required,\ne) The supply of minor material (i.e. bends, joints, galvanised steel tape, buckles, etc.),\nf) Telkom shall furnish approved drawings by the respective road and rail authorities, illustrating approaches and methods to be used to attach pipes to bridge structures, to the Service Provider.\ng) Supply of all pipes and fittings (must be galvanised in accordance with the requirements of SANS 121 / SABS ISO 1461: Hot-dip (galvanized) zinc coatings (other than on continuously zinc coated sheet and wire)). The fittings must be treated with a 10% solution of hydrochloric acid, washed down with clear water dried completely (in order for the paint to adhere to the surface) and finally painted as follows: \ni. 1st Coat: Epidermix 352 Black\nii. 2nd Coat: Epidermix 352 Aluminium\nh) Supply of approved expansion joints and pipe butt joints where required on structures.\ni) Reinstatement of all other surfaces when cleating pipe.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',400.00,'INSTL,PIPE:CI3.31,BRDG XNG,100MM,GALV','INSTALL, PIPE:ITEM NUMBER CI3.31, TYPE BRDG XNG, SIZE 100 MM, MATERIAL GALV, ADDITIONAL TASK SUPPLY:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT\nLIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF THE 100MM GALVANISED METAL PIPE (INTERNAL DIAMETER) - SPECIFY WALL THICKNESS AND CLASS\nOF PIPE 3.9 # 4.5 MM, THE CLEATING / FASTENING OF THE PIPE (I.E. TO STRUCTURES, BRIDGE, ETC.), THE SUPPLY OF THE CLEATING MATERIAL.\n(GALVANIZED STEEL TAPE, BUCKLES, SADDLES ETC.), AS PER REQUIREMENT SET OUT BY LOCAL AUTHORITIES, THE INSTALLING OF ALL SIZES AND\nTYPES OF CABLE / DUCTS IN THE PIPE WHEN REQUIRED, THE SUPPLY OF MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. BENDS, JOINTS, GALVANISED STEEL TAPE, BUCKLES,\nETC.), TELKOM SHALL FURNISH APPROVED DRAWINGS BY THE RESPECTIVE ROAD AND RAIL AUTHORITIES, ILLUSTRATING APPROACHES AND METHODS TO\nBE USED TO ATTACH PIPES TO BRIDGE STRUCTURES, TO THE SERVICE PROVIDER, SUPPLY OF ALL PIPES AND FITTINGS (MUST BE GALVANISED IN\nACCORDANCE WITH THE REQUIREMENTS OF SANS 121 / SABS ISO 1461: HOT-DIP (GALVANIZED) ZINC COATINGS (OTHER THAN ON CONTINUOUSLY ZINC\nCOATED SHEET AND WIRE)). THE FITTINGS MUST BE TREATED WITH A 10% SOLUTION OF HYDROCHLORIC ACID, WASHED DOWN WITH CLEAR WATER DRIED\nCOMPLETELY (IN ORDER FOR THE PAINT TO ADHERE TO THE SURFACE) AND FINALLY PAINTED AS FOLLOWS: 1ST COAT: EPIDERMIX 352 BLACK, 2ND\nCOAT: EPIDERMIX 352 ALUMINIUM, SUPPLY OF APPROVED EXPANSION JOINTS AND PIPE BUTT JOINTS WHERE REQUIRED ON STRUCTURES, REINSTATEMENT\nOF ALL OTHER SURFACES WHEN CLEATING PIPE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT)'),(3046810,'CI5.1','CI5.1 MINR SCP CHNG','This item consists of a Minor Scope Change / Deviation to a contracted Service.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Assessing the deviation from an existing service item/s,\n2) Providing a detailed quote for the deviation,\n3) Submission to Telkom for approval,\n4) Executing the minor scope change within the contracted timelines\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) Changes to the price of a contracted item,\n2) Services not provided for in the scope of the contract,\n\nNote:  \n1) This item may only be used after obtaining an approval reference number from the approval committee. \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per Minor Scope Change, each (EA)','EA',1.00,'PAY,FEE:CI5.1 MINR SCP CHNG','PAY, FEE:PURPOSE CI5.1 MINR SCP CHNG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ASSESSING THE DEVIATION FROM AN EXISTING SERVICE\nITEM/S, PROVIDING A DETAILED QUOTE FOR THE DEVIATION, SUBMISSION TO TELKOM FOR APPROVAL, EXECUTING THE MINOR SCOPE CHANGE WITHIN\nTHE CONTRACTED TIMELINES. THE RATE EXCLUDES: CHANGES TO THE PRICE OF A CONTRACTED ITEM, SERVICES NOT PROVIDED FOR IN THE SCOPE OF\nTHE CONTRACT. NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED AFTER OBTAINING AN APPROVAL REFERENCE NUMBER FROM THE APPROVAL COMMITTEE. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER MINOR SCOPE CHANGE, EACH (EA)'),(3046863,'MEA2.6','MEA2.6 INSTL AGGRN DVC: ATN950','This item consists of the complete installation, commissioning, and testing of Aggregate Device (i.e. ATN950, etc.)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1)	Making and/or confirming customer appointment\n2)	Arranging and obtaining all site access approvals\n3)	All project management and administrative activities\n4)	Dispatching resources and all logistical activities\n5)	Obtaining all work refs\n6)	The complete installation of the Aggregate device (i.e. ATN950, etc.), power cable, earth cable, patch cords, all SFPΓÇÖs, E1 cables, tie cables, T&P frame (in rack), connection of TMNET cable to device, connection of E1 for Sync to existing network.  (only in Exchange)\n7)	Installation, termination and testing of a new set of E1, 15-way T&P, and tie cables (filotex) from the bay to a test and patch position for the 2Meg service (as per planning) when required (maximum 32 TX and 32 RX pairs per card.)\n8)	Minor build material (i.e. cable ties, Velcro straps, labels, etc.)\n9)	Confirmation of Optical levels (nodes and customer)\n10)	Labelling\n11)	Commissioning and testing of the Aggregate device (Ports and Uplink, as per the relevant Acceptance Test Procedure (ATP) for ATN950, etc.\n12)	Recording and updating of all the necessary information on the relevant Telkom systems / platforms\n13)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site\n14)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections\n15)	Site management\n16)	Taking and submitting photos of the complete installation for QA purposes\n17)	All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.	Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb.	Johannesburg.\nc.	Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd.	eThekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne.	Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata)\nf.	Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1)	Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n2)	Supply of the Aggregate device (Telkom to supply)\n3)	Supply of Patch cord (Telkom to supply)\n4)	Filotex Cable, plugs and krone blocks and krone labels\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per ATN950 Aggregate device, each (EA)','EA',7039.68,'INSTL,EQUIP:MEA2.6,ATN950','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER MEA2.6, TYPE ATN950:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MAKING AND/OR CONFIRMING CUSTOMER\nAPPOINTMENT, ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS APPROVALS, ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES, DISPATCHING\nRESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL ACTIVITIES, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS, THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION OF THE AGGREGATE DEVICE (I.E. ATN950,\nETC.), POWER CABLE, EARTH CABLE, PATCH CORDS, ALL SFP#S, E1 CABLES, TIE CABLES, T&P FRAME (IN RACK), CONNECTION OF TMNET CABLE TO\nDEVICE, CONNECTION OF E1 FOR SYNC TO EXISTING NETWORK.  (ONLY IN EXCHANGE), INSTALLATION, TERMINATION AND TESTING OF A NEW SET OF\nE1, 15-WAY T&P, AND TIE CABLES (FILOTEX) FROM THE BAY TO A TEST AND PATCH POSITION FOR THE 2MEG SERVICE (AS PER PLANNING) WHEN\nREQUIRED (MAXIMUM 32 TX AND 32 RX PAIRS PER CARD.), MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, VELCRO STRAPS, LABELS, ETC.),\nCONFIRMATION OF OPTICAL LEVELS (NODES AND CUSTOMER), LABELLING, COMMISSIONING AND TESTING OF THE AGGREGATE DEVICE (PORTS AND\nUPLINK, AS PER THE RELEVANT ACCEPTANCE TEST PROCEDURE (ATP) FOR ATN950, ETC., RECORDING AND UPDATING OF ALL THE NECESSARY\nINFORMATION ON THE RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS / PLATFORMS, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE,\nQUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE MANAGEMENT, TAKING AND SUBMITTING PHOTOS OF THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION FOR QA\nPURPOSES, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE FOLLOWING DISPATCH POINTS, TO AND FROM THE SITE: PRETORIA,\nMIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM,\nETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY\n(EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS\nFROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES), SUPPLY OF THE AGGREGATE DEVICE (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), SUPPLY OF PATCH CORD'),(3046864,'MEA1.1','MEA1.1 ENG ME AGGRN SITE VISIT','This item consists of a site visit, full investigation, detailed engineering survey for an ME Aggregate device site.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1)	Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. manhole / Exchange keys etc.)\n2)	Informing the CNFO supervisors per e-mail 48 hours prior to site investigations.\n3)	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements with CNFO sites and customer sites.\n4)	making appointments with MCO Spoc within 48 hours at new building sites. \n5)	Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom system/s \n6)	Conducting a site visit at the customer premises and exchange site when required,\n7)	Clarification of the requirements with the customer on site\n8)	Obtaining written permission from the customer / Landlord or their contact details\n9)	Administration costs\n10)	A full technology investigation and solutions (Single site investigations and / or bulk orders)\n11)	Performing a detailed engineering survey including the exposing / accessing / opening of route access points such as FDP, FTH, housings, boxes, buildings, etc.\n12)	Providing the sketches of the requirements (i.e. fibre entry / route, power, cable trays, rack, floor plan, ducts, etc.) as well as related information including photos, spider diagram, tick sheets, etc.\n13)	The compilation of the RFO Spec document/s including pipe entries, AC / DC power, ducting, wireways, etc.\n14)	Attaching photos or drawings of RFO requirements on RFO specifications.\n15)	Compiling and submitting an RFO build Estimate/Quotation \n16)	Submitting and/or attaching all information including completed RFO Specification.\n17)	Obtaining / confirming GPS co-ordinates.\n18)	Obtaining all required information to place the site building on Netplan\n19)	Confirming cable size. \n20)	Updating all documentation / system requirements\n21)	Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\n22)	Labour\n23)	Administration costs\n24)	All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.	Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb.	Johannesburg.\nc.	Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd.	Ethekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne.	Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata).\nf.	Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1)	Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n\nNote: \nThis item may be only be claimed once per customer site irrespective of the number of services / serials required.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per customer site, each (EA)','EA',4539.68,'ENGNR,STE:MEA1.1,ME AGGRN','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER MEA1.1, TYPE ME AGGRN:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS\nCONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. MANHOLE / EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), INFORMING THE CNFO SUPERVISORS PER\nE-MAIL 48 HOURS PRIOR TO SITE INVESTIGATIONS, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS WITH CNFO SITES\nAND CUSTOMER SITES, MAKING APPOINTMENTS WITH MCO SPOC WITHIN 48 HOURS AT NEW BUILDING SITES, OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END RECORDS\nFROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S, CONDUCTING A SITE VISIT AT THE CUSTOMER PREMISES AND EXCHANGE SITE WHEN REQUIRED, CLARIFICATION OF THE\nREQUIREMENTS WITH THE CUSTOMER ON SITE, OBTAINING WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM THE CUSTOMER / LANDLORD OR THEIR CONTACT DETAILS,\nADMINISTRATION COSTS, A FULL TECHNOLOGY INVESTIGATION AND SOLUTIONS (SINGLE SITE INVESTIGATIONS AND / OR BULK ORDERS), PERFORMING A\nDETAILED ENGINEERING SURVEY INCLUDING THE EXPOSING / ACCESSING / OPENING OF ROUTE ACCESS POINTS SUCH AS FDP, FTH, HOUSINGS, BOXES,\nBUILDINGS, ETC., PROVIDING THE SKETCHES OF THE REQUIREMENTS (I.E. FIBRE ENTRY / ROUTE, POWER, CABLE TRAYS, RACK, FLOOR PLAN, DUCTS,\nETC.) AS WELL AS RELATED INFORMATION INCLUDING PHOTOS, SPIDER DIAGRAM, TICK SHEETS, ETC., THE COMPILATION OF THE RFO SPEC\nDOCUMENT/S INCLUDING PIPE ENTRIES, AC / DC POWER, DUCTING, WIREWAYS, ETC., ATTACHING PHOTOS OR DRAWINGS OF RFO REQUIREMENTS ON RFO\nSPECIFICATIONS, COMPILING AND SUBMITTING AN RFO BUILD ESTIMATE/QUOTATION, SUBMITTING AND/OR ATTACHING ALL INFORMATION INCLUDING\nCOMPLETED RFO SPECIFICATION, OBTAINING / CONFIRMING GPS CO-ORDINATES, OBTAINING ALL REQUIRED INFORMATION TO PLACE THE SITE BUILDING\nON NETPLAN, CONFIRMING CABLE SIZE, UPDATING ALL DOCUMENTATION / SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS, INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM\nSUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, LABOUR, ADMINISTRATION COSTS, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE FOLLOWING\nDISPATCH POINTS, TO AND FROM THE SITE: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG,'),(3046865,'MEA2.7','MEA2.7 INSTL AGGRN DVC: ME','This item consists of the complete installation, commissioning, and testing of a Metro-Ethernet Aggregate Device (i.e. SAR-8, SAR-R, ATN950B, NE40x2, etc.)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1)	Making and/or confirming customer appointment\n2)	Arranging and obtaining all site access approvals\n3)	All project management and administrative activities\n4)	Dispatching resources and all logistical activities\n5)	Obtaining all work refs\n6)	The complete installation of the ME Aggregate Device (i.e. SAR-8, SAR-R, ATN950B, NE40x2, etc.), power cable, earth cable, patch cords, all SFPΓÇÖs\n7)	Minor build material (i.e. cable ties, Velcro straps, labels, etc.)\n8)	Confirmation of metro levels (node and customer)\n9)	Labelling\n10)	Commissioning and testing of the ME Aggregate Device (Ports and Uplink) as per the relevant Acceptance Test Procedure (ATP) for SAR-8, SAR-R, ATN950B, NE40x2, etc.\n11)	Recording and updating of all the necessary information on the relevant Telkom systems / platforms\n12)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site\n13)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections\n14)	Site management\n15)	Taking and submitting photos of the complete installation for QA purposes\n16)	All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.	Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb.	Johannesburg.\nc.	Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd.	eThekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne.	Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata)\nf.	Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1)	Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n2)	Supply of the Aggregate device (Telkom to supply)\n3)	Supply of Patch cord (Telkom to supply)\n4)	Filotex Cable, krone blocks and krone labels (only for SAR-8)\n\nThe specifications for this item:\n1)	CTO-011636\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per ME Aggregate Device, each (EA)','EA',8039.68,'INSTL,EQUIP:MEA2.7,ME','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER MEA2.7, TYPE ME:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MAKING AND/OR CONFIRMING CUSTOMER\nAPPOINTMENT, ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS APPROVALS, ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES, DISPATCHING\nRESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL ACTIVITIES, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS, THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION OF THE ME AGGREGATE DEVICE (I.E. SAR-8,\nSAR-R, ATN950B, NE40X2, ETC.), POWER CABLE, EARTH CABLE, PATCH CORDS, ALL SFP#S, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, VELCRO\nSTRAPS, LABELS, ETC.), CONFIRMATION OF METRO LEVELS (NODE AND CUSTOMER), LABELLING, COMMISSIONING AND TESTING OF THE ME AGGREGATE\nDEVICE (PORTS AND UPLINK) AS PER THE RELEVANT ACCEPTANCE TEST PROCEDURE (ATP) FOR SAR-8, SAR-R, ATN950B, NE40X2, ETC., RECORDING\nAND UPDATING OF ALL THE NECESSARY INFORMATION ON THE RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS / PLATFORMS, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS,\nAND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE MANAGEMENT, TAKING AND SUBMITTING PHOTOS OF THE\nCOMPLETE INSTALLATION FOR QA PURPOSES, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE FOLLOWING DISPATCH POINTS, TO AND\nFROM THE SITE: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN),\nWORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT\nELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS\nIN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES), SUPPLY OF THE AGGREGATE DEVICE (TELKOM TO\nSUPPLY), SUPPLY OF PATCH CORD (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), FILOTEX CABLE, KRONE BLOCKS AND KRONE LABELS (ONLY FOR SAR-8). THE SPECIFICATIONS\nFOR THIS ITEM: CTO-011636. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ME AGGREGATE DEVICE, EACH (EA)'),(3046866,'MEA2.4','MEA2.4 INSTL CSTMR DVC: ATN910i','This item consists of the complete installation, commissioning, and testing of ATN910i Customer Device.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1)	Making and/or confirming customer appointment\n2)	Arranging and obtaining all site access approvals\n3)	All project management and administrative activities\n4)	Dispatching resources and all logistical activities\n5)	Obtaining all work refs\n6)	The complete installation of the ATN910i Customer Device, power cable, earth cable, patch cords, all SFPΓÇÖs, E1 cabling, etc.\n7)	Installation at Exchange on existing ATN950 of a card, SFPΓÇÖs, if need exist for E1 expansion, filotex ties between rack and T&P frame (maximum 32 cables)\n8)	Installation, termination and testing of a new set of subs cables (included with ATN910i) from the bay ATN910i to a test and patch position for the 2Meg service (as per planning) (maximum 16 cables)\n9)	Minor build material (i.e. cable ties, Velcro straps, labels, etc.)\n10)	Confirmation of metro levels (node and customer)\n11)	Labelling\n12)	Commissioning and testing of the customer device (Ports, Uplink and E1 soak test after NNOC loaded soak) as per the relevant Acceptance Test Procedure (ATP) for ATN910i\n13)	Recording and updating of all the necessary information on the relevant Telkom systems / platforms\n14)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site\n15)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections\n16)	Site management\n17)	Taking and submitting photos of the complete installation for QA purposes\n1)	All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.	Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb.	Johannesburg.\nc.	Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd.	eThekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne.	Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata)\nf.	Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\nIf the distance exceeds a 50-km radius, 2 trips might be claimed, due to time-delay from Telkom\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1)	Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n2)	Supply of the Aggregate device (Telkom to supply)\n3)	Supply of Patch cord (Telkom to supply)\n4)	Filotex Cable, krone blocks and krone labels\n\nThe specifications for this item:\n1)	CTO-011636\n\nNote:  In the case of an E1 card expansion, this item may be used in conjunction with item MEA2.5 \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per ATN910i Customer Device, each (EA)','EA',7039.68,'INSTL,EQUIP:MEA2.4,ATN910I','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER MEA2.4, TYPE ATN910I:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MAKING AND/OR CONFIRMING CUSTOMER\nAPPOINTMENT, ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS APPROVALS, ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES, DISPATCHING\nRESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL ACTIVITIES, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS, THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION OF THE ATN910I CUSTOMER DEVICE, POWER\nCABLE, EARTH CABLE, PATCH CORDS, ALL SFP#S, E1 CABLING, ETC., INSTALLATION AT EXCHANGE ON EXISTING ATN950 OF A CARD, SFP#S, IF NEED\nEXIST FOR E1 EXPANSION, FILOTEX TIES BETWEEN RACK AND T&P FRAME (MAXIMUM 32 CABLES), INSTALLATION, TERMINATION AND TESTING OF A NEW\nSET OF SUBS CABLES (INCLUDED WITH ATN910I) FROM THE BAY ATN910I TO A TEST AND PATCH POSITION FOR THE 2MEG SERVICE (AS PER PLANNING)\n(MAXIMUM 16 CABLES), MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. CABLE TIES, VELCRO STRAPS, LABELS, ETC.), CONFIRMATION OF METRO LEVELS (NODE AND\nCUSTOMER), LABELLING, COMMISSIONING AND TESTING OF THE CUSTOMER DEVICE (PORTS, UPLINK AND E1 SOAK TEST AFTER NNOC LOADED SOAK) AS\nPER THE RELEVANT ACCEPTANCE TEST PROCEDURE (ATP) FOR ATN910I, RECORDING AND UPDATING OF ALL THE NECESSARY INFORMATION ON THE\nRELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS / PLATFORMS, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY\nACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE MANAGEMENT, TAKING AND SUBMITTING PHOTOS OF THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION FOR QA PURPOSES, ALL TRAVEL\nRELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE FOLLOWING DISPATCH POINTS, TO AND FROM THE SITE: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP,\nPOLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN),\nRICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON),\nMTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. IF THE DISTANCE EXCEEDS A 50-KM RADIUS, 2 TRIPS MIGHT BE CLAIMED, DUE TO TIME-DELAY FROM\nTELKOM. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE'),(3046867,'MEA1.2','MEA1.2 ENGR ME AGGRN DVC (FBR)','This item consists of the detailed Engineering for a new existing / upgrade / cut over or new Metro Ethernet aggregation device. (i.e. SAR-8,SAS-R, ATN950/B, ATN910I, etc.)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1)	Detailed Engineering of Metro Ethernet solution on Telkom approved system / software, including patch tails\n2)	Detailed engineering of the Metro Ethernet device and all Customer premises / Inside Plant / network elements on Telkom approved system software, (i.e. Equipment racks / cabinets, Wireways, device, etc.)\n3)	Submission of Wayleaves to required utilities\n4)	Capturing and updating on Netplan (Includes the placement of the Building on NetPlan when required)\n5)	Creation of STAC\n6)	Application of WAP\n7)	Tasking for:\na.	CTS-Pretesting\nb.	RINP ref\nc.	WBS creations\n8)	Loading of:\na.	all cost on SAP/R3 (SAP Estimator)\nb.	Deliverables\n9)	Submission of an Executable file\n10)	Capturing/Updating of all as-built elements /device after completion of the installation.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1)	The initial site visit\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per site, each (EA)','EA',5000.00,'ENGNR,STE:MEA1.2,ME AGGRN DVC (FBR)','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER MEA1.2, TYPE ME AGGRN DVC (FBR):THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: DETAILED ENGINEERING OF METRO\nETHERNET SOLUTION ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM / SOFTWARE, INCLUDING PATCH TAILS, DETAILED ENGINEERING OF THE METRO ETHERNET DEVICE\nAND ALL CUSTOMER PREMISES / INSIDE PLANT / NETWORK ELEMENTS ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE, (I.E. EQUIPMENT RACKS / CABINETS,\nWIREWAYS, DEVICE, ETC.), SUBMISSION OF WAYLEAVES TO REQUIRED UTILITIES, CAPTURING AND UPDATING ON NETPLAN (INCLUDES THE PLACEMENT\nOF THE BUILDING ON NETPLAN WHEN REQUIRED), CREATION OF STAC, APPLICATION OF WAP, TASKING FOR: CTS-PRETESTING, RINP REF, WBS\nCREATIONS, LOADING OF: ALL COST ON SAP/R3 (SAP ESTIMATOR), DELIVERABLES, SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE, CAPTURING/UPDATING OF\nALL AS-BUILT ELEMENTS /DEVICE AFTER COMPLETION OF THE INSTALLATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE INITIAL SITE VISIT. THE UNIT OF MEASURE\n(UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046894,'CE2.8','CE2.8 INCOMING WAYLVE','This item consists of the marking up of wayleave/s submitted to Telkom.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Receiving of an incoming wayleave, i.e. customer letter / plans, facing sheet, plans, etc.,\n2) Sourcing of existing infrastructure via various systems, i.e. Google Earth, etc.,\n3) Capturing of current / future infrastructure, cable runs, contact person information using Telkom information as a guideline,\n4) Obtaining hard copies of paper-based documents\n5) Liaising with relevant Telkom persons, if necessary\n6) Submitting all documentation (i.e. marked up files, letter to requestor, plans, etc.) to Telkom Turf Ops Manager (RNE-HLP/PLO) for verification of quality and accuracy, if applicable.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per applicant request/s, irrespective of the number of wayleave sheets, each (EA)','EA',500.00,'PAY,FEE:CE2.8 INCOMING WAYLVE','PAY, FEE:PURPOSE CE2.8 INCOMING WAYLVE:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: RECEIVING OF AN INCOMING WAYLEAVE, I.E. CUSTOMER\nLETTER / PLANS, FACING SHEET, PLANS, ETC., SOURCING OF EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE VIA VARIOUS SYSTEMS, I.E. GOOGLE EARTH, ETC.,\nCAPTURING OF CURRENT / FUTURE INFRASTRUCTURE, CABLE RUNS, CONTACT PERSON INFORMATION USING TELKOM INFORMATION AS A GUIDELINE,\nOBTAINING HARD COPIES OF PAPER-BASED DOCUMENTS, LIAISING WITH RELEVANT TELKOM PERSONS, IF NECESSARY, SUBMITTING ALL DOCUMENTATION\n(I.E. MARKED UP FILES, LETTER TO REQUESTOR, PLANS, ETC.) TO TELKOM TURF OPS MANAGER (RNE-HLP/PLO) FOR VERIFICATION OF QUALITY AND\nACCURACY, IF APPLICABLE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER APPLICANT REQUEST/S, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF WAYLEAVE\nSHEETS, EACH (EA).'),(3046904,'EE1.1','EE1.1 ENG RCVY ISP','This item consists of the detailed Engineering for the decommissioning and recovery of all Inside Plant (ISP) related equipment (Switching, Access, Transmission, Legacy, etc.) at an Exchange / Central Office location.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n0)1) Site visit/s and Survey/s,\n0)2) Detailed engineering (Reverse Engineering) of all ISP technologies / equipment (i.e. Switching & Access ΓÇô E10, EWSD, UMC, DCS, TDMA Racks, DSLAM; Transmission ΓÇô SMA, NGSDH, SHDSL, FL1531, FL1521, SAR8 and T5C, Martis, TMNET; Legacy ΓÇô OLS, OLT, OLP, PCM, LTA, etc.),\n0)3) Obtaining all necessary working refs and site access control approvals,\n0)4) Making access arrangements including the obtaining of keys / access devices from the landlord (Exchange / gate / building keys),\n0)5) Environmental, Health and Safety Controls,\n0)6) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required,\n0)7) Establishing existing records \n0)8) Investigating / verifying all associated circuits pertaining to the technology being decommissioned and recovered \n0)9) Tracing of circuits, cables, jumpers, patch tails, etc. where required,\n0)10) Submission of an executable recovery (Reverse Engineering) file,\n0)11) Processing of all Variation Orders (VOΓÇÖs) during the recovery of the Equipment,\n0)12) Obtaining all quality acceptance documents from the relevant sections in Openserve on completion of work,\n0)13) Updating of all Telkom records on Telkom systems once the recovery is complete (i.e. Netplan TXOPS, TED, Cramer, asset sheets etc.)\n0)14) All travel related costs to and from site within a 50 km radius of the Telkom nominated dispatch point.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n0)1) Travel related costs >50 km radius of the Telkom nominated dispatch point,\n0)2) Engineering for the recovery of DC Power equipment,\n0)3) Engineering for the recovery of UPLinks.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per technology per site, each (EA)','EA',5500.00,'ENGNR,STE:EE1.1,RCVY ISP','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER EE1.1, TYPE RCVY ISP:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: SITE VISIT/S AND SURVEY/S, DETAILED\nENGINEERING (REVERSE ENGINEERING) OF ALL ISP TECHNOLOGIES / EQUIPMENT (I.E. SWITCHING & ACCESS # E10, EWSD, UMC, DCS, TDMA RACKS,\nDSLAM; TRANSMISSION # SMA, NGSDH, SHDSL, FL1531, FL1521, SAR8 AND T5C, MARTIS, TMNET; LEGACY # OLS, OLT, OLP, PCM, LTA, ETC.),\nOBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND SITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS, MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS INCLUDING THE OBTAINING OF KEYS\n/ ACCESS DEVICES FROM THE LANDLORD (EXCHANGE / GATE / BUILDING KEYS), ENVIRONMENTAL, HEALTH AND SAFETY CONTROLS, INTERFACE\nMANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, ESTABLISHING EXISTING RECORDS, INVESTIGATING / VERIFYING ALL\nASSOCIATED CIRCUITS PERTAINING TO THE TECHNOLOGY BEING DECOMMISSIONED AND RECOVERED, TRACING OF CIRCUITS, CABLES, JUMPERS, PATCH\nTAILS, ETC. WHERE REQUIRED, SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE RECOVERY (REVERSE ENGINEERING) FILE, PROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS\n(VO#S) DURING THE RECOVERY OF THE EQUIPMENT, OBTAINING ALL QUALITY ACCEPTANCE DOCUMENTS FROM THE RELEVANT SECTIONS IN OPENSERVE ON\nCOMPLETION OF WORK, UPDATING OF ALL TELKOM RECORDS ON TELKOM SYSTEMS ONCE THE RECOVERY IS COMPLETE (I.E. NETPLAN TXOPS, TED,\nCRAMER, ASSET SHEETS ETC.), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM SITE WITHIN A 50 KM RADIUS OF THE TELKOM NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT.\nTHE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS >50 KM RADIUS OF THE TELKOM NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT, ENGINEERING FOR THE RECOVERY OF DC\nPOWER EQUIPMENT, ENGINEERING FOR THE RECOVERY OF UPLINKS. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER TECHNOLOGY PER SITE, EACH (EA)'),(3046924,'CE2.5','CE2.5 DRAFTG CIVL ENGR DWRG: CU/ME','This item consists of the drafting and certification of professional civil engineering drawing/s by a qualified Civil Engineer on behalf of Openserve. (Scale of drawing  1:500)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Drawings for Copper/ME,\n2) Drafting and certification of engineering drawing/s of all the relevant civil elements required by the Local Authorities (municipalities / utilities / stake holders),\n3) Submission of drawing/s to the authorities,\n4) All travel related costs to and from the Local Authorities / utilities / stake holders and/or sites within a 50km radius of the nominated dispatch point.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See service fee item: light vehicle, 2-man team).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per drawing per Copper/ME project, irrespective of the number of locality sheets (A4 to A0 sizes) each (EA)','EA',450.00,'FNLZ,DOC:CE2.5 DRF CIVL ENGR DWRG CU/ME','FINALIZE, DOCUMENT:TYPE CE2.5 DRF CIVL ENGR DWRG CU/ME:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: DRAWINGS FOR COPPER/ME, DRAFTING\nAND CERTIFICATION OF ENGINEERING DRAWING/S OF ALL THE RELEVANT CIVIL ELEMENTS REQUIRED BY THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES (MUNICIPALITIES /\nUTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS), SUBMISSION OF DRAWING/S TO THE AUTHORITIES, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES\n/ UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS AND/OR SITES WITHIN A 50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED\nCOSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEM: LIGHT VEHICLE, 2-MAN TEAM). THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DRAWING PER FTTX AREA, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF LOCALITY SHEETS (A4 TO A0 SIZES)\nEACH (EA)'),(3046925,'CE2.4','CE2.4 WAYLEAVE EXCTN: JRA','This item consists of receiving and executing approved way leaves from the Johannesburg Roads Agency (Pty) Ltd, on behalf of Telkom. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \n1) Collecting the approved way leaves from the JRA,\n2) Arranging and attending site meeting/s with the council representative/s and/or Engineer/s,\n3) Communicating with the relevant authorities regarding possible affected services, \n4) Arranging for final inspection and site sign-off,\n5) Administration costs (i.e. Stationary, copies, telephone calls, etc.), \n6) All travel related costs to and from the local authorities and/or sites. \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per project, irrespective of the number of wayleave approvals, each (EA)','EA',1000.00,'FNLZ,DOC:CE2.4 WAYLEAVE EXCTN: JRA','FINALIZE, DOCUMENT:TYPE CE2.4 WAYLEAVE EXCTN: JRA:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: COLLECTING THE APPROVED WAY LEAVES FROM\nTHE JRA, ARRANGING AND ATTENDING SITE MEETING/S WITH THE COUNCIL REPRESENTATIVE/S AND/OR ENGINEER/S, COMMUNICATING WITH THE\nRELEVANT AUTHORITIES REGARDING POSSIBLE AFFECTED SERVICES, ARRANGING FOR FINAL INSPECTION AND SITE SIGN-OFF, ADMINISTRATION COSTS\n(I.E. STATIONARY, COPIES, TELEPHONE CALLS, ETC.), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES AND/OR SITES. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PROJECT, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF WAYLEAVE APPROVALS, EACH (EA)'),(3046926,'CE2.2','CE2.2 OUTGOING WAYLVE: RE-APPLN','This item consists of re-application / time extension of expired wayleave/s from the relevant Local Authorities (municipalities / utilities / stake holders) on behalf of Telkom (Wayleave section)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \n1) Re-application of expired wayleave/s,\n2) Communicating and following up with authorities until obtaining the approved wayleave/s,\n3) Administration costs (i.e. Stationary, copies, telephone calls, etc.)\n4) All travel related costs to and from the Local Authorities / utilities / stake holders and/or sites within a 50km radius of the nominated dispatch point. \n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) Any payment for the application as demanded by some municipalities. As per the Telecommunication Act 36, Section 22 of 2005, Telkom has no legal obligation to make any payment for the application.\n2) Distances in excess of 50km radius (See service fee item: light vehicle, 2-man team)\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per project, irrespective of the number of wayleave applications / sheets submitted, each (EA)','EA',800.00,'FNLZ,DOC:CE2.2 OUTGOING WAYLVE: RE-APPLN','FINALIZE, DOCUMENT:TYPE CE2.2 OUTGOING WAYLVE: RE-APPLN:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: RE-APPLICATION OF EXPIRED\nWAYLEAVE/S, COMMUNICATING AND FOLLOWING UP WITH AUTHORITIES UNTIL OBTAINING THE APPROVED WAYLEAVE/S, ADMINISTRATION COSTS (I.E.\nSTATIONARY, COPIES, TELEPHONE CALLS, ETC.), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS\nAND/OR SITES WITHIN A 50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ANY PAYMENT FOR THE APPLICATION AS DEMANDED\nBY SOME MUNICIPALITIES, DISTANCES IN EXCESS OF 50KM RADIUS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEM: LIGHT VEHICLE, 2-MAN TEAM). THE UNIT OF MEASURE\n(UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PROJECT, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF WAYLEAVE APPLICATIONS / SHEETS SUBMITTED, EACH (EA)'),(3046927,'CE2.7','CE2.7DRAFTG CIVL ENG DWRG:FTTX (0-600HP)','This item consists of the drafting and certification of professional civil engineering drawing/s by a qualified Civil Engineer on behalf of Openserve. (Scale of drawing  1:500)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Drawings for FTTX area up to 600 Homes Passed,\n2) Drafting and certification of engineering drawing/s of all the relevant civil elements required by the Local Authorities (municipalities / utilities / stake holders),\n3) Submission of drawing/s to the authorities,\n4) All travel related costs to and from the Local Authorities / utilities / stake holders and/or sites within a 50km radius of the nominated dispatch point.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See service fee item: light vehicle, 2-man team).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per drawing per FTTx area, irrespective of the number of locality sheets (A4 to A0 sizes) each (EA)','EA',4500.00,'FNLZ,DOC:CE2.7 DRFT DWRG FTTX (0-600HP)','FINALIZE, DOCUMENT:TYPE CE2.7 DRAFTG CIVL ENG DWRG FTTX (0-600HP):THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: DRAWINGS FOR FTTX AREA\nUP TO 600 HOMES PASSED, DRAFTING AND CERTIFICATION OF ENGINEERING DRAWING/S OF ALL THE RELEVANT CIVIL ELEMENTS REQUIRED BY THE\nLOCAL AUTHORITIES (MUNICIPALITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS), SUBMISSION OF DRAWING/S TO THE AUTHORITIES, ALL TRAVEL RELATED\nCOSTS TO AND FROM THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS AND/OR SITES WITHIN A 50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH\nPOINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEE\nITEM: LIGHT VEHICLE, 2-MAN TEAM). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DRAWING PER FTTX AREA, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER\nOF LOCALITY SHEETS (A4 TO A0 SIZES) EACH (EA)'),(3046928,'CE2.6','CE2.6 DRAFTG CIVL ENG DWRG:BCK BONE FBR','This item consists of the drafting and certification of professional civil engineering drawing/s by a qualified Civil Engineer on behalf of Openserve. (Scale of drawing  1:500)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Drawings for Backbone fibre,\n2) Drafting and certification of engineering drawing/s of all the relevant civil elements required by the Local Authorities (municipalities / utilities / stake holders),\n3) Submission of drawing/s to the authorities,\n4) All travel related costs to and from the Local Authorities / utilities / stake holders and/or sites within a 50km radius of the nominated dispatch point.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See service fee item: light vehicle, 2-man team).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per drawing per Backbone project, irrespective of the number of locality sheets (A4 to A0 sizes) each (EA)','EA',3000.00,'FNLZ,DOC:CE2.6 DRFT DWRG BCK BONE FBR','FINALIZE, DOCUMENT:TYPE CE2.6 DRAFTG CIVL ENG DWRG BCK BONE FBR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: DRAWINGS FOR BACKBONE\nFIBRE, DRAFTING AND CERTIFICATION OF ENGINEERING DRAWING/S OF ALL THE RELEVANT CIVIL ELEMENTS REQUIRED BY THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES\n(MUNICIPALITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS), SUBMISSION OF DRAWING/S TO THE AUTHORITIES, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM THE\nLOCAL AUTHORITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS AND/OR SITES WITHIN A 50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES:\nTRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEM: LIGHT VEHICLE,\n2-MAN TEAM). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DRAWING PER FTTX AREA, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF LOCALITY SHEETS\n(A4 TO A0 SIZES) EACH (EA)'),(3046929,'CE2.3','CE2.3 OUTGOING WAYLVE: EMERG','This item consists of the co-ordination and submission of emergency wayleave/s to the Local Authorities (municipalities / utilities / stake holders), on behalf of Telkom.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Co-ordinating and Consolidating all documentation for approval\n2) Submitting (in any which way or form, such as but not limited to physical handing in, posting, electronically) emergency application form with the consolidated file (topo, sketch, etc.) to the utilities such as: \na. Local municipality and/or its disciplines \nb. Eskom \nc. Gas \nd. Water Boards \ne. Transnet \nf. Other Telecommunication companies \n3) Administration costs (i.e. Stationary, copies, telephone calls, etc.)\n4) All travel related costs to and from the Local Authorities / utilities / stake holders and/or sites within a 50km radius of the nominated dispatch point.\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) Wayleave applications for GAUTRANS or SANRAL\n2) Wayleave application for Conventional road crossings where horizontal road drilling is not possible \n3) Any payment for the application as demanded by some municipalities. As per the Telecommunication Act 36, Section 22 of 2005, Telkom has no legal obligation to make any payment for the application.\n4) Distances in excess of 50km radius (See service fee item: light vehicle, 2-man team)\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per project, irrespective of the number of wayleave applications / sheets submitted, each (EA)','EA',1500.00,'FNLZ,DOC:CE2.3 OUTGOING WAYLVE: EMERG','FINALIZE, DOCUMENT:TYPE CE2.3 OUTGOING WAYLVE: EMERG:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CO-ORDINATING AND CONSOLIDATING ALL\nDOCUMENTATION FOR APPROVAL, SUBMITTING (IN ANY WHICH WAY OR FORM, SUCH AS BUT NOT LIMITED TO PHYSICAL HANDING IN, POSTING,\nELECTRONICALLY) EMERGENCY APPLICATION FORM WITH THE CONSOLIDATED FILE (TOPO, SKETCH, ETC.) TO THE UTILITIES SUCH AS: LOCAL\nMUNICIPALITY AND/OR ITS DISCIPLINES, ESKOM, GAS, WATER BOARDS, TRANSNET, OTHER TELECOMMUNICATION COMPANIES, ADMINISTRATION COSTS\n(I.E. STATIONARY, COPIES, TELEPHONE CALLS, ETC.), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE\nHOLDERS AND/OR SITES WITHIN A 50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: WAYLEAVE APPLICATIONS FOR GAUTRANS OR\nSANRAL, WAYLEAVE APPLICATION FOR CONVENTIONAL ROAD CROSSINGS WHERE HORIZONTAL ROAD DRILLING IS NOT POSSIBLE, ANY PAYMENT FOR THE\nAPPLICATION AS DEMANDED BY SOME MUNICIPALITIES, DISTANCES IN EXCESS OF 50KM RADIUS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEM: LIGHT VEHICLE, 2-MAN\nTEAM). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PROJECT, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF WAYLEAVE APPLICATIONS / SHEETS\nSUBMITTED, EACH (EA)'),(3046940,'MEA2.5','MEA2.5 INSTL AGGRN DVC: ATN950 E1 CRD','This item consists of the complete installation, commissioning, and testing of a E1 Card, E1 cables and Ties expansion on Aggregate Device (i.e. ATN950, etc.).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1)	Making and/or confirming customer appointment\n2)	Arranging and obtaining all site access approvals\n3)	All project management and administrative activities\n4)	Dispatching resources and all logistical activities\n5)	Obtaining all work refs\n6)	The complete installation of E1 card, E1 cables and Ties for E1 expansion on Aggregate Device (i.e. ATN950, etc.), E1 cables, tie cables, T&P frame (in rack) (only in the Exchange)\n7)	Installation, termination and testing of a new set of E1, 15-way T&P, and tie cables (filotex) from the bay to a test and patch position for the 2Meg services (as per planning) when required (maximum 32 TX and 32 RX pairs per card) \n8)	Minor build material (i.e. cable ties, Velcro straps, labels, etc.)\n9)	Confirmation of metro levels (node and customer)\n10)	Labelling\n11)	Commissioning and testing of the Aggregate Device (Ports and Uplink) as per the relevant Acceptance Test Procedure (ATP) for ATN950, etc.\n1)	Recording and updating of all the necessary information on the relevant Telkom systems / platforms\n2)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from site\n3)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections\n4)	Site management\n5)	Taking and submitting photos of the complete installation for QA purposes\n6)	All travel related costs up to a 50-km radius from the following dispatch points, to and from the site:\na.	Pretoria, Middelburg, Klerksdorp, Polokwane, Vereeniging, Rustenburg.\nb.	Johannesburg.\nc.	Bellville (Cape Town), Worcester, Vredenburg, Swellendam\nd.	eThekwini (Durban), Richards bay, Pietermaritzburg, Newcastle.\ne.	Nelson Mandela Metropolitan (Port Elizabeth), George, Buffalo City (East London), Mthatha (Umtata)\nf.	Bloemfontein, Kimberley.\nIf the distance exceeds a 50-km radius, 2 trips might be claimed, due to time-delay from Telkom\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1)	Travel related costs in the excess of a 50-km radius from the designated dispatch points (See Service fees).\n2)	Supply of the Aggregate device (Telkom to supply)\n3)	Supply of Patch cord (Telkom to supply)\n4)	Filotex Cable, krone blocks and krone labels\n\nThe specifications for this item:\n1)	CTO-011636\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per ATN950 E1 card, each (EA)','EA',1789.68,'INSTL,EQUIP:MEA2.5,ATN950 E1 CRD','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER MEA2.5, TYPE ATN950 E1 CRD:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: MAKING AND/OR CONFIRMING\nCUSTOMER APPOINTMENT, ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS APPROVALS, ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES,\nDISPATCHING RESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL ACTIVITIES, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS, THE COMPLETE INSTALLATION OF E1 CARD, E1 CABLES AND\nTIES FOR E1 EXPANSION ON AGGREGATE DEVICE (I.E. ATN950, ETC.), E1 CABLES, TIE CABLES, T&P FRAME (IN RACK) (ONLY IN THE EXCHANGE),\nINSTALLATION, TERMINATION AND TESTING OF A NEW SET OF E1, 15-WAY T&P, AND TIE CABLES (FILOTEX) FROM THE BAY TO A TEST AND PATCH\nPOSITION FOR THE 2MEG SERVICES (AS PER PLANNING) WHEN REQUIRED (MAXIMUM 32 TX AND 32 RX PAIRS PER CARD), MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E.\nCABLE TIES, VELCRO STRAPS, LABELS, ETC.), CONFIRMATION OF METRO LEVELS (NODE AND CUSTOMER), LABELLING, COMMISSIONING AND TESTING OF\nTHE AGGREGATE DEVICE (PORTS AND UPLINK) AS PER THE RELEVANT ACCEPTANCE TEST PROCEDURE (ATP) FOR ATN950, ETC., RECORDING AND\nUPDATING OF ALL THE NECESSARY INFORMATION ON THE RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS / PLATFORMS, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND\nEQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE MANAGEMENT, TAKING AND SUBMITTING PHOTOS OF THE\nCOMPLETE INSTALLATION FOR QA PURPOSES, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE FOLLOWING DISPATCH POINTS, TO AND\nFROM THE SITE: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN),\nWORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT\nELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. IF THE DISTANCE EXCEEDS A 50-KM RADIUS,\n2 TRIPS MIGHT BE CLAIMED, DUE TO TIME-DELAY FROM TELKOM. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS\nFROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES), SUPPLY OF THE AGGREGATE DEVICE (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), SUPPLY OF PATCH CORD'),(3047046,'CI1.452','CI1.452 CORE DRILG PIPE ENTR >100MM DIA','This item consists of core drilling of pipe entries through existing concrete structures (i.e. existing manholes, buildings and existing jointing pits).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Removal of spoil, cleaning of manhole and surrounding area, \nb) Core drilling a greater than 100mm diameter hole through a brick and concrete structure for pipe / cable entries,\nc) Repairing of wall and finishing off.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pipe entry each (EA)','EA',495.84,'DRIL,HOLE:CI1.452,CRE, PIP >100MM DIA','DRILL, HOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.452, PURPOSE CORE, PIPE ENTR >100MM DIA:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: REMOVAL OF SPOIL,\nCLEANING OF MANHOLE AND SURROUNDING AREA, CORE DRILLING A GREATER THAN 100MM DIAMETER HOLE THROUGH A BRICK AND CONCRETE STRUCTURE\nFOR PIPE / CABLE ENTRIES, REPAIRING OF WALL AND FINISHING OFF. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE\nFEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PIPE ENTRY EACH (EA)'),(3047047,'CI1.451','CI1.451 CORE DRILG PIPE ENTR 30-100MM DIA','This item consists of core drilling of pipe entries through existing brick and concrete structures (i.e. existing manholes, buildings and existing jointing pits).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Removal of spoil, cleaning of manhole and surrounding area, \nb) Core drilling a 30-100mm diameter hole through a brick and concrete structure for pipe / cable entries.\nc) Repairing of wall and finishing off.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pipe entry each (EA)','EA',150.00,'DRIL,HOLE:CI1.451,CRE PIP 30-100MM DIA','DRILL, HOLE:ITEM NUMBER CI1.451, PURPOSE CORE PIPE ENTR 30-100MM DIA:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: REMOVAL OF SPOIL,\nCLEANING OF MANHOLE AND SURROUNDING AREA, CORE DRILLING A 30-100MM DIAMETER HOLE THROUGH A BRICK AND CONCRETE STRUCTURE FOR PIPE /\nCABLE ENTRIES. REPAIRING OF WALL AND FINISHING OFF. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PIPE ENTRY EACH (EA)'),(3047254,'CI3.35','CI3.35 INSTL YLW FBR TRNKG','This item consists of the Installation of Yellow FiberGuide Raceway Trunking only.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. Exchange keys etc.)\n2) Obtaining work refs.\n3) Labour for the mounting of the yellow trunking\n4) Labelling\n5) Minor build material (i.e. mushroom bolts, etc.)\n6) Submission of documents, I.e. Quality Acceptance Certificate\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) All travel related costs (See Service fee document) which also includes Transportation of material/equipment to and from site.\n2) The supply of the Yellow trunking (Telkom to supply)\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per meter (MT)','MT',50.00,'INSTL,TRUNK:CI3.35,YLW FBR','INSTALL, TRUNKING:ITEM NUMBER CI3.35, TYPE YLW FBR:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS\nCONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., LABOUR FOR THE MOUNTING OF\nTHE YELLOW TRUNKING, LABELLING, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. MUSHROOM BOLTS, ETC.), SUBMISSION OF DOCUMENTS, I.E. QUALITY ACCEPTANCE\nCERTIFICATE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT) WHICH ALSO INCLUDES TRANSPORTATION OF\nMATERIAL/EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE, THE SUPPLY OF THE YELLOW TRUNKING (TELKOM TO SUPPLY). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM\nIS PER METER (MT)'),(3047293,'CE1.13','CE1.13 ENG FBR IFC','This item consists of the detailed engineering for an Optic Fibre Inter-Facility Cable (IFC), all sizes and types.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals (i.e. Exchange keys etc.)\nb) Obtaining work refs.\nc) Site visit / Survey including the accessing / opening of route access points such as cable trays, housings, boxes, risers, buildings, etc.\nd) Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\ne) Labour\nf) Obtaining existing records from Telkom system/s\ng) Determination of complete IFC route including termination positions, termination type (OFTP, FOMS, etc), type of connector required as well as slack management requirements\nh) Detailed engineering of all IFCΓÇÖs on Telkom approved system software. (I.e. IFCΓÇÖs, ducts, runways, grids, risers, etc.)\ni) Providing the sketches of the requirements (i.e. IFC route, cable trays, rack, floor plan, ducts, etc.) as well as related information including photos, spider diagram, tick sheets, etc.\nj) Creating and registering of STAC codes where required. \nk) Detailed engineering for recoveries of any IFCΓÇÖs to be recovered when applicable.\nl) Submission of an Executable file as per Telkom SpecΓÇÖs, Work Instructions, Method &Procedures, Policies, etc.\nm) Submission of an Executable file with all the relevant recovery information, where applicable, such as:\na. asset decommissioning form\nb. inventory list of all equipment and cables to be recovered (copper, fibre, cards, modules, racks, sub-racks, etc.)\nn) Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\no) Capturing of all as-built IFCΓÇÖs / elements after completion of the work. (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Travel related costs (See Service fees).\n\nNote: \na) This item may only be claimed where the Engineering for the installation of IFCΓÇÖs is a standalone project and not done in conjunction with any other project (i.e. ME DL and/or KL).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per IFC  engineered, each (EA)','EA',2500.00,'ENGNR,STE:CE1.13,FBR IFC','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE1.13, TYPE FBR IFC:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR AN OPTIC FIBRE INTER-FACILITY CABLE (IFC) ON EXISTING OR NEW ROUTES. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO:, ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., SITE VISIT / SURVEY INCLUDING THE ACCESSING / OPENING OF ROUTE ACCESS POINTS SUCH AS CABLE TRAYS, HOUSINGS, BOXES, RISERS, BUILDINGS, ETC., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, LABOUR, OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END RECORDS FROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S, DETERMINATION OF COMPLETE FIBRE ROUTE INCLUDING TERMINATION POSITIONS, TERMINATION TYPE (OFTP, FOMS, ETC), TYPE OF CONNECTOR REQUIRED AS WELL AS SLACK MANAGEMENT REQUIREMENTS, DETAILED ENGINEERING OF ALL PLANT / INFRASTRUCTURE / NETWORK ELEMENTS ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE. (I.E. FIBRE CABLES, DUCTS, RUNWAYS, GRIDS, RISERS, ETC.), PROVIDING THE SKETCHES OF THE REQUIREMENTS (I.E. FIBRE ENTRY / ROUTE, POWER, CABLE TRAYS, RACK, FLOOR PLAN, DUCTS, ETC.) AS WELL AS RELATED INFORMATION INCLUDING PHOTOS, SPIDER DIAGRAM, TICK SHEETS, ETC., CREATING AND REGISTERING OF STAC CODES WHERE REQUIRED, DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR RECOVERIES OF ALL TYPES OF PLANT AND/OR EQUIPMENT, SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE AS PER TELKOM SPEC#S, WORK INSTRUCTIONS, METHOD &PROCEDURES, POLICIES, ETC., SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE WITH ALL THE RELEVANT RECOVERY INFORMATION, WHERE APPLICABLE, SUCH AS: ASSET DECOMMISSIONING FORM, INVENTORY LIST OF ALL EQUIPMENT AND CABLES TO BE RECOVERED (COPPER, FIBRE, CARDS, MODULES, RACKS, SUB-RACKS, ETC.), PROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE PROJECT (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS), CAPTURING OF ALL AS-BUILT PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER COMPLETION OF THE WORK. (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS UP TO A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE FOLLOWING DISPATCH POINTS, TO AND FROM THE SITE: PRETORIA, MIDDELBURG, KLERKSDORP, POLOKWANE, VEREENIGING, RUSTENBURG, JOHANNESBURG, BELLVILLE (CAPE TOWN), WORCESTER, VREDENBURG, SWELLENDAM, ETHEKWINI (DURBAN), RICHARDS BAY, PIETERMARITZBURG, NEWCASTLE, NELSON MANDELA METROPOLITAN (PORT ELIZABETH), GEORGE, BUFFALO CITY (EAST LONDON), MTHATHA (UMTATA), BLOEMFONTEIN, KIMBERLEY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: TRAVEL RELATED COSTS IN THE EXCESS OF A 50-KM RADIUS FROM THE DESIGNATED DISPATCH POINTS (SEE SERVICE FEES). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE CLAIMED FOR THE ENGINEERING OF AN IFC WHEN IT IS NOT INCLUDED IN THE ENGINEERING OF THE EQUIPMENT ON THE PROJECT. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER IFC ENGINEERED, EACH (EA)'),(3048206,'EE1.5','EE1.5 ENG LNI RTNG','This item consists of the detailed Engineering of the Logical Network Inventory (LNI) routing for Megaline E1 , STM-1 ,STM-4 traffic.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n1) Detailed engineering of Megaline E1 , STM-1 and STM-4 path on LNI over PDH and SDH equipment\n2) Applying for Telkom Divert serial/s\n3) The verification of traffic on TXops, TED and LNI\n4) The verification of STAC codes on TXOPS and STAC Register\n5) The creation of the TRF file and NULL RFO Spec\n6) The creation of a u-serial on UNIWEB/SERVACT\n7) Tasking on BPM\n8) Attaching of TRF file documentation on BPM doc manager\n9) Informing the Openserve Traffic planning SPOC/PLO by email of traffic file attachment on BPM\n10) Updating all system records (example: TED and LNI)\n11) Resolving all failures from NNOC Configs and hand backs from CPC within 24 hours, e.g. double allocation\n12) Closing all tasks and release serials on BPM\n13) Traffic planning file will include the old and new routing in case of traffic diverts. \n\nThe rate excludes:\n1) All travelling to and from site (See Service Fee items). \n\nNote: this item may not be used in conjunction with the engineering of a new Metro Ethernet Client Device.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per link, each (EA)','EA',1400.00,'ENGNR,RTE:EE1.5,ENG LNI RTNG','ENGINEER, ROUTE:ITEM NUMBER EE1.5, TYPE ENG LNI RTNG:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE DETAILED ENGINEERING OF THE LOGICAL NETWORK\nINVENTORY (LNI) ROUTING FOR MEGALINE E1, STM-1, STM-4 TRAFFIC. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: DETAILED ENGINEERING OF\nMEGALINE E1 , STM-1 AND STM-4 PATH ON LNI OVER PDH AND SDH EQUIPMENT, APPLYING FOR TELKOM DIVERT SERIAL/S, THE VERIFICATION OF\nTRAFFIC ON TXOPS, TED AND LNI, THE VERIFICATION OF STAC CODES ON TXOPS AND STAC REGISTER, THE CREATION OF THE TRF FILE AND NULL RFO\nSPEC, THE CREATION OF A U-SERIAL ON UNIWEB/SERVACT, TASKING ON BPM, ATTACHING OF TRF FILE DOCUMENTATION ON BPM DOC MANAGER,\nINFORMING THE OPENSERVE TRAFFIC PLANNING SPOC/PLO BY EMAIL OF TRAFFIC FILE ATTACHMENT ON BPM, UPDATING ALL SYSTEM RECORDS (EXAMPLE:\nTED AND LNI), RESOLVING ALL FAILURES FROM NNOC CONFIGS AND HAND BACKS FROM CPC WITHIN 24 HOURS, E.G. DOUBLE ALLOCATION, CLOSING ALL\nTASKS AND RELEASE SERIALS ON BPM, TRAFFIC PLANNING FILE WILL INCLUDE THE OLD AND NEW ROUTING IN CASE OF TRAFFIC DIVERTS. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVELLING TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY NOT BE USED IN CONJUNCTION WITH THE\nENGINEERING OF A NEW METRO ETHERNET CLIENT DEVICE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER LINK, EACH (EA).'),(3048281,'CI3.36','CI3.36 INSTL BCK FRAME','This item consists of the installation of a back frame (all sizes such as 3-way, 5-way, 10-way, 33-way)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to;\n1. Labour for the installation of a back frame (all sizes)\n2. Supply of a wooden back-board when required)\n3. Drilling of holes\n4. Inserting of connecting modules (Quante or Krone)\n5. Minor build material (i.e. fastening materials, crews, rings, etc.)\n\nThe rate excludes:\n1. All travel related costs (See Service fee document) which also includes Transportation of material/equipment to and from site.\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per back frame, each (EA)','EA',120.00,'INSTL,FRAM:CI3.36,BCK','INSTALL, FRAME:ITEM NUMBER CI3.36, TYPE BACK:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION OF A BACK FRAME\n(ALL SIZES), SUPPLY OF A WOODEN BACK-BOARD WHEN REQUIRED), DRILLING OF HOLES, INSERTING OF CONNECTING MODULES (QUANTE OR KRONE),\nMINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. FASTENING MATERIALS, CREWS, RINGS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT) WHICH ALSO INCLUDES TRANSPORTATION OF MATERIAL/EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM SITE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nBACK FRAME, EACH (EA)'),(3048872,'ER1.12','ER1.12 RECVR BCKPLAN SML REUSE 0ΓÇæ200KM','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of any type of redundant Back Plane / Sub-Frame ΓÇô Small as directed by Telkom for Re-use or to be Sold within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all equipment to be recovered for re-use.\nc.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nd.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\ne.	Test and make sure equipment are not live.\nf.	The recovery of any Back Plane or sub-frame with a volume not exceeding 0.06 m┬│ (Small - Typical dimensions = 0,3m (h) x 0.3m (d) x 0.6m (w))\ng.	Update an inventory list of all recovered cards, modules and systems\nh.	 Disconnect and remove if terminated without damage to environment or loss of service.\ni.	Package Back Planes on site according to Telkom SA specifications.\nj.	Complete IE 6 Documentation as per Telkom SA procedure\nk.	Update list of recovered cards with IE 6 Number per item.\nl.	Transport to Local MC Store (Details will be provided by Telkom)\nm.	Telkom to provide a value of the equipment to be transported the service provider must ensure that adequate insurance is provided.\nn.	Stack recovered equipment in safe place which is not a fire risk.\no.	Stack recovered equipment in safe place which is environmentally friendly.\n\nThe unit for this item is per Back Plane, each.','EA',328.00,'RCVR,EQUIP:ER1.12,BCKPLAN SML REUSE','RECOVER, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER ER1.12, TYPE BCKPLAN SML REUSE, LOCATION 0-200KM:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO:\nUNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT MEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS\nTO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT (NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL EQUIPMENT TO BE RECOVERED FOR RE-USE,\nCOMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, TEST AND MAKE SURE\nEQUIPMENT ARE NOT LIVE, THE RECOVERY OF ANY BACK PLANE OR SUB-FRAME WITH A VOLUME NOT EXCEEDING 006 M┬│ (SMALL - TYPICAL DIMENSIONS\n= 0,3M (H) X 03M (D) X 06M (W)), UPDATE AN INVENTORY LIST OF ALL RECOVERED CARDS, MODULES AND SYSTEMS,  DISCONNECT AND REMOVE IF\nTERMINATED WITHOUT DAMAGE TO ENVIRONMENT OR LOSS OF SERVICE, PACKAGE BACK PLANES ON SITE ACCORDING TO TELKOM SA SPECIFICATIONS,\nCOMPLETE IE 6 DOCUMENTATION AS PER TELKOM SA PROCEDURE, UPDATE LIST OF RECOVERED CARDS WITH IE 6 NUMBER PER ITEM, TRANSPORT TO\nLOCAL MC STORE (DETAILS WILL BE PROVIDED BY TELKOM), TELKOM TO PROVIDE A VALUE OF THE EQUIPMENT TO BE TRANSPORTED THE SERVICE\nPROVIDER MUST ENSURE THAT ADEQUATE INSURANCE IS PROVIDED, STACK RECOVERED EQUIPMENT IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS NOT A FIRE RISK, STACK\nRECOVERED EQUIPMENT IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS ENVIRONMENTALLY FRIENDLY. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER BACK PLANE, EACH'),(3048873,'ER1.14','ER1.14 RECVR BAYS/RACKS REUSE 0ΓÇæ200KM','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of redundant Bays / Racks for re-use or sale as directed by Telkom where the site is within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all bays or Racks to be recovered for re-use.\nc.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nd.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\ne.	Test and make sure racks /bays are not live.\nf.	Update an inventory list of all recovered Bays / Racks.\ng.	Disconnect and remove Bays / Racks without damage to environment and loss of traffic.\nh.	Package Bays / Racks according to packaging specification\ni.	Stack recovered Bays / Racks in safe place which is not a fire risk.\nj.	Stack recovered Bays / Racks in safe place which is environmentally friendly.\nk.	Complete IE 6 recovery voucher and return to Local MC Procurement Services.\n\nThe unit for this item per rack or bay recovered (each).','EA',590.00,'RCVR,EQUIP:ER1.14,BAYS/RACKS REUSE','RECOVER, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER ER1.14, TYPE BAYS/RACKS REUSE, LOCATION 0-200KM:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO:\nUNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT MEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS\nTO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT (NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL BAYS OR RACKS TO BE RECOVERED FOR RE-USE,\nCOMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, TEST AND MAKE SURE RACKS\n/BAYS ARE NOT LIVE, UPDATE AN INVENTORY LIST OF ALL RECOVERED BAYS / RACKS, DISCONNECT AND REMOVE BAYS / RACKS WITHOUT DAMAGE TO\nENVIRONMENT AND LOSS OF TRAFFIC, PACKAGE BAYS / RACKS ACCORDING TO PACKAGING SPECIFICATION, STACK RECOVERED BAYS / RACKS IN SAFE\nPLACE WHICH IS NOT A FIRE RISK, STACK RECOVERED BAYS / RACKS IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS ENVIRONMENTALLY FRIENDLY, COMPLETE IE 6\nRECOVERY VOUCHER AND RETURN TO LOCAL MC PROCUREMENT SERVICES. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM PER RACK OR BAY RECOVERED (EACH)'),(3048874,'ER1.17','ER1.17 REHABLT ROOM >200KM','This item consists of the rehabilitation of a room where equipment has been removed, as directed by Telkom, where the site is more than a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	The rehabilitation of walls, ceilings, floors, structures, frames, fittings, equipment, plant, electrical, air-conditioning systems, etc. as per Telkom specification.\nb.	Rehabilitation activities such as closing of holes, painting, supporting, moving, re-positioning and provisioning of cable trays, run-ways, structures, frames, fittings, equipment, plant, electrical, air-conditioning, etc.\nc.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nd.	Identify and record in the SOS the items in the room to be rehabilitated. \ne.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nf.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\ng.	Rehabilitate items in the room where equipment has been removed as per Telkom specification.\n\nThe use of this item is subject to the provision and approval of an Estimate / quotation.\n\nThe unit for this item is per room, each (EA)','EA',1.00,'REPR,ROOM:ER1.17,>200KM','REPAIR, ROOM:ITEM NUMBER ER1.17, LOCATION >200KM:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE REHABILITATION OF WALLS,\nCEILINGS, FLOORS, STRUCTURES, FRAMES, FITTINGS, EQUIPMENT, PLANT, ELECTRICAL, AIR-CONDITIONING SYSTEMS, ETC AS PER TELKOM\nSPECIFICATION, REHABILITATION ACTIVITIES SUCH AS CLOSING OF HOLES, PAINTING, SUPPORTING, MOVING, RE-POSITIONING AND PROVISIONING OF\nCABLE TRAYS, RUN-WAYS, STRUCTURES, FRAMES, FITTINGS, EQUIPMENT, PLANT, ELECTRICAL, AIR-CONDITIONING, ETC, UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT\nMEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT\n(NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS THE ITEMS IN THE ROOM TO BE REHABILITATED, COMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK\nSHEET, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, REHABILITATE ITEMS IN THE ROOM WHERE EQUIPMENT HAS BEEN\nREMOVED AS PER TELKOM SPECIFICATION. THE USE OF THIS ITEM IS SUBJECT TO THE PROVISION AND APPROVAL OF AN ESTIMATE / QUOTATION. THE\nUNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ROOM, EACH (EA)'),(3048875,'ER1.11','ER1.11 RECVR EQUIP SCRP 0ΓÇæ200KM.','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of any type 