RECOVERY VOUCHER AND RETURN TO LOCAL MC PROCUREMENT\nSERVICES. THE UNIT FOR THIS IS PER KILOGRAM (KG)'),(3048876,'ER1.8','ER1.8 MIGRT ANLG CRCT 0-200KM','This item consists of the Migration of analogue circuits including preparation, assistance with ΓÇ£cut overΓÇ¥ and recording of migration data as directed by Telkom within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all services to be migrated.\nc.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nd.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\ne.	Update migration sheets.\nf.	Migrate circuits without damage to environment or loss of service.\ng.	Trace Circuits to be migrated.\nh.	Install new cross-connect, co-ax etc as per migration specification\ni.	Assist with the ΓÇ£cut overΓÇ¥.\n\nThe unit for this item is per analogue circuit, each','EA',28.00,'MIGRT,CON:ER1.8,ANLG CRCT 0-200KM','MIGRATE, CONNECTION:ITEM NUMBER ER1.8, TYPE ANLG CRCT 0-200KM:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE MIGRATION OF ANALOGUE CIRCUITS INCLUDING\nPREPARATION, ASSISTANCE WITH #CUT OVER# AND RECORDING OF MIGRATION DATA AS DIRECTED BY TELKOM WITHIN A 200KM RADIUS (AS THE CROW\nFLIES) FROM THE NOMINATED TELKOM REGIONAL DESPATCH POINT. THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT\nMEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT\n(NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL SERVICES TO BE MIGRATED, COMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET,\nOBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, UPDATE MIGRATION SHEETS, MIGRATE CIRCUITS WITHOUT DAMAGE TO\nENVIRONMENT OR LOSS OF SERVICE, TRACE CIRCUITS TO BE MIGRATED, INSTALL NEW CROSS-CONNECT, CO-AX ETC AS PER MIGRATION SPECIFICATION,\nASSIST WITH THE #CUT OVER#. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ANALOGUE CIRCUIT, EACH'),(3048877,'ER1.5','ER1.5 RECVR CRSS CONCT WRE 0ΓÇæ200KM','This item consists of the tracing and recovery of twisted pair cross connections (Jumper wire) from a live distribution frame (IDF/MDF) in a Telkom equipment room within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all cross connections that needs to be recovered.  Estimate the number of units to be recovered.\nc.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\nd.	Test and make sure cross connections are not live. \ne.	Disconnect the cross connect on the V side and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the V side to the E side, recover the Tie Cable where possible and the cross connect on the MDF.\nf.	Recover all redundant cross connect found on the IDF/MDF and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the point where the cross connect is found redundant on the IDF/MDF to the Tie cable, recover the Tie Cable where possible and the cross connect on the IDF/MDF\ng.	Provide detailed record on a standard template of all cross connections recovered, verticals, ports, and tie cables removed so that records may be updated.\nh.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\ni.	Recover cross connections without damage to environment or loss of service. \nj.	Stack recovered cross connections in a safe place which is not a fire risk.\nk.	Stack recovered cross connections in a safe place which is environmentally friendly.\nl.	Stack recovered cross connections in a safe place where it cannot be stolen.\nm.	Remove cross connections as per existing contract arrangement with Telkom.\n\nThe unit for this item is per kilogram (kg).','KG',441.00,'RCVR,CBL:ER1.5,CRSS CONCT WRE 0-200KM','RECOVER, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER ER1.5, TYPE CRSS CONCT WRE 0-200KM:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE TRACING AND RECOVERY OF TWISTED PAIR CROSS\nCONNECTIONS (JUMPER WIRE) FROM A LIVE DISTRIBUTION FRAME (IDF/MDF) IN A TELKOM EQUIPMENT ROOM WITHIN A 200KM RADIUS (AS THE CROW\nFLIES) FROM THE NOMINATED TELKOM REGIONAL DESPATCH POINT. THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT\nMEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT\n(NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL CROSS CONNECTIONS THAT NEEDS TO BE RECOVERED  ESTIMATE THE NUMBER OF\nUNITS TO BE RECOVERED, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, TEST AND MAKE SURE CROSS CONNECTIONS\nARE NOT LIVE, DISCONNECT THE CROSS CONNECT ON THE V SIDE AND RECOVER TO THE FINAL TERMINATION POINT EG FROM THE V SIDE TO THE E\nSIDE, RECOVER THE TIE CABLE WHERE POSSIBLE AND THE CROSS CONNECT ON THE MDF, RECOVER ALL REDUNDANT CROSS CONNECT FOUND ON THE\nIDF/MDF AND RECOVER TO THE FINAL TERMINATION POINT EG FROM THE POINT WHERE THE CROSS CONNECT IS FOUND REDUNDANT ON THE IDF/MDF TO\nTHE TIE CABLE, RECOVER THE TIE CABLE WHERE POSSIBLE AND THE CROSS CONNECT ON THE IDF/MDF, PROVIDE DETAILED RECORD ON A STANDARD\nTEMPLATE OF ALL CROSS CONNECTIONS RECOVERED, VERTICALS, PORTS, AND TIE CABLES REMOVED SO THAT RECORDS MAY BE UPDATED, COMPLETE\nTELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET, RECOVER CROSS CONNECTIONS WITHOUT DAMAGE TO ENVIRONMENT OR LOSS OF SERVICE, STACK RECOVERED CROSS\nCONNECTIONS IN A SAFE PLACE WHICH IS NOT A FIRE RISK, STACK RECOVERED CROSS CONNECTIONS IN A SAFE PLACE WHICH IS ENVIRONMENTALLY\nFRIENDLY, STACK RECOVERED CROSS CONNECTIONS IN A SAFE PLACE WHERE IT CANNOT BE STOLEN, REMOVE CROSS CONNECTIONS AS PER EXISTING\nCONTRACT ARRANGEMENT WITH TELKOM. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER KILOGRAM (KG)'),(3048878,'ER1.4','ER1.4 RECVR FOC COMPX 0-200KM','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of any type of optic fibre cable in a Telkom equipment room, where the cable harness contains cables that carry live traffic (Complex), within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all optic fibre cables that needs to be recovered.  Estimate the number of units to be recovered.\nc.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\nd.	Test and make sure the cables are not live.\ne.	Disconnect cable at Equipment and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the equipment to the OMDF the Inter Facilities Fibre on the OMDF to the Interconnect Fibre, recover the Interconnect Fibre where possible. \nf.	Recover all redundant cable found under the floor / overhead and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the point where the cable is found redundant under the floor to the OMDF the Inter Facilities cable on the OMDF to the Interconnect cable, recover the Interconnect Cable where possible.\ng.	Provide a detailed record on a standard template of all cables recovered, verticals, ports, and tie cables removed so that records may be updated.\nh.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\ni.	Recover cable without damage to environment or loss of service. \nj.	Stack recovered cable in safe place which is not a fire risk.\nk.	Stack recovered cable in safe place which is environmentally friendly.\nl.	Stack recovered Optic fibre cable in a safe place where it cannot be stolen. \nm.	Remove cable as per existing contract arrangement with Telkom.\n\nThe unit for this item is per kilogram (kg).','