-200KM','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of any type of Optic cable in a Telkom equipment room, where the cable form is not carrying any traffic (Simplex), within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all optic fibre cables that needs to be recovered.  Estimate the amount of units to be recovered.\nc.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\nd.	Test and make sure cables are not live.\ne.	Disconnect cable at Equipment and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the equipment to the OMDF the Inter Facilities Fibre on the OMDF to the Interconnect Fibre, recover the Interconnect Fibre where possible. \nf.	Recover all redundant cable found under the floor / overhead and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the point where the cable is found redundant under the floor to the OMDF, the Inter Facilities cable on the OMDF to the Interconnect cable, recover the Interconnect Cable where possible.\ng.	Provide a detailed record on a standard template of all cables recovered, verticals, ports, and tie cables removed so that records may be updated.\nh.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\ni.	Recover cable without damage to environment or loss of service.\nj.	Stack recovered cable in safe place which is not a fire risk.\nk.	Stack recovered cable in safe place which is environmentally friendly.\nl.	Remove cable as per existing contract arrangement with Telkom.\n\nThe unit for this item is per kilogram (kg).','KG',51.00,'RCVR,CBL:ER1.3,FOC SIMPLX 0-200KM','RECOVER, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER ER1.3, TYPE FOC SIMPLX 0-200KM:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE REMOVAL, RECORDING, AND RECOVERY OF ANY TYPE OF\nOPTIC CABLE IN A TELKOM EQUIPMENT ROOM, WHERE THE CABLE FORM IS NOT CARRYING ANY TRAFFIC (SIMPLEX), WITHIN A 200KM RADIUS (AS THE\nCROW FLIES) FROM THE NOMINATED TELKOM REGIONAL DESPATCH POINT. THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT\nMEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT\n(NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL OPTIC FIBRE CABLES THAT NEEDS TO BE RECOVERED  ESTIMATE THE AMOUNT OF\nUNITS TO BE RECOVERED, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, TEST AND MAKE SURE CABLES ARE NOT LIVE,\nDISCONNECT CABLE AT EQUIPMENT AND RECOVER TO THE FINAL TERMINATION POINT EG FROM THE EQUIPMENT TO THE OMDF THE INTER FACILITIES\nFIBRE ON THE OMDF TO THE INTERCONNECT FIBRE, RECOVER THE INTERCONNECT FIBRE WHERE POSSIBLE, RECOVER ALL REDUNDANT CABLE FOUND UNDER\nTHE FLOOR / OVERHEAD AND RECOVER TO THE FINAL TERMINATION POINT EG FROM THE POINT WHERE THE CABLE IS FOUND REDUNDANT UNDER THE\nFLOOR TO THE OMDF, THE INTER FACILITIES CABLE ON THE OMDF TO THE INTERCONNECT CABLE, RECOVER THE INTERCONNECT CABLE WHERE POSSIBLE,\nPROVIDE A DETAILED RECORD ON A STANDARD TEMPLATE OF ALL CABLES RECOVERED, VERTICALS, PORTS, AND TIE CABLES REMOVED SO THAT RECORDS\nMAY BE UPDATED, COMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET, RECOVER CABLE WITHOUT DAMAGE TO ENVIRONMENT OR LOSS OF SERVICE, STACK\nRECOVERED CABLE IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS NOT A FIRE RISK, STACK RECOVERED CABLE IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS ENVIRONMENTALLY FRIENDLY,\nREMOVE CABLE AS PER EXISTING CONTRACT ARRANGEMENT WITH TELKOM. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER KILOGRAM (KG).'),(3048940,'ER1.9','ER1.9 MIGRT DGTL CRCT 0ΓÇæ200KM','This item consists of the Migration of digital circuits including preparation, assistance with ΓÇ£cut overΓÇ¥ and recording of migration data as directed by Telkom within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all services to be migrated.\nc.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nd.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\ne.	Update migration sheets.\nf.	Migrate circuits without damage to environment or loss of service.\ng.	Package Back Planes on site according to Telkom SA specifications.\nh.	Trace Circuits to be migrated.\ni.	Install new cross-connect, co-ax etc as per migration specification\nj.	Assist with the ΓÇ£cut overΓÇ¥.\n\nThe unit for this item is per digital circuit, each.','EA',31.00,'MIGRT,DTA:ER1.9 DGTL CRCT 0-200KM','MIGRATE, DATA:TYPE ER1.9 DGTL CRCT 0-200KM:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT MEETING TO DETERMINE\nTHE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT (NPM: ANCILLARY\nSERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL SERVICES TO BE MIGRATED, COMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY\nWORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, UPDATE MIGRATION SHEETS, MIGRATE CIRCUITS WITHOUT DAMAGE TO ENVIRONMENT OR LOSS OF\nSERVICE, PACKAGE BACK PLANES ON SITE ACCORDING TO TELKOM SA SPECIFICATIONS, TRACE CIRCUITS TO BE MIGRATED, INSTALL NEW\nCROSS-CONNECT, CO-AX ETC AS PER MIGRATION SPECIFICATION, ASSIST WITH THE #CUT OVER#. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DIGITAL CIRCUIT,\nEACH'),(3048941,'ER1.16','ER1.16 REHABLT ROOM 0ΓÇæ200KM','This item consists of the rehabilitation of a room where equipment has been removed as directed by Telkom where the site is within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	The rehabilitation of walls, ceilings, floors, structures, frames, fittings, equipment, plant, electrical, air-conditioning systems, etc. as per Telkom specification.\nb.	Rehabilitation activities such as closing of holes, painting, supporting, moving, re-positioning and provisioning of cable trays, run-ways, structures, frames, fittings, equipment, plant, electrical, air-conditioning, etc.\nc.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nd.	Identify and record in the SOS the items in the room to be rehabilitated. \ne.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nf.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\n\nThe use of this item is subject to the provision and approval of an Estimate / quotation.\n\nThe unit for this item is per room, each (EA)','EA',1.00,'REPR,ROOM:ER1.16,0-200KM','REPAIR, ROOM:ITEM NUMBER ER1.16, LOCATION 0-200KM:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE REHABILITATION OF WALLS,\nCEILINGS, FLOORS, STRUCTURES, FRAMES, FITTINGS, EQUIPMENT, PLANT, ELECTRICAL, AIR-CONDITIONING SYSTEMS, ETC AS PER TELKOM\nSPECIFICATION, REHABILITATION ACTIVITIES SUCH AS CLOSING OF HOLES, PAINTING, SUPPORTING, MOVING, RE-POSITIONING AND PROVISIONING OF\nCABLE TRAYS, RUN-WAYS, STRUCTURES, FRAMES, FITTINGS, EQUIPMENT, PLANT, ELECTRICAL, AIR-CONDITIONING, ETC, UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT\nMEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT\n(NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS THE ITEMS IN THE ROOM TO BE REHABILITATED, COMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK\nSHEET, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS. THE USE OF THIS ITEM IS SUBJECT TO THE PROVISION AND\nAPPROVAL OF AN ESTIMATE / QUOTATION. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ROOM, EACH (EA)'),(3048942,'ER1.13','ER1.13 RECVR BCKPLAN LRG REUSE 0ΓÇæ200KM','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of any type of redundant Back Plane / Sub-Frame ΓÇô Large as directed by Telkom for Re-use or to be Sold, within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all equipment to be recovered for re-use.\nc.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nd.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\ne.	Test and make sure equipment are not live.\nf.	Update an inventory list of all recovered cards, modules and systems.\ng.	The recovery of any Back Plane or sub-frame with a volume exceeding 0.06m┬│.  (Large - Typical dimensions = 1.2m (h) x 0.3m (d) x 0.6m (w))\nh.	Disconnect and remove if terminated without damage to environment or loss of service.\ni.	Package Back Planes on site according to Telkom SA specifications.\nj.	Complete IE 6 Documentation as per Telkom SA procedure\nk.	Update list of recovered cards with IE 6 Number per item.\nl.	Transport to Local MC Store (Details will be provided by Telkom)\nm.	Telkom to provide a value of the equipment to be transported the service provider must ensure that adequate insurance is provided.\nn.	Stack recovered equipment in safe place which is not a fire risk.\no.	Stack recovered equipment in safe place which is environmentally friendly.\n\nThe unit for this item is per Back Plane, each.','EA',580.00,'RCVR,EQUIP:ER1.13,BCKPLAN LRG REUSE','RECOVER, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER ER1.13, TYPE BCKPLAN LRG REUSE, LOCATION 0-200KM:THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO:,\nUNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT MEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS\nTO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT (NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL EQUIPMENT TO BE RECOVERED FOR RE-USE,\nCOMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY 