COVERED DUCTING IN SAFE PLACE WHICH\nIS NOT A FIRE RISK, STACK RECOVERED DUCTING IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS ENVIRONMENTALLY FRIENDLY, REMOVE DUCTING AS PER EXISTING\nCONTRACT ARRANGEMENT WITH TELKOM. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METER (MT)'),(3048947,'ER1.6','ER1.6 RECVR DCTN 0-200KM','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of any type of redundant Ducting or Trunking under floor / overhead as directed by Telkom within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization Requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all ducting that needs to be recovered.\nc.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\nd.	Determine that ducting is redundant.\ne.	Remove Redundant Ducting. \nf.	Provide detailed record on a standard template of all ducting removed.\ng.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\nh.	Recover Ducting without damage to environment or loss of service. \ni.	Stack recovered Ducting in safe place which is not a fire risk.\nj.	Stack recovered Ducting in safe place which is environmentally friendly.\nk.	Remove Ducting as per existing contract arrangement with Telkom.\n\nThe unit for this item is per meter (MT).','MT',60.00,'RCVR,EQUIP:ER1.6,DCTN 0-200KM','RECOVER, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER ER1.6, TYPE DCTN 0-200KM:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE REMOVAL, RECORDING, AND RECOVERY OF ANY TYPE OF\nREDUNDANT DUCTING OR TRUNKING UNDER FLOOR / OVERHEAD AS DIRECTED BY TELKOM WITHIN A 200KM RADIUS (AS THE CROW FLIES) FROM THE\nNOMINATED TELKOM REGIONAL DESPATCH POINT. THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: UNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT MEETING TO DETERMINE\nTHE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS TO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT (NPM: ANCILLARY\nSERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL DUCTING THAT NEEDS TO BE RECOVERED, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING\nACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, DETERMINE THAT DUCTING IS REDUNDANT, REMOVE REDUNDANT DUCTING, PROVIDE DETAILED RECORD ON A STANDARD TEMPLATE\nOF ALL DUCTING REMOVED, COMPLETE TELKOM RECOVERY TICK SHEET, RECOVER DUCTING WITHOUT DAMAGE TO ENVIRONMENT OR LOSS OF SERVICE,\nSTACK RECOVERED DUCTING IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS NOT A FIRE RISK, STACK RECOVERED DUCTING IN SAFE PLACE WHICH IS ENVIRONMENTALLY\nFRIENDLY, REMOVE DUCTING AS PER EXISTING CONTRACT ARRANGEMENT WITH TELKOM. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METER (MT)'),(3048950,'ER1.2','ER1.2 RECVR CU CABL COMPX 0-200KM','This item consists of the removal, recording, and recovery of any type of copper cable in a Telkom equipment room, where the cable harness contains cables that carry live traffic, (Complex) within a 200km radius (as the crow flies) from the nominated Telkom regional despatch point.\n\nThe rate will include but is not limited to:\na.	Undertake a site visit meeting to determine the Scope of Services (SOS) of the Optimization requirement. The relevant role players to be involved up-front (NPM: Ancillary Services)\nb.	Identify and record in the SOS all copper cables that need to be recovered.  Estimate the amount of units to be recovered.\nc.	Obtaining all necessary working refs and making access arrangements.\nd.	Test and make sure cable is not live.\ne.	Disconnect cable at Equipment and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the equipment to the IDF the cross connect on the IDF to the Tie cable, recover the Tie Cable where possible and the cross connect on the MDF.\nf.	Recover all redundant cable found under the floor / overhead and recover to the final termination point e.g. from the point where the cable is found redundant under the floor to the IDF, the cross connect on the IDF to the Tie cable, recover the Tie Cable where possible and the cross connect on the MDF.\ng.	Provide a detailed record on a standard template of all cables recovered, verticals, ports, and tie cables removed so that records may be updated.\nh.	Complete Telkom recovery tick sheet.\ni.	Recover cable without damage to environment or loss of service. \nj.	Stack recovered cable in safe place which is not a fire risk.\nk.	Stack recovered cable in safe place which is environmentally friendly.\nl.	Stack recovered Copper cable in a safe place where it cannot be stolen. \nm.	Remove cable as per existing contract arrangement with Telkom.\n\nThe unit for this item is per kilogram (kg).','KG',29.46,'RCVR,CBL:ER1.2,CU CABL COMPX 0-200KM','RECOVER, CABLE:ITEM NUMBER ER1.2, TYPE CU CABL COMPX 0-200KM:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE REMOVAL, RECORDING, AND RECOVERY OF ANY TYPE\nOF COPPER CABLE IN A TELKOM EQUIPMENT ROOM, WHERE THE CABLE HARNESS CONTAINS CABLES THAT CARRY LIVE TRAFFIC, (COMPLEX) WITHIN A\n200KM RADIUS (AS THE CROW FLIES) FROM THE NOMINATED TELKOM REGIONAL DESPATCH POINT. THE RATE WILL INCLUDE BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO:\nUNDERTAKE A SITE VISIT MEETING TO DETERMINE THE SCOPE OF SERVICES (SOS) OF THE OPTIMIZATION REQUIREMENT THE RELEVANT ROLE PLAYERS\nTO BE INVOLVED UP-FRONT (NPM: ANCILLARY SERVICES), IDENTIFY AND RECORD IN THE SOS ALL COPPER CABLES THAT NEED TO BE RECOVERED\nESTIMATE THE AMOUNT OF UNITS TO BE RECOVERED, OBTAINING ALL NECESSARY WORKING REFS AND MAKING ACCESS ARRANGEMENTS, TEST AND MAKE\nSURE CABLE IS NOT LIVE, DISCONNECT CABLE AT EQUIPMENT AND RECOVER TO THE FINAL TERMINATION POINT EG FROM THE EQUIPMENT TO THE IDF\nTHE CROSS CONNECT ON THE IDF TO THE TIE CABLE, RECOVER THE TIE CABLE WHERE POSSIBLE AND THE CROSS CONNECT ON THE MDF, RECOVER ALL\nREDUNDANT CABLE FOUND UNDER THE FLOOR / OVERHEAD AND RECOVER TO THE FINAL TERMINATION POINT EG FROM THE POINT WHERE THE CABLE IS\nFOUND REDUNDANT UNDER THE FLOOR TO THE IDF, THE CROSS CONNECT ON THE IDF TO THE TIE CABLE, RECOVER THE TIE CABLE WHERE POSSIBLE AND\nTHE CROSS CONNECT ON THE MDF, PROVIDE A DETAILED RECORD ON A STANDARD TEMP