DES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: COST OF THE 63A SINGLE\nPHASE EARTH LEAKAGE, SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER EARTH LEAKAGE, EACH (EA)'),(3049442,'AC1.12','AC1.12 PRVD AC DB 12 WAY','This item consists of the provisioning of an AC distribution box, 12-way\n The rate includes but is not limited to:\nΓÇó	Cost of the AC distribution box, 12-way\nΓÇó	Shipping (Local and Foreign)\nΓÇó	Storage\n The unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per distribution box, each (EA)','EA',250.00,'PRVD,EQUIP:AC1.12,AC DB 12 WAY','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER AC1.12, TYPE AC DB 12 WAY:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE PROVISIONING OF AN AC DISTRIBUTION BOX, 12-WAY.\nTHE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: COST OF THE AC DISTRIBUTION BOX, 12-WAY, SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE. THE UNIT\nOF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DISTRIBUTION BOX, EACH (EA)'),(3049443,'AC1.18','AC1.18 PRVD SNGL PH CRCT BRKR 40A','This item consists of the provisioning of a Single Phase circuit breaker, 40A.\n The rate includes but is not limited to:\nΓÇó	Cost of the 40A Single Phase circuit breaker.\nΓÇó	Shipping (Local and Foreign)\nΓÇó	Storage\n The unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per circuit breaker, each (EA)','EA',200.00,'PRVD,EQUIP:AC1.18,SNGL PH CRCT BRKR 40A','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER AC1.18, TYPE SNGL PH CRCT BRKR 40A:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: COST OF THE 40A SINGLE\nPHASE CBI CIRCUIT BREAKER, SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CIRCUIT BREAKER,\nEACH (EA)'),(3049549,'B6.1.8','B6.1.8 PAINT WALL, CONDUIT AND BACKBOARD','This item consists of the painting of the backboard, any conduit and wall onto which the backboard or conduit has been fastened or secured.\nThe rate includes:\nΓÇó	The preparation of the surfaces to be painted.\nΓÇó	The supply of the paint and other relevant materials.\nThe unit for this item is per SQ metre.','M2',78.24,'PAINT,SURF:B6.1.8,WALL, CND & BACKBOARD','PAINT, SURFACE:ITEM NUMBER B6.1.8, TYPE WALL, CONDUIT AND BACKBOARD:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE PAINTING OF THE BACKBOARD, ANY\nCONDUIT AND WALL ONTO WHICH THE BACKBOARD OR CONDUIT HAS BEEN FASTENED OR SECURED. THE RATE INCLUDES: THE PREPARATION OF THE\nSURFACES TO BE PAINTED. THE SUPPLY OF THE PAINT AND OTHER RELEVANT MATERIALS. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SQ METRE'),(3049675,'FTTX 1.2','FTTX 1.2 HOM CONCTN (DURING PROJECT)','This item consists of the installation and commissioning, and integration of a FTTH service (Home Connection) from the Demarcation point (Slim/Budi-box) to the ONT during the Project period.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na)	Aerial home connections. \nb)	Underground home connections where existing infrastructure is available. \nc)	Standard entries into the home using light machinery/tools.\nd)	The supply of an average of 40m drop cable per home.\ne)	Home connections that are done during the HP Build, and up to a maximum of 30 days after submission for Acceptance/ECC of Homes Passed Group (splitter area)\nf)	All project management and administrative activities\ng)	Obtaining all work orders\nh)	Complete Installation and Commissioning of FTTH service from the last Demarcation point to the single point where the customer wants the service (i.e. slim-box / budi-box to ONT at customer premises) \ni)	Installation of the ATB\nj)	Supply and installation of the optic fibre from the Network Demarcation point to the ONT (i.e. drop fibre)\nk)	Installation of Micro duct, where required (i.e. single / dual / 4way)\nl)	Installation Patch cords, \nm)	Supply of all minor materials (i.e. Fasteners, Saddles, Screw Ring, Glue etc.)\nn)	Underground access where infrastructure is available \no)	Overhead access (from the Slimbox / FlatFist / Helleman to the ONT)\np)	HC POE (pipe of entry) installation where required.\nq)	Clear vegetation around drop fibre (1 meter radius x maximum girth of 300mm)\nr)	Slack management\ns)	Termination of the optic fibre (i.e. Demarcation point, ATB, ONT)\nt)	fusion Splicing and/or Mechanical Splicing and/or hardened connector at the following elements:\ni).	Demarcation Point\nii).	ATB\niii).	ONT\nu)	FTTH service testing over the full access network (including voice and FTTH ports)\nv)	Activation of FTTH service / Migration of service with DTAC \nw)	Installation, set-up, configuration of FTTH compatible modem / router when required.\nx)	Recording and updating of all the necessary information on the relevant Telkom systems / platforms (i.e. Clik)\ny)	Shipping (local and foreign)\nz)	Storage of drop cable and miscellaneous items\naa)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from the site \nbb)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections \ncc)	Site management\ndd)	All travel related costs, such as:\ni).	Vehicle costs,\nii).	Fuel,\niii).	Travelling losses (Labour)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na)	The supply of Micro duct, where required (i.e. single / dual / 4way) (Telkom to supply)\nb)	The supply of Legacy services\nc)	Patch cords, (Telkom to supply)\nd)	The supply of the ATB (Telkom to supply)\ne)	The supply of ONT (Telkom to supply)\nf)	The supply of FTTH compatible modem / router (ISP to provide)\n\nNote: \na)	This item may only be used where an order is placed for at least 50 Homes connect in an area.\nb)	The Scheduling, dispatching, appointments, and management of HCΓÇÖs is the responsibility of OS and will be managed by OS via the Click system tools. \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per home connected, each (EA)','EA',1500.00,'BLD,SYS:FTTX 1.2,HOM CONCTN (DRNG PROJ)','BUILD, SYSTEM:ITEM NUMBER FTTX 1.2, TYPE HOM CONCTN (DURING PROJECT):THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE INSTALLATION AND COMMISSIONING, AND\nINTEGRATION OF A FTTH SERVICE (HOME CONNECTION) FROM THE DEMARCATION POINT (SLIM/BUDI-BOX) TO THE ONT DURING THE PROJECT PERIOD.\nTHE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: AERIAL HOME CONNECTIONS, UNDERGROUND HOME CONNECTIONS WHERE EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE IS\nAVAILABLE, STANDARD ENTRIES INTO THE HOME USING LIGHT MACHINERY/TOOLS, THE SUPPLY OF AN AVERAGE OF 40M DROP CABLE PER HOME, HOME\nCONNECTIONS THAT ARE DONE DURING THE HP BUILD, AND UP TO A MAXIMUM OF 30 DAYS AFTER SUBMISSION FOR ACCEPTANCE/ECC OF HOMES PASSED\nGROUP (SPLITTER AREA), ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES, OBTAINING ALL WORK ORDERS, COMPLETE INSTALLATION AND\nCOMMISSIONING OF FTTH SERVICE FROM THE LAST DEMARCATION POINT TO THE SINGLE POINT WHERE THE CUSTOMER WANTS THE SERVICE (I.E.\nSLIM-BOX / BUDI-BOX TO ONT AT CUSTOMER PREMISES), INSTALLATION OF THE ATB, SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF THE OPTIC FIBRE FROM THE\nNETWORK DEMARCATION POINT TO THE ONT (I.E. DROP FIBRE), INSTALLATION OF MICRO DUCT, WHERE REQUIRED (I.E. SINGLE / DUAL / 4WAY),\nINSTALLATION PATCH CORDS, SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS (I.E. FASTENERS, SADDLES, SCREW RING, GLUE ETC.), UNDERGROUND ACCESS WHERE\nINFRASTRUCTURE IS AVAILABLE, OVERHEAD ACCESS (FROM THE SLIMBOX / FLATFIST / HELLEMAN TO THE ONT), HC POE (PIPE OF ENTRY)\nINSTALLATION WHERE REQUIRED, CLEAR VEGETATION AROUND DROP FIBRE (1 METER RADIUS X MAXIMUM GIRTH OF 300MM), SLACK MANAGEMENT,\nTERMINATION OF THE OPTIC FIBRE (I.E. DEMARCATION POINT, ATB, ONT), FUSION SPLICING AND/OR MECHANICAL SPLICING AND/OR HARDENED\nCONNECTOR AT THE FOLLOWING ELEMENTS: DEMARCATION POINT, ATB, ONT, FTTH SERVICE TESTING OVER THE FULL ACCESS NETWORK (INCLUDING\nVOICE AND FTTH PORTS), ACTIVATION OF FTTH SERVICE / MIGRATION OF SERVICE WITH DTAC, INSTALLATION, SET-UP, CONFIGURATION OF FTTH\nCOMPATIBLE MODEM / ROUTER WHEN REQUIRED, RECORDING AND UPDATING OF ALL THE NECESSARY INFORMATION ON THE RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS /'),(3049691,'FTTX1.1','FTTX1.1 ENG & BLD HOM PASS (BROWN FIELD)','This item consists of the survey, design/engineering, installation, commissioning, and integration activities for FTTX from the FDP to the demarcation point (i.e. Slim / Budi-box, etc.) on existing infrastructure, Overhead and / or Underground (Brown field). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na)	Arranging and obtaining all site access approvals\nb)	All project management and administrative activities\nc)	Dispatching resources and all Logistical activities \nd)	Site surveys \ne)	Detailed Design/Engineering\nf)	Installation of: \ni).	Fibre cable (OH)\nii).	Fittings and fasteners\niii).	Boxes and enclosures (i.e. Slim box, B8G, FOSC400AG, Budi box, or related products), \niv).	Splitters, \nv).	Micro ducts (7/4/2/ way) in existing pipes (110mm)\nvi).	Fibre cable (UG) into micro ducts (Blow-in / Floating)\ng)	Supply of minor materials (i.e. labels, micro duct couplings, cable ties, consumables / cleaning materials, etc.)\nh)	Splicing \ni)	Testing, Handover/ECC\nj)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from the site \nk)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections \nl)	Site management\nm)	Capturing of as-built documentation & updating of systems\nn)	All travel related costs, such as:\ni).	Vehicle costs,\nii).	Fuel,\niii).	Travelling losses (Labour)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na)	The supply of Major material (i.e. Fibre cable, Ducts, poles, enclosures, etc.)\nb)	Backbone infrastructure, \nc)	The actual submission of wayleave applications to the authorities and management thereof.\nd)	CBS uploading. \ne)	Any new infrastructure build (i.e. new Manholes / utility boxes, trenching and laying pipes / ducts, planting additional poles, etc.)\nf)	Repair of existing infrastructure. (i.e. Locating and repairing of blocked pipes, repairing or rebuilding PJBΓÇÖs / AJBΓÇÖs / M/HΓÇÖs, replacing broken poles, etc.)\n\nNote: \na)	This item may only be used where an order is placed for at least 500 Homes passed in an area.\nb)	All new infrastructure and repair of existing infrastructure may be claimed separately, according to the contracted BOQ items. Approval needs to be obtained from Telkom (CR) via a site instruction before any excluded work is undertaken.\n\nThe unit of measure is per home passed, each (EA).','EA',1500.00,'PRVD,EQUIP:FTTX1.1,ENG & BLD HOM PASS','PROVIDE, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER FTTX1.1, TYPE ENG AND BLD HOM PASS:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE SURVEY, DESIGN/ENGINEERING,\nINSTALLATION, COMMISSIONING, AND INTEGRATION ACTIVITIES FOR FTTX FROM THE FDP TO THE DEMARCATION POINT (I.E. SLIM / BUDI-BOX, ETC.)\nON EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE, OVERHEAD AND / OR UNDERGROUND (BROWN FIELD). THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND\nOBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS APPROVALS, ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES, DISPATCHING RESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL\nACTIVITIES, SITE SURVEYS, DETAILED DESIGN/ENGINEERING, INSTALLATION OF: FIBRE CABLE (OH), FITTINGS AND FASTENERS, BOXES AND\nENCLOSURES (I.E. SLIM BOX, B8G, FOSC400AG, BUDI BOX, OR RELATED PRODUCTS), SPLITTERS, MICRO DUCTS (7/4/2/ WAY) IN EXISTING PIPES\n(110MM), FIBRE CABLE (UG) INTO MICRO DUCTS (BLOW-IN / FLOATING), SUPPLY OF MINOR MATERIALS (I.E. LABELS, MICRO DUCT COUPLINGS,\nCABLE TIES, CONSUMABLES / CLEANING MATERIALS, ETC.), SPLICING, \nTESTING, HANDOVER/ECC, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND\nEQUIPMENT TO AND FROM THE SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE MANAGEMENT, CAPTURING OF AS-BUILT DOCUMENTATION &\nUPDATING OF SYSTEMS, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS, SUCH AS: VEHICLE COSTS, FUEL, TRAVELLING LOSSES (LABOUR). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE\nSUPPLY OF MAJOR MATERIAL (I.E. FIBRE CABLE, DUCTS, POLES, ENCLOSURES, ETC.), BACKBONE INFRASTRUCTURE, THE ACTUAL SUBMISSION OF\nWAYLEAVE APPLICATIONS TO THE AUTHORITIES AND MANAGEMENT THEREOF, CBS UPLOADING, ANY NEW INFRASTRUCTURE BUILD (I.E. NEW MANHOLES /\nUTILITY BOXES, TRENCHING AND LAYING PIPES / DUCTS, PLANTING ADDITIONAL POLES, ETC.), REPAIR OF EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE. (I.E.\nLOCATING AND REPAIRING OF BLOCKED PIPES, REPAIRING OR REBUILDING PJB#S / AJB#S / M/H#S, REPLACING BROKEN POLES, ETC.). NOTE: THIS\nITEM MAY ONLY BE USED WHERE AN ORDER IS PLACED FOR AT LEAST 500 HOMES PASSED IN AN AREA, ALL NEW INFRASTRUCTURE AND REPAIR OF\nEXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY, ACCORDING TO THE CONTRACTED BOQ ITEMS. APPROVAL NEEDS TO BE OBTAINED FROM TELKOM'),(3049882,'FTTX2.1','FTTX2.1 BLD HOM PASS (BROWN FIELD)','This item consists of the installation, commissioning, and integration activities for FTTX from the FDP to the demarcation point (i.e. Slim / Budi-box, etc.) on existing infrastructure, Overhead and / or Underground (Brown field). \n \nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na)	Arranging and obtaining all site access approvals\nb)	All project management and administrative activities\nc)	Dispatching resources and all Logistical activities \nd)	Installation of: \ni).	Fibre cable (OH)\nii).	Fittings and fasteners\niii).	Boxes and enclosures (i.e. Slim box, B8G, FOSC400AG, Budi box, or related products), \niv).	Splitters, \nv).	Micro ducts (7/4/2/ way) in existing pipes (110mm)\nvi).	Fibre cable (UG) into micro ducts (Blow-in / Floating)\ne)	Supply of minor materials (i.e. labels, micro duct couplings, cable ties, consumables / cleaning materials, etc.)\nf)	Splicing \ng)	Testing, Handover/ECC\nh)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from the site \ni)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections \nj)	Site management\nk)	All travel related costs, such as:\ni).	Vehicle costs,\nii).	Fuel,\niii).	Travelling losses (Labour)\n \nThe rate excludes:\na)	The supply of Major material (i.e. Fibre cable, Ducts, poles, enclosures, etc.)\nb)	Backbone infrastructure, \nc)	Any new infrastructure build (i.e. new Manholes / utility boxes, trenching and laying pipes / ducts, planting additional poles, etc.)\nd)	Repair of existing infrastructure. (i.e. Locating and repairing of blocked pipes, repairing or rebuilding PJBΓÇÖs / AJBΓÇÖs / M/HΓÇÖs, replacing broken poles, etc.)\n \nNote: \na)	This item may only be used where an order is placed for at least 500 Homes passed in an area.\nb)	All new infrastructure and repair of existing infrastructure may be claimed separately, according to the contracted BOQ items. Approval needs to be obtained from Telkom (CR) via a site instruction before any excluded work is undertaken.\n \nThe unit of measure is per home passed, each (EA).','EA',1180.00,'FTTX2.1 BLD HOM PASS (BROWN FIELD)','BUILD, SYSTEM:ITEM NUMBER FTTX2.1, TYPE HOM PASS BROWN FIELD:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE INSTALLATION, COMMISSIONING, AND INTEGRATION\nACTIVITIES FOR FTTX FROM THE FDP TO THE DEMARCATION POINT (I.E. SLIM / BUDI-BOX, ETC.) ON EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE, OVERHEAD AND /\nOR UNDERGROUND (BROWN FIELD). THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS APPROVALS, ALL\nPROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIES, DISPATCHING RESOURCES AND ALL LOGISTICAL ACTIVITIES, INSTALLATION OF: FIBRE CABLE\n(OH), FITTINGS AND FASTENERS, BOXES AND ENCLOSURES (I.E. SLIM BOX, B8G, FOSC400AG, BUDI BOX, OR RELATED PRODUCTS), SPLITTERS, MICRO\nDUCTS (7/4/2/ WAY) IN EXISTING PIPES (110MM), FIBRE CABLE (UG) INTO MICRO DUCTS (BLOW-IN / FLOATING), SUPPLY OF MINOR MATERIALS\n(I.E. LABELS, MICRO DUCT COUPLINGS, CABLE TIES, CONSUMABLES / CLEANING MATERIALS, ETC.), SPLICING, TESTING, HANDOVER/ECC,\nTRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM THE SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE\nMANAGEMENT, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS, SUCH AS: VEHICLE COSTS, FUEL, TRAVELLING LOSSES (LABOUR). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE SUPPLY OF\nMAJOR MATERIAL (I.E. FIBRE CABLE, DUCTS, POLES, ENCLOSURES, ETC.), BACKBONE INFRASTRUCTURE, ANY NEW INFRASTRUCTURE BUILD (I.E. NEW\nMANHOLES / UTILITY BOXES, TRENCHING AND LAYING PIPES / DUCTS, PLANTING ADDITIONAL POLES, ETC.), REPAIR OF EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE.\n(I.E. LOCATING AND REPAIRING OF BLOCKED PIPES, REPAIRING OR REBUILDING PJB#S / AJB#S / M/H#S, REPLACING BROKEN POLES, ETC.). NOTE:\nTHIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED WHERE AN ORDER IS PLACED FOR AT LEAST 500 HOMES PASSED IN AN AREA, ALL NEW INFRASTRUCTURE AND REPAIR OF\nEXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY, ACCORDING TO THE CONTRACTED BOQ ITEMS. APPROVAL NEEDS TO BE OBTAINED FROM TELKOM\n(CR) VIA A SITE INSTRUCTION BEFORE ANY EXCLUDED WORK IS UNDERTAKEN. THE UNIT OF MEASURE IS PER HOME PASSED, EACH (EA)'),(3052856,'CI6.2','CI6.2 CNDCT GPR TEST','This item consists of the detection of utility services by means of a ground penetrating radar (GPR) device up to a maximum depth of 8m.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	Obtaining all access approvals\nb.	Safeguarding the site where the tests will be conducted\nc.	Traffic control\nd.	The setting up of the GPR testing equipment\ne.	Detecting all utility services within a 3m width (1.5m on either side of the planned infrastructure) such as;\ni.	Water pipes, including both water supply and private irrigation pipes;\nii.	Communication ducts;\niii.	Sewer pipes;\niv.	Direct buried power and telecommunications cables; and\nv.	Any other underground infrastructure (gas lines, fuel lines, etc.).\nf.	Plotting of all the services in the scanned area indicating the position (GPS co-ordinates) and depth thereof,\ng.	Marking of the area scanned, indicating the services detected.\nh.	Generating records to prove each scanning application.\ni.	Storing of these records (5 years) and making them freely available upon request by Telkom or as defined by the scope of work.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee items).\nb.	3-Dimensional scanning.\n\nNote:\na.	This item may only be used for payment with prior approval from Telkom. \nb.	The Operator/s of GPR device shall be competent. Evidence of competency shall be made available on request by Telkom.\nc.	Scans should be at least 1 m deeper than the planned drilling / excavation depth.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na.	OS-001559 (OS-CTSO-GL-0066)\nb.	SPEC-000325 (SP-0325)\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per linear meter scanned, (MT)','MT',110.00,'CI6.2 CNDCT GPR TEST','TEST, EARTH:ITEM NUMBER CI6.2, TYPE CNDCT GPR TEST:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE DETECTION OF UTILITY SERVICES BY MEANS OF A GROUND\nPENETRATING RADAR (GPR) DEVICE UP TO A MAXIMUM DEPTH OF 8M. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: OBTAINING ALL ACCESS\nAPPROVALS, SAFEGUARDING THE SITE WHERE THE TESTS WILL BE CONDUCTED, TRAFFIC CONTROL, THE SETTING UP OF THE GPR TESTING EQUIPMENT,\nDETECTING ALL UTILITY SERVICES WITHIN A 3M WIDTH (1.5M ON EITHER SIDE OF THE PLANNED INFRASTRUCTURE) SUCH AS: WATER PIPES,\nINCLUDING BOTH WATER SUPPLY AND PRIVATE IRRIGATION PIPES, COMMUNICATION DUCTS, SEWER PIPES, DIRECT BURIED POWER AND\nTELECOMMUNICATIONS CABLES, AND ANY OTHER UNDERGROUND INFRASTRUCTURE (GAS LINES, FUEL LINES, ETC.). PLOTTING OF ALL THE SERVICES IN\nTHE SCANNED AREA INDICATING THE POSITION (GPS CO-ORDINATES) AND DEPTH THEREOF, MARKING OF THE AREA SCANNED, INDICATING THE SERVICES\nDETECTED, GENERATING RECORDS TO PROVE EACH SCANNING APPLICATION, STORING OF THESE RECORDS (5 YEARS) AND MAKING THEM FREELY\nAVAILABLE UPON REQUEST BY TELKOM OR AS DEFINED BY THE SCOPE OF WORK. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE\nSERVICE FEE ITEMS), 3-DIMENSIONAL SCANNING. NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED FOR PAYMENT WITH PRIOR APPROVAL FROM TELKOM, THE\nOPERATOR/S OF GPR DEVICE SHALL BE COMPETENT. EVIDENCE OF COMPETENCY SHALL BE MADE AVAILABLE ON REQUEST BY TELKOM, SCANS SHOULD BE\nAT LEAST 1 M DEEPER THAN THE PLANNED DRILLING / EXCAVATION DEPTH. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: OS-001559 (OS-CTSO-GL-0066),\nSPEC-000325 (SP-0325). THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER LINEAR METER SCANNED, (MT)'),(3053037,'CI1.55','CI1.55 REINST HOT TAR 20ΓÇô50mm SD WALK','This item consists of the surface reinstatements for driveways, sidewalks and private properties (hot tar) 25 ΓÇô 50 mm thick. \nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	The supply of 100 mm G2 crusher run and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification, \nb.	The DCP test requirements, according to roads authority specification, \nc.	The preparation and cleaning of the re-instatement area and the removal of spoil from site, \nd.	The supply and brushing on of liquid emulsion to the vertical sides of the existing trench, \ne.	The supply of hot tar and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification, \nf.	The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing road / sidewalk levels.\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document). \nNote:\na.	If the local authority executes the reinstatements on behalf of the Service Provider, then the Service Provider remains liable for the payment to the local authority,\nb.	The Service Provider must familiarize himself with the re-instatement specifications of the various authorities.\nc.	Quantities will be calculated against the applicable proposed trenching dimensions.\nThe Specification for this item is: \na.	325. CTO-004654.\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M2).','M2',280.20,'CI1.55 REINST HOT TAR 20ΓÇô50mm SD WALK','REINSTATE, TAR:ITEM NUMBER CI1.55, TYPE HOT 20#50MM SD WALK:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE SURFACE REINSTATEMENTS FOR DRIVEWAYS,\nSIDEWALKS AND PRIVATE PROPERTIES (HOT TAR) 25 # 50 MM THICK. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY OF 100 MM G2\nCRUSHER RUN AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION,\nTHE DCP TEST REQUIREMENTS, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE RE-INSTATEMENT AREA AND\nTHE REMOVAL OF SPOIL FROM SITE, THE SUPPLY AND BRUSHING ON OF LIQUID EMULSION TO THE VERTICAL SIDES OF THE EXISTING TRENCH, THE\nSUPPLY OF HOT TAR AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY\nSPECIFICATION, THE FINISHING OF LEVELS TO BE AESTHETICALLY TRUE TO THE SURROUNDING EXISTING ROAD / SIDEWALK LEVELS, THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT), NOTE: IF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY EXECUTES THE REINSTATEMENTS ON\nBEHALF OF THE SERVICE PROVIDER, THEN THE SERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS LIABLE FOR THE PAYMENT TO THE LOCAL AUTHORITY, THE SERVICE\nPROVIDER MUST FAMILIARIZE HIMSELF WITH THE RE-INSTATEMENT SPECIFICATIONS OF THE VARIOUS AUTHORITIES, QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED\nAGAINST THE APPLICABLE PROPOSED TRENCHING DIMENSIONS, THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR\nTHIS ITEM IS PER SQUARE METRE (M2).'),(3053141,'CI1.2','CI1.2 EXCVT NORM SOIL','This item consists of all excavations deviating from the standard trench size of 0.450 metres, splays, manholes, utility boxes, etc. in normal ground conditions (no pneumatic tools required).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Cutting of tar or concrete (up to 100mm thick) and / or removal of paving slabs or bricks,\nb) Clearing and re-planting of grass where required,\nc) Clearing the surface from trees, all vegetation, removing of boulders and / or rubble,\nd) All excavations in normal soil conditions, \ne) Pilot holes/crossing of services (to determine the ground condition and to identify / locate underground services or obstructions),\nf) Backfilling,\ng) Compacting, \nh) D.C.P testing, \ni) The supply of water if necessary to obtain optimum moisture content,\nj) Tunnelling under obstacles (i.e. kerbstones, tree roots, road signs etc.),  \nk) Supporting of all services (i.e. electrical, water, sewerage, etc.), \nl) Laying danger tape and screen-wire (where required),\nm) Laying of trench crete where required, \nn) Laying of all pipes/ducts and buried cable, \no) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling), \np) Ensure pipe is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc., \nq) Handling, cutting and repairing of existing pipes (supply PVC),\nr) Bedding and padding (reuse of existing material upon Openserve approval), \ns) Removal of all spoil including boulders,\nt) Clearing the surface, \nu) Removing and or erecting fencing when required,  \nv) Grubbing of tree stumps, \nw) Backfilling of cavities, \nx) Removing, transporting and disposing of all surplus material, \ny) Shoring, when required, \nz) Pumping and controlling of water, \naa) Barricading of the excavation, \nbb) Grading of the trench where ducts need to be laid. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\nb) The cost of the supply and delivery of the Trench crete.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per cubic metre (m┬│).','M3',151.48,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.2,NORM SOIL','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.2, TYPE NORM SOIL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CUTTING OF TAR OR CONCRETE (UP TO 100MM\nTHICK) AND / OR REMOVAL OF PAVING SLABS OR BRICKS, CLEARING AND RE-PLANTING OF GRASS WHERE REQUIRED, CLEARING THE SURFACE FROM\nTREES, ALL VEGETATION, REMOVING OF BOULDERS AND / OR RUBBLE, ALL EXCAVATIONS IN NORMAL SOIL CONDITIONS, PILOT HOLES/CROSSING OF\nSERVICES (TO DETERMINE THE GROUND CONDITION AND TO IDENTIFY / LOCATE UNDERGROUND SERVICES OR OBSTRUCTIONS), BACKFILLING,\nCOMPACTING, D.C.P TESTING, THE SUPPLY OF WATER IF NECESSARY TO OBTAIN OPTIMUM MOISTURE CONTENT, TUNNELLING UNDER OBSTACLES (I.E.\nKERBSTONES, TREE ROOTS, ROAD SIGNS ETC.), SUPPORTING OF ALL SERVICES (I.E. ELECTRICAL, WATER, SEWERAGE, ETC.), LAYING DANGER TAPE\nAND SCREEN-WIRE (WHERE REQUIRED), LAYING OF TRENCH CRETE WHERE REQUIRED, LAYING OF ALL PIPES/DUCTS AND BURIED CABLE, PIPE ENTRIES\n(EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING), ENSURE PIPE IS USEABLE BY MEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., HANDLING, CUTTING\nAND REPAIRING OF ALL TYPES & SIZES OF EXISTING PIPES (SUPPLY PVC), BEDDING AND PADDING (REUSE OF EXISTING MATERIAL UPON OPENSERVE\nAPPROVAL), REMOVAL OF ALL SPOIL INCLUDING BOULDERS, CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING AND OR ERECTING FENCING WHEN REQUIRED, GRUBBING\nOF TREE STUMPS, BACKFILLING OF CAVITIES, REMOVING, TRANSPORTING AND DISPOSING OF ALL SURPLUS MATERIAL, SHORING, WHEN REQUIRED,\nPUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER, BARRICADING OF THE EXCAVATION, GRADING OF THE TRENCH WHERE DUCTS NEED TO BE LAID. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE COST OF THE SUPPLY AND DELIVERY OF THE TRENCH CRETE.\nTHE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CUBIC METRE (M3)'),(3053204,'CI1.56','CI1.56 REINST COLD TAR 80ΓÇô100mm RD','This item consists of the surface re-instatements road (cold tar) 80 ΓÇô 100 mm thick. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply of 150 mm G2 crusher run and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification, \nb) The DCP test requirements, according to roads authority specification,\nc) The preparation and cleaning of the re-instatement area and the removal of spoil from site, \nd) The supply and brushing on of liquid emulsion to the vertical sides of the existing trench, \ne) The supply of cold tar and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification,\nf) The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing road / sidewalk levels.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) If the local authority executes the re-instatements on behalf of the Service Provider, then the Service Provider remains liable for the payment to the local authority, \nb) The Service Provider must familiarize himself with the re-instatement specifications of the various authorities, \nc) Quantities will be calculated against the applicable proposed trenching dimensions.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M2).','M2',791.44,'REINST,TAR:CI1.56,COLD 80#100MM RD','REINSTATE, TAR:ITEM NUMBER CI1.56, TYPE COLD, 80#100MM RD:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE SURFACE RE-INSTATEMENTS ROAD (COLD TAR) 80 #\n100 MM THICK. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY OF 150 MM G2 CRUSHER RUN AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE\nPREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE DCP TEST REQUIREMENTS, ACCORDING TO ROADS\nAUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE RE-INSTATEMENT AREA AND THE REMOVAL OF SPOIL FROM SITE, THE SUPPLY AND\nBRUSHING ON OF LIQUID EMULSION TO THE VERTICAL SIDES OF THE EXISTING TRENCH, THE SUPPLY OF COLD TAR AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR\nTHE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE FINISHING OF LEVELS TO BE AESTHETICALLY\nTRUE TO THE SURROUNDING EXISTING ROAD / SIDEWALK LEVELS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE\nDOCUMENT). NOTE: IF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY EXECUTES THE REINSTATEMENTS ON BEHALF OF THE SERVICE PROVIDER, THEN THE SERVICE PROVIDER\nREMAINS LIABLE FOR THE PAYMENT TO THE LOCAL AUTHORITY, THE SERVICE PROVIDER MUST FAMILIARIZE HIMSELF WITH THE RE-INSTATEMENT\nSPECIFICATIONS OF THE VARIOUS AUTHORITIES, QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED AGAINST THE APPLICABLE PROPOSED TRENCHING DIMENSIONS. THE\nSPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SQUARE METRE (M2).'),(3053205,'CI1.57','CI1.57 REINST COLD TAR 20ΓÇô50mm SD WALK','This item consists of the surface re-instatements for driveways, sidewalks and private properties (Cold tar) 25 ΓÇô 50 mm thick. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) The supply of 150 mm G2 crusher run and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification, \nb) The DCP test requirements, according to roads authority specification,\nc) The preparation and cleaning of the re-instatement area and the removal of spoil from site, \nd) The supply and brushing on of liquid emulsion to the vertical sides of the existing trench, \ne) The supply of cold tar and the equipment necessary for the preparation, placement and compaction, according to roads authority specification,\nf) The finishing of levels to be aesthetically true to the surrounding existing road / sidewalk levels.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na) If the local authority executes the re-instatements on behalf of the Service Provider, then the Service Provider remains liable for the payment to the local authority, \nb) The Service Provider must familiarize himself with the re-instatement specifications of the various authorities, \nc) Quantities will be calculated against the applicable proposed trenching dimensions.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per square metre (M2).','M2',380.78,'REINST,TAR:CI1.57,COLD 20#50MM SD WALK','REINSTATE, TAR:ITEM NUMBER CI1.57, TYPE COLD, 20#50MM SD WALK:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE SURFACE REINSTATEMENTS FOR DRIVEWAYS,\nSIDEWALKS AND PRIVATE PROPERTIES (COLD TAR) 25 # 50 MM THICK. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY OF 150 MM G2\nCRUSHER RUN AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION,\nTHE DCP TEST REQUIREMENTS, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY SPECIFICATION, THE PREPARATION AND CLEANING OF THE RE-INSTATEMENT AREA AND\nTHE REMOVAL OF SPOIL FROM SITE, THE SUPPLY AND BRUSHING ON OF LIQUID EMULSION TO THE VERTICAL SIDES OF THE EXISTING TRENCH, THE\nSUPPLY OF COLD TAR AND THE EQUIPMENT NECESSARY FOR THE PREPARATION, PLACEMENT AND COMPACTION, ACCORDING TO ROADS AUTHORITY\nSPECIFICATION, THE FINISHING OF LEVELS TO BE AESTHETICALLY TRUE TO THE SURROUNDING EXISTING ROAD / SIDEWALK LEVELS. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: IF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY EXECUTES THE REINSTATEMENTS ON\nBEHALF OF THE SERVICE PROVIDER, THEN THE SERVICE PROVIDER REMAINS LIABLE FOR THE PAYMENT TO THE LOCAL AUTHORITY, THE SERVICE\nPROVIDER MUST FAMILIARIZE HIMSELF WITH THE RE-INSTATEMENT SPECIFICATIONS OF THE VARIOUS AUTHORITIES, QUANTITIES WILL BE CALCULATED\nAGAINST THE APPLICABLE PROPOSED TRENCHING DIMENSIONS. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR\nTHIS ITEM IS PER SQUARE METRE (M2).'),(3053206,'CI1.1','CI1.1 TRNCH & LAY 0.45x0.8m NORM SOIL','This item consists of the trenching within vicinity of existing services up to width of 0.450 metre x depth 0.8 metre (nominal depth 0.9 metre) and laying of Ducts / Micro-Ducts and buried cables.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na) Cutting of tar or concrete (up to 100mm thick) and / or removal of paving slabs or bricks\nb) Clearing and re-planting of grass where required,\nc) Clearing the surface from trees, all vegetation, removing of boulders and / or rubble\nd) All excavations in normal soil conditions, \ne) Pilot holes/crossing of services (to determine the ground condition and to identify / locate underground services or obstructions),\nf) Backfilling,\ng) Compacting,\nh) D.C.P testing,\ni) The supply of water if necessary to obtain optimum moisture content,\nj) Tunnelling under obstacles (i.e. kerbstones, tree roots, road signs etc.),  \nk) Supporting of all services (i.e. electrical, water, sewerage, etc.), \nl) Laying danger tape and screen-wire (where required),\nm) Laying of all pipes/ducts and buried cable,\nn) Pipe entries (excluding core drilling),\no) Ensure pipe is useable by means of mandrill, brush, pressure test, test cable, etc., \np) Handling, cutting and repairing of existing pipes (supply PVC),\nq) Bedding and padding (reuse of existing material upon Openserve approval),\nr) Removal of all spoil including boulders, \ns) Clearing the surface,\nt) Removing and or erecting fencing when required, \nu) Grubbing of tree stumps,\nv) Backfilling of cavities, \nw) Removing, transporting and disposing of all surplus material,\nx) Shoring, when required,\ny) Pumping and controlling of water,\nz) Barricading of the excavation, \naa) Grading of the trench where ducts need to be laid.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na) Road/railway crossings, \nb) Hard rock excavation,\nc) All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document)\n\nNote:\na) Any excavations deviating from 0.450-metre-width and 0.8 metre depth will be paid item under item CI1.2.\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na) 325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',140.69,'EXPOS,TRNCH:CI1.1,0.45X0.8M NORM SOIL','EXPOSE, TRENCH:ITEM NUMBER CI1.1, TYPE 0.45X0.8M NORM SOIL:THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: CUTTING OF TAR OR CONCRETE (UP\nTO 100MM THICK) AND / OR REMOVAL OF PAVING SLABS OR BRICKS, CLEARING AND RE-PLANTING OF GRASS WHERE REQUIRED, CLEARING THE SURFACE\nFROM TREES, ALL VEGETATION, REMOVING OF BOULDERS AND / OR RUBBLE, ALL EXCAVATIONS IN NORMAL SOIL CONDITIONS, PILOT HOLES/CROSSING\nOF SERVICES (TO DETERMINE THE GROUND CONDITION AND TO IDENTIFY / LOCATE UNDERGROUND SERVICES OR OBSTRUCTIONS), BACKFILLING,\nCOMPACTING, D.C.P TESTING, THE SUPPLY OF WATER IF NECESSARY TO OBTAIN OPTIMUM MOISTURE CONTENT, TUNNELLING UNDER OBSTACLES (I.E.\nKERBSTONES, TREE ROOTS, ROAD SIGNS ETC.), SUPPORTING OF ALL SERVICES (I.E. ELECTRICAL, WATER, SEWERAGE, ETC.), LAYING DANGER TAPE\nAND SCREEN-WIRE (WHERE REQUIRED), LAYING OF ALL PIPES/DUCTS AND BURIED CABLE, PIPE ENTRIES (EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING), ENSURE PIPE\nIS USEABLE BY MEANS OF MANDRILL, BRUSH, PRESSURE TEST, TEST CABLE, ETC., HANDLING, CUTTING AND REPAIRING OF ALL TYPES & SIZES OF\nEXISTING PIPES (SUPPLY PVC), BEDDING AND PADDING (REUSE OF EXISTING MATERIAL UPON OPENSERVE APPROVAL), REMOVAL OF ALL SPOIL\nINCLUDING BOULDERS, CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING AND OR ERECTING FENCING WHEN REQUIRED, GRUBBING OF TREE STUMPS, BACKFILLING OF\nCAVITIES, REMOVING, TRANSPORTING AND DISPOSING OF ALL SURPLUS MATERIAL, SHORING, WHEN REQUIRED, PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF WATER,\nBARRICADING OF THE EXCAVATION, GRADING OF THE TRENCH WHERE DUCTS NEED TO BE LAID.THE RATE EXCLUDES: ROAD/RAILWAY CROSSINGS, HARD\nROCK EXCAVATION, ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: ANY EXCAVATIONS DEVIATING FROM\n0.450-METRE-WIDTH AND 0.8 METRE DEPTH WILL BE PAID ITEM UNDER ITEM CI1.2. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT).'),(3053632,'CI6.1','CI6.1 CNDCT NUC DENS TEST','This item consists of the specialized soil density, moisture and grading sample test for re-instatements by means of an approved nuclear radiation test method. \nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	Obtaining all access approvals\nb.	Safeguarding the site where the tests will be conducted\nc.	Traffic control\nd.	The setting up of testing equipment\ne.	Conducting a sample test at various depths (i.e. Surface level, 300mm depth and 600mm depth) by a certified operator\nf.	Excavating, replacing / backfilling and compacting of soil (300x300x600mm) to enable successful testing\ng.	Repair and reinstatement of the test site / road to its original state \nh.	All laboratory and admin costs\ni.	All 3rd party arrangements and costs\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee items).\nNote:\na.	This item may only be used for payment with prior approval from Telkom. \nb.	Measurement for payment will be done per sample test \nc.	Only laboratory test results that pass the density and moisture content may be claimed.\nd.	For a standard trench depth, 3 soil samples will be taken at 300mm depth intervals. \ne.	It is expected that each test position will be 3m apart along the excavation.\nThe Specification for this item is: \na.	325. CTO-004654.\nThe unit of measure for this item is per successful sample test, each (EA)','EA',600.00,'PAY,FEE:CI6.1 CNDCT NUC DENS TEST','PAY, FEE:PURPOSE CI6.1 CNDCT NUC DENS TEST:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE SPECIALIZED SOIL DENSITY, MOISTURE AND GRADING SAMPLE TEST FOR\nRE-INSTATEMENTS BY MEANS OF AN APPROVED NUCLEAR RADIATION TEST METHOD. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: OBTAINING ALL\nACCESS APPROVALS, SAFEGUARDING THE SITE WHERE THE TESTS WILL BE CONDUCTED, TRAFFIC CONTROL, THE SETTING UP OF TESTING EQUIPMENT,\nCONDUCTING A SAMPLE TEST AT VARIOUS DEPTHS (I.E. SURFACE LEVEL, 300MM DEPTH AND 600MM DEPTH) BY A CERTIFIED OPERATOR, EXCAVATING,\nREPLACING / BACKFILLING AND COMPACTING OF SOIL (300X300X600MM) TO ENABLE SUCCESSFUL TESTING, REPAIR AND REINSTATEMENT OF THE TEST\nSITE / ROAD TO ITS ORIGINAL STATE, ALL LABORATORY AND ADMIN COSTS, ALL 3RD PARTY ARRANGEMENTS AND COSTS. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL\nTRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED FOR PAYMENT WITH PRIOR APPROVAL FROM\nTELKOM, MEASUREMENT FOR PAYMENT WILL BE DONE PER SAMPLE TEST, ONLY LABORATORY TEST RESULTS THAT PASS THE DENSITY AND MOISTURE\nCONTENT MAY BE CLAIMED, FOR A STANDARD TRENCH DEPTH, 3 SOIL SAMPLES WILL BE TAKEN AT 300MM DEPTH INTERVALS, IT IS EXPECTED THAT\nEACH TEST POSITION WILL BE 3M APART ALONG THE EXCAVATION. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325. CTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE\nFOR THIS ITEM IS PER SUCCESSFUL SAMPLE TEST, EACH (EA)'),(3054236,'CI1.70','CI1.70 FIT OPTC SLCK BX/ORGNSR UG','This item consists of the fitting of an Optic slack box / organizer (all types) on a wall, in a manhole, jointing pit, accessible Pipe Junction Box or similar facility / utility box, where a future joint is required. \n \nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \na.	The securing the slack box/organiser on the wall, coiling and inserting of the slack into the slack box/organiser\nb.	The marking/labelling of the slack box/organiser\nc.	The pumping and control of water\nd.	The cleaning of the manhole / utility box and the immediate surrounding area\ne.	The supply of all minor materials (i.e. fastening material, rawl bolts, cable ties, labels/label holders, etc.)\nf.	The use of power tools, mechanical aids or specialised services/equipment to complete the fitting of the optic slack box/organiser to specification. \n \nThe rate excludes: \na.	The optic slack box/organiser (Telkom to supply)\n \nNote: \nThis Item may only be used, where a future underground FDP / optic joint is required and not in conjunction with prep joint / splicing items.\n \nThe specification for this item is CTO-000786. \n \nThe unit for this item is per slack box/organizer, each (EA).','EA',204.52,'CI1.70 FIT OPTC SLCK BX/ORGNSR UG','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER CI1.70, TYPE OPTC SLCK BX/ORGNSR UG:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE FITTING OF AN OPTIC SLACK BOX /\nORGANIZER (ALL TYPES) ON A WALL, IN A MANHOLE, JOINTING PIT, ACCESSIBLE PIPE JUNCTION BOX OR SIMILAR FACILITY / UTILITY BOX, WHERE\nA FUTURE JOINT IS REQUIRED. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SECURING THE SLACK BOX/ORGANISER ON THE WALL, COILING AND\nINSERTING OF THE SLACK INTO THE SLACK BOX/ORGANISER, THE MARKING/LABELLING OF THE SLACK BOX/ORGANISER, THE PUMPING AND CONTROL OF\nWATER, THE CLEANING OF THE MANHOLE / UTILITY BOX AND THE IMMEDIATE SURROUNDING AREA, THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS (I.E.\nFASTENING MATERIAL, RAWL BOLTS, CABLE TIES, LABELS/LABEL HOLDERS, ETC.), THE USE OF POWER TOOLS, MECHANICAL AIDS OR SPECIALISED\nSERVICES/EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE FITTING OF THE OPTIC SLACK BOX/ORGANISER TO SPECIFICATION. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE OPTIC SLACK\nBOX/ORGANISER (TELKOM TO SUPPLY). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED, WHERE A FUTURE UNDERGROUND FDP / OPTIC JOINT IS REQUIRED AND\nNOT IN CONJUNCTION WITH PREP JOINT / SPLICING ITEMS. THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS CTO-000786. THE UNIT FOR THIS ITEM IS PER\nSLACK BOX/ORGANIZER, EACH (EA).'),(3054357,'FTTX 1.3','FTTX 1.3 HOM CONCTN ATB (DURING PROJECT)','This item consists of the installation of a drop fibre for a future FTTH service (Home Connection) from the Demarcation point (Slim/Budi/FAT-box) to the ATB during the Project period.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na)	Aerial home connections. \nb)	Underground home connections where existing infrastructure is available. \nc)	Standard entries into the home using light machinery/tools.\nd)	The supply of an average of 40m drop cable per home.\ne)	Home connections that are done during the HP Build, and up to a maximum of 30 days after submission for Acceptance/ECC of Homes Passed Group (splitter area)\nf)	All project management and administrative activities\ng)	Obtaining all work orders\nh)	Complete supply & Installation of the drop fibre from the last Network Demarcation point to the single point where the customer wants the service (i.e. slim-box / budi-box to ATB at customer premises) \ni)	Installation of the ATB\nj)	Installation of Micro duct, where required (i.e. single / dual / 4way)\nk)	Supply of all minor materials (i.e. Fasteners, Saddles, Screw Ring, Glue etc.)\nl)	Underground access where infrastructure is available and fit for purpose,\nm)	Overhead access (from the Slimbox / FlatFist / Helleman / FAT to the ATB)\nn)	Clear vegetation around drop fibre (1 meter radius x maximum girth of 300mm)\no)	Slack management\np)	Termination of the optic fibre (i.e. NDP, ATB)\nq)	fusion Splicing and/or Mechanical Splicing and/or hardened connector at the following elements:\ni.	Network Demarcation Point\nii.	ATB\nr)	Testing over the full access network, up to the ATB using a light source (Exchange side) and power meter (at the ATB), and provide test results indicating that the signal levels are within the power budget.\ns)	Recording and updating of all the necessary information on the relevant Telkom systems / platforms (i.e. TXOPS completion sheet)\nt)	Shipping (local and foreign)\nu)	Storage of drop cable and miscellaneous items\nv)	Transportation of all tools, materials, and equipment to and from the site \nw)	Quality and Safety activities / inspections\nx)	Site management\ny)	All travel related costs, such as:\ni.	Vehicle costs,\nii.	Fuel,\niii.	Travelling losses (Labour)\n\nThe rate excludes:\na)	The repair / replace / build new POE (Customer pipe)\nb)	The supply of Micro duct, where required (i.e. single / dual / 4way) (Telkom to supply)\nc)	The supply of the ATB (Telkom to supply)\n\nNote: \na)	This item may only be used where an order is placed for at least 50 Homes connect in an FDA. \n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per Drop fibre cable terminated, each (EA)','EA',1000.00,'FTTX 1.3 HOM CONCTN ATB (DURING PROJECT)','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER FTTX 1.3, TYPE HOME CONNECTION ATB (DURING PROJECT):THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE INSTALLATION OF A DROP FIBRE FOR A FUTURE FTTH SERVICE (HOME CONNECTION) FROM THE DEMARCATION POINT (SLIM/BUDI/FAT-BOX) TO THE ATB DURING THE PROJECT PERIOD. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: AERIAL HOME CONNECTIONS, UNDERGROUND HOME CONNECTIONS WHERE EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE IS AVAILABLE, STANDARD ENTRIES INTO THE HOME USING LIGHT MACHINERY/TOOLS, THE SUPPLY OF AN AVERAGE OF 40M DROP CABLE PER HOME, HOME CONNECTIONS THAT ARE DONE DURING THE HP BUILD, AND UP TO A MAXIMUM OF 30 DAYS AFTER SUBMISSION FOR ACCEPTANCE/ECC OF HOMES PASSED GROUP (SPLITTER AREA), ALL PROJECT MANAGEMENT AND ADMINISTRATIVE ACTIVITIESOBTAINING ALL WORK ORDERS, COMPLETE SUPPLY & INSTALLATION OF THE DROP FIBRE FROM THE LAST NETWORK DEMARCATION POINT TO THE SINGLE POINT WHERE THE CUSTOMER WANTS THE SERVICE (I.E. SLIM-BOX / BUDI-BOX TO ATB AT CUSTOMER PREMISES), INSTALLATION OF THE ATB, INSTALLATION OF MICRO DUCT, WHERE REQUIRED (I.E. SINGLE / DUAL / 4WAY), SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS (I.E. FASTENERS, SADDLES, SCREW RING, GLUE ETC.), UNDERGROUND ACCESS WHERE INFRASTRUCTURE IS AVAILABLE AND FIT FOR PURPOSE, OVERHEAD ACCESS (FROM THE SLIMBOX / FLATFIST / HELLEMAN / FAT TO THE ATB), CLEAR VEGETATION AROUND DROP FIBRE (1 METER RADIUS X MAXIMUM GIRTH OF 300MM), SLACK MANAGEMENT, TERMINATION OF THE OPTIC FIBRE (I.E. NDP, ATB), FUSION SPLICING AND/OR MECHANICAL SPLICING AND/OR HARDENED CONNECTOR AT THE FOLLOWING ELEMENTS: NETWORK DEMARCATION POINT, ATB, TESTING OVER THE FULL ACCESS NETWORK, UP TO THE ATB USING A LIGHT SOURCE (EXCHANGE SIDE) AND POWER METER (AT THE ATB), AND PROVIDE TEST RESULTS INDICATING THAT THE SIGNAL LEVELS ARE WITHIN THE POWER BUDGET, RECORDING AND UPDATING OF ALL THE NECESSARY INFORMATION ON THE RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS / PLATFORMS (I.E. TXOPS COMPLETION SHEET), SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE OF DROP CABLE AND MISCELLANEOUS ITEMS, TRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM THE SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE MANAGEMENT, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS, SUCH AS: VEHICLE COSTS, FUEL, TRAVELLING LOSSES (LABOUR). THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE REPAIR / REPLACE / BUILD NEW POE (CUSTOMER PIPE), THE SUPPLY OF MICRO DUCT, WHERE REQUIRED (I.E. SINGLE / DUAL / 4WAY) (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), THE SUPPLY OF THE ATB (TELKOM TO SUPPLY). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED WHERE AN ORDER IS PLACED FOR AT LEAST 50 HOMES CONNECT IN AN FDA. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER DROP FIBRE CABLE TERMINATED, EACH (EA)'),(3054358,'FTTX 1.4','FTTX 1.4 HOM CONCTN ONT (DURING PROJECT)','This item consists of the installation of an ONT and commissioning of the FTTH service/s (Home Connection) during the Project period.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na)	Home connections that are done during the HP Build, and up to a maximum of 30 days after submission for Acceptance/ECC of Homes Passed Group (splitter area)\nb)	All project management and administrative activities\nc)	Obtaining all work orders\nd)	Installation of the ONT and patch cords\ne)	Commissioning of FTTH service/s on the ONT at customer premises \nf)	Slack management\ng)	Activation of FTTH service / Migration of service with DTAC\nh)	Installation, set-up, configuration of FTTH compatible modem / router when required,\ni)	Connection of existing indoor wiring to the 