OF ALL THE NECESSARY\nINFORMATION ON THE RELEVANT TELKOM SYSTEMS / PLATFORMS (I.E. CLICK), SHIPPING (LOCAL AND FOREIGN), STORAGE OF MISCELLANEOUS ITEMS,\nTRANSPORTATION OF ALL TOOLS, MATERIALS, AND EQUIPMENT TO AND FROM THE SITE, QUALITY AND SAFETY ACTIVITIES / INSPECTIONS, SITE\nMANAGEMENT, ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS, SUCH AS: VEHICLE COSTS, FUEL, TRAVELLING LOSSES (LABOUR). THE RATE EXCLUDES: PATCH CORDS,\n(TELKOM TO SUPPLY), THE SUPPLY OF ONT (TELKOM TO SUPPLY), THE SUPPLY OF FTTH COMPATIBLE MODEM / ROUTER (ISP TO PROVIDE). NOTE:\nTHIS ITEM MAY ONLY BE USED WHERE AN ORDER IS PLACED FOR AT LEAST 50 HOMES CONNECT IN AN FDA, THE INITIAL SCHEDULING WILL BE MANAGED\nBY OS VIA THE CLICK SYSTEM TOOLS BUT THE DISPATCHING AND FINAL APPOINTMENTS ACCORDING TO THE END CUSTOMER AVAILABILITY IS THE\nSERVICE PROVIDERS RESPONSIBILITY. THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ONT INSTALLED (HOME CONNECTED), EACH (EA)'),(3054489,'CI1.7.1','CI1.7.1 SPCLZD XNG BORE NORM SOIL 75MM DIA','This item consists of the specialized crossings (not trenching) of boring / drilling / moling to accommodate and install one micro-duct (Up to 75mm outside diameter) in all soil conditions except rock.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	The setting up of the boring / drilling / moling equipment, \nb.	Excavating on both sides, when necessary, \nc.	Boring / drilling / moling up to a 75mm diameter hole and installing a micro-duct (typically a 7-way micro duct), \nd.	Tunnelling under kerbstones, supporting of services, backfilling and removal of soil, \ne.	The cost for damages incurred by the Service Provider and the repair of roads or existing services, \nf.	The cost of clearing the surface, removing boulders with a size of up to 0.015 cubic metres (If the boulders are bigger than 0.015 cubic metres in size, a separate rate must be negotiated.), grubbing of tree stumps, \ng.	Backfilling of cavities, demolishing structures and removal thereof, \nh.	Pipe entries (excluding core drilling). \n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nNote:\na.	This item will be used for payment when boring / drilling / moling is to be done instead of trenching at roads, driveways etc.,\nb.	Measurement for payment will be done from kerbstone to kerbstone, per meter, and only for successful attempts,\nc.	This item will be applicable in all soil conditions except in rock. (including clay and or waterlogged ground conditions).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na.	325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT)','MT',960.00,'EXCAVT,GRND:CI1.7.1,SPC XNG BR NRM 75MM','EXCAVATE, GROUND:ITEM NUMBER CI1.7.1, TYPE SPCLZD XNG BORE NORM SOIL 75MM DIA:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE SPECIALIZED CROSSINGS (NOT\nTRENCHING) OF BORING / DRILLING / MOLING TO ACCOMMODATE AND INSTALL ONE MICRO-DUCT (UP TO 75MM OUTSIDE DIAMETER) IN ALL SOIL\nCONDITIONS EXCEPT ROCK. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SETTING UP OF THE BORING / DRILLING / MOLING EQUIPMENT,\nEXCAVATING ON BOTH SIDES, WHEN NECESSARY, BORING / DRILLING / MOLING UP TO A 75MM DIAMETER HOLE AND INSTALLING A MICRO-DUCT\n(TYPICALLY A 7-WAY MICRO DUCT), TUNNELLING UNDER KERBSTONES, SUPPORTING OF SERVICES, BACKFILLING AND REMOVAL OF SOIL, THE COST FOR\nDAMAGES INCURRED BY THE SERVICE PROVIDER AND THE REPAIR OF ROADS OR EXISTING SERVICES, THE COST OF CLEARING THE SURFACE, REMOVING\nBOULDERS WITH A SIZE OF UP TO 0.015 CUBIC METRES (IF THE BOULDERS ARE BIGGER THAN 0.015 CUBIC METRES IN SIZE, A SEPARATE RATE MUST\nBE NEGOTIATED.), GRUBBING OF TREE STUMPS, BACKFILLING OF CAVITIES, DEMOLISHING STRUCTURES AND REMOVAL THEREOF, PIPE ENTRIES\n(EXCLUDING CORE DRILLING). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). NOTE: THIS ITEM WILL BE\nUSED FOR PAYMENT WHEN BORING / DRILLING / MOLING IS TO BE DONE INSTEAD OF TRENCHING AT ROADS, DRIVEWAYS ETC., MEASUREMENT FOR\nPAYMENT WILL BE DONE FROM KERBSTONE TO KERBSTONE, PER METER, AND ONLY FOR SUCCESSFUL ATTEMPTS, THIS ITEM WILL BE APPLICABLE IN ALL\nSOIL CONDITIONS EXCEPT IN ROCK. (INCLUDING CLAY AND OR WATERLOGGED GROUND CONDITIONS). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: 325.\nCTO-004654. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT)'),(3054546,'CE2.1.1','CE2.1.1 OUTGOING WAYLVE: APPLN','This item consists of the revision and submission of wayleave/s application/s to the relevant Local Authority/ies (municipalities / utilities / stake holders), on behalf of Telkom (Wayleave section). \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to: \na.	Obtaining, reviewing/scrutinizing and evaluating all documentation as per the executable file from the Engineering section (Internal or External),\nb.	Co-ordinating and Consolidating all documentation received,\nc.	Completion of the applicable application templates as per applicable website and / or format required,\nd.	Submitting the application / letter of intent in any which way or form, (i.e. physically handing in, courier, posting, electronically, via a web site, software application, etc.) with the consolidated file (topo, sketches, etc.) to the utilities such as: \ni.	Local municipality and/or its disciplines \nii.	Eskom \niii.	Gas \niv.	Water Board\nv.	Transnet (i.e. oil pipelines)\nvi.	Other Telecommunication companies,\nvii.	Other road agencies, \nviii.	Department of public works, \nix.	Department of environmental affairs, etc.\ne.	Communicating and following up with authorities until obtaining the approved wayleave/s,\nf.	Updating of all relevant Openserve systems,\ng.	Administration costs (i.e. Stationary, copies, telephone calls, etc.),\nh.	All travel related costs to and from the Local Authorities / utilities / stake holders and/or sites within a 50km radius of the nominated dispatch point. \n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	The compilation of the actual wayleave documents.  This is an Engineering function and is included as such in the Engineering items,\nb.	Wayleave applications for GAUTRANS or SANRAL \nc.	Any payment for the application as demanded by some municipalities. \nd.	Distances in excess of 50km radius (See service fee item: light vehicle, 2-man team)\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per project, irrespective of the number of wayleave applications / sheets submitted, each (EA)','EA',2000.00,'CE2.1.1 OUTGOING WAYLVE: APPLN','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER CE2.1.1, TYPE OUTGOING WAYLVE: APPLN:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE REVISION AND SUBMISSION OF WAYLEAVE/S\nAPPLICATION/S TO THE RELEVANT LOCAL AUTHORITY/IES (MUNICIPALITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS), ON BEHALF OF TELKOM (WAYLEAVE\nSECTION). THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO:  OBTAINING, REVIEWING/SCRUTINIZING AND EVALUATING ALL DOCUMENTATION AS PER THE\nEXECUTABLE FILE FROM THE ENGINEERING SECTION (INTERNAL OR EXTERNAL), CO-ORDINATING AND CONSOLIDATING ALL DOCUMENTATION RECEIVED,\nCOMPLETION OF THE APPLICABLE APPLICATION TEMPLATES AS PER APPLICABLE WEBSITE AND / OR FORMAT REQUIRED, SUBMITTING THE APPLICATION /\nLETTER OF INTENT IN ANY WHICH WAY OR FORM, (I.E. PHYSICALLY HANDING IN, COURIER, POSTING, ELECTRONICALLY, VIA A WEB SITE, SOFTWARE\nAPPLICATION, ETC.) WITH THE CONSOLIDATED FILE (TOPO, SKETCHES, ETC.) TO THE UTILITIES SUCH AS: LOCAL MUNICIPALITY AND/OR ITS\nDISCIPLINES, ESKOM, GAS, WATER BOARD, TRANSNET (I.E. OIL PIPELINES), OTHER TELECOMMUNICATION COMPANIES, OTHER ROAD AGENCIES,\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC WORKS, DEPARTMENT OF ENVIRONMENTAL AFFAIRS, ETC., COMMUNICATING AND FOLLOWING UP WITH AUTHORITIES UNTIL\nOBTAINING THE APPROVED WAYLEAVE/S, UPDATING OF ALL RELEVANT OPENSERVE SYSTEMS, ADMINISTRATION COSTS (I.E. STATIONARY, COPIES,\nTELEPHONE CALLS, ETC.), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES / UTILITIES / STAKE HOLDERS AND/OR SITES WITHIN\nA 50KM RADIUS OF THE NOMINATED DISPATCH POINT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE COMPILATION OF THE ACTUAL WAYLEAVE DOCUMENTS.  THIS IS AN\nENGINEERING FUNCTION AND IS INCLUDED AS SUCH IN THE ENGINEERING ITEMS, WAYLEAVE APPLICATIONS FOR GAUTRANS OR SANRAL, ANY PAYMENT\nFOR THE APPLICATION AS DEMANDED BY SOME MUNICIPALITIES, DISTANCES IN EXCESS OF 50KM RADIUS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEM: LIGHT VEHICLE,\n2-MAN TEAM). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PROJECT, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF WAYLEAVE APPLICATIONS / SHEETS\nSUBMITTED, EACH (EA)'),(3054870,'CE1.5.1','CE1.5.1 ENG NETW FBR FTTX HP','This item consists of the complete detailed engineering for FTTx on existing or new routes and / or sites consisting of ΓÇô Underground (UG) and / or Overhead (OH) Plant, from the Fibre Distribution Point (FDP) to the Network Demarcation Point (NDP).\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals including access devices from Telkom (i.e. manhole / streetbox / Exchange keys etc.)\nb.	Obtaining work refs.\nc.	Site visit / Survey including the exposing / accessing / opening of route access points such as manholes, streetboxes, DPΓÇÖs, housings, boxes, buildings, cabinets, mini OMDFΓÇÖs, etc.\nd.	Pumping of manholes where necessary, irrespective of site conditions\ne.	Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nf.	Labour\ng.	Obtaining existing end-to-end records from Telkom system/s\nh.	Detailed engineering of all plant / infrastructure / network elements from the FDP to the NDP / customers, on Telkom approved system software. (I.e. Fibre / copper cables, Splitter, Distribution points, Manholes, junction boxes, pipes, ducts, runways, grids, risers, etc.)\ni.	Creating splitter boundaries and splitter information\nj.	Preparing TXOPS\nk.	Creating of STAC codes for manholes, splitter, FDPΓÇÖs etc.\nl.	Capturing of existing infrastructure (i.e. poles, pipes, utility boxes, etc.) directly related to the new cable installation that does not exist on NETPLAN\nm.	Compilation and submission of wayleaves to Telkom representative / Wayleave section, irrespective of the number of agencies / departments / divisions / utilities, such as municipality, power, water, road, rail, gas, etc.\nn.	Update wayleave database / systems & archive the records\no.	Submission of Executable file/s (i.e. KL, recoveries, etc.) as per Telkom SpecΓÇÖs, Work Instructions, Method & Procedures, Policies, etc.\np.	Detailed engineering for recoveries of all types of plant and/or equipment\nq.	Submission of an Executable file with all the relevant recovery information, such as:\ni.	asset decommissioning form\nii.	inventory list of all equipment and cables to be recovered (copper, fibre, etc.)\nr.	Processing of all Variation Orders for the duration of the project (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\ns.	Capturing of all as-built plant / elements after completion of the work. (it is expected that the project should be completed within 12 months)\nt.	Capturing of the drop fibre and ATB on Telkom systems (i.e. NetPlan).\nu.	Connectivity to be done on NETPLAN\n\nNotes: \na.	If the entire project consists of only a single splitter, then 32 HP may be claimed irrespective if there is less than 32 HP required /Engineered.\nb.	This item may also be used for an ME over GPON, in which case it also includes the detailed Engineering from the FDP to the NDP and / or into the customer premises (all KL Engineering for ME over GPON)\nc.	If one of the HP consists of an ME over GPON customer then, where applicable, the additional ME site visit item may be claimed in conjunction with this item to determine the additional ISP requirements such as the fibre cable within the customer premises, ISP confirmation/requirements, RFO spec, etc.\nd.	If the project consists of more than one splitter, then the claim will be for the actual number of HP engineered.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\nb.	The opening and closing of welded manholes (May be claimed separately)\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is Engineering per Homes Passed, each (EA)','EA',320.00,'CE1.5.1 ENG NETW FBR FTTX HP','ENGINEER, SITE:ITEM NUMBER: CE1.5.1, TASK: NETWORK FIBRE FTTX HP:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE COMPLETE DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR FTTX ON EXISTING OR NEW ROUTES AND / OR SITES CONSISTING OF; UNDERGROUND (UG) AND / OR OVERHEAD (OH) PLANT, FROM THE FIBRE DISTRIBUTION POINT (FDP) TO THE NETWORK DEMARCATION POINT (NDP). THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS INCLUDING ACCESS DEVICES FROM TELKOM (I.E. MANHOLE / STREETBOX / EXCHANGE KEYS ETC.), OBTAINING WORK REFS., SITE VISIT / SURVEY INCLUDING THE EXPOSING / ACCESSING / OPENING OF ROUTE ACCESS POINTS SUCH AS MANHOLES, STREETBOXES, DPS, HOUSINGS, BOXES, BUILDINGS, CABINETS, MINI OMDFS, ETC., PUMPING OF MANHOLES WHERE NECESSARY, IRRESPECTIVE OF SITE CONDITIONS, INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, LABOUR, OBTAINING EXISTING END-TO-END RECORDS FROM TELKOM SYSTEM/S, DETAILED ENGINEERING OF ALL PLANT / INFRASTRUCTURE / NETWORK ELEMENTS FROM THE FDP TO THE NDP / CUSTOMERS, ON TELKOM APPROVED SYSTEM SOFTWARE. (I.E. FIBRE / COPPER CABLES, SPLITTER, DISTRIBUTION POINTS, MANHOLES, JUNCTION BOXES, PIPES, DUCTS, RUNWAYS, GRIDS, RISERS, ETC.), CREATING SPLITTER BOUNDARIES AND SPLITTER INFORMATION, PREPARING TXOPS, CREATING OF STAC CODES FOR MANHOLES, SPLITTER, FDPS ETC., CAPTURING OF EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE (I.E. POLES, PIPES, UTILITY BOXES, ETC.) DIRECTLY RELATED TO THE NEW CABLE INSTALLATION THAT DOES NOT EXIST ON NETPLAN, COMPILATION AND SUBMISSION OF WAYLEAVES TO TELKOM REPRESENTATIVE / WAYLEAVE SECTION, IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF AGENCIES / DEPARTMENTS / DIVISIONS / UTILITIES, SUCH AS MUNICIPALITY, POWER, WATER, ROAD, RAIL, GAS, ETC., UPDATE WAYLEAVE DATABASE / SYSTEMS & ARCHIVE THE RECORDS, SUBMISSION OF EXECUTABLE FILE/S (I.E. KL, RECOVERIES, ETC.) AS PER TELKOM SPECS, WORK INSTRUCTIONS, METHOD & PROCEDURES, POLICIES, ETC., DETAILED ENGINEERING FOR RECOVERIES OF ALL TYPES OF PLANT AND/OR EQUIPMENT, SUBMISSION OF AN EXECUTABLE FILE WITH ALL THE RELEVANT RECOVERY INFORMATION, SUCH AS:, ASSET DECOMMISSIONING FORM, INVENTORY LIST OF ALL EQUIPMENT AND CABLES TO BE RECOVERED (COPPER, FIBRE, ETC.), PROCESSING OF ALL VARIATION ORDERS FOR THE DURATION OF THE PROJECT (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS), CAPTURING OF ALL AS-BUILT PLANT / ELEMENTS AFTER COMPLETION OF THE WORK. (IT IS EXPECTED THAT THE PROJECT SHOULD BE COMPLETED WITHIN 12 MONTHS), CAPTURING OF THE DROP FIBRE AND ATB ON TELKOM SYSTEMS (I.E. NETPLAN), CONNECTIVITY TO BE DONE ON NETPLAN. NOTES: IF THE ENTIRE PROJECT CONSISTS OF ONLY A SINGLE SPLITTER, THEN 32 HP MAY BE CLAIMED IRRESPECTIVE IF THERE IS LESS THAN 32 HP REQUIRED /ENGINEERED, THIS ITEM MAY ALSO BE USED FOR AN ME OVER GPON, IN WHICH CASE IT ALSO INCLUDES THE DETAILED ENGINEERING FROM THE FDP TO THE NDP AND / OR INTO THE CUSTOMER PREMISES (ALL KL ENGINEERING FOR ME OVER GPON), IF ONE OF THE HP CONSISTS OF AN ME OVER GPON CUSTOMER THEN, WHERE APPLICABLE, THE ADDITIONAL ME SITE VISIT ITEM MAY BE CLAIMED IN CONJUNCTION WITH THIS ITEM TO DETERMINE THE ADDITIONAL ISP REQUIREMENTS SUCH AS THE FIBRE CABLE WITHIN THE CUSTOMER PREMISES, ISP CONFIRMATION/REQUIREMENTS, RFO SPEC, ETC. IF THE PROJECT CONSISTS OF MORE THAN ONE SPLITTER, THEN THE CLAIM WILL BE FOR THE ACTUAL NUMBER OF HP ENGINEERED.THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS), THE OPENING AND CLOSING OF WELDED MANHOLES (MAY BE CLAIMED SEPARATELY). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS ENGINEERING PER HOMES PASSED, EACH (EA)'),(3055591,'CI1.73','CI1.73 ASMBL SPLTR PNL','This item consists of the assembling of splitters in a splitter panel\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na. All Labour costs\nb. Unpacking, assembling and installation of all the required splitters in the Splitter Panel and associated components according to Openserve M&PΓÇÖs WIΓÇÖs, specifications\nc. The fitting, routing, and labelling of the splitters / fibre tails\nd. Cleaning of mid-couplers, connectors, etc.\ne. Testing of each splitter / fibre tails for continuity with the appropriate test equipment (i.e. Light source and power meter)\nf. Labelling\ng. Checking the installation of all hardware (I.e. cable connections, 1:2 splitters, etc)\nh. The supply and use of all minor materials, tools, test equipment, or specialised services /equipment to complete the installation required to specification.\n\nNote:\na. The assembly of the splitter panel is normally conducted off site.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na. The supply of the splitters and splitter panel\nb. Installation of the splitter panel into the cabinet (See separate item)\nc. All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per Splitter Panel (Irrespective of the number of splitters fitted/assembled into the splitter panel), each (EA)','EA',561.00,'MAINT,EQUIP:CI1.73,ASMBL SPLTR PNL','MAINTAIN, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER: CI1.73, TYPE: ASSEMBLING OF SPLITTERS IN A SPLITTER PANEL:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE ASSEMBLING OF\nSPLITTERS IN A SPLITTER PANEL. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ALL LABOUR COSTS, UNPACKING, ASSEMBLING AND INSTALLATION OF\nALL THE REQUIRED SPLITTERS IN THE SPLITTER PANEL AND ASSOCIATED COMPONENTS ACCORDING TO OPENSERVE M AND P#S WI S, SPECIFICATIONS,\nTHE FITTING, ROUTING, AND LABELLING OF THE SPLITTERS / FIBRE TAILS, CLEANING OF MID-COUPLERS, CONNECTORS, ETC., TESTING OF EACH\nSPLITTER / FIBRE TAILS FOR CONTINUITY WITH THE APPROPRIATE TEST EQUIPMENT (I.E. LIGHT SOURCE AND POWER METER), LABELLING, CHECKING\nTHE INSTALLATION OF ALL HARDWARE (I.E. CABLE CONNECTIONS, 1:2 SPLITTERS, ETC), THE SUPPLY AND USE OF ALL MINOR MATERIALS, TOOLS,\nTEST EQUIPMENT, OR SPECIALISED SERVICES /EQUIPMENT TO COMPLETE THE INSTALLATION REQUIRED TO SPECIFICATION. NOTE: THE ASSEMBLY OF\nTHE SPLITTER PANEL IS NORMALLY CONDUCTED OFF SITE. THE RATE EXCLUDES: THE SUPPLY OF THE SPLITTERS AND SPLITTER PANEL, INSTALLATION\nOF THE SPLITTER PANEL INTO THE CABINET (SEE SEPARATE ITEM), ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE UNIT OF MEASURE\n(UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SPLITTER PANEL (IRRESPECTIVE OF THE NUMBER OF SPLITTERS FITTED/ASSEMBLED INTO THE SPLITTER PANEL), EACH\n(EA)'),(3055633,'CI1.71','CI1.71 INSTL SLCK MANGR','This item consists of the Installation of a fibre Slack manager.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\n\na. Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals\nb. Obtaining all work refs.\nc. Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nd. Labour for the installation of the Slack manager\ne. Labelling\nf. Minor build material\ng. Submission of documentation, such as:\ni. Quality acceptance certificate\nii. Quality tick sheet\niii. IE6 document.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel related costs (See Service fee items).\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per Slack manager, each (EA).','EA',552.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI1.71,SLCK MNGR','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER: CI1.71, TYPE: SLACK MANAGER:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE INSTALLATION OF A FIBRE SLACK MANAGER. THE\nRATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS CONTROL APPROVALS, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS., INTERFACE\nMANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SLACK MANAGER, LABELLING, MINOR\nBUILD MATERIAL, SUBMISSION OF DOCUMENTATION, SUCH AS: QUALITY ACCEPTANCE CERTIFICATE, QUALITY TICK SHEET, IE6 DOCUMENT. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE ITEMS). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SLACK MANAGER, EACH (EA).'),(3055638,'CI1.72','CI1.72 INSTL SPLTR PNL','This item consists of the Installation of a pre-assembled Splitter Panel into a cabinet.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na. Arranging and obtaining all site access control approvals\nb. Obtaining all work refs.\nc. Interface management with own or Telkom Sub-Contractors, when required\nd. Labour for the installation of the pre-assembled splitter panel into a cabinet\ne. Labelling\nf. Minor build material\ng. Submission of documentation, such as:\ni. Quality acceptance certificate\nii. Quality tick sheet\niii. IE6 document.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na. All travel related costs (See Service fee items)\nb. Assembly of the splitter panel (See separate item)\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per splitter panel installed, each (EA).','EA',552.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI1.72,SPLTR PNL','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER: CI1.72, TYPE: PRE-ASSEMBLED SPLITTER PANEL:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE INSTALLATION OF A\nPRE-ASSEMBLED SPLITTER PANEL INTO A CABINET. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: ARRANGING AND OBTAINING ALL SITE ACCESS\nCONTROL APPROVALS, OBTAINING ALL WORK REFS., INTERFACE MANAGEMENT WITH OWN OR TELKOM SUB-CONTRACTORS, WHEN REQUIRED, LABOUR FOR THE\nINSTALLATION OF THE PRE-ASSEMBLED SPLITTER PANEL INTO A CABINET, LABELLING, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL, SUBMISSION OF DOCUMENTATION, SUCH\nAS: QUALITY ACCEPTANCE CERTIFICATE, QUALITY TICK SHEET, IE6 DOCUMENT. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS (SEE SERVICE FEE\nITEMS) ,ASSEMBLY OF THE SPLITTER PANEL (SEE SEPARATE ITEM). THE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER SPLITTER PANEL\nINSTALLED, EACH (EA).'),(3057513,'CI1.69.1','CI1.69.1 SUPLY + INSTLN ENCLSR: ALLBRO UT7','This item consists of the supply and installation of an Allbro UT7 screw lid enclosure (310 x 210 x 125mm)\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	The cost of the Allbro UT7 screw lid enclosure (310 x 210 x 125mm)\nb.	The mounting/installation of the enclosure.\nc.	Minor build material (i.e. screws, bolts, etc.) \n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel related costs to and from site (See Service fee document)\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per enclosure, each (EA)','EA',819.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI1.69.1,ENCLSR: ALLBRO U','INSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER: CI1.69.1, TYPE: ALLBRO UT7 SCREW LID ENCLOSURE (310 X 210 X 125MM), ADDITIONAL TASK: SUPPLY:THE\nRATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE COST OF THE ALLBRO UT7 SCREW LID ENCLOSURE (310 X 210 X 125MM), THE MOUNTING/INSTALLATION\nOF THE ENCLOSURE, MINOR BUILD MATERIAL (I.E. SCREWS, BOLTS, ETC.). THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL RELATED COSTS TO AND FROM SITE\n(SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER ENCLOSURE, EACH (EA)'),(3057810,'CI3.19.1','CI3.19.1 SUPL, INSTL GALV CND 50MM','This item consists of the supply and installation of 50mm galvanised conduit to walls.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	The supply of the 50mm galvanised conduit,\nb.	The fastening of the conduit to walls, towers, structures, etc.,\nc.	The installing of all sizes and types of cable / ducts in the conduit when required,\nd.	The supply of all minor material (i.e. bends, joints, couplings, fastening material, saddles, wall plugs, straps, galvanised steel tape, buckles, etc.),\ne.	Reinstatement of surfaces where necessary.\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\nb.	The supply of all cables and ducts that need to be inserted into the 50mm conduit (OS to supply) \nNote: This item may NOT be used on poles. (See separate installation item exclusive for installation of 50mm conduit on poles)\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',126.35,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.19.1,GALV CND 50MM,SUPLY','INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.19.1,GALV CND 50MM,SUPLYINSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER: CI3.19.1, TYPE: 50MM GALVANISED CONDUIT TO WALLS, ADDITIONAL TASK: SUPPLY:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE\nSUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF 50MM GALVANISED CONDUIT TO WALLS. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY OF THE 50MM\nGALVANISED CONDUIT, THE FASTENING OF THE CONDUIT TO WALLS, TOWERS, STRUCTURES, ETC., THE INSTALLING OF ALL SIZES AND TYPES OF CABLE\n/ DUCTS IN THE CONDUIT WHEN REQUIRED, THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. BENDS, JOINTS, COUPLINGS, FASTENING MATERIAL, SADDLES,\nWALL PLUGS, STRAPS, GALVANISED STEEL TAPE, BUCKLES, ETC.), REINSTATEMENT OF SURFACES WHERE NECESSARY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nCOSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT), THE SUPPLY OF ALL CABLES AND DUCTS THAT NEED TO BE INSERTED INTO THE 50MM\nCONDUIT (OS TO SUPPLY)NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY NOT BE USED ON POLES. (SEE SEPARATE INSTALLATION ITEM EXCLUSIVE FOR INSTALLATION OF 50MM\nCONDUIT ON POLES). THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT).'),(3057811,'CI3.18.2','CI3.18.2 SUPL, INSTL GALV CND 32MM','This item consists of the supply and installation of 32mm galvanised conduit to walls. \n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	The supply of the 32mm galvanised conduit, \nb.	The fastening of the conduit to walls, towers, structures, etc.,\nc.	The installing of all sizes and types of cable /ducts in the conduit when required,\nd.	The supply of all minor material (i.e. bends, joints, couplings, fastening material, saddles, wall plugs, straps, galvanised steel tape, buckles, etc.),\ne.	Reinstatement of surfaces where necessary.\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document),\nb.	The supply of all cables and ducts that need to be inserted into the 32mm conduit (OS to supply) \n\nNote: This item may NOT be used on poles. \n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per metre (MT).','MT',95.06,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.18.2,GALV CND 32MM,SUPLY','INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.18.2,GALV CND 32MM,SUPLYINSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER: CI3.18.2, TYPE: 32MM GALVANISED CONDUIT TO WALLS, ADDITIONAL TASK: SUPPLY:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE\nSUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF 32MM GALVANISED CONDUIT TO WALLS. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: THE SUPPLY OF THE 32MM\nGALVANISED CONDUIT, THE FASTENING OF THE CONDUIT TO WALLS, TOWERS, STRUCTURES, ETC., THE INSTALLING OF ALL SIZES AND TYPES OF CABLE\n/DUCTS IN THE CONDUIT WHEN REQUIRED, THE SUPPLY OF ALL MINOR MATERIAL (I.E. BENDS, JOINTS, COUPLINGS, FASTENING MATERIAL, SADDLES,\nWALL PLUGS, STRAPS, GALVANISED STEEL TAPE, BUCKLES, ETC.), REINSTATEMENT OF SURFACES WHERE NECESSARY. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL\nCOSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT), THE SUPPLY OF ALL CABLES AND DUCTS THAT NEED TO BE INSERTED INTO THE 32MM\nCONDUIT (OS TO SUPPLY). NOTE: THIS ITEM MAY NOT BE USED ON POLES. THE UNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER METRE (MT).'),(3057812,'CI3.42','CI3.42 INSTL CND 50MM','This item consists of the Installation of a 50mm conduit (i.e. pole piece) (PE100 plastic conduit or 50mm galvanised steel conduit) from 350mm below the ground level up against a pole.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	Labour for the installation of a 50mm conduit (PE100 plastic conduit or 50mm galvanised steel conduit) on a pole, \nb.	Exposure (Digging), backfilling, compacting and reinstatements at the base of the pole, to obtain the necessary slow bend entry / access to the pole.\nc.	The cleating / fastening of the 50mm conduit to the pole, above and below the ground surface.\nd.	The supply of all cleating / fastening material. (galvanised steel tape, buckles, etc.),\ne.	The installing of all sizes and types of cables / ducts (i.e. direct buried (CST) cables, 2-way 16/13mm black UV protected micro duct, 32mm duct, etc.) into the 50mm conduit according to Specifications and approved Methods and Procedures,\nf.	The testing of poles when working on all existing poles / routes. It is the Service ProviderΓÇÖs responsibility to ensure that all existing poles are safe to be worked on, \n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document),\nb.	The supply of the 50mm conduit (50mm PE100 plastic or 50mm galvanised steel conduit) (OS to supply),\nc.	The supply of all cables and ducts that need to be inserted into the 50mm conduit (OS to supply) \n\nThe specification for this item is:\na.	OS-000854\nb.	CTO-003908\n\nThe unit of measure (UOM) for this item is per conduit / pole piece (5m x 50mm PE100 plastic conduit or 4m x 50mm galvanised steel conduit), each (EA)','EA',162.00,'INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.42,CND 50MM','INSTL,EQUIP:CI3.42,CND 50MMINSTALL, EQUIPMENT:ITEM NUMBER: CI3.42, TYPE: 50MM CONDUIT (I.E. POLE PIECE) (PE100 PLASTIC CONDUIT OR 50MM GALVANISED STEEL\nCONDUIT):THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE INSTALLATION OF A 50MM CONDUIT (I.E. POLE PIECE) (PE100 PLASTIC CONDUIT OR 50MM GALVANISED STEEL\nCONDUIT) FROM 350MM BELOW THE GROUND LEVEL UP AGAINST A POLE. THE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: LABOUR FOR THE INSTALLATION\nOF A 50MM CONDUIT (PE100 PLASTIC CONDUIT OR 50MM GALVANISED STEEL CONDUIT) ON A POLE, EXPOSURE (DIGGING), BACKFILLING, COMPACTING\nAND REINSTATEMENTS AT THE BASE OF THE POLE, TO OBTAIN THE NECESSARY SLOW BEND ENTRY / ACCESS TO THE POLE, THE CLEATING / FASTENING\nOF THE 50MM CONDUIT TO THE POLE, ABOVE AND BELOW THE GROUND SURFACE, THE SUPPLY OF ALL CLEATING / FASTENING MATERIAL. (GALVANISED\nSTEEL TAPE, BUCKLES, ETC.), THE INSTALLING OF ALL SIZES AND TYPES OF CABLES / DUCTS (I.E. DIRECT BURIED (CST) CABLES, 2-WAY 16/13MM\nBLACK UV PROTECTED MICRO DUCT, 32MM DUCT, ETC.) INTO THE 50MM CONDUIT ACCORDING TO SPECIFICATIONS AND APPROVED METHODS AND\nPROCEDURES, THE TESTING OF POLES WHEN WORKING ON ALL EXISTING POLES / ROUTES. IT IS THE SERVICE PROVIDER#S RESPONSIBILITY TO ENSURE\nTHAT ALL EXISTING POLES ARE SAFE TO BE WORKED ON. THE RATE EXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT),\nTHE SUPPLY OF THE 50MM CONDUIT (50MM PE100 PLASTIC OR 50MM GALVANISED STEEL CONDUIT) (OS TO SUPPLY), THE SUPPLY OF ALL CABLES AND\nDUCTS THAT NEED TO BE INSERTED INTO THE 50MM CONDUIT (OS TO SUPPLY). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS: OS-000854,  CTO-003908.\nTHE UNIT OF MEASURE (UOM) FOR THIS ITEM IS PER CONDUIT / POLE PIECE (5M X 50MM PE100 PLASTIC CONDUIT OR 4M X 50MM GALVANISED STEEL\nCONDUIT), EACH (EA)'),(3058140,'CI3.43','CI3.43 CTNG METLC PIPE','This item consists of the cutting and removal of all sizes and types of existing metallic pipes (empty or occupied), in manholes, non-standard manholes, accessible pipe junction box, jointing pit etc.\n\nThe rate includes but is not limited to:\na.	Handling, cutting, removal and disposal of all cut pipe pieces and lengths,\nb.	All tools and equipment required to complete the work,\nc.	Minor materials (i.e. cleaning, fastening materials, etc.),\nd.	Pumping and controlling of water, \ne.	Supporting of all services during execution (i.e. telecommunication cables, electrical cables, water, sewerage pipes, etc.), \nf.	Protection of cables within and surrounding the pipe to be cut to ensure that they are not damaged in the process.\n\nThe rate excludes:\na.	All travel costs to and from site (See Service fee document).\n\nThe Specification for this item is: \na.	325. CTO-004654.\n\nThe unit of measure for this item is per pipe, each (EA)','EA',250.00,'REMV,PIPE:CI3.43,METLC','REMOVE, PIPE:ITEM NUMBER: CI3.43, MATERIAL: METALLIC:THIS ITEM CONSISTS OF THE CUTTING AND REMOVAL OF ALL SIZES AND TYPES OF\nEXISTING METALLIC PIPES (EMPTY OR OCCUPIED), IN MANHOLES, NON-STANDARD MANHOLES, ACCESSIBLE PIPE JUNCTION BOX, JOINTING PIT ETC.\nTHE RATE INCLUDES BUT IS NOT LIMITED TO: HANDLING, CUTTING, REMOVAL AND DISPOSAL OF ALL CUT PIPE PIECES AND LENGTHS, ALL TOOLS AND\nEQUIPMENT REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THE WORK, MINOR MATERIALS (I.E. CLEANING, FASTENING MATERIALS, ETC.), PUMPING AND CONTROLLING OF\nWATER, SUPPORTING OF ALL SERVICES DURING EXECUTION (I.E. TELECOMMUNICATION CABLES, ELECTRICAL CABLES, WATER, SEWERAGE PIPES, ETC.),\nPROTECTION OF CABLES WITHIN AND SURROUNDING THE PIPE TO BE CUT TO ENSURE THAT THEY ARE NOT DAMAGED IN THE PROCESS. THE RATE\nEXCLUDES: ALL TRAVEL COSTS TO AND FROM SITE (SEE SERVICE FEE DOCUMENT). THE SPECIFICATION FOR THIS ITEM IS:  325. CTO-004654. THE\nUNIT OF MEASURE FOR THIS ITEM IS PER PIPE, EACH');
